window.FWN_MARTIAL_PEAK_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_PEAK_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6001,"title":"Chapter 6001: Price","paragraphs":["This was the reason why Yang Kai thanked Mo in the end.","“I’m afraid this is the end he wanted.”","Mu had protected the Human Race and the Universe for countless years, and even after her death, she had left behind many contingencies and hidden hands.","Although the world was in ruins and the Human Race were like ants to Mo, it was still what Mu wanted to protect. Under the premise that the world had someone else strong enough to protect it, Mo was willing to go along with Mu’s Will.","Of course, if Yang Kai didn’t have the necessary strength, Mo wouldn’t mind killing him. In that case, Mo would have still set aside a Great Territory for the Human Race to live and multiply after he dominated the entire Universe. This way, the Human Race wouldn’t be wiped out and he would have a reasonable explanation for Mu.","At the end of the day, Mo was not inherently evil. In the Late Ancient Era, he had even protected the Human Race and took it upon himself to help them gain their freedom. If it weren’t for him and the 10 Martial Ancestors working together, the Human Race of that era would not have been able to defeat the Early Ancient Era’s Great Monsters.","It was just that he was unable to control his gradually growing power and eventually lost his way, especially after Mu’s demise. When she died, no one was able to restrain him anymore.","Today’s ending was something Mo himself probably sought from the start.","Everyone sunk into silence after listening to Yang Kai’s explanation of what truly happened, as what Mu would want others to know. Their current feelings were tough to describe.","Mo’s life might have been filled with misery, but he was still the one who had brought about the pain and suffering of the Human Race for millions of years. Had there been no Mo, the Human Race would have ruled the world unchallenged after defeating the Early Ancient Era’s Great Monsters. There would not have been a war that lasted for so many eons.","The Black Ink disaster had caused unimaginable losses to the Human Race, with countless elites having sacrificed their lives to bring it to an end.","As far as the Human Race was concerned, no matter how miserable Mo’s life had been, it was an irrefutable fact that he was the Human Race’s greatest enemy.","As the adage goes, ‘The winner is the King, and the loser is the villain!’","*Kacha...*","Suddenly, it sounded as if something had cracked. Everyone promptly turned to look at the source, and was immediately shocked.","“Big Brother!” Yang Xue called out, staring at Yang Kai’s face in horror.","Everyone also looked serious as a crack appeared on Yang Kai’s face. It was not a normal wound, and neither was Yang Kai bleeding from it.","After the first crack, another one appeared soon after, and then another, and another...","They were not just on Yang Kai’s face, but on his hands as well.","The current Yang Kai looked like a piece of porcelain that was on the verge of shattering, and everyone could feel fearsome Daos Strengths seeping from these cracks.","Yang Kai looked down at his hands and muttered to himself, “It came faster than I expected!”","He seemed to have anticipated his current situation.","“What’s happening?” Su Yan asked from behind him, her tender body uncontrollably trembling.","After so many years of struggle, Mo was finally defeated and the Black Ink disaster was resolved. The future belonged to the Human Race, and it was foreseeable that the world would become a far better place.","Yang Kai was the biggest contributor in the final battle, but at this moment, his entire body was shrouded in an inexplicable crisis. Everyone could not help but be nervous.","What was even more disturbing was that no one had ever seen such injuries before.","Yang Kai gently patted the back of Su Yan’s hand, comforting her, “I won’t die, but I don’t have much time left.”","“What does that mean?” Xiao Xiao asked.","“How should I put it...” Everyone around him was worried to death, but Yang Kai, the main person involved, remained completely calm and composed, “The Shadow Technique was created by Mu with the Space-Time River as its foundation. I inherited her legacy and walked the same path as her, so naturally I can also use this Secret Technique.”","“However, Mu’s Space-Time River was incomplete, so her Shadow Technique was actually incomplete. She could only summon shadows from the past, and once those shadows dispersed, the memories of that period would also disappear. On the other hand, I have perfected this Secret Technique and can summon shadows from the future. Each shadow I summoned in the battle just now was from 1,000 years in my future. Now that the shadows have already been destroyed, I must pay the price.”","The more powerful a Secret Technique was, the harder it was to use it. The Shadow Technique was undoubtedly the most powerful Secret Technique that had ever appeared in this world, especially since Yang Kai had surpassed his predecessor and used it to defeat Mo. The price he had to pay would definitely not be small either.","“Once the shadows of the past are destroyed, the memories of the corresponding past will also disappear. So, what kind of price do you have to pay when your future shadow is destroyed?” Mi Jing Lun asked solemnly.","“I won’t exist in those periods in the future.”","“You won’t exist? What do you mean?”","“Although I can’t explain it clearly, you can think of it as a literal statement.”","Mi Jing Lun was silent for a moment, digesting this unbelievable news, “You summoned eight shadows, so does that mean 8,000 years of your future just... disappeared?”","“Indeed!”","“What happens after 8,000 years?”","Yang Kai shook his head, “I have no idea.”","After all, this was the first time he had used the Shadow Technique, so although he knew that he would cease to exist for the next 8,000 years, all traces of his existence would be erased by the Space-Time Dao Strength of the Universe, he couldn’t say for certain what would happen after that.","“How could this be?” Yang Xue’s eyes turned red.","“It’s not a big problem, I should be able to return after 8,000 years,” Yang Kai comforted.","Despite his assurance, everyone could hear the uncertainty in his voice.","His back suddenly became lighter as Su Yan suddenly left.","She returned soon after, but this time she brought Yu Ru Meng and the others with her.","The eyes of all the women turned red as they tried to hold back their grief, preventing their tears from rolling down. Su Yan had already briefed everyone of the situation, so they knew the crisis Yang Kai was about to encounter.","In the short time Su Yan was not there though, further cracks had appeared on Yang Kai and the leakage of Dao Strengths had become more and more obvious.","Yang Kai really didn’t have much time left, and the backlash from the Shadow Technique was even stronger than he had imagined.","Mi Jing Lun shot a glance at the crowd, whereupon everyone apart from Yang Kai’s close relatives retreated to the side.","The women who had been brought here by Su Yan finally couldn’t hold it in any further and burst into tears.","In the end, it was Yu Ru Meng who acted like the Big Sister of the family and managed to compose herself first.","Before she could say anything more though, the skin on Yang Kai’s face began to peel off and disappear. Even though they were all Eighth and Ninth-Order Masters now, there was nothing they could do.","Everyone held back their grief as they helplessly watched Yang Kai’s figure gradually vanish.","At the very last moment, Yu Ru Meng shouted at Yang Kai, “You heartless bastard! Mark my words, if you don’t come back after 8,000 years, I’ll take my Sisters and marry someone else!”","Yang Kai gave her a smile, “This sounds so familiar...”","Yu Ru Meng’s Will finally shattered, and she broke into tears. She tightly grabbed Yang Kai’s hand, and begged, “You must come back! You must!”","Yang Kai swept his gaze over all of them one by one, as if he wanted to imprint their faces into the depths of his Soul, before gently nodding and assuring, “Of course!”","Right then, scattered specks of light emerged before an enormous river spanning across the void appeared, enveloping Yang Kai. Soon after, an enormous wave came crashing down on him, swallowing him into the river.","The river slowly disappeared, and so did Yang Kai along with it, leaving behind a group of women standing there in a daze, their endless sorrow flowing like a river.","“Something’s not right,” Mi Jing Lun, who was watching from afar, suddenly whispered before turning to Xiang Shan, “Do you feel it?”","Xiang Shan nodded his agreement, “There’s something wrong.”","The other Ninth-Order Masters more or less felt the same way. Although they couldn’t figure out what exactly was wrong, Ninth-Order Masters were extremely perceptive. Their senses were so sharp that even just a slight disparity around them would arouse their suspicion.","Everyone made their respective probes, but none of them were able to find anything amiss.","Unable to find anything wrong, they had no choice but to put this matter aside, but they still maintained a certain degree of vigilance.","The curtain of the final battle had already fallen. The allied Army had finished off the Black Ink Clan Army, while Mo had been completely sealed by Yang Kai. Although the greatest contributor had suffered severe backlash from his Secret Technique and had his existence wiped out by Space and Time for the next 8,000 years, when all was said and done, the victory needed to be publicized.","When Mi Jing Lun and the others returned and spread the news that Mo had been ended, the Human Race Army of millions that had been waiting here all cheered and danced in joy.","The war that had been going on for millions of years had finally come to an end. Now, all under the Heavens belonged to the Human Race!","After the battle, the casualties were counted and the aftermath was dealt with in an orderly manner.","The Small Stone Race Army had already withdrawn and returned to the Chaotic Dead Territory through the Void Corridor. The Human Race also began their withdrawal half a month later.","The Void Corridor created by Zhang Ruo Xi saved the Human Race a lot of time.","Not everyone left however, headed by Su Yan and Yu Ru Meng, Yang Kai’s Wives, his Disciples, Yang Xue, Yang Xiao, and several others all stayed behind.","They remained in the place where Yang Kai had disappeared, quietly waiting for his return.","The next 8,000 years would definitely be very dull and long, but so long as they could see Yang Kai the moment he returned, any amount of waiting would be worth it.","A fleet of dilapidated Warships entered the Chaotic Dead Territory through the Void Corridor. The current Zhang Ruo Xi could still somehow maintain the balance of Yin and Yang in her body, so the Chaotic Dead Territory was now a safe place.","Be that as it may, she couldn’t maintain this state for much longer. In order to fight Mo and kill the Royal Lords, she had burned too much of her Heavens Order Bloodline.","Once the Human Race Army left the Chaotic Dead Territory, she would break the harmony with the two. At that time, Big Brother Huang and Big Sister Lan would reappear, and Zhang Ruo Xi would lose her previous strength.","At the end of the day, if she didn’t have her Heavens Order Bloodline that could maintain the harmony of Yin and Yang, she would just be a Ninth-Order Master.","The fleet passed through the Chaotic Dead Territory and soon returned to the 3,000 Worlds.","Many years ago, when the Human Race Army first set off from the Star Boundary, they had some 30 million soldiers, but now, only slightly more than 10 million remained; around 60% of the soldiers had died in this final war.","Despite the terrible losses, compared to the solemn and miserable atmosphere they had when they first set out, everyone was high in spirits, and every Warship was buzzing with cheers and laughter, despite the sad state of the army.","On a certain Purifying Black Ink Warship that was so wrecked that it looked like it would fall apart at any moment, Mi Jing Lun was standing at the bow with Xiang Shan beside him.","The two calmly listened to the hustle and bustle on the other Warships and exchanged a knowing glance.","“The Human Race has won, but the greatest contributor is unable to celebrate with us, it’s quite regretful,” Mi Jing Lun couldn’t help but lament.","Xiang Shan nodded his agreement, “Now that I think about it, had he not forced those peace treaties with the Black Ink Clan, the Human Race wouldn’t have been able to accumulate enough strength.”","“That’s right,” Mi Jing Lun nodded, “By the looks of it, that treaty was an important turning point in the rise of the Human Race.”","“What was that treaty called?”","“What’s it called again?”","The two Ninth-Order Masters glanced at each other before the smiles on their faces slowly faded away, gradually replaced by solemn looks..."]},{"number":6002,"title":"Chapter 6002: Response","paragraphs":["While the millions of Human Race Soldiers were making the trek back home, all the Ninth-Order Masters gathered aboard the only intact Purifying Black Ink Warship remaining.","Compared to their peak, the number of Ninth-Order Masters had undoubtedly decreased significantly, with many of the recently advanced Ninth-Order Masters having perished in the battle.","Only 20 or so had managed to survive.","Apart from the Ninth-Order Masters, Fu Guang was also invited.","Everyone took their seats. Most of them were still injured, their auras weak and unstable. The battle ended not that long ago, and even with the recuperative abilities of Ninth-Order Masters, it was impossible for them to fully recover in such a short time, especially since the Human Race was running low on supplies, especially recovery pills.","One by one, the Ninth-Order Masters noticed the heavy air. They might not have an idea as to why Supreme Commander Mi had gathered all of them together, but they could tell that bad news was in store for them from his expression.","After the last Ninth-Order Master took their seat, Mi Jing Lun finally started addressing the crowd, “I’ve summoned you here today to confirm something.”","He looked around, paused for a moment, then recounted his conversation with Xiang Shan.","When the Ninth-Order Masters heard this, some were confused, some were lost in thought, and a few who realized the issue right away furrowed their brow.","Ou Yang Lie casually asked, “What’s there to fret about with your conversation with Big Head Xiang?”","He did not find anything wrong, it sounded just a normal chat to him.","“There’s a big problem!” Mi Jing Lun stared at him with a solemn expression, causing Ou Yang Lie to realize the gravity of the situation, despite not understanding what was the problem.","Xiang Shan explained, “The peace treaty we signed with the Black Ink Clan back then was of paramount importance and could be said to be the turning point in the entire war. It is impossible for Brother Mi and I to forget the details of such an important matter. It would’ve been nothing if it was just one of us having a hard time recalling certain trivial points of the treaty, but the problem is that neither of us can remember them. When we were discussing the treaty, both of us were unable to immediately recall even some of the basic details of the agreement. That should be absolutely impossible.”","Ou Yang Lie speculated, frowning, “Maybe you’re too tired from the battle?”","Xiang Shan focused his gaze on him, “Do you remember the first time you met Yang Kai?”","“Of course I remember,” Ou Yang Lie replied readily, “How could I forget such a thing? At that time, he...”","He slowly stopped talking. Obviously, he too had noticed the problem as his expression changed and a furrow appeared on his brow.","Xiang Shan then turned to the other Ninth-Order Masters and asked, “Everyone, why don’t you try recalling your encounters with Yang Kai, or some common knowledge about him!”","The Ninth-Order Masters complied.","Soon, a bewildered look took over everyone’s face.","Observing everyone’s expressions, Ou Yang Lie immediately understood that they too had encountered the same situation as him. He could not help but mumble, “How is this possible?”","When Xiang Shan asked him to, Ou Yang Lie attempted to recall the first time he met Yang Kai, but he actually couldn’t immediately remember it. It was as if his memory was blocked by an invisible barrier. It was right on the tip of his tongue, but he couldn’t enunciate it for some reason.","After struggling for a few breaths, he finally remembered that the first time he met Yang Kai was outside Great Evolution Pass. At that time, Ou Yang Lie was on a scouting mission with his Disciples, and Yang Kai arrived to meet him under Xiang Shan’s orders.","At that time, Yang Kai was only a Seventh-Order Master!","Mi Jing Lun’s voice sounded in everyone’s ears, “It’s not just you. After Brother Xiang and I discovered this problem, we ordered our men to ask the soldiers the same questions, and they too encountered the same situation. Regardless of whether they personally met with Yang Kai or simply heard stories about him, they were unable to immediately recall the details.”","“What caused this phenomenon?” Wu Qing asked in a low voice. He had just tried to recall things about Yang Kai, and it was indeed as Mi Jing Lun had described.","“I don’t know the exact reason, but I’m certain it has something to do with his Shadow Technique,” Mi Jing Lun continued, “Everyone should remember that Yang Kai said that the eight shadows were summoned from the next 8,000 years. He also said that because those eight shadows were destroyed, it meant that he would not exist for the next 8,000 years.”","Everyone nodded in acknowledgement as all of them were present when Mi Jing Lun and Yang Kai were discussing this.","“Yang Kai said that it was the price he paid to use the Shadow Technique, but now it seems that Yang Kai himself had underestimated the severity of this price. He thought that the price he had to pay would be to disappear for the next 8,000 years, but in reality, some kind of invisible force is slowly erasing all traces of his existence from this world! So, anything related to him would slowly become blurred in the memories of others.”","“Is such a thing really possible?” Ou Yang Lie found it hard to believe","The most direct way one would think that removing the traces of a person’s existence in this world meant was to kill that person, but the elimination that everyone encountered now was no longer as simple as just killing Yang Kai, even their memories of him were being lost.","Mi Jing Lun added, “Before Yang Kai used the Shadow Technique, even I hadn’t expected for such a bizarre Secret Technique to exist.”","Ou Yang Lie immediately fell silent.","The mysteries of the Shadow Technique were beyond their comprehension, so the price for using it was also unfathomable. As such, no matter how unbelievable Mi Jing Lun’s speculations were, there was indeed a possibility they were true.","“This is just the beginning. What I’m worried about is we might even forget everything about Yang Kai with time.”","All of the Ninth-Order Masters were shocked.","As the greatest hero who led the Human Race to victory and defeated Mo, Yang Kai should be remembered for all generations, but if the Human Race were to completely forget about him, that would truly be a tragic misfortune.","“What will happen if we completely forget about Yang Kai?” Mi Jing Lun asked.","No one could answer.","He didn’t ask any more, and instead postulated, “Before disappearing, Yang Kai said that he would return after 8,000 years, but even he did not sound certain of that. So, he might be able to return, or he might completely disappear. Right now, the traces of his existence are slowly being erased, which is akin to him disappearing. If one day everyone completely forgets about him, perhaps he might never appear again!”","Fu Guang, who had been silent all this time, finally spoke, “Supreme Commander Mi, do you mean to say that if many people in this world remember him and his fame remains widespread, perhaps it can help him return?”","Mi Jing Lun shook his head, “I’m not sure, but it is possible.”","“Then, it’s worth a shot!” Fu Guang nodded.","“However, the most important thing right now is to investigate the speed at which his traces are being erased. Only by confirming this matter can we make appropriate arrangements.”","“Agreed!”","“Agreed!”","“We’ll do as Supreme Commander Mi says.”","...","After many days of investigation by Ninth-Order Masters and questioning thousands of randomly selected soldiers, everyone reached an unfortunate conclusion.","The speed at which Yang Kai’s traces were being erased was increasing; more and more things related to Yang Kai were being forgotten. At this rate, everything related to Yang Kai would be completely gone in short order. By then, no one in this world would remember that there was once a hero who had saved the entire Human Race.","Mi Jing Lun couldn’t help but feel a sense of urgency. He immediately sent people back to the original location of the Primordial Heavens Source Grand Restriction to inform Su Yan and the others who were staying there. Although Su Yan and the others would most likely notice this on their own, it was always better to be prepared.","An advanced team had already been sent back to relay the news of their victory to the Human Race forces in the rear, so a joyful mood was already spreading.","When the Army returned, they were naturally received with warmth and celebration.","The Human Race Army had suffered heavy casualties in this battle, losing more than 60% of its soldiers. Be that as it may, it was all worth it as in the future, the world would no longer face the threat of Black Ink Strength.","But contrary to the expectations of everyone who had remained behind, the Crusade Force showed no signs of celebrating after their return; instead, they quickly dispersed as if there was a new mission waiting for them.","Soon, great statues were erected in the Star Boundary, Myriad Monsters World, and everywhere else the Human Race lived, whether it was a village, a town, or a city.","The statue depicted a brave and heroic man wielding a long spear that seemed to have a Dragon coiling around it. This man seemed to be staring down an invisible enemy, confronting them in battle.","At the base of the statue was Yang Kai’s name.","Meanwhile, Mi Jing Lun entered High Heaven Palace, and with the cooperation of Hua Qing Si and Xia Ning Chang, gathered all the people who had close relationships with Yang Kai. Afterwards, under Mi Jing Lun’s supervision, they jointly wrote a biography.","Naturally, it was Yang Kai’s biography, and it included all the big and small matters that had happened in his life.","There were no excessively embellished accounts in it, just the simple and factual descriptions. Nonetheless, anyone who read this biography would understand how magnificent Yang Kai’s life was.","Everyone would come to know that in the darkest era of the Human Race, it was he who tore through the darkness and brought a bright ray of hope to them.","They would also come to know that Yang Kai had ultimately paid a huge price to finally defeat the ancient being named Mo and end the war between the two Races that had lasted for millions of years!","Most importantly, they would know that the world could not forget him; otherwise, he would never be able to return!","After this biography was written, countless copies of it were made by High Heaven Palace disciples and distributed to all the places where the Human Race lived, especially the places where Yang Kai’s statue was erected. The Ninth-Order Masters even personally placed these jade slips containing Yang Kai’s biography into the statues.","This way, as long as someone examined the statue, they would be able to immediately perceive the contents of the jade slip and understand Yang Kai’s life experiences.","Many of the Human Race’s upper echelons were trying their best to prevent the Human Race from forgetting their greatest hero, Yang Kai.","On top of that, the Ninth Order Master once again convened a meeting after the Army had returned. Everyone felt that the world was vast and time was difficult to measure, so they decided that the year the Crusade Force returned to the Star Boundary would be designated as the first year of the Void Era!","Void was a title, the title of one of the greatest heroes that was slowly being forgotten.","As time passed away, new generations of Humans were born, matured, and aged. Everyone had already forgotten about Yang Kai, even the Ninth-Order Masters who had fought alongside him, but the statues that had been erected remained standing tall."]},{"number":6003,"title":"Chapter 6003 - 8,000 Years","paragraphs":["Void Era, year 7,999...","The Star Boundary, where High Heaven Cave Heaven, which was ranked first among the 36 Cave Heavens, was located, had its ban on entry lifted. Immediately, countless cultivators who were waiting outside the Star Boundary swarmed in and spread out.","The cultivators were entering the Star Boundary from every possible direction, and were in huge numbers. Although there were all sorts of people among the crowd, no one dared to act rashly on the Star Boundary; no matter what their temperament was, they had become kind and simple after setting foot onto this Universe World.","This wasn’t just because the Star Boundary was the domain of the strongest Cave Heaven, but also because Dao Temples of all the other Cave Heavens and Paradises were located here.","It could be said that one could find Seventh-Order Masters casually walking the streets in the Star Boundary, even Eighth-Order Masters were as common as dogs. Only the sighting of the legendary Ninth-Order Masters, who generally remained hidden, would cause some minor sensation.","If anyone acted irreverently here, not to mention the Sun tomorrow, he or she might not even see the Moon tonight.","The main reason why the Star Boundary was so lively was because the Void Festival that was celebrated once every millennia would be held here. Many of the younger generation didn’t know the origins of this festival, only that a ceremony was held at the turn of every millennium of the Void Era, and it had been celebrated seven times already. And if the one that was about to be held was also counted, this would be the eighth.","Rumour had it that 8,000 years ago, the living environment of the Human Race was extremely harsh. At that time, there was a species called the Black Ink Clan that nearly wiped out the Human Race and conquered the known Universe. Back then, the Human Race was truly on the verge of extinction.","However, thanks to its many great heroes and brave soldiers, the Human Race slowly regained their footing. In the end, the entire Human Race launched a grand crusade and completely eradicated the Black Ink Clan. From then on, the Human Race became the true rulers of this world.","As for the Void Festival, it was held to commemorate all the Humans who gave their lives in the war against the Black Ink Clan. It could be considered the biggest event in the entire Human Race.","The festival would be celebrated for an entire year, during which, anyone could freely enter the Star Boundary. It had to be known that as the territory of the strongest Cave Heaven, it was normally forbidden for outsiders to enter.","This wasn’t because High Heaven Cave Heaven was tyrannical, but because they had no other choice.","Since the end of the great war 8,000 years ago, although the Human Race had managed to quell the Black Ink disaster that had lasted for millions of years, they had paid an extremely heavy price.","Countless Masters had died in battle, while the entire 3,000 Worlds had been devastated by the Black Ink Clan. The only Universe Worlds suitable for the survival of the Human Race were the ones in High Heaven Territory and the Myriad Monsters Territory.","The number of habitable Universe Worlds had been significantly reduced, and as such, the living environment had also suffered. Cultivation resources were also in short supply.","As such, the birth of too many cultivators would inevitably lead to chaos. So, the current cultivators could no longer be as unrestrained as they were before the Black Ink Clan invaded the 3,000 Worlds. Everything had to be done in a planned manner.","8,000 years ago, the Ninth-Order Masters had jointly held a discussion and reached a consensus, which was that anyone with the aptitude to cultivate would have to report to the Cave Heavens and Paradises, and their cultivation matters would be arranged by one of these top forces.","This decision was strictly enforced with the joint efforts of all the Human Race Forces. So, all cultivators of the Human Race, regardless of their background or cultivation, were duly noted and recorded.","This decision made the already special Star Boundary even more exclusive.","The Star Boundary had a World Tree Clone, and was the first Open Heaven Realm Cradle!","The second Open Heaven Realm Cradle was the Myriad Monsters World.","In the years when the Human Race was fighting the Black Ink Clan, the two Open Heaven Realm Cradles, the Star Boundary and Myriad Monsters World, had given birth to many High-Rank Open Heaven Realm Masters. It could be said that these two Open Heaven Realm Cradles played a huge role in the Human Race’s victory in the final battle.","However, after the war ended, because of the limit in habitable areas, it was difficult for the Human Race to withstand the birth of so many new generation cultivators, which put the Star Boundary and Myriad Monster World in an extremely awkward position.","After returning from the crusade and realizing this problem, the Human Race’s higher-ups made another decision, which was to withdraw everyone from the Star Boundary and Myriad Monster World, especially the large number of ordinary people.","These ordinary people could not cultivate, but given their huge numbers, they could give birth to many children, some of which would have the aptitude for cultivation. If restrictions weren’t put in place, it wouldn’t be long before new generations of cultivators were born, which would inevitably lead to unnecessary unrest.","Even the people who remained in the Star Boundary and Myriad Monsters World were forbidden from having children. If they wanted to have children, they would have to leave these two Open Heaven Realm Cradles.","Of course, the Human Race’s upper echelons also knew that cutting off all avenues forward was not sustainable, so they left behind a glimmer of hope.","That hope lay in the Void Festival that was held every 1,000 years.","During this one-year-long grand festival, everyone was allowed to freely enter and exit the Star Boundary. If one could join one of the Dao Temples of the various Cave Heavens and Paradises, they would naturally be qualified to remain in the Star Boundary to cultivate.","It was difficult to calculate how many people had entered the Star Boundary every time the grand festival started, but the number who could truly worship the various Dao Temples was not that high.","This led to a strange phenomenon, which was that many pregnant women or young married couples would enter the Star Boundary during the festival. Those pregnant women would then find a place with excellent World Energy and live with their families, nourishing their fetus in peace, so that their unborn babies could enjoy the feedback from the World Tree Clone.","As for those young couples... They were only two when they arrived, but when they left, their wives’ stomachs would most likely be bulging.",".....","Jade Mountain Square, an extremely common market in the Star Boundary.","Because of the decisions made in the past, a large number of Humans were relocated away from the Star Boundary, leaving it quite sparsely populated. Owing to which, places like Jade Mountain Square were usually deserted.","In other words, this place was only bustling with Humans because the grand festival was approaching and countless people had poured into the Star Boundary.","A young couple was strolling around the market, holding hands. The man was suave and handsome, whereas the woman was as beautiful as a flower; they were a perfect match.","The woman’s belly happened to be slightly bulging; she was obviously pregnant.","At this moment, the Husband and Wife arrived before a tall statue and looked up.","The Wife kept reaching out to her Husband’s hand, who helplessly handed her the food in his hands and grumbled, “I told you not to eat so many sweets, why don’t you listen?”","His Wife didn’t even spare him a glance and bit down on the candied fruit in her hand, mumbling, “Who says I am the one who wants to eat it? Clearly it’s the child in my stomach who wants to eat!”","The Husband couldn’t help but roll his eyes. Every time she brought up the child in her womb, he couldn’t do anything about it.","“Dear, do you think this Yang Kai really exists?” The Wife quickly finished a stick of candied fruit and took another stick from her Husband’s hand, “Why are his statues everywhere?”","Wherever they went, wherever a Human settlement was present, they always found such statues. Rumour had it that these statues had been standing for nearly 8,000 years and had not been eroded by the passage of time at all. Obviously, they were protected by the power of an expert.","“How would I know?” The Husband brusquely replied.","His Wife muttered to herself, “His biographies are everywhere, and it seems that everyone has read it intensively. Moreover, according to his biography, he used some kind of profound Space-Time Secret Technique in order to defeat the ancient enemy, which caused all traces of him to be erased from people’s minds, and that he would never be able to return if everyone truly forgot about him. Counting the time, it just so happens that when this festival starts, it will be the time for him to return. Dear, why don’t we go take a look?”","The Husband’s face darkened, “Why are you looking for him?”","“He’s a hero! We Humans can have today thanks to his efforts and sacrifices. It’s only right that we pay respect to him.”","“His biography has been passed down for 8,000 years, who knows if it’s true or not...”","“I think he must be a wise and mighty man!”","*Crunch...Crunch...*","“Why are you eating my candied fruit?”","“So sour!”","“It’s obviously very sweet!”","“According to his biography, he had many Wives!”","“Hmph, you finally exposed your wild ambitions. My dear child, your Father doesn’t want us anymore, our lives are really miserable.”","“No, that’s not what I said, don’t be ridiculous!”","...","Everywhere where the Humans were gathered, similar conversations were happening between the young couples. Under the vigorous promotion and maintenance of various major Sects, the biography compiled by Mi Jing Lun had been widely circulated these past 8,000 years. It could be said that any Human older than 10 had read Yang Kai’s biography at least once.","As far as the later generation was concerned, this biography was just a storybook, allowing them to understand the magnificent life of a man named Yang Kai. As for whether the records in this biography were true or fabricated, no one could confirm.","This was something even the ancient cultivators of the Cave Heavens and Paradises were unable to determine, because in their memories, many of the things recorded in the biography had indeed happened, but none of them had the slightest impression of the man named Yang Kai being there.","If this was really the backlash of the so-called Shadow Secret Technique, it would be too terrifying.","Meanwhile, the Ninth-Order Masters had gathered at High Heaven Palace.","Compared to the crusade back then, the number of Ninth-Order Masters had undoubtedly increased.","There were more than 100 Ninth-Order Masters!","After all, all those rising stars, who possess the aptitude to advance to the Ninth-Order Open Heaven Realm, had gradually advanced over the last 8,000 years.","In the main hall, everyone was talking in small groups. Unless there was something important, the Ninth-Order Masters seldom gathered together. The Ninth-Order Masters also rarely appeared in public. Only a grand event like the Void Festival could gather all the Ninth-Order Masters together.","With over 100 Ninth-Order Masters, the Human Race’s foundation had reached a peak that it had not seen in over 10,000 years. Whether it was the newly advanced Ninth-Order Masters, or the old veterans, all of them had participated in the war against the Black Ink Clan.","Now that they had gathered together, it was only natural for them to reminisce about the glorious past and as they watched the current generation compete against each other.","Ou Yang Lie was especially boisterous as he moved through the crowd. When he started talking about the great battles he had fought in the past, he unceasingly beamed with joy. When he got excited, he even pulled his Disciple, Gong Lian over, “In the past, when this Old Master was only an Eighth-Order Open Heaven Realm Master, when I fought against a Pseudo-Royal Lord alone, that Pseudo-Royal Lord wet his pants in terror. This brat saw it with his own eyes. Hey, tell them!”"]},{"number":6004,"title":"Chapter 6004: Chanting","paragraphs":["Gong Lian, who was still called brat by Ou Yang Lie, had already reached the Ninth Order. Basically, his cultivation was the same as Ou Yang Lie’s, but as there was still a Master and Disciple relationship between them. Even if he was a Ninth-Order Master, he could not go against Ou Yang Lie. So, he could not help but nod his confirmation after hearing this, “Honoured Master is telling the truth!”","Ou Yang Lie’s laughter became even more carefree.","A few of the newly advanced Ninth-Order Masters also started laughing, all of them knowing how Ou Yang Lie loved to brag and deciding to just go along with it.","All of them had witnessed or experienced the might of a Pseudo-Royal Lord first-hand, and it was definitely not something an Eighth-Order Master could contend with, unless they formed a Battle Formation.","Be that as it may, back when there weren’t many Eighth-Order Masters, Ou Yang Lie had indeed fought a Pseudo-Royal Lord alone, and it was him who was beaten to the point that he had wet his pants. Even so, fighting a Pseudo-Royal Lord alone was still an incredible feat in itself.","At that moment, the noisy hall suddenly fell silent, everyone stopped blowing their own trumpet and raised their eyes, looking directly above.","In that direction was a calm and composed, half-white-haired Ninth-Order Master with a smile on his lips. He swept his gaze over everyone before addressing them, “Ladies and gentlemen, it’s been 1,000 years since we last met, but it seems everyone’s noble bearing is still the same. Hmm, there are also a few new faces, very good.”","Everyone greeted with a bow, “Greetings, Supreme Commander Mi.”","The person who had arrived was none other than Mi Jing Lun. Although the Human Race’s Crusade Force and the various Armies had been disbanded, Mi Jing Lun’s title of Supreme Commander had remained. In terms of cultivation, Mi Jing Lun might not be the strongest Ninth-Order Master, but in every battle against the Black Ink Clan, he had played a far greater role than any other Ninth-Order Master. There was no battle in which he had not wracked his brain hard to map out a strategy for victory, and it was he who had ultimately coordinated and dispatched the various troops.","He was a cultivator of the same era as Ou Yang Lie, Xiang Shan, and Wei Jun Yang, but if they were to stand together, Mi Jing Lun would definitely look older because he had been under even greater stress and for a longer duration during the thousands of years of war.","Above the main hall, Mi Jing Lun returned the greeting before continuing, “It’s the day of the Void Festival. Counting the time, this is already the eighth celebration, and I’m sure everyone knows what this means.”","Hearing this, everyone’s expressions became solemn.","“For a long time, there have been gaps in our memories. There appears to be traces of a person’s existence in many key memories, but whether it’s us or others, none of us can remember this person. I don’t know what kind of mood I was in when I oversaw the compilation of this person’s biography, but now that I think about it, it was definitely the best decision I’ve ever made in my life. All the signs indicate that this person should’ve really existed, and that all the accounts in this person’s biography should indeed be true. This person is the greatest contributor to the Human Race’s victory over the Black Ink Clan!”","Unlike the cultivators with low cultivation, although the Ninth-Order Masters present here had some gaps in their memories, these missing memories could be perfectly filled in by Yang Kai’s biography; therefore, they could conclude that Yang Kai really did exist and the records in his biography were not fabricated.","The reason they had forgotten about Yang Kai was because of the mysteries of the Shadow Secret Technique.","“A Hero cannot be allowed to be forgotten; otherwise, the current Human Race does not deserve to live. 8,000 years have already passed, and it is time for him to return. The Void Ceremony has been conducted precisely for this moment. Everyone, the arrangements we had laid back then should be used, it’s time to witness the truth!”","The world only knew that the Void Festival’s ceremony was a grand event for the entire Human Race, but didn’t know that it was a hidden hand Mi Jing Lun and the other Ninth-Order Masters had arranged long ago.","When they had set up this contingency back then, perhaps they had still not completely forgotten about Yang Kai; but now, they really could not remember anything about him. It didn’t matter if they didn’t remember though, as long as the plan worked.","“Please instruct us, Supreme Commander Mi!” The Ninth-Order Masters cupped their fists.","Mi Jing Lun lightly smiled, “Then let us see if all of this is just an unrealistic conjecture on our part or if we really have forgotten something!”","One after another, the Ninth-Order Masters received their orders and flew out of the hall, quickly disappearing, leaving only one Ninth-Order Master behind.","This was a Titled Great Emperor recognized by the Star Boundary and the only surviving Great Emperor who had managed to break through to the Ninth Order. There had been other Ninth-Order Great Emperors from the Star Boundary, but they had all fallen during the crusade.","The hall sunk into complete silence as Mi Jing Lun and the Great Emperor patiently waited.","10 days later, Mi Jing Lun finally opened his eyes and glanced at the Ninth-Order Great Emperor, “It’s about time.”","The Ninth-Order Great Emperor slightly nodded before slowly closing his eyes and spreading his Divine Sense; the next instant, he had become one with the entire Star Boundary.","Right then, in every settlement across the Universe World, Yang Kai’s statues, which had stood tall for 8,000 years, suddenly started glowing, attracting the attention of countless people.","Soon after, a voice started to reverberate from the statue, chanting something. What the voice was reciting was the contents of Yang Kai’s biography.","The voice seemed to contain some kind of mysterious power, causing everyone who heard it to involuntarily stop in their tracks and quietly listen. As the chanting continued, an enormous picture scroll seemed to have filled everyone’s vision. The picture scroll was impressively portraying the life of a cultivator named Yang Kai and how he gradually grew to become the strongest, eventually leading the Human Race to defeat their enemies.","Not just in the Star Boundary, even in Myriad Monsters Territory, on every Universe World where the Humans lived, the set up in the statues was activated by the Ninth-Order Masters.","At this moment, that chanting was simultaneously ringing in the ears of trillions of Humans.","Once, twice, three times...","Gradually, people began to read along the voice coming from the statue. Almost everyone had read Yang Kai’s biography, and many scholars had even memorized it by heart. Only, the biography which in the past was only read to pass time was given heavy importance today.","Trillions of Humans were chanting the Void Great Emperor’s real name.","At the same time, in the distant void, on the battlefield where the final battle between Yang Kai and Mo was fought, a few people were gathered together inside a floating palace.","There weren’t many people, only a dozen or so, but apart from a middle-aged couple, the lowest cultivation of the others was the Eighth-Order, and there were actually quite a number of Ninth-Order Masters present.","Everyone gathered here was Yang Kai’s close relative.","His parents, his Wives, his Disciples, Yang Xiao, Yang Xue...","These people had been waiting here for 8,000 years. Xia Ning Chang had originally stayed behind to guard High Heaven Palace because, despite her high cultivation, she had very little experience in fighting; moreover, she was an Alchemy Great Grandmaster and was more useful stationed in the rear. However, for the final crusade, even she was roped in.","After their triumphant return, once Xia Ning Chang had helped compile Yang Kai’s biography with Mi Jing Lun, she immediately returned here.","Naturally, Mi Jing Lun immediately set out to fetch all those close to Yang Kai, bringing Yang Ying Feng and Dong Su Zhu here to meet up with Su Yan and the others to wait for Yang Kai’s return.","Their wait had now lasted for 8,000 years!"]},{"number":6005,"title":"Chapter 6005: Supreme Master","paragraphs":["The Shadow Technique’s backlash struck without any notice, and was impossible to guard against. At first, Yang Kai’s relatives could still remember him, but gradually, all their memories of him began to fade away, and eventually disappeared.","One after another, gaps began to appear in everyone’s memories.","For a period of time, everyone had even forgotten why they had gathered here until they remembered that they were waiting for a very important person. As for who that person was, none of them had any impression of him.","The biography that Xia Ning Chang brought back with her had a great effect. The things recorded in the biography and the remaining memories in their minds perfectly complemented each other. This helped them know that a person named Yang Kai had appeared in their lives, and that person held quite a huge place in their hearts.","Not far from their location was a Void Corridor leading straight to Chaotic Dead Territory.","At this moment, a figure walked out from the Void Corridor. It was none other than Zhang Ruo Xi.","Ruo Xi’s cultivation was currently at the peak of the Ninth Order, though the wings on her back had disappeared due to separating from the power of Yin and Yang.","Her Heaven’s Order Bloodline had been almost completely burned out in the final battle, so she was no longer able to maintain the delicate balance between the two opposing powers. So, she had no choice but to return to Chaotic Dead Territory and strip away the power of Yin and Yang.","Although the loss of her Heaven’s Order Bloodline was a significant detriment to her, it didn’t have much of an impact on her personal strength. It was just that it would be difficult for her to regain the phenomenal power she had displayed that time in the future.","Walking out of the Void Corridor, and identifying her bearing, Ruo Xi quickly arrived at Su Yan and the others’ location.","Noticing her appearance, everyone looked at her.","“It’s starting,” Ruo Xi stated softly.","Everyone nodded as a solemn look took over their faces.","On the platform in front of the palace, everyone sat down cross-legged and calmly started reciting Yang Kai’s name.","At first, nothing out of the ordinary happened. Over the past 8,000 years, everyone had done similar things countless times just to remind themselves not to forget that name.","However, as time went by, a different feeling slowly began to rise in their hearts. Everyone felt suffocated, as if there was a mountain pressing down on them, one that was becoming heavier and heavier. As this suffocating feeling grew stronger and stronger, the forgotten emotions also began to awaken, and along with them, a painful longing gripped their hearts. No one knew who they were missing, and none of them had a clear picture of them in their heart, but they had this feeling that someone who had left a deep mark in their lives had been forgotten, and that person’s name was...","...","“Yang Kai!”","In a vivid and colourful mysterious void filled with chaos and distortions, a tall and stalwart man with a sword in his hands let out an angry roar before swinging it down.","This sword strike almost cut the Space-Time River in two, revealing Yang Kai’s flickering figure behind it. By the time the water rolled back after the strike, Yang Kai had already arrived before the sword-wielding man. He then raised his hand and pointed a finger towards the opponent, sending a wave of water towards the stalwart figure.","The stalwart man’s expression instantly changed. Having fought Yang Kai for thousands of years, he naturally understood the might of this seemingly unremarkable wave. This wave contained the might of 10,000 Grand Daos, so even he didn’t dare to let himself get swallowed by it.","The stalwart man raised his sword and slashed out, shattering the incoming wave and splashing droplets of water flying in all directions. At the same time, the stalwart man quickly withdrew as if he was avoiding snakes and scorpions.","Yang Kai didn’t chase after him and simply stood in place.","Yang Kai sighed in his heart. When he had used the Shadow Secret Technique to defeat Mo and was corroded by the Space-Time Dao Strength, he basically thought that he would fall into a deep slumber or something similar, but how could he have known he would appear in this mysterious place in the blink of an eye.","After arriving here, Yang Kai began exploring and to his astonishment, he discovered he was not alone here! There were actually many other Masters!","These Masters were no weaker than him, with some even being stronger.","This revelation left him in total shock, because in the entire world, whether it was his cultivation or his comprehension of his Grand Daos, no one could hold a candle to him. Even Mo, who had 30% of his Source sealed, had been killed by him, so who in this Universe could be his opponent?","But here, there were many Masters here who could exchange blows evenly with Yang Kai.","What left him even more speechless was that the people here were all extremely belligerent. It did not matter whether there were any grievances between them or not, once two parties met, a fight broke out at least 90% of the time. Battles seemed to become the prime motivation for the survival of the living beings here.","In the beginning, Yang Kai had suffered quite a bit.","But his situation gradually improved over time as his injuries healed and his comprehension of the 10,000 Grand Daos deepened.","He also made a friend.","That man’s name was Chong Jiu, and he was also very powerful. When Yang Kai was being hunted down after first arriving, the man acted out of righteousness and helped him out.","Through his conversation with Chong Jiu, Yang Kai finally understood that this was a place of exile for all Masters who had touched upon the taboo.","In other words, everyone who was here had touched upon the secrets of the Heavens at one time or another. Yang Kai had summoned shadows from the future, which was a taboo. Although he didn’t know what Chong Jiu had done, he was certain he had done something similar.","As such, this place was simply dubbed the Taboo Realm.","What’s more, anyone who entered this place would be quickly forgotten by the outside world.","All memories related to those who entered this place would be erased in short order.","In the 3,000 Worlds, there were definitely very few living beings who could compare to Yang Kai. Yang Kai then recalled the Universe Furnace and its process of creating new Universe Worlds, and immediately understood that the Masters here all came from different Worlds or even Universes, ones far beyond the boundaries of the 3,000 Worlds.","Each and every one of them had reached the pinnacle of their strength in their own realm and had even touched upon that which should not be touched.","Yang Kai had once asked Chong Jiu how to escape this place, and the latter hid nothing. He knew more things than Yang Kai as he had arrived a bit earlier than him.","According to him, it wasn’t impossible to escape from this place; in fact, there were two methods to escape from here. However, whether these two methods really worked or not was still open to debate, because there had never been a precedent of anyone leaving this place.","The first method was to continue fighting and kill the Masters from other Worlds. Perhaps if they killed enough of them, they might be able to leave.","No one knew who proposed this idea, but it sounded a bit unreliable because there was no basis for it.","The second method was much more plausible, and it was to have the people of your Universe still remember you and wish for your return.","“A person will die twice in their lifetime. The first time is when their life ends, and the second time is when the last person who remembers forgets them. As far as we are concerned, we may still be alive here, but the world we used to live in no longer remembers us, so we are dead to that world. If we want to rise from the dead, enough people must remember you for you to break through the restrictions here.”","These were the exact words of Chong Jiu, and Yang Kai remembered them very clearly. At that time, Chong Jiu had been drinking the spirit wine he had taken out from his Small Universe while saying these words.","Although this second method was much more reliable than the first, it was still impractical, because once someone entered this place, his or her respective Universe would be affected by the restrictions, wiping every single memory related to him or her in a very short time.","Once the memories were wiped out, everything was lost. Even if there were some written records left behind, they would just become dust in history over time.","Saying so, Chong Jiu patted Yang Kai’s shoulder, “Little Brother, just stay here. Although there’s no way out of here, it’s still quite lively.”","It was indeed quite lively. Supreme Masters of many Worlds were gathered here, fighting non-stop every day. This kind of thing would be rarely seen in the outside world, but here it was a common occurrence.","At that time, Yang Kai just responded to Chong Jiu in one sentence, “I will be able to get out. My world will never forget me!”","Chong Jiu looked at him like he was looking at an idiot and threw a sentence, “I’ll be waiting for that day!”","Calculating the time, that day should be arriving soon.","While Yang Kai was lost in a daze, the tall and stalwart man had returned at some point, and sent a fearsome sword wave at him, forcing him to dodge.","From nearby, Chong Jiu’s playful laughter rang out, “Yang Kai, don’t die! If you die, I won’t be able to watch the good show!”","He had already arrived a few days ago as promised, wanting to see if Yang Kai could really leave this place. Although he felt that Yang Kai didn’t have much hope, since he made a deal, he naturally had to abide by it.","Unexpectedly, someone came to seek revenge on Yang Kai at this point.","Although it was called ‘seeking revenge’, the truth was that there was no great enmity between them. The sword-wielding man had fought with Yang Kai at least 100 times over the past few thousand years, and neither of them had been able to do anything to the other. But this time, he actually brought a companion, wanting to overwhelm Yang Kai with numbers.","But unbeknownst to them, Chong Jiu happened to be together with Yang Kai. A battle had broken out immediately afterwards. Yang Kai was up against the sword-wielding stalwart man while Chong Jiu dealt with his companion.","At this moment, a towering tree had emerged behind Chong Jiu. It was gently swaying, glittering and shining as if it was cast from gold. One after another, its leaves whizzed through the void, cutting space apart. Its every move carried endless power. Chong Jiu’s opponent was forced to retreat every time he tried to press forward.","After fighting for a while, the Master couldn’t help size up Chong Jiu before asking, “The Dao Tree lineage!?”","Chong Jiu raised his brow, “You’ve seen it?”","The Master continued, “The Dao Tree lineage is famous throughout the Heavens, and I had the honour of experiencing it first-hand once before.”","Saying so, he put away his weapon, “I won’t fight anymore.”","Chong Jiu smiled slightly, “I was thinking the same.”","Battles were common occurrences in the Taboo Realm, but there were many cases where a simple smile and greeting could wipe away all enmity; after all, everyone’s strength was about the same, so unless there was some kind of irreconcilable grudge between them, no one was willing to really fight to the death.","For example, someone like the sword-wielding stalwart man who repeatedly sought trouble with Yang Kai was actually quite rare. He kept attacking Yang Kai mainly because Yang Kai had only been here for a short time, and the sword-wielding man believed that he was an easy target.","Owing to repeated battles, Yang Kai’s strength had grown significantly over the past 8,000 years.","This wasn’t surprising though as Yang Kai did not get the time to consolidate his foundation and perfect it after swallowing and refining Mu’s Space-Time River before he was forced to fight Mo to the death.","It wasn’t until he had entered this place and fought battle after battle that Yang Kai finally digested the benefits he had obtained from Mu’s final gift.","Furthermore, his Small Universe’s foundation was constantly increasing. If he was allowed to go 8,000 years back in time to deal with Mo, he would definitely not end up as miserable as before."]},{"number":6006,"title":"Chapter 6006: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["The Masters in the Taboo Realm came from different Universes, so the cultivation systems were naturally different as well. For example, the World where Chong Jiu came from did not cultivate the Open Heaven Realm Method, the denizens of his world had their own way of dividing the Realms.","Be that as it may, the fundamental principles of cultivation were more or less the same. At Yang Kai’s and the others’ Realm, the prime focus of cultivation was the comprehension and application of the Grand Daos.","The shining golden tree behind Chong Jiu was his Dao, the Space-Time River was Yang Kai’s Dao, and the sword-wielding stalwart man fighting Yang Kai had a Dao of his own.","The sword in his hand was precisely his Dao!","Yang Kai had never seen a Master with such a pure Dao. Yang Kai had seen and fought many Masters over the past 8,000 years, but none could compare to the sword-wielding stalwart man in terms of pure offence and aggression.","In any battle, the stalwart man was constantly on the attack, essentially disregarding defence entirely. At most, he would dodge a little when necessary.","Fighting such a person was incredibly frustrating and it was extremely difficult to reach a conclusion as the only way to settle things with any sense of finality, was for someone to die.","“Jian Ba, there is no enmity between us, why must you insist on fighting?” After exchanging blows for a while longer, Yang Kai shouted as the waves under him swirled.","Jing Ba, who was standing right across from him, hideously grinned, “Why bring up enmity in this damned place? Since I’m here, one of us will die today, the question is whether it will be you or I!”","Yang Kai slowly shook his head. He was completely unable to reason with him.","If the Shadow Secret Technique could be used, Yang Kai was confident he could defeat Jian Ba, but he had already summoned shadows from 8,000 years of his future when he was fighting with Mo, which ultimately caused him to be trapped here. He was basically unable to use the Shadow Secret Technique.","Shadows of the same Space-Time could only be summoned once.","Helpless, Yang Kai could only use the power of his Space-Time River to fight ceaselessly with Jian Ba.","However, Yang Kai was feeling uneasy for some unknown reason today. He thought that he was feeling unnerved because the 8,000-year deadline was approaching, but later he realized that wasn’t the case.","He could not afford to get distracted when fighting someone as powerful as Jian Ba; so, how could he have the spare energy to consider the 8,000-year deadline?","What caused him to feel uneasy must be something external!","As such, he was slowly losing ground against Jian Ba.","Chong Jiu, who was watching the battle from afar, noticed this unusual situation and couldn’t help but furrow his brow. Nonetheless, he too had no idea what was going on with Yang Kai. Furthermore, he was being marked by Jiang Ba’s companion. He could not lend Yang Kai a hand, and could only wait and watch.","Fearsome Dao Strength shockwaves spread into the surroundings as the two men clashed endlessly until at one point, Yang Kai suddenly heard a shout ring in his ear.","Yang Kai instantly fell into a trance, but before he could hear it clearly, Jian Ba had already disappeared.","Immediately, a sense of crisis gripped his entire body. Yang Kai knew that he was in real trouble. His figure quickly distorted and faded away, but the next moment, Jiang Ba arrived before him and slashed down at his fading figure.","A splash of blood spattered into the void while Yang Kai’s figure appeared in another direction, promptly covering his abdomen. Apparently, Jiang Ba’s sword had cut him, leaving a gaping wound.","The indistinct shout once again rang in his ear. Yang Kai shook his head, trying to disperse this strange sound, but to no avail.","Just after the first shout, a second shout soon followed, and then a third, a fourth...","In just a few breaths, Yang Kai felt countless voices ringing in his head. These countless voices jumbled into an incoherent noise before eventually converging into two words.","It was naturally his name!","Having wounded Yang Kai, Jian Ba doggedly pursued him, but just as he was about to make his move, a great sense of horror suddenly gripped his heart. The moment this sense of horror emerged, Jian Ba’s eyes went wide. It was not terror or fear Jian Ba felt though, but instead extreme excitement.","Because ever since his cultivation had reached its peak, no one had been able to give him such a feeling. Even in this Taboo Realm, where he had encountered countless Masters, no one had struck true terror into his heart.","But at this moment, against an enemy who had been wounded by him, this long-lost feeling had reappeared.","Jian Ba couldn’t help but recall the Masters he had faced when he was weak.","The sword that had accompanied him all his life began to hum, warning him to retreat.","Jian Ba didn’t retreat though; instead, he swung his sword down, causing the expressions of Chong Jiu and the other experts watching from afar to become extremely solemn. Because this attack could be said to be the strongest sword attack they had ever seen. It was Jiang Ba’s all-out strike.","Once he executed this attack, his target would definitely die!","The sword light filled everyone’s vision, blinding them.","When the sword light disappeared, Chong Jiu and the other Master quickly looked up and what entered their sight made their eyes crack wide open in shock.","Much to their surprise, Yang Kai had not blocked that sword strike at all and simply let it fall on his shoulder. It almost severed his arm, but it didn’t, as the endless river water happened to be wrapped around Jian Ba’s sword and wrist, preventing him from following through.","Although Yang Kai was injured, his expression was extremely strange, he seemed a little confused yet also a little relieved.","What caught Chong Jiu’s attention was the Void behind Yang Kai, which looked extremely unusual at the moment. It happened to be continuously distorting, and through this distorted space, a faint distortion of Space-Time emerged from some unknown place.","[The restriction of this place had been broken!]","When Chong Jiu recalled Yang Kai’s confident words, his heart began to pound violently, [Could it be that the rumours circulating in the Taboo Realm are true? Did enough people in Yang Kai’s Universe still remember him? But, how is that possible?]","Anyone who entered this place would be quickly forgotten; otherwise, how could the Masters who had entered this place be unable to leave even after so many aeons?","But other than this possibility, Chong Jiu could not find a better explanation.","“Yang Kai!” He quickly called out.","Yang Kai, who was immersed in this wonderful feeling, raised his head and smiled at him before turning to look at Jian Ba, who was still standing at arm’s length. Under Jian Ba’s stunned gaze, Yang Kai stretched out two fingers and grabbed his sword.","“It turns out that only by breaking the restriction here can one pry into the higher realms of the Martial Dao!”","Saying so, Yang Kai gently raised his fingers, lifting up the long sword that had cut into his shoulder.","The corners of Jian Ba’s eyes twitched violently as his instincts were giving off warning bells.","At this moment, Yang Kai gave him a very strange feeling, as if he was about to achieve some kind of breakthrough.","This feeling left him in a great shock. The Masters in the Taboo Realm had already reached their limits. The reason they were trapped here was because they wanted to break through to higher realms, but in the end, they had touched upon the Taboos of the Heavens.","Today, he had seen both an amazing truth and an incredible secret.","Breaking the restriction of this place would allow one to gain insight into the next realm!","This was a huge blow to Jian Ba’s mental state. Not to mention him, even Chong Jiu, who was watching from afar, and the companion Jian Ba had invited, felt the same way.","“Stand down!” Yang Kai looked at Jian Ba and declared.","Jian Ba naturally ignored him, gritting his teeth as he poured all his strength into the long sword and pushed it down without muttering a word, seemingly intent on cutting Yang Kai in two.","The sword in his hand was his Dao, backing down would be equivalent to abandoning his Dao, so how could he possibly agree?"]},{"number":6007,"title":"Chapter 6007: He Left!?","paragraphs":["Whether it was High Heaven Territory’s Star Boundary, or the Universe Worlds of Myriad Monsters Territory, everywhere where Humans had settled, Humans were chanting Yang Kai’s name non-stop, singing his praises, spreading the name of Void Great Emperor.","For the first few days, nothing unusual happened, but as time passed, a strange sound started ringing in everyone’s ears, like waves crashing onto the shore.","Furthermore, the sound became louder and louder with the continuous actions of the Humans. Finally, at a certain moment, a strange phenomenon occurred.","Everywhere the Humans were gathered, a river suddenly appeared out of nowhere.","The sonorous sounds of waves crashing were originating from the river, and everyone witnessed this magical sight.","The water in the river swelled and flowed towards the horizon, passing through the endless void, flowing through one Great Territory after another, to the Late Ancient Era battlefield, and finally converging on the final battlefield where Yang Kai and Mo fought each other.","The dozen or so of Yang Kai’s close relatives in the palace looked excited at the sight of this. Their chanting became more hurried, and their expressions more fervent.","The river was illusory at first, as if it existed in another Space-Time, but it soon became real and tangible. Immediately afterwards, a figure emerged from the tumultuous waves in the river.","Looking at the figures standing in the palace, the figure cracked a smile and stated, “I’m back!”","The figures in the palace broke into tears of joy as they swarmed towards the figure one after another.",".....","Meanwhile, the Masters in the Taboo Realm soon got the news and rushed over. Over 100 people had gathered in a short time, and more were still coming from afar.","These people were all Supreme Masters of their respective Universes. Each and every one of them had reached their own limits. Every single one of them used to be a legendary figure where they came from.","But now, their worlds had long forgotten about them, causing them to be trapped in this Taboo Realm.","Over 100 of the strongest Masters in existence were calmly standing around the location where Yang Kai had fought with Jiang Ba, staring at a corpse floating nearby.","The corpse naturally belonged to Jian Ba. Jian Ba was tightly holding a broken sword in his hand, while the cause of his death was none other than the other half of his sword being rammed through his chest.","Dead!","There was no shortage of brave and ruthless men in the Taboo Realm, and battles broke out all the time. These were the kind of battles one would seldom see in the outside world.","Be that as it may, very few people actually lost their lives during these fights.","Because although the cultivation methods were different for Universe to Universe, everyone’s prime focus would be their Dao, after their cultivation had reached its utmost limit. It could be said that all things lead to the same destination; as a result, everyone’s strength was basically the same here. So, no matter how intense a battle was, very few people would die.","The last time someone died was over 100,000 years ago, and that was because a certain man with a horrible personality ultimately drew everyone’s ire and was besieged by many Supreme Masters.","But the current situation was far from that. It was pretty obvious that Jian Ba had not died because he was ganged up on. No matter what kind of Dao they were cultivating here, they all had sharp vision and insight.","The one who had killed Jian Ba was just a single man! Furthermore, Jian Ba’s opponent had killed him so easily that he had even snapped Jian Ba’s sword in two!","Even if these Supreme Masters present here weren’t very familiar with Jian Ba, most of them had fought him at least once in the past.","Jian Ba’s sword was his Dao. So, killing someone might not be a big deal, but killing someone while destroying their Dao at the same time was inconceivable.","What the Supreme Masters were concerned about was that they had sensed some unusual fluctuations a while ago. Even when they were far away, those fluctuations were as bright as a match in the darkness.","Those were clearly the fluctuations caused by someone breaking through their current cultivation realm! But by the time they arrived here, they didn’t see anything.","Under everyone’s watchful eyes, the faces of Chong Jiu and Jian Ba’s companion were filled with a bitterness, their expressions way worse than eating a bitter pill.","Both had witnessed Jian Ba’s death at the hands of Yang Kai, which had shook them to the core. By the time they came back to their senses, the Supreme Masters had already arrived here to investigate after noticing the commotion.","As a result, they were unable to leave.","If they tried to leave now, they would definitely be forced to stay.","The Supreme Masters had been trapped here for far too long, so any unusual movements would definitely attract their attention, let alone a disturbance that exceeded the limits of their current strength.","“Who was here?” Someone suddenly asked.","Although it was a random question without a head or tail, the meaning behind it was obvious. The speaker was obviously asking who had witnessed Jian Ba’s death.","No one answered.","“Who arrived here first?” Someone asked.","Still no answer, but the eyes of the Supreme Masters began to wander across each other, their gazes swiftly changing as they reached a certain unspoken agreement.","Finally, everyone’s eyes landed on Chong Jiu.","Chong Jiu scowled in anger as he stared at the colleague invited by Jian Ba, “Why are you only looking at me? He was here as well!”","Although the two were originally on different sides, they clearly had no choice but to band together at this moment. If they didn’t handle this situation well, they might become the public enemies of all the Supreme Masters, so they couldn’t afford to be careless.","There was no escape from this Taboo Realm. If they became public enemies, things would be hard-pressed for them in the future.","“Who killed Jian Ba?” An old man with small stature asked. This old man had been trapped in the Taboo Realm for who knows how many years. It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to say that he was one of the oldest Supreme Masters in the Taboo Realm; at least, these 100 or so Supreme Masters present had all come to the Taboo Realm later than him.","“It wasn’t me,” Chong Jiu quickly clarified, “I’m not that capable.”","The Supreme Master standing beside him also quickly denied, “I didn’t kill him either.”","“You were here first, didn’t you see who did it?” The short old man asked. Although he was the only one who spoke, he represented everyone.","“Well...” Chong Jiu hesitated for a moment. He knew that no matter what, he couldn’t avoid this matter. Rather than drawing everyone’s ire, he might as well speak the truth. After understanding this point, he finally answered, “Yang Kai killed him.”","“Who is Yang Kai?” The short old man frowned. He had never heard of this name before.","“He was a newcomer whose Dao Strengths had manifested into a river. He arrived about 8,000 years ago,” someone explained.","The short old man finally understood, “I seem to have some impression of him, but how could a newcomer kill Jian Ba? Where is he?”","“He left,” Chong Jiu replied.","“Where did he go?”","“He left, from this place.”","The Supreme Masters were stunned for a moment before staring at Chong Jiu in shock.","Being the focus of attention of so many Supreme Masters, Chong Jiu felt as if an enormous mountain was weighing down on him. The Supreme Master who was standing by his side subtly stepped away from him, drawing a clear line between them.","“You said... he left this place?” The short old man asked. Although his tone remained calm, his heart was in turmoil.","“Brothers, Sisters, there’s no need to stare at me like that, he really did leave. This friend and I saw it with our own eyes,” Chong Jiu stated as he pointed towards the Supreme Master who had just stepped away from him.","The man’s face darkened, but he knew he couldn’t avoid it. All he could do was brace himself and nodded, “Yes, he did leave.”","Chong Jiu smiled and said, “Weren’t you all attracted by those strange fluctuations? I’ll be frank with you, according to the rumours, there are two ways to leave the Taboo Realm, and the second method is apparently true. Yang Kai used that method to leave this place. What’s more, when he broke through the restrictions here, he seemed to also break through to the next realm, allowing him to kill Jian Ba!”","Since ancient times, it had been passed down that there were two ways to escape the Taboo Realm. One was to constantly fight and kill other Supreme Masters. So long as you killed enough Supreme Masters, you would have a chance to leave this place. The second was to have enough people from your original Universe remember you and wish for your return.","Whether the first method would work or not, no one knew, because few people ever died in the Taboo Realm.","But now, the second method had been proven effective. If Chong Jiu wasn’t lying, Yang Kai had left the Taboo Realm using this method.","Under these circumstances, there was no need for Chong Jiu to lie, everyone was well aware of this.","“How is that possible? Once we arrive here, the denizens of our Worlds would’ve quickly forgotten about us. Without any memories, how can they remember us? This is simply impossible,” Someone questioned.","Chong Jiu spread out his hands and stated, “I don’t know. In any case, Yang Kai told me a long time ago that his world would never forget him. Perhaps because he saved his Universe, the people of that world still remember him?”","The Supreme Masters still found it difficult to accept this, because from ancient times until now, there had never been a precedent of anyone leaving this place.","But now, a newcomer who had only entered 8,000 years ago had done just that.","This made them envious, but at the same time, they also saw a glimmer of hope.","If someone could leave here, it meant that this Taboo Realm wasn’t a prison they couldn’t escape from, it was just that they had not found the right way.","It was definitely impossible to count on Yang Kai’s methods. Not mentioning who knows how his world still remembered him, the main reason was that he had only been here for 8,000 years.","The others had simply been here for far too long. Before Yang Kai, the previous Supreme Master to arrive here had done so some 20,000 years ago. After tens of thousands of years, all traces of his existence in his world would have long since vanished","“You can get a glimpse of the next realm after breaking the restrictions here? What kind of Realm is that?” The short old man asked.","Chong Jiu shook his head, “I don’t know what Realm he reached, but once he broke through, he casually snapped Jian Ba’s sword with just two fingers.”","All the Supreme Masters gasped in shock.","What those two fingers destroyed was not just a sword, but Jian Ba’s Dao!","One could only imagine what amazing realm Yang Kai must have reached at that instant.","“Everyone, before Yang Kai left, he told me that he will find a way to rescue me. Although I don’t know if he would be able to do it, if he does, everyone here will have new hope of finding a way out.” Chong Jiu threw out another piece of news that excited everyone.","In an instant, the expressions of all the Supreme Masters present changed.","Half a day later, the Supreme Masters finally dispersed.","Chong Jiu let out a long sigh and wiped the sweat from his forehead. Although he was also a Supreme Master and didn’t fear any individual in the Taboo Realm, being stared at by hundreds of Masters just as strong as him still felt like being stabbed multiple times.","If he hadn’t thrown those words at the last moment, Chong Jiu believed that these guys would have attacked him together and then interrogated him for more information.","Even if he had already divulged everything he knew...","However, everything was different once he spoke those last words. As long as they still wished to leave the Taboo Realm, they would not make things difficult for him in the future. In fact, if anyone dared to make things difficult for him, they would become public enemies of this Taboo Realm!"]},{"number":6008,"title":"Chapter 6008: World Creation","paragraphs":["An enormous river stretched across the void, its waters fiercely surging, with waves rising and falling one after another.","Yang Kai was sitting in a cross-legged position over this enormous river, forming a set of profound hand seals. As his hands moved, the water in the river would cycle through states of agitation and calm.","The myriad of Daos Strengths would also undulate with the current in the river.","It had been several years since Yang Kai returned from the Taboo Realm.","Whenever he recalled his absurd experiences over the past few years, Yang Kai didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","On the day, when he finally returned from the Taboo Realm, all his relatives came to meet him tearfully, complaining about their pain of parting. Soon after, everyone returned to the Star Boundary together, and after learning of the news of his return, all rejoiced.","In the 8,000 years after Yang Kai’s disappearance, all their memories about him had been erased, but the moment he returned, all the vanished memories were restored. No one knew what extraordinary power could cause something like this.","Only Yang Kai seemed to notice something.","After that, Yang Kai was placed under house arrest!","He, a mighty expert who had surpassed the Open Heaven Realm, who had reached an unprecedented Realm never seen before, who could call the wind and rain with just the flip of his hand, had actually been placed under house arrest!","The ones who put him under house arrest were none other than Yang Ying Feng and Dong Su Zhu!","His Wives were also under house arrest like him.","According to his parents, they were growing old. It was already a miracle that they had been able to give birth to Yang Xue in the past, but there was no way for them to have any more children. So, the responsibility of continuing the Yang Family’s bloodline fell squarely on Yang Kai’s shoulders!","The old couple didn’t make any outrageous demands, just that he should father as many children as the number of Wives he had. So, each of his Wives should give birth to at least one child. When this condition had been fulfilled, they would release them.","In terms of strength, his parents were naturally not Yang Kai’s opponents and he could easily escape if he really wanted to; however, his parents had also said that if their unfilial son dared to disobey them this time, they would bash their heads against High Heaven Peak until they died!","Yang Kai was left with no choice!","According to his parents, Yang Kai had been cultivating for many years and had explored many worlds, big and small. He had been constantly on the move. But now that the world was at peace and his cultivation had already reached the limit, there was nothing he needed to worry about in this world. As such, he should pay attention to continuing the Yang Family’s bloodline!","Helpless, Yang Kai, Su Yan, Yu Ru Meng, and the others were locked up on a lone peak in High Heaven Palace.","It wasn’t until several years later that Yang Kai walked out of the mountain peak with a tired look on his face, his eyes sunken and his face pale. Right behind him was a large group of beautiful women with big bellies.","Yang Ying Feng and Dong Su Zhu were overjoyed. As the saying went, ‘people need to be pushed to get results!’ In the past, they had tried to make Yang Kai continue their bloodline, but he had always brushed them off with all kinds of excuses. If they had known it would be this simple, they would have put him under house arrest long ago!","After having completed this vital mission, Yang Kai finally had time to catch up with his old friends.","Mi Jing Lun and the others were naturally aware of what was going on with Yang Kai over these past few years; so, they could not help but tease him when they finally met up.","Soon, Yang Kai learned about the current situation of the Human Race from the other Ninth-Order Masters.","With the end of the war more than 8,000 years ago, the Black Ink Clan was completely wiped out, and the Universe had finally achieved a state of peace. Now, the Human Race were the sole rulers of the world.","Be that as it may, the scars of countless years of war were difficult to erase.","The 3,000 Worlds used to be extremely prosperous, but now, apart from those in High Heaven Territory and Myriad Monsters Territory, the Universe Worlds in the rest of Great Territories had either been completely corrupted by Black Ink Strength or had long since been destroyed.","It could be said that the habitable space for the Human Race had been greatly reduced.","Originally, traces of Human activity could be seen in every Great Territory, but now, all the surviving Humans were gathered in High Heaven Territory and Myriad Monsters Territory, with more than 90% of them living in the latter.","In fact, because of the scarcity of cultivation resources, the two Open Heaven Realm Cradles, the Star Boundary and Myriad Monsters World, had essentially been evacuated and cordoned off. The Human Race didn’t dare let too many people live in these two Open Heaven Realm Cradles, lest too many good seedlings were born and there were no resources to nurture them!","If the number of people suitable for cultivation increased, but there were no resources for them to cultivate with, fights over cultivation resources would definitely break out, which would ultimately lead to chaos.","Currently, the population living on the Star Boundary and Myriad Monsters World was extremely small, and if one wanted to enter these two Open Heaven Realm Cradles, they would need to undergo a rigorous series of tests and selections.","This was the current state of the Human Race; they had won the war, but it was a pyrrhic victory.","Nonetheless, they could not do anything about it. The Black Ink Clan had simply done too much damage to the 3,000 Worlds.","In addition, the Human Race didn’t have the means to repair these corrupted Universe Worlds. If no solution was found, the Human Race would have many dark days ahead of them.","Fortunately, Yang Kai had returned from the Taboo Realm, and at this moment, he was repairing a Universe World.","This was an uninhabited Great Territory. Perhaps this Great Territory once used to be bustling with Human activity, with its Universe Worlds being rich and prosperous; however, after the Black Ink Clan occupation, all that was left was deathly silence, and all the Universe Worlds had died.","The massive Space-Time River stretched across the void, with Universe Worlds floating up and down in the river, Daos Strengths fluctuating rhythmically.","The Black Ink Strength that had corrupted these Universe Worlds was quickly stripped away and then sent into the Profound Source Gate by Yang Kai to be sealed. After that, Yang Kai evolved Yin and Yang, then harmonized the Five Elements, which gave birth to the 10,000 Grand Daos.","The flow of time in the Space-Time River was different from the outside world, and with Yang Kai’s current cultivation, this flow rate had reached an extremely exaggerated degree.","Perhaps 1,000 years were elapsing inside the river for each breath that passed in the outside world...","The lifeless Universe World slowly regained its vitality in the Space-Time River.","Suddenly, a small figure stepped out and walked over to Yang Kai’s side before pursing his lips in frustration, “It’s empty outside, there’s nothing here, so boring.”","Yang Kai fiercely turned to him and shot him a glare, “It’s all your fault!”","The figure immediately tried to explain, “What does Mo’s evil deeds have to do with this Little Eleven?”","The small figure standing next to Yang Kai at this moment was none other than ‘Little Eleven’, or rather, it was the same person Yang Kai had seen in the Primordial World’s Dawn City.","8,000 years ago, Yang Kai defeated Mo and sealed it with the Profound Source Gate; however, as the most ancient being in this Universe, even Yang Kai was unable to completely destroy Mo.","After all, Black Ink Strength was a power born at the beginning of the Universe. As long as the Universe still existed, and as long as there was darkness in living beings, Black Ink Strength would never be extinguished.","However, Yang Kai spent some effort to extract the consciousness born from this power from the Profound Source Gate.","This consciousness was Little Eleven, who was standing beside him.","Strictly speaking, Mo was Little Eleven, but these two were different.","In other words, Little Eleven was not making excuses, he was indeed not Mo. During the Early Ancient Era, he had fought alongside the 10 Martial Ancestors to protect the Human Race.","Only Mu had noticed the problem in Mo at the time. She had set up the Primordial Heavens Source Grand Restriction and sealed Mo before its consciousness was completely corrupted.","Afterwards, under Mu’s secret arrangements, Mo’s Source was divided into 3,000 pieces and sealed in different Universe Worlds while Mu kept Mo’s consciousness by her side to guard him.","Unlike what Mu did, the current Little Eleven was not some weak child in Dawn City who did not even have the strength to strangle a chicken; otherwise, he would not have been able to wander the void alone.","Looking at the surging river stretching across the void before him, Little Eleven couldn’t help wondering, “Speaking of which, what Realm are you in now?”","Little Eleven was completely unaware of the fact that Yang Kai was trapped in the Taboo Realm, as Mo was sealed by Yang Kai after his defeat, and Little Eleven was freed just a few days ago. However, Little Elven was surprised to discover that Yang Kai’s strength was far greater than the last time Mo fought with him. It seemed to have gone beyond the scope of the Open Heaven Realm.","Little Eleven reckoned that even if Mo had been at his peak, he would still be no match for the current Yang Kai.","“You’re supposed to be a Master in the Creation Realm, can’t you see through my cultivation?” Yang Kai asked instead of answering.","Little Eleven explained, shaking his head, “That’s a false claim. Mo never reached the Creation Realm. He could at most be described as a Pseudo-Creation Realm Master. The main reason Mo was able to create the Black Ink Clan is because of the unique properties of Black Ink Strength, not because Mo had reached the necessary realm; but you, you’re different. Your current cultivation has indeed exceeded the Open Heaven Realm, so I’m very curious about what Realm you’ve reached.”","Yang Kai had already noticed that there was something wrong with Mo’s ‘Creation Realm’ a long time ago, but at that time, his strength and vision were simply insufficient; as such, he was unable to determine anything.","Now that Little Eleven had personally admitted it, Yang Kai wasn’t too surprised.","“My Realm...” Yang Kai muttered before shaking his head, “No one has reached this Realm before, so I don’t know what it should be called.”","Saying so, he quickly changed his hand seals before raising them towards the Space-Time River, making a grabbing motion.","The next moment, the enormous river was gripped by Yang Kai, who gently shook it and shouted, “Go!”","Immediately after, tiny grains of sand were flung out from the Space-Time River one after another and began rapidly expanding. Surprisingly, these grains were Universe Worlds.","These Universe Worlds were the remaining Universe Worlds of this Great Territory. Originally, they had been corrupted by Black Ink Strength and were devoid of any life. Some were even destroyed by the Black Ink Clan’s resource exploitation.","But now, all these Universe Worlds had completely changed. Although there were no sentient beings on them, each of these Universe Worlds looked completely new, without a trace of Black Ink Strength left on them. The dilapidated Universe Worlds had been repaired and were filled with perfect Grand Daos. Furthermore, each of these Universe Worlds was lush and green, full of life and vigour.","These Universe Worlds were already teeming with vitality, so they would give birth to their first life forms in just a few years.","Even with Little Eleven’s vast experience, he was still shocked by this amazing sight.","The Universe Worlds were not artifacts, nor were they pieces of furniture; they were not something that could be repaired so easily. However, these devastated Universe Worlds had been brought back to life by Yang Kai. This was not something a normal Human could do.","“Creating something out of nothing, a Divine Ability to create a new world, truly amazing,” looking at the Universe Worlds flying out into the void and slowly coming to a stop at certain spots, Little Eleven couldn’t help but sigh with emotion. He felt that his sins had been significantly reduced.","Hearing this, Yang Kai raised his brow as a smile flashed on his face, “Then let’s call it the World Creation Realm.”","“Huh?” Little Eleven was stunned, but quickly recovered and muttered, “The World Creation Realm... it’s quite appropriate.”","In the past, the Universe Furnace created all Worlds, but now, Yang Kai’s Space-Time River was also able to create Universe Worlds.","The Space-Time River itself was modelled after the Infinite River inside the Universe Furnace, and the Infinite River was the foundation of the entire Universe Furnace. All the Universe Worlds in this Universe had been created by the Infinite River. Yang Kai felt that his own Space-Time River would reach the level of the Infinite River sooner or later.","“Let’s go to the next place.” Yang Kai stood up and rushed towards the adjacent Great Territory, with Little Eleven following closely behind him."]},{"number":6009,"title":"Chapter 6009: The Future","paragraphs":["Every Great Territory Yang Kai passed though had its once-dead Universe Worlds now radiating with new vitality. By the time Yang Kai was finished restoring all the Great Territories in the 3,000 Worlds, 1,000 years had already passed.","Yang Kai then spent another 1,000 years doing the same thing to the Universe Worlds in the Black Ink Battlefield.","After 2,000 years, the entire 3,000 Worlds and even the Black Ink Battlefield were no longer desolate and barren as they had been in the past. They were once again brimming with endless vitality. In time, these Universe Worlds would definitely be able to produce new cultivation resources, and the increasing number of Humans would slowly become the masters of these Universe Worlds.","Void World was originally Yang Kai’s Small Universe, the crystallization of his life’s cultivation, his very foundation, but now, he had stripped away his Small Universe from himself and turned it into a real Universe World, placing it in High Heaven Territory, next to the Star Boundary. He did this after he broke through the shackles of the Open Heaven Realm and advanced to the World Creation Realm.","It was quite an incredible feat. Upon learning of this, all the Ninth-Order Masters were totally shocked, but considering that it was Yang Kai’s handiwork, they were able to accept it; after all, he was the only World Creation Realm Master in the history of the Human Race, so any kind of absurd and impossible feat suddenly became perfectly normal for him.","At this moment, somewhere on Void World, Yang Kai looked at a child in front of him and exhorted in a serious manner, “I’ll leave Little Eleven in your care. If there are any abnormalities, seal him immediately, I will deal with him when I return.”","Although the child did not look very old, he spoke in a steady voice like an elder, “Understood, Big Brother.”","This child’s appearance bore some resemblance to Fang Tian Ci.","As a matter of fact, he was none other than Fang Tian Ci. After Yang Kai used the Three Selves Source Reconstitution Art to advance to the Ninth-Order Open Heaven Realm, Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow lost their physical bodies, but their consciousnesses remained in Yang Kai’s Knowledge Sea, accompanying him for many years.","Because of the uniqueness of the Three Selves Source Reconstitution Art, while they were Yang Kai’s Soul Clones, they were also independent entities.","Over the years, while Yang Kai was repairing the Universe Worlds, he had also been thinking about how to bring Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow back to the world of the living. He couldn’t possibly allow them to remain in his Knowledge Sea forever without a flesh body.","Reincarnation was certainly a good choice, but in that case, they would most likely lose their original memories and become another unfamiliar Soul. After all, it was not the same as when he had cast his Secret Technique, and left many seals on his Soul Clones, ensuring that his Soul Clones would grow aware of their mission and memories at the right time.","Finally, when Yang Kai decided to strip off his Small Universe, he was struck with an indigenous idea.","That was to integrate Void World’s Source into Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow, allowing them to reincarnate along with the World itself. This way, not only would they be able to retain their original memories, but they would also become the Masters of Void World. From then on, they would share the same fate as Void World; if one suffered, all suffered, and if one prospered, all prospered. So long as Void World was not destroyed, they would be immortal.","Yang Kai’s Small Universe’s foundation was extremely strong, and now that they had become this Universe World’s Masters, it would be easier for them to progress in the future. It was easy to foresee that the 3,000 Worlds would have two more top Masters in the near future.","Yang Kai had also left Little Eleven here to be watched over by Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow as it would be grossly inconvenient for him to bring Little Eleven along for the rest of his journey.","After the child Fang Tian Ci responded, a black kitten sitting on his shoulder also nodded and spoke like a Human, “Meow... Big Brother, don’t worry, if there’s anything wrong with this brat, Second Brother and I will beat him to death!”","A look of anguish and frustration appeared on Little Eleven’s face as he rebuked, “Don’t make me sound like some wicked demon, at least show some basic respect to a Senior like me!”","The kitten immediately let out a snort.","“Then, I’ll take my leave,” Yang Kai nodded before soaring into the sky.","The trio’s gazes followed after him until Yang Kai finally disappeared from their sight.","A moment later, the child, Fang Tian Ci, and the kitten, Thunder Shadow, stared at Little Eleven together, causing him to frown, “What do you want...”","The kitten shouted, “Let’s beat him up, meow!”","Having said so, his figure left afterimages as he pounced at Little Eleven’s face, while his pair of cat claws swiped furiously, leaving multiple afterimages.","Little Eleven cried in surprise, and just as he was about to dodge, the child, Fang Tian Ci, threw him on the ground.","A moment later, two Humans and a kitten were lying on the ground with their faces black and blue.","Thunder Shadow gasped for breath as he stated, “I’ve wanted to beat you up for a long time now! Satisfying!”","The child Fang Tian Ci did not fare any better. His nose was bleeding, but there was a content smile on his face.","Little Eleven’s face was covered in claw marks. He was undoubtedly much stronger than these two, but this was Void World, and the child Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow were the Masters of this place. Little Eleven was just asking for trouble by being hostile to them while within the bounds of this Universe World; thus, their fight ultimately ended in both sides being defeated and wounded.","Nonetheless, Little Eleven stubbornly declared, “Once I recover, I’ll deal with you two!”",".....","Outside Void World, when Yang Kai arrived in the void, what he saw next took him aback, because there were many familiar faces waiting.","Putting aside the group of women led by Su Yan, Yu Ru Meng, and the others, many of the Ninth-Order Masters were also here.","[How did my whereabouts get leaked...]","Yang Kai secretly reflected for a moment, wondering how he gave himself away. All he could say was that his Wives understood him too well.","“Are you planning on going on a long journey?” Old Ancestor Xiao Xiao looked at him and asked.","“En,” Yang Kai nodded his affirmation, “I made a promise to someone. I have to at least try to save him.”","Inside the Taboo Realm, Chong Jiu was not lying when he said to the many Supreme Masters that Yang Kai vowed to save him. Yang Kai had indeed sent him a Divine Sense transmission just before he left declaring as much.","Chong Jiu had helped Yang Kai quite a bit during his 8,000 years in the Taboo Realm; furthermore, the two of them shared the same ideals. If possible, Yang Kai wanted to rescue him from the Taboo Realm, despite the fact that he had no idea where Chong Jiu’s Universe was.","This would probably take a lot of time and effort to find, and there was no guarantee his trip would bear any results.","Having fallen into the Taboo Realm, Chong Jiu’s world had forgotten about him a long time ago. Even if Yang Kai found his home, he might not be able to discover any traces of Chong Jiu’s existence.","However, as the saying goes, put forward your best, and leave the rest to the Heavens!","“I also want to find a way to overcome the shackles of the Open Heaven Realm Method.”","The Open Heaven Realm Method that the Human Race was currently cultivating was comprehended by the 10 Martial Ancestors from the World Tree and passed down through the ages. The Open Heaven Realm Method allowed the Human Race to gain a foothold in this world and gave them a chance to become the overlords of this Universe, but in the end, this cultivation method was flawed.","All cultivators who ascended to the Open Heaven Realm had innate limits imposed on them.","Such a cultivation system was obviously imperfect.","In the Taboo Realm, Yang Kai had come into contact with many Supreme Masters from different Universes, each of them had a different cultivation method, but very few of their methods had such obvious shackles as the Open Heaven Realm.","As the popular adage goes, stones from other hills may be used to polish one’s own jade. So, Yang Kai’s purpose of venturing out to explore was firstly to find traces of Chong Jiu, and secondly, to study the cultivation systems of other places to see if he could make use of them to improve the Open Heaven Realm Method.","Since the Human Race was now thriving, and countless Universe Worlds had been restored, even the originally desolate and dilapidated Black Ink Battlefield had regained its vitality, the Humans no longer needed to worry about living space and cultivation resources. Yang Kai felt that it was time to shift his attention to future issues.","What’s more, there was not just his Universe in the vast and endless void. Although he had now reached the World Creation Realm, no one could say with absolute certainty that there were not any existences stronger than him out there.","If one day a Master from another Universe came to invade, their side must have enough strength to protect themselves.","This was also a form of preparation for the rainy days.","“If you can find such a thing, could we break through to the World Creation Realm?” Xiang Shan asked.","“Probably not,” Yang Kai shook his head. He had experienced breaking through to the World Creation Realm first hand, so he knew the method to do so and understood it was not something that could be achieved by solving the shackles of the Open Heaven Method Realm. Rather, this breakthrough was more about opportunities, luck, and several other conditions. “The ideal situation is to allow the current Human Race to advance through the Open Heaven Realm without being affected by their innate shackles first.”","Originally, a cultivator who directly ascended to the Third-Order Open Heaven Realm would have an upper limit of the Fifth-Order, but if Yang Kai found a solution to this flaw, then a Third-Order Master would not only be able to reach the Sixth-Order in the future, but he would also be able to cultivate to the limit of what he could achieve, perhaps even reaching the Ninth-Order one day.","In that case, the Human Race, with the help of two Open Heaven Realm Cradles, would be able to give birth to even more Eighth-Order, and Ninth-Order Masters...","If a Ninth-Order Master wanted to break through to the World Creation Realm, they would first need to study the 10,000 Grand Daos. When his or her mastery of the Grand Daos had reached a certain level, they would finally be able to touch the Taboo of this world. Finally, if that person could break the restriction of the Taboo Realm, they would then advance to the World Creation Realm.","Yang Kai had already traversed this path, so if the Ninth-Order Masters took this path again in the future, it would be a bit easier and more relaxed than when he had first ventured onto it.","“That’s not a bad idea,” Mi Jing Lun nodded his acknowledgement, “Then I wish you all the best, but we won’t be able to provide much help in this matter. You can only count on yourself.”","With Yang Kai confirming the existence of the World Creation Realm, the Ninth-Order Masters were all diligently cultivating and studying the mysteries of various Grand Daos. Furthermore, with Yang Kai’s current cultivation, they would not be able to provide any support to him even if they accompanied him.","Yang Kai nodded before turning to his Wives.","Yu Ru Meng stated with a snort, “You can forget about leaving us behind this time.”","Although the other women didn’t say anything, their determined expressions were speaking for themselves.","Yang Kai smiled, “Then, let’s go together.”","The group of women immediately broke into cheers. They were obviously overjoyed as they had not expected Yang Kai to agree so easily. Immediately, the group of women gathered around Yang Kai, chatting and laughing.","“Old Tree!” Yang Kai suddenly called out to the void, “Let’s go.”","In response to his call, the World Tree’s illusory phantom appeared in everyone’s field of vision. The towering giant tree was no longer lifeless as it used to be; rather, it was lush and brimming with vitality. Not only that, but countless World Fruits were also hanging from its branches.","In the past, Yang Kai had borrowed the World Tree’s power to travel to the Grand Ancient Ruins Boundary from the edge of the Universe. This made the Old Tree consume too much energy and it fell into deep slumber.","Only when Yang Kai returned after reaching the World Creation Realm and began using his Space-Time River to repair the Universe Worlds in the various Great Territories did the Old Tree slowly wake from his slumber.","The World Tree was closely connected to the Universe Worlds in the 3,000 Worlds; everyone’s rise and fall was connected with each other. When the Black Ink Clan occupied the 3,000 Worlds, the World Tree was shrouded in a miasma of gray energy for many years, which left it in a desolate state. As the Universe Worlds died one after another, the fruits hanging on its branches also began to wither and fall. This caused the Old Tree to shrivel and grow older.","It had to be brought to notice that these World Fruits were the embodiments of the vitality of the various Universe Worlds. If the Universe Worlds were alive, their corresponding fruits were fresh and alive, if the Universe Worlds died, their corresponding fruits withered and fell.","Apart from the countless Universe Worlds Yang Kai had repaired over the past few thousand years, he had also placed the 3,000 Universe Worlds that Mu had left behind in her Space-Time River in the various Great Territories. Not only that, Yang Kai had also restored the Universe Worlds on the Black Ink Battlefield.","In light of this, the Old Tree’s vitality had significantly increased, and the number of fruits hanging from it was more than twice of when it was at its prior peak.","In the past, it was impossible for the Old Tree to manifest its figure outside the Grand Ancient Ruins Boundary, but now, it could easily do so.","Its thick trunk might give off the appearance of an old tree, but it bore no marks to show its age; rather, it seemed much younger than before.","It could be said that ever since Yang Kai began repairing the Universe Worlds, the Old Tree’s days had become more and more comfortable.","Old Tree smiled cheerfully at Yang Kai as it stretched out a branch which wrapped around Yang Kai and the various Women, before it gradually started glowing green.","By the time the glow faded away, Yang Kai and the others had disappeared.","In the Grand Ancient Ruins Boundary, when Yang Kai and the others reappeared, the Old Tree gently withdrew its branches wrapped around them, and then sent over 10 seedlings, World Tree Clones, to Yang Kai with another branch.","“Be careful on your journey,” Old Tree advised before prompting its strength, sending Yang Kai and the others out of Grand Ancient Ruins Boundary.","When they reappeared, they were already standing on the edge of the Black Ink Battlefield.","Yang Kai carefully put away the 10 seedlings as they were necessary for his return journey. This would surely be a long and arduous journey, so without the guidance of Old Tree, even a World Creation Realm Master like him might get lost in the endless void.","Drawing on his experience the last time he returned from distant lands, Yang Kai had Old Tree prepare some seedlings in advance. This way, when he ventured deep into the vast, endless void, he could plant the seedlings on some Universe Worlds he found and use them to contact the Old Tree.","Furthermore, this would also help in strengthening the Old Tree’s foundation, because the Universe Worlds with World Tree clones planted on them would be included into the Old Tree’s teleportation range. All the Universe Worlds within this range would be imprinted onto Old Tree’s body, manifesting in the form of World Fruits.","In all likelihood, the World Tree’s teleportation range would increase with Yang Kai’s exploration. Perhaps after Yang Kai found a new Universe, he would be able to connect it to the 3,000 Worlds and travel freely between them.","Yang Kai summoned a Warship, whereupon everyone gathered in the cabin.","“Husband, which way should we go?”","“Let’s go this way.”","“Alright then, sit tight.”","“Right, if we’re all traveling outside, what about our children?”","“Their Grandfather and Grandmother are looking after them, there’s no need to worry. Also, it’s not like they are kids anymore.”","“Mhm, Father and Mother must be very happy with so many grandsons and granddaughters. It’s really envious! But they’ve gotten old, will they be able to look after them?”","“Their Uncle and Aunty are also looking after them.”","“That brat Yang Xiao, I’ve only seen him a few times over the years!”","*Peng!*","“Hey, if you want to talk, just talk. Why are you closing the door?”","“I don’t care. Big Sister has already given birth to two, but I’ve only given birth to one, I want to have another kid too. Husband, you can’t be unfair!”","“This isn’t something I can decide, eh... ahh, don’t tear my clothes, let’s talk it out!”","THE END.","Silavin: Not sure why the author said that the children are playing on their grandparent’s lap in ‘Mhmm, Father and Mother must be very happy with so many grandsons and granddaughters.’","It’s been a few thousand years since they got impregnated. So, they should have grown up by now. – Changed!","Also, “I don’t care, Elder Sister had already given birth to two, but I’ve not given birth yet, I want to have a kid too. Husband, you can’t be impartial!” – Technically, they were all pregnant when he went to fix up the Universe Worlds. So, this doesn’t make sense. Changed!","Overall, it was a nice ending. Plot holes here are there but overall, I think this was a satisfactory ending.","I’ll continue on with the side-stories as planned. I will be live streaming while I write the chapters so that I can get your input. Chapter 6010 is already done. Will detail more at another date.","...","Silavin","Anyways, I would like to thank everyone for helping. In this long running novel. This is the first project I picked up and it has been ongoing for more than seven years.","I would like to thank PewPewLaserGun for always being there throughout the journey. Leo and Dhael for sticking with me for so long. The other translators, like Ashish, Raikov, Tia, Jon for helping out.","Also, I would like to thank all the readers. We would have never reached this point if not for your support. You guys helped bring this project to a close as well. Otherwise, at the initial 4 chapters a week, I think I would be dead before this gets done haha.","The author had another work, Humanity’s Great Sage. We are also translating that. Hopefully, we will complete it as well. For some reason, the author has included Yang Kai in Humanity’s Great Sage. He won’t appear till the later chapters. Let’s see if we can get there.","...","PewPewLaserGun here!","Wow... I started working on this project as a random side project as I enjoyed the novel. At the time it looked like it might even be dropped cause of a lack of translators, so I randomly offered up my own translation to keep it going until someone more qualified took over.","7 years and 5,000 chapters later, here we are...","I’m more of a behind the scenes type, so I’ll keep this short and simple. Thanks to all the readers and the team members, past and present, from Divine Dao Library for making this possible, it’s been a wild ride!","As for what comes next... think I’ll sleep on it and let you know in the morning =).","....","Dhael here. This feels strange. This is also my first project. Joined in the early 1000s—1316 to be specific. Great run and a lot of fun.","Thank you all for the support.","Join us for the next project. Humany’s Great Sage. Got on that one from the start. Definitely worth a read.","....","Guys, you want to leave any remarks? This is the last chapter anyways. Best to go off with a Bang."]},{"number":6010,"title":"Chapter 6010, Children","paragraphs":["“Yang Ji! Yang Xu! Get back here!” A man scolded as a pair of Dragon and Phoenix teleported away.","The two children, looking to be around 12, giggled as they disappeared. Meanwhile, the man slumped his shoulders in exhaustion.","A beautiful woman with luscious lips and phoenix like eyes appeared from behind him as she sighed. “Yang Xiao, why didn’t you just trap them within your Domain?”","She was none other than Yang Xue, Yang Kai’s Sister.","“You think I didn’t want to do that? How in the world did these two monsters get born? They sensed it before I could even use Time Principles and escaped. These twins are such a headache. Even Adoptive Father has a hard time dealing with them.” Yang Xiao lamented, tasked with taking care of them while his Adoptive Father was having another one of his honeymoons.","“As their Uncle, you should already know how capable they are. Their Dragon and Phoenix Bloodlines are much purer than others. If they could manage to use it to suppress you, that would be a good laugh.” Yang Xue teased as she patted him on his head.","Yang Xiao felt as though a headache was rushing in.","In fact, he could have done something about those two if he used a lot more of his strength. It was just, these children were too sly.","To be more accurate, Yang Xu was the cunning one and Yang Ji was the mischievous mastermind. Yang Xu would always follow her Brother’s wishes, and if that meant pranks, that would be.","He could not use his full strength because within the compound they were in, there were other children as well. These twin’s half siblings. A large number of which were still young and still sleeping. Even when he scolded the two, he had to keep his voice down. If they all woke up and started crying, all Hell would truly break loose.","Since both the twins and him could not make a scene, what else could he realistically do?","Yang Xiao signed once again and complained. “Very funny. Well, not like the world can cause them any issues if they go out and run around. Those two schemers just so happen to choose the best time to run away when their Grandparents are gone.”","Yang Xue chuckled, “They do resemble you when you were young. Guess that’s what it means to be a young Dragon? Well, I guess it’s best if we tell the others about their escape.”","“What do you mean ‘resemble me when I was young’? I was never that naughty!” Yang Xiao quipped, snorting at the idea. “But, aren’t you going to go after them?”","“If I go, who is going to deal with the aftermath of when all the children wake up?” Yang Xue rolls her eyes at the obvious problem they faced.","*Haaa...*","The two sighed as they stared out to the sky where those twins ran off to.","...","“Yay! We finally got out!” Yang Ji, in the form of a small Golden Phoenix, cheered. He looked to his Sister to see her checking on the item they took from their Uncle.","“Yang Xu, what did you get?” Yang Ji asked, curious as to what that orb was. It was completely black, as though light did not reflect from it. Rather, it seemed as though light itself got absorbed by it to never return.","“Big Brother, I don’t really know. But, I think we can ask Uncle Little Eleven about it. Out of everyone, he is the only one we can trust. The rest of them will turn us in and force us back home.” Yang Xu thought for a while before replying. She had already turned to head towards where Little Eleven was.","Yang Xu nodded and they soon, together, manipulated Space Principles to instantly close the distance to their destination.","Little Eleven, Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow were living quite a distance away from any major cities. In fact, the place they settled on within Void World had been labelled as a Restricted Zone.","Although the whole Black Ink Clan mess had been dealt with, there was too much bad blood that could not be washed away. Even if Yang Kai had pardoned Little Eleven for his actions, that was not the case for the rest of the world. Even so, the wish of Mu needed to be honoured, and Little Eleven had to have a chance at normalcy.","The best they could do was to keep him out of harm from others who might try to take revenge by setting up this Restricted Zone.","It was not so much that Little Eleven could not go out. Rather, it was a Restricted Zone where he would be safe if inside. Nevertheless, to atone for his mistake as Mo, he rather stayed inside.","Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow, who were tasked to watch over Little Eleven, naturally stayed by his side. Though they were his observers, after growing up together, they had become more or less friends. The occasional fist or claw exchange still happens, but overall, they were close.","Over the years, Yang Kai had visited them in their homes. Sometimes, he would even bring his children here to shave off some of the trio’s boredom.","It was on these trips that Yang Xu and Yang Ji got to know of their Uncles. It was also from these trips that they memorised the location and route.","When kilometres outside of the Restricted Zone, Yang Ji raised his arm to stop his Sister. He looked around and checked his surroundings, scrutinising every detail.","“Phew. Looks like no one has caught up to us yet.” Yang Ji smiled and said.","“Big Brother, I don’t think anyone would look for us out here. If they wanted to catch us, they would have waited for us inside.” Yang Xu said, giving him a side-eye.","“No no no. We have to play it safe. Look, before we even get close, we need to avoid Uncle Fang Tian Ci and Uncle Thunder Shadow’s Divine Sense right? If they catch onto us, then we’ll immediately be sent back.” Yang Ji said, convinced that would happen.","“Then what should we do? I’m pretty sure that their Divine Sense encompasses the whole Restricted Zone. I doubt we would be able to sneak past them.” Yang Xu asked, not understanding her Brother’s thoughts.","“Before I answer that, let me ask you, do you think both of us are faster than them?” Yang Ji asked, already knowing the answer.","“Erm... if we work together, maybe? We’ve never really seen them use their full powers before so I doubt we can beat them in terms of speed. Uncle Fang Tian Ci is also proficient in the Dao of Space. If we were to compare who had better control, him or us, I doubt we would win...” Yang Xu said while looking at her small white fist clenching and opening.","“You’re right. Actually, no matter how I see it, I don’t think we’ll be able to beat either of them. Even Uncle Thunder Shadow is ridiculously fast. So, what we need to do is to lure them away. The stratagen known as ‘luring the Tiger away from the mountain’!” Yang Ji said as he puffed up his chest and beat it.","The little boy seemed to have thought that he seemed impressive but his Sister had already thought of this.","“That’s far easier said than done. How are we supposed to lure them away? If one leaves, the other will remain.” Yang Xu shook her head, believing this to be unfeasible.","Yang Ji placed his index finger on her lips and smirked.","“There’s where you are wrong my dear Sister. You are forgetting that I have a Storage Ring with me.?” Yang Ji said, as though everything – every little detail had already been thought up.","“...” Yang Xu stood silent and just decided to go with the flow.","Silavin: From 6010 onwards, it is just fanfic. It will be once a week on Monday."]},{"number":6011,"title":"Chapter 6011, Trapped","paragraphs":["Chapter 6011, Trapped","Author: Silavin","Within the Restricted Zone, a Man, a Black Panther and a little boy, sat around a circular table. It was their usual gathering time, where they would enjoy the simplicities in life. Treats and banters were always abound during these gatherings, gathered at the centre for whoever wants to take them.","“Hey, the Communication Artifact had lit up. What did it say?” the little boy asked in wonder. It was obvious that something must have happened for the usual stoic man to suddenly sigh.","Fang Tian Ci sighed again. “It’s Big Brother’s children. Two of them seem to have escaped from home while their parents are on a honeymoon.”","Thunder Shadow tilted his head. “Wait. They are going on a honeymoon again?”","Fang Tian Ci scratched his face. “With so many Wives, Big Brother does have it rough. Besides, they are most likely not just playing around. They are most likely looking around for materials to build the Artifact Big Brother wants.”","“The one he is going to use for that long voyage?” Little Eleven asked, while in deep thought.","“Yeah. The trip definitely won’t be easy. But, not like there’s much we can do about it. Judging from the description of those people he had to deal with, and the Taboo Realm, it’s best to prepare.” Fang Tian Ci added. He considered joining his Big Brother, but his priority was to remain by Little Eleven’s side. At the same time, all three of them would feel uneasy if they all left the 3,000 Worlds. Thus, at one of their gatherings, they had already discussed and decided Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow would be staying to guard the 3,000 Worlds just in case.","Naturally, Little Eleven was also present at the scene during these discussions. He had made the active decision to remain here, as this was Mu’s final resting place. It was also the least he could do for terrorising the 3,000 Worlds for so long.","At this time, all three sensed two familiar auras. They all immediately looked at each other and two pairs of eyes fell on Fang Tian Ci.","“Alright. I’ll go.” Fang Tian Ci stood up and leaped, disappearing in an instant.","Little Eleven and Thunder Shadow both shrugged. They both nodded, as though it was the expected outcome. After all, Little Eleven needed to stay within the Restricted Zone. As for Thunder Shadow, although he was fast, he by no means could hope to beat his Second Brother. It was naturally by no means that they just wanted to watch the show. Certainly not.","...","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could both sense a disturbance in Space. They immediately threw out one of the Artifacts that Yang Ji had brought with him.","It was an Array Plate.","The Array Plate landed on the Space that started to ripple, and it immediately activated. The area it captured was so large that it encompassed at least 10 kilometres. Naturally, that meant whoever was going to appear and the two children would get caught up in this trap at the same time.","Yang Ji immediately grabbed hold of Yang Xu’s hand, and they flew. He took out a Token and they immediately escaped from the Array.","The Array Plate was made specially to contain whatever was inside. However, it was far from simple. It was made by Grandmaster Ma Fan and Yang Kai. This was a gift to the twins, whereby they would be able to train in.","It would create an independent space, whereby the twins would be able to go through different illusionary environments. There were places with sweltering lava pools, there were canyons with Astral Winds, there were caves of freezing ice. Regardless, even till now, the two had not cleared all regions. Still this Array Plate functioned as both a training ground and a means of protection. They could trap their enemies inside and leave them there while they escaped.","As for the two, they naturally had a Token to escape the Array Plate.","When Yang Ji and Yang Xu got out, they looked at each other. They both knew that with Fang Tian Ci’s abilities, escaping this Array was only a matter of time. Still, they could not help but smile since they’ve trapped him.","They both gave each other a high-five and Yang Ji said. “Okay. That’s one down. I don’t think Uncle Thunder Shadow will come out anytime soon though. So, we need to just continue onwards. Let’s do this as planned. We need to get past the Restriction Array first.”","“Okay.” Yang Xu nodded and took out another Token. This time, it was a Token for the Restriction Array. In general, this was a special Identification Token. It could be for the various Arrays around Void World. Naturally, this Restriction Array was no exception, since most of the Yang Family would come here from time to time.","The two children took out their Identification Token and placed it against the Restriction Array. The typically transparent dome suddenly had some blue hue to it. A small hole soon appeared and it quickly enlarged till the side of three men.","The two children went in with little regard for the Array Plate they left behind.","The path to the centre was straightforward. In fact, a small path within this dense forest would light up in front of them to guide them.","This path was not real. It was an illusion created with some bored modification made by Little Eleven.","The path was created such that glowing rectangles were painted on the ground. Little Eleven even took the effort to make them always perfectly contour the ground, to make it seemed as though the ground had been painted over. Any shrubs protruding would be circled, as though they should be watched out for.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu did not understand how such a thing was made, but that was just what made Uncle Eleven more impressive in their hearts.","The two continue forward as guided by the path. To say the scenery here was picturesque would be an understatement. With how much time they had, Fang Tian Ci, Thunder Shadow and Little Eleven would decorate their surroundings. It was not an exaggeration to say that everything here had been ‘made-made’. Since, regardless if a blade of grass or dirt had been here, they would have been moved or replaced by any of the three at some point in time.","In fact, a common topic of their discussions, if not about cultivation and news, was about their place.","Looking at such sights again, with certain mountains having changed location and certain trees being replaced by another breed, Yang Ji and Yang Xu had their gazes taken.","However, as they moved closer to the centre, they remembered what they needed to do and they ceased getting distracted.","There, they saw a Black Panther and a little boy, who looked to be around their age, who they call Uncle."]},{"number":6012,"title":"Chapter 6012, Leaving the Restricted Zone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6012, Leaving the Restricted Zone","Author: Silavin","When the twins could be spotted, the two on the table just minded their own business. They had already sensed them before they entered. Naturally, their presence came as no surprise. Thunder Shadow even lazily opened one of his eyes to peak, almost intent on not doing anything.","As for Little Eleven, he waved at the twins to welcome them over. For him, who had always been close to the two, this was a great time to catch up.","Yang Ji could not help but look at Yang Xu before turning his head back at the two by the table. He was a little taken aback by Thunder Shadow’s nonchalance. He had imagined they needed to do something to stop their capture. However, it turned out that nothing really needed to be done.","As for Yang Xu, she half-predicted this outcome. She never believed that Fang Tian Ci had any true intention of catching up. In fact, she wanted to question her brother – why he had to go this far. It was just, was it not more entertaining to just play along?","Seeing that Yang Ji was not planning to move, Yang Xu took the initiative to take his hand and bring him forward.","The two slowly walked up to the table, where Little Eleven asked, “Hey, what are you two doing here?”","Thunder Shadow seemed to completely ignore these two, instead, his attention was fully focused on the outside, as though he was waiting for Fang Tian Ci to get out of his predicament.","Yang Xu was the one who answered. “We got this from back home. We were wondering what this is”","Yang Ji immediately took the initiative to take out the black orb. His hands were still a little shaky due to nervousness.","The moment Little Eleven saw the orb, his eyes lit up. He immediately took it into his small hands and smirked. He asked, “Do you have any guess as to what this is?”","The twins looked at each other and then back at him to only shake their heads. [If we knew, why would we need to come and look for you?]","Little Eleven’s smile widened, as though he had won. He moved his arms around the two, and whispered, “This is a really fun toy that you’ve brought. I can’t believe that you’ve managed to get a hold of this.”","The twins’ eyes brightened with expectation. They could not wait for him to tell them already. However, before they could push Little Eleven for an answer, he pushed the topic aside to further agitate them, “Okay, how about we deal with this later. For now, let’s get those two killjoys out of the picture first.”","Once he said that, the space around him seemed to darken. Even Thunder Shadow was alarmed by this development.","Before Thunder Shadow could act, his body was engulfed in darkness. Sticky darkness that he felt his limbs could not manoeuvre through. He raged, annoyed that this prankster got the best of him. “When did you! Damn it!”","A playful voice could be heard from above, “You don’t have to get so mad. You’ve done worse to me and we are all still such best of friends, no? I’ll take care of the kids for a while. Not to worry. I’ll bring them back.”","“Friends! You call us friends!?” Thunder Shadow roared, but his voice seemed to have gone unheard. Seeming as though Little Eleven had disappeared, he scoffed. “Out of all the Techniques you could have used, you had to use Abyssal Dome... Do you plan to keep me locked up here until you get back!?”","Abyssal Dome was a Secret Technique Little Eleven had developed to keep Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow confined in one space. It worked to a certain extent against Fang Tian Ci, but it worked too well against Thunder Shadow. The last time Little Eleven used it on Thunder Shadow, the latter could not come out until he started begging. Seeing this Secret Technique again just poured salt into his wounds.","Thankfully, *crack!* After a few minutes had passed, a crack started to form at the top of the dome. It slowly became like a Spider web, spreading out.","Not wasting a single second, Thunder Shadow rushed out, crashing his head against the weak spot, causing the whole thing to collapse.","The sight before him came as no surprise. It was Fang Tian Ci, who was already waiting with folded arms.","The two stared at each other in silence for a while. It was Thunder Shadow who took the initiative to speak, “Why did you not catch them when you were just loitering around?”","Fang Tian Ci simply looked at the direction where the twins and Little Eleven had run off to. He shook his head and sighed, “Haaa... just let them be. The thing those two took is something that was meant for Little Eleven in the first place. If you’re so worried, we could just go and follow them in secret.”","Thunder Shadow scoffed and then asked, “But, they might leave the Restricted Zone, you know? Aren’t we supposed to keep an eye on Little Eleven and ensure that he does not leave?”","“After being with him for so long, we both know that he had no desire to cause harm to any of us. In the first place, this Restricted Zone is more of keeping the others out than keeping him in. It’s fine. I’m actually more interested to see what they plan on doing with that orb. Besides, weren’t you the one who tried to persuade him to go out to play?” Fang Tian Ci sighed as he mounted on top of Thunder Shadow, as if it were natural.","Thunder Shadow knew about the Artifact. However, he felt it to be strange. There was no need for Little Eleven to leave the Restricted Zone to use it, much less bring the children along with him.","He wanted to ask Fang Tian Ci about his guess as to why this was the case. However, seeing Fang Tian Ci having no intent of explaining, Thunder Shadow just followed along and started moving.","The moment he took his first step, Space was split and a Void Crack appeared.","The Two, Panther and Human, soon entered.","...","Little Eleven was quick to bring Yang Ji and Yang Xu out of the Restricted Zone. It was as if nothing hindered him anymore.","Instead of bringing them in any other direction, he brought them to where the twins had supposedly trapped Fang Tian Ci.","The Array that had been established from the Array Plate had already been broken through. There was a huge hole at the top, which was slowly closing up.","When Yang Ji saw the initial destruction, his heart had dropped. If his Array Plate got destroyed, who knew what kind of punishment awaited him? His spirit only got lifted after he realised that the Array Plate had a self-repairing function.","Little Eleven was quick to point at the Array as he said, “Hurry up and keep your toy.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at him in wonder. They had not seen him in such a hurry before. It was certainly a rare sight to see.","They did as they were told. The Array Token was fished out, allowing for easy access into and through the Array. These two quickly went back into the core of the Array and shut it down.","When the Array disappeared with the two children exposed to the outside world, Little Eleven immediately appeared beside them. He moved his arm to wrap them in his shoulders, and they soon disappeared.","On the group, where they had stood, a small text was carved into the ground, ‘Heading to the World Tree’."]},{"number":6013,"title":"Chapter 6013, Glimpses","paragraphs":["Chapter 6013, Glimpses","Author: Silavin","In front of Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s eyes, Space seemed to warp. From what they knew, it was not so much the application of Space Principles but something far more profound. It was not that they moved through the Void. Rather, Space itself seemed to have folded, and they arrived at a large open area.","This large open area was not an unfamiliar place. They have been here before. Typically, if they wish to travel to distant Worlds, their Father would bring them here first.","As per their memories, there was a gigantic tree at the centre of the area. On its branches were what seemed to be fruits.","With their current mastery over the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time, they could vaguely feel that these fruits were far from ordinary. They seem to have an explicit connection to some kind of distant place.","Little Eleven walked up to the large tree and asked while displaying the black orb in his hand. “Old Tree, long time no see.”","The Old Tree, which was withered, frail and aged, had seemed to have its life completely turned around. Since its vitality was linked to the Universe Worlds connected to it, once Yang Kai started repairing the damages caused by the Black Ink Clan, the World Tree had gotten a new lease in life.","Not as lethargic as before, the Old Tree responded, a little wary, “I don’t think that we’ve met for quite a long time. I believe the last time was establishing an alternative route to transport to me without using my clones. What is it this time?”","Little Eleven, Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow had visited the World Tree before. While Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow seeked it out to find an alternative to reach the Ninth-Order, Little Eleven was different. He wanted to find a way to transport others to the World Tree without needing Yang Kai to ferry them around.","This alternative method had some requirements, namely, a third party without a World Tree clone would be able to use it. He also did not want the World Tree to be able to constantly spy on them through this connection.","While Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow found no luck in cracking through the Ninth-Order barrier, Little Eleven had made great strides. It was just that he needed some ‘sacrifices’ from the World Tree. In short, he needed parts from the World Tree.","The World Tree was initially unwilling to participate in this, after all it had no real relationship with Little Eleven. In fact, they should have bad blood against each other. However, with Yang Kai, Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow’s encouragement, it eventually relented. It understood that Yang Kai was going to leave eventually, and a method to move around through connected Universe Worlds would be invaluable for others – especially those close to him.","Knowing that this would benefit its saviour, and knowing that it still had the discretion of who to send and where, the World Tree eventually caved.","Little did the World Tree know, Little Eleven at that time was a complete beginner at Artifact Refining and Arrays. Little Eleven definitely had help, and he progressed very quickly thanks to that. However, the amount of parts the World Tree had to sacrifice would make even a grown man weep.","Seeing this boy again, who treated his own body as mere ingredients, the World Tree could not help but be wary. It was just instinctual at this point.","“I know you don’t really like me. I understand that we haven’t gotten along on the best of terms. But, I do need your help in this. I need to get to where that Heavens Order girl is. I’m also bringing these two kids along with me.” Little Eleven said and pushed the twins beside him to the front.","The World Tree looked at the twins and recognised them. He asked, curious, “These two are Yang Kai’s children are they not? Why are you bringing them all the way here, you’re even going as far as to bring them so far out? Although they are Divine Spirits, they are not strong enough to go out there just yet.”","Little Eleven took out the black orb and held it up high for the World Tree. “They were the ones who brought this to me. So, I believe that they have the right to see what lies beyond. Besides, these kids will most likely get agitated if I take what they have passed onto me and just disappear.”","The World Tree initially could not tell what that orb was at first sight. It had to stare for at least a couple of seconds to understand what it was. This orb was like the antithesis of light. It would absorb all the light around it.","It could feel a faint connection to this orb. It was similar to the Artifact Little Eleven wanted to refine. Just that this was not an Artifact for transportation.","The World Tree could sense that one of its clones was inside, but the connection was really faint. It was as though there was something profound blocking all connections into whatever was inside the orb.","The World Tree pondered over it for a moment and its eyes widened with shock. It could not help but ask, “Are you certain you want to go through with this? There may be no return. What’s more, you want to bring two innocent children along with you? What if something goes wrong?”","Little Eleven added, “That’s why I’m bringing them to her right? Anyways, I don’t think they visited her before. It’ll be fine. Yang Kai had already given me his word.”","The World Tree, not having heard about this from Yang Kai, doubted Little Eleven’s words. It closed its eyes for a moment before opening them up again.","“Alright. I’ve just asked. Yang Kai has given me his word that everything will be fine. If so, then I’ll allow you passage to the Chaotic Dead Territory.” The World Tree said and tried to sense nearby Universe Worlds. When it spotted one, it gave a perplexed look.","“You’re fortunate that the person you are seeking is in a Universe World at the moment.” The World Tree added, thinking that it was strange for the Chaotic Dead Territory to have a Universe World inside of it. The other closest one would take a few days to reach the edge of the Chaotic Dead Territory.","“Fortunate, huh?” Little Eleven muttered as he looked at those two children in front of him. It was obvious that they were lost as to what was going on. However, explaining it all now would ruin the surprise.","*Haaa...* The World Tree sighed and waved a branch. A portal soon opened behind the trio.","However, before they turned, the World Tree tossed out three seedlings, one to each person. It added, “None of us can afford it if something were to go wrong. Take these just in case.”","Little Eleven bowed. He noticed that the twins were quite proactive in this regard, and they also followed him to bow.","They took the seedlings with both hands and walked away. As they drifted a distance, and the portal started to close, another opened up behind theirs..."]},{"number":6014,"title":"Chapter 6014, Chaotic Dead Territory","paragraphs":["Chapter 6014, Chaotic Dead Territory","Author: Silavin","For Yang Ji and Yang Xu, the whole thing had been a blur. One moment, they were in the Restricted Zone, the next, they were meeting with the World Tree and finally, a place where the skies were devoid of anything.","If anything, the twins found the place called ‘Chaotic Dead Territory’ to be frightening. They had never heard of a place where there were no celestial bodies, except for the thing under their feet. This place felt no different to an abandoned land. Worst, there were powerful and bright yellow and blue flashes in the sky.","It was only thanks to Little Eleven’s presence that they could remain calm.","It was also fortunate for them that within five minutes of travel, they already spotted a small hut. Its exterior was completely plain, as though the owner had no conscious thoughts about luxury and only enjoyed the simplicities of life. Except for a simple garden, and a table and a few chairs set up outside, there was nothing else.","A woman could be seen tending to her garden, seeming to be unconcerned about the flashes in the sky. She looked young and had a graceful appearance. She was a beauty, certainly, but in the eyes of Yang Ji and Yang Xu, who had so many world destroying beauties as Mothers, she would not be considered to be anything that special.","Other than her appearance, the twins could sense that her cultivation was unfathomable. They could not tell her cultivation realm but they knew that this one woman was stronger than any of their Mothers.","They immediately knew this woman must be the ‘Heavens Order girl’ Little Eleven was referring to.","She was such a powerful woman, yet, the moment they approached, they could clearly see her stop whatever she was doing to go up to them and bowed.","The twins’ immediate reaction was to look at Little Eleven. After all, they had never met this woman before and would not deserve such honours. However, when they saw Little Eleven’s fierce reaction of shaking his head, they got even more confused.","That was until Zhang Ruo Xi greeted, “Young Master, Young Mistress, I welcome you two to my humble abode. I believe this is the first time we are meeting. I’m Zhang Ruo Xi, your Father’s maid. To what do I owe the pleasure of your visit?”","The twins looked at each other and glared at Little Eleven, as though questioning, ‘like I know?’.","Little Eleven gave a light cough and quickly took out the orb. He showed it to Zhang Ruo Xi and stated, “We are here for this.”","Zhang Ruo Xi’s eyes seemed to shine with a perturbed glimmer as she looked at the two young children in front of her. She checked their cultivation and was astonished. In them hide a ton of secrets that were more than meets the eye.","These two were Divine Spirits, but were already equivalent to Dao Source Realm Masters. If they were Monster Beasts, they would be regarded as Eleventh-Order Monster Beasts. Furthermore, these two both had Divine Spirit Sources, and not just ordinary Divine Spirit Sources. They both had Sources that seem to be greater than the Ancestral level, which should have been impossible.","It had to be noted that Yang Kai’s Ancestral Dragon Source was from a Dragon that had reached the pinnacle of known cultivation before the World Creation Realm was achieved by him.","For these two to have Sources that were greater than that meant only one thing, their existence was on par with her Heavens Order Bloodline. In other words, when she was still at her peak, her Heavens Order Bloodline would have no suppressive effects on them at all.","It was frightening to know that these two were merely around twelve. Still, it might be reasonable as these two were the result of a union between a Ninth Order Phoenix and a World Creation Realm Dragon, a never seen before combination.","Although Zhang Ruo Xi could roughly gauge how strong they were, she could not really say that these kids fell into any of the normal categories in terms of cultivation realms. The strangest thing about these two was that their cultivation did not over rely on their natural born Divine Spirit Source. It was some other technique that was too complex for her to grasp. The one thing she knew was that there was a harmonious link between the twins, whereby both basically have the same aura.","Still, for what Little Eleven wants to do, Zhang Ruo Xi still felt that bringing along two children only around the Dao Source Realm would be too dangerous. She wanted to warn him, but, before she could do so, the flashes in the sky ceased and two figures rushed towards them.","Naturally, these two figures were Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer. They had come down after their round had ended.","Moon’s Serene Glimmer had a beam on her face while Sun’s Burning Light was downcast, obviously highlighting who had won.","These two had naturally sensed the visitors when they had arrived, especially the one which they attested.","Still, seeing that there were two kids here, they held back their ire. Especially since the two kids had even taken a few steps back once they had arrived.","To be fair, Yang Ji and Yang Xu did not take a step back because the two had imposing appearances. It was more to do with their unconstrained aura that seemed to be constantly lashing out in the air. If it was not for that, they would be more than willing to befriend these other two kids.","“You two are scaring them. Try restraining your aura some more. If not, best to just merge with me so that you can remain here.” Zhang Ruo Xi said as she sighed. Although they had been working hard on controlling their powers, Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer still could not fully do so on their own at all times.","“Ah!” Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer exclaimed as though this thought had finally hit them. To be fair, they hardly had guests, and of the few, most would bear with it. If they were fearful, they would try their best to hide it.","The duo tried their best to contain as much of their power inside of them. Although it was difficult, after so many years of practice and with Zhang Ruo Xi’s help, they could at least manage to maintain this state for an hour.","Once they did so, the two quickly approached the twins. Sun’s Burning Light immediately went to Yang Ji and Moon’s Serene Glimmer to Yang Xu. The two of them inspected the one in front of them like they were looking at a rare animal.","Naturally, this drew the ire of the twins and they snapped back. “Are you done looking!? Has no one told you, you ought to respect your Seniors!?”"]},{"number":6015,"title":"Chapter 6015, Sun and Moon Marks","paragraphs":["“Seniors!?” Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light looked at each other with wide eyes. Their gaze naturally fell on Little Eleven, who had both his hands against his mouth, hiding his smirk.","They respectively pulled Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s ear as they roared. “You’re the Juniors!”","The aura those two exuded was one in which no question could be asked. They completely dominated the conversation, as they stared daggers at Little Eleven.","Initially, the twins tried to struggle, but it was fruitless. The strength difference was just that vast. Worse, their ears really started to hurt.","Zhang Ruo Xi could not bear this sight anymore and interjected. “Enough. Let those two go. They might have been rude but you two haven’t properly presented yourselves as Seniors.”","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light pouted and they both argued, “But...”","“No buts. If you want to be treated as Seniors, you must act like Seniors.” Zhang Ruo Xi added as she pulled on both their ears.","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light both let go. They put up a struggle as well, but their struggle seemed weak. As though they were just putting on a show of reluctance rather than actually struggling.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both rubbed their ears and glared at Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light.","Meanwhile, Little Eleven was just enjoying the show. Truth be told, Little Eleven did not hate the two. It was just a natural instinct to dislike them, just like how they disliked him. It had nothing to do with their personality. In fact, if they had to spend a million years together, he was certain he would still dislike them.","Both Zhang Ruo Xi and Little Eleven were aware of this. The only ones who most likely had not noticed were Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light themselves. It was like how their actions towards Zhang Ruo Xi were instinctually so amicable.","Zhang Ruo Xi would like to lecture the two, but she did not wish to waste any more time. It was best for Little Eleven and these two to be separated as soon as possible. Keeping them in the same space was just asking for trouble.","“They’ll be gone soon enough so don’t cause anymore trouble. They are here for the Profound Source Gate.” Zhang Ruo Xi placated.","“The Profound Source Gate!?” Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light both questioned as they turned to Little Eleven, who was holding the orb in hand. They both showed looks of disgust at the idea.","As for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, they both tilted their heads. This was the first time they were hearing about this. Yang Xu looked at her Brother, but he could only shrug his shoulders and point to Little Eleven.","Little Eleven walked forward and explained to the two. “Let me explain. Your Father had helped me seal my home inside of this orb. I describe it as home, since that’s where I’m from. But, things are not that simple.”","“Before I met your Father, I was a monster who could not control my powers. I was consumed by it. Right now, most of my powers are basically being sealed inside of my home. I wish to regain some of my powers, and for that, I would need your help.” Little Eleven explained in the most concise way he could think of.","The twins looked at each other, confused. After all, why would he need them out of everyone? Surely, their Father would be able to help.","As if he had seen through their thoughts, Little Eleven continued, “We’ve tried already, your Father and I have entered before. But, it did not work. My powers were not there. It was scared away by your Father. We’ve tried it a few times before, with different people. I’ve even tried going back with those two.”","Little Eleven pointed to the two other children who still had their ears gripped. “Overall. We have tried those that are powerful enough to not get corrupted by my powers. It is too risky to take anyone else. But, you two have a special constitution that would prevent you from getting corrupted by my powers.”","[Your power can run away?] Yang Ji and Yang Xu had never heard of such an absurd thing before. Nevertheless, since it was their Uncle Eleven saying it, it must be true. Still, it was hard to believe. The twins soon heard a woman interject.","“It’s not confirmed that you two will not get corrupted. It’s only a guess.” Zhang Ruo Xi added. She was opposed to this plan. She believed it was too risky.","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light finally had their ears released as they added, “Exactly. There is no telling what might happen if you two go in. You shouldn’t bring them in.”","Little Eleven shook his head. “I know this is risky, but I cannot go in by myself. I have a high chance of being corrupted. Without these two, I can’t think of any other candidate that can join me. Right now, they would not be deemed as a threat. If we wait any longer, when they reach the Open Heaven Realm, it might be too late. So, this is the only time.”","‘Besides, this is the only time where their Mothers are away.’ Little Eleven wanted to add that in but refrained from doing so. Saying that would only serve to have Zhang Ruo Xi more adamant on refusing to cooperate.","Zhang Ruo Xi proposed, “There is no need to do it now. We can wait till they are older. Their cultivation has not even reached the Emperor Realm. We can wait till then.”","Little Eleven remained adamant, “There would be no difference between now and later. They cannot be corrupted by Black Ink Strength. This is a fact. If you don’t believe me, let those two test them.”","Zhang Ruo Xi hesitated for a moment, but as though curiosity got the better of Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light, they just went up to the twins. They both forcibly grabbed the other’s hand and laid down their Sun Mark and Moon Mark.","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light felt strange. This was the first time that they felt their Marks only needed to be placed on different individuals. Typically, a person would require a pair of Marks to fully utilise its powers. However, Yang Ji and Yang Xu only needed one Mark each. Yang Ji had the Sun Mark while Yang Xu had the Moon Mark.","With one Mark on each child, they already seem complete?"]},{"number":6016,"title":"Chapter 6016, Preparations Complete","paragraphs":["Chapter 6016, Preparations Complete","Author: Silavin","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light looked at each other, confused. This has certainly never happened before. With the Marks on them, Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light realised the intricacies of their powers.","Though all of their heritage could be said to have originated from the Primordial Light, these two were slightly different. They definitely had the identity of being Divine Spirits, and their connection to the Primordial Light, along with connection to Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light were unquestionable. However, their existence was at the same time out of the sphere of influence of the Primordial Light.","In other words, the twins could obtain the Sun and Moon Marks due to their connection. However, Sun and Moon Marks would have no real influence on them. Their existence has in essence exceeded the Marks, and their cultivation would not grow or improve from the Marks. There was no Bloodline to purity, nor Divine Spirit Source to Strengthen.","In fact, the Sun and Moon Marks were to the twins, no different from just tools.","It might really be the case where the Black Ink Strength could not affect them, since even power close to the Primordial Light did not affect them.","Naturally, for Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light, their minds had never developed to go so deep. It was just like Little Eleven had said, they tested the twins and they had instinctively felt the two to be incorruptible. After all, they could not influence these two, how could Black Ink Strength possibly do so? They refuse to accept it.","Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light looked at each other and gave a nod. They acted like the ‘Great Seniors’ they were, “Yes, very powerful. About to reach our level.”","“Yes, about to reach our level.”","Little Eleven had to open his lips to help Zhang Ruo Xi confirm. After all, if these two started acting, it would take an eternity to get things done. “So, they won’t be influenced by Black Ink Strength right?”","““Yeah. Won’t.”” The two answered simultaneously.","Little Eleven turned to Zhang Ruo Xi and added, “There you have it. All three of us have basically reached the same conclusion. I understand that you are worried for them, but I can assure you that they will be absolutely safe. I can even swear to Heaven.”","Zhang Ruo Xi sighed and relented. She believed that if there was really something to worry about, Yang Kai would have done something beforehand. These were his two children, after all. He must have a certain level of confidence in this plan to allow the situation to evolve to this.","“Alright. I understand. So, we just have to prepare as usual, right?” Zhang Ruo Xi said as she used her hand to signal to Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light to get ready.","The two split away and appeared behind Zhang Ruo Xi before they left. Since this was not the first time they’ve tried to do this, they were pretty familiar with the procedure. Previously, besides Yang Kai, others like Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow had tried to go in with Little Eleven. Naturally, they had a World Tree clone inside of their Small Universe to protect themselves before they attempted this.","Zhang Ruo Xi had led the way, and Little Eleven had led the twins to follow along. While walking, Little Eleven explained to them, “Later, inside of the Profound Source Gate, you will need to stick close to me. Never wander too far away. It’ll be pitch black inside, and the other me might attack us.”","“Other you?” Yang Ji asked.","“Yes, you can think of him as my evil twin Brother. You can sort of say that all the bad things I did was because of him, but I would still like to claim responsibility for my failure to stop him.” Little Eleven said with a heavy heart. If Mu was here, she would definitely say that it was not his fault. However, it was a fact that his own inability to control his powers had led to so many years of tragedy.","“Uncle, then what would you like to do with your twin Brother?” This time, it was Yang Xu that asked.","“Well, we were originally one. I wish to be able to get back to that state.” Little Eleven replied.","“So, you’re getting remarried to your Brother?” Yang Xu asked with a twinkle in her eye.","*Cough* Little Eleven scratched his head and tried his best to come up with an easy to understand response. “No. No... hmmm... merging would be the more accurate term. In the past, I could not control my powers and it ran amok. It has essentially become another person. So, I’m just trying to take back control over my powers. When inside, you will see me trying to absorb it. It will resist, maybe attack, maybe try to flood into me to erase my consciousness. I would need you to protect me. Can you do that for me?”","“En” The twins responded in unison.","Little Eleven further elaborated on what they needed to do while inside, and the twins listened so attentively that their tutors would be envious.","The lecture took quite a while until they reached an open area with clear Arrays on the ground. In the middle was a dent with markings around it and spreading out from it.","Mountains, rivers, trees, stones, structures all seem to be in harmony as a complex network of nested Arrays were abound.","Although it was not something viewable from the ground, the whole Universe World had in fact been made into an Array. The purpose was twofold, to prevent this Universe World from breaking apart while Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light played, and to prevent any hazards from escaping if something were to go wrong.","In fact, the reason why this whole venture had been done in the Chaotic Dead Territory was to limit the risk of another outbreak of Black Ink Strength. After all, Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light were here. Even if they could not ultimately stop Black Ink Strength from spreading, they would be able to buy enough time for Yang Kai to come and secure the area."]},{"number":6017,"title":"Chapter 6017, Descend into the Orb","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Little Eleven looked around in remembrance, while the twins stared at the patterns on the ground and structures. If they were to describe their feelings towards this Array, it would be ‘overbearing’. Even their own home and the Restricted Zone did not have such dense Array patterns.","The weight of everything seemed to really hit them at this moment, as they felt the invisible pressure of the expectation from what they were about to do. After all, words to describe were incomparable from first hand experience in going up on stage.","The amount of effort it took to build this stage was incalculable. For Arrays, every detail had to be taken note of, and these were nested Arrays. Though the twins did not know the whole Universe World had been made into an Array, just from seeing the distant mountains and rivers having such intricate patterns, they now knew how critical this was.","Unconsciously, their hands slowly moved to hold each other.","Little Eleven took out the orb as though displaying it. He pointed to the dent in the middle and started to explain. “Before I place it there, do note that your safety is of utmost importance. If something awful happens, past the point of what you feel is safe, retreat.”","It was at this time Zhang Ruo Xi moved towards them with two Space Rings. As though continuing from where Little Eleven left off, “These are two Space Rings that are vital. Do put them on and make sure you do not lose them under any circumstances. Inside are Yin and Yang Crystals. Blue Crystals for Yin and Yellow Crystals for Yang. There is also a Token in each ring. Break it to immediately leave the place.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu accepted the ring with both hands. They used their Divine Sense to check through the contents and were astonished to find mountains upon mountains of Blue and Yellow Crystals. There were other items like Pills and Artifacts as well, but the second most eye-catching thing inside the ring was definitely the Token with a ‘Return’ written on it. Compared to the rest, this Token had an overt aura of someone familiar. Someone who the twins often joked as Grandmaster Trouble (Ma Fan).","The twins looked at each other, and without a word, they swapped rings. They each compared what they got and nodded before putting the ring on.","Once they wore it, the band of the rings seemed to tighten as to perfectly fit their fingers.","Yang Ji looked at Little Eleven and asked, “Uncle Eleven, why don’t you also get a Space Ring.”","Little Eleven chuckled and explained how he had gone on this trip so many times that he had already prepared what he needed. That they should not worry about him.","Zhang Ruo Xi just shook her head and proceeded to instruct. “Before you go in, let me brief you on another Artifact you need to take note of.”","Zhang Ruo Xi took out something that seemed to look like a lantern. However, the Artifact was not fueled with charcoal. Rather, it required the use of Blue and Yellow Crystals. From what the twins could see, the area it lit up was considerable enough, around a hundred metre radius. The rate of consumption was also not too fast, with them needing to replace the Crystals inside every four hours or so.","Zhang Ruo Xi continued to explain about each Artifact in detail within the ring, about the other use of the Crystals, as though this was the only way she could soothe her worries. Nevertheless, the time had come and nothing else needed to be said.","“That’s about everything. You understand everything right?” Zhang Ruo Xi asked, to which the twins replied with a firm nod. Naturally, Zhang Ruo Xi knew that with their cultivation, everything that was said were all remembered. She just could not help herself from asking.","Little Eleven stepped in and signalled for the twins to come closer. He was already standing on the circular platform with a dent in it. “Okay. I think we’ve already gone through everything. Yang Ji, Yang Xu, come here and stand within this circle.”","Knowing there was nothing else she could do, Zhang Ruo Xi sighed and took a few steps back.","Meanwhile, the twins followed their Uncle’s instructions and stepped into the same circular platform as him. Once they were within it, Little Eleven asked in confirmation. “Ready?”","“En!” The twins held each other’s hand as they gave a firm nod.","Little Eleven soon placed the orb in the dent and the whole Universe World seemed to tremble. The patterns all around them started glowing, and the structure beneath their feet began to drop down.","The whole circular area had begun to sink into the ground. When Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at their surroundings in astonishment, they saw the whole mountains and rivers start to glow with countless mysterious patterns being lit up.","Finally, their eyes laid on the three not in the circle, who waved their hands for a farewell. They could see Zhang Ruo Xi being reluctant. As for Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light, who had been playful this whole time, they wore solemn expressions.","That was the last scene they saw of the outside world as the circular platform beneath their feet quickened in its descent.","Over the course of the next few seconds, the hole above their heads, leading to the sky, got as small as an apple. Eventually, even the sky could not be seen anymore as the exit got covered, with the only light source being the glowing patterns of the Array of the walls and floor.","They could even hear the sounds of what seemed to be multiple gates above them being closed, with this sound being continuously played and getting closer.","At some point, Little Eleven spoke up. Maybe due to his own emotions, or maybe due to seeing how the kids were so tense that they did not speak. “I have to thank you two for this. Honestly, I doubt any other person could accompany me on this journey. For the two of you, you need not worry too much. I’ll handle everything.”","Even though Little Eleven said such words, the twins were not fools. If he could truly handle everything, then what were they here for? They obviously had a special role in the grand scheme of things. They were just worried they would mess up.","Yang Xu, the more tactful one, was the first one to answer with a nod. “En”","Yang Ji also gave a nod as a follow up.","Not too long, the walls and everything seem to start to get brighter, and in a flash, the whole space they were in had changed.","Silavin: Hmm... I feel like I’ve dragged the prep work for too long. I can’t help but feel like they need this much prep work done though. Well, in the next chapter, we’ll be inside the Profound Source Gate."]},{"number":6018,"title":"Chapter 6018, Try Touching","paragraphs":["The next moment Yang Ji and Yang Xu opened their eyes, they were already in an empty space with a gate in front of them. The empty space was completely white. It was not painted white, but rather, glowing white.","Even without explanation, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could feel the warm and mighty energy emitted from their feet. Meanwhile, the white sky was merely a reflection of the ground. In fact, they believe the reason why the orb looked so dark from the outside was because all kinds of energy could not escape from the orb and was trapped inside by this ‘reflective’ sky.","As for the gate, it was larger than any other gate they had seen before and tightly sealed. It was carved with intricate patterns, and every one of them seemed to be the essence of numerous Grand Daos.","Although Yang Ji and Yang Xu did not know much about the Dao of Artifact refining, they could nevertheless tell that this gate was not something Humans created. It perfectly resonated with Heaven and Earth, as though it had been birthed along with the Universe.","Little Eleven proceeded to approach the gate and the twins followed. Before anything else, Little Eleven instructed them to touch the gate first.","When they did, memories of the past flooded their minds, terrible memories.","For Yang Ji, he remembered the time when he got scolded by his Mother for catching him not studying seriously. The spanking that followed was not one he wished to remember. He could already feel his butt turn red.","For Yang Xu, she remembered the time when she caught her Brother saying he wanted to be like their Father, and have his own Harem. She beat him up afterwards and their relationship was on thin ice for a while.","Memories continued to replay, and the twins all made sad expressions.","Little Eleven, who was checking up on the changes, simply waited. Overtime, the two children broke free on their own without needing his help. He gave a nod as though this had been expected.","“Making contact with Black Ink Strength would normally lead to Humans being corrupted. Divine Spirits are naturally more resistant to it. Just the surface of the Profound Source Gate is hard to make contact with for most Humans.”","Little Eleven touched the gate and swept his fingers over it. There seemed to be small dark dust particles on his fingers, which he licked.","These particles were the escaped Black Ink Strength from when he opened the gate previously.","In general, Black Ink Strength would be eliminated by the surrounding white space within the orb, as Yin and Yang energies were constantly being exuded. However, since this was from Mo’s Source, it took a lot more time to purify. What was left on the door was Black Ink Strength trying to retreat back into the Profound Source Gate but could not do so. It had been so long that only dust-like particles were left of them.","“Did either of you feel anything change in your Knowledge Sea?”","Both shook their heads with Yang Ji explaining first. “Uncle Eleven, all we experienced was recalling some bad memories. I don’t think I feel anything different with my Knowledge Sea...”","“I’m the same with Big Brother.” Yang Xu continued and asked, “Are we supposed to feel something?”","“I guess it is different from person to person. Your Father, when he was weaker, and a few others, reported that they would feel as if their Knowledge Sea and Small Universe were slowly being dyed black and get out of their control. Dark memories of the past would flash by and they relieved it while slowly losing themselves. For you two, I did expect it to have some effect but the extent was questionable. If you two couldn’t handle it, we might as well call this whole thing off.” Little Eleven said, a little impressed that these two were completely fine after all that. “What did you two experience?”","“Erm... just a nightmare...” Yang Ji stated, not wanting to delve much deeper into the topic.","“En. I did not see much.” Yang Xu answered straightforwardly, with eyes that did not know the word deceit.","Little Eleven gave a knowing nod of approval and said. “Well, if it affected you so little, then we might as well just enter directly.”","Upon those words he placed his hand on the Gate and started to push.","The world seemed to tremble as the seemingly immovable gate doors started to vibrate. The ‘dust’ on the gate also seemed to come alive and they drifted more fervently towards the centre.","When a slit had just opened up, what seemed to be a large black blade immediately shot out.","The twins could barely react, with their eyes only seeing a blurry shadow quickly approaching Little Eleven.","As for Little Eleven, he had already predicted this would happen. He swiftly removed his hands from the gate and retreated to the side. The blade passed by him, narrowly snipping off a part of his fringe.","As though the blade had eyes, it knew that it had missed its target. Instead of retreating back to the slit, it became more aggressive and branched out into three sharp abyssal black spear-like weapons.","These three black spears immediately pointed themselves towards whoever was present. In this case, the twins were now also in its crosshair.","Little Eleven’s eyes narrowed and he swiftly took out a Token. He was reluctant to use it now, but he seemed to have no choice. It was clear the children would not be able to dodge this attack on their own.","Injecting his Qi into the Token, the whole world trembled. The sky now had Array Patterns all over it, with the intensity of the light from the ground becoming exponentially more blinding.","“Close your eyes!” Little Eleven roared as the spears raced across the space between them.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu immediately reacted by closing their own eyes. Though frightened, they trusted their Uncle’s words.","The spears that approached them initially seemed to sizzle due to the surrounding light. But soon, a bright flash engulfed the world, turning everything into white. No matter how dark an object was, the light was so strong that all manner of darkness was eradicated for that brief moment.","The spears lost their structural integrity and they started to crack. Those web-like cracks spread and reached the ‘trunk’ of those branched out spears, even affecting past whatever it was behind the gate.","Soon, those parts furthest from the door started to break down into dust as they scattered. However, with the strong light still in the surroundings, they broke down further as if nothing was left.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu, who managed to protect their eyes from that flash, could clearly hear someone screaming. However, it was not from any of them. The scream was from behind the gate.","The scream was of great anguish, filled with rage and reluctance.","The next moment, they could hear something slamming against the gate, but the gate did not seem to be able to close. The thing behind the gate obviously wanted to prevent any more light from outside to enter. However, the slit in the gate still persisted despite all the effort it gave."]},{"number":6019,"title":"Chapter 6019, The Surprise Behind The Profound Source Gate","paragraphs":["Chapter 6019, The Surprise Behind The Profound Source Gate","Author: Silavin","Despite the screaming backdrop, Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt a comfortable sensation all over their body. It felt as though the air around them was caressing them in a warm embrace.","Soon enough, this warm sensation faded and the screams behind the door also slowly mellowed out. When silence returned, without any instructions, they both slowly opened one eye to check on the situation.","Seeing how everything had calmed down, Yang Xu sighed in relief while Yang Ji went to check on his Sister.","“Don’t let your guard down! The enemy is still there!” Little Eleven warned. Though, he knew Mo well enough that it was fine to take a breather at this point. After all, that child would never want to do something that could potentially harm it. Nevertheless, better safe than sorry.","This was the first time Little Eleven had to use the Primordial Flash to defend against Mo. All previous attempts were always with experts who knew of Mo’s strength first hand. They were on guard before they even tried to open the gate, so it was unnecessary to go as far as to use the Primordial Flash.","Little Eleven naturally would prefer not to use the Primordial Flash if possible, since it did take up mountain piles of Ninth-Order Yin and Yang Element Materials. Even with Moon’s Serene Glimmer and Sun’s Burning Light, such an amount would take time to accumulate. Currently, it could at most be fired two more times.","Still, Little Eleven was a little surprised by this sudden attack. This was the first Mo had been so aggressive. Normally, once the gate opens up, Mo would not attack. Rather, Mo tended to be more cautious when dealing with any newcomers.","The last time Yang Kai was here with Little Eleven, Mo literally hid some corner of the space behind the Profound Source Gate. Even for Yang Kai, the space behind this gate was too large to explore, with only darkness in sight and his limited Divine Sense. Even if he wanted to find Mo, how could he be certain that Mo would not just hide in another location once it sensed him approaching?","For Mo, it was like a fish swimming in water while for others, it was like walking in a quagmire.","For Yang Kai, he did not feel like he could spend so much time on a wild goose chase. Not after he had already spent more than a decade searching without any fruitful result.","Even the Profound Source Gate was only a gate to this unknown space. It did not contain this space itself. Even after refining it, and studying it, all Yang Kai could do was open and close the gate. In fact, for all its grandeur and mystery, Yang Kai truly believes that was the sole purpose of the Profound Source Gate – to keep whatever was in this other world from getting out to their world. All Yang Kai managed to do after so long was to ensure that nothing would leak out of the gate under his control, and open it for Little Eleven’s goals.","That being said, when it was others that ventured deeper into the Profound Source Gate with Little Eleven, Mo would be open to attacking them. After all, it knew who it could pick a fight against and who it needed to avoid. Nevertheless, with their preparations, these attacks could be shrugged off.","Unfortunately, the environment inside was not exactly friendly to the others. Regardless of the preparation, prolonged exposure to this space seems to corrupt them in one form or another. Without exception, all would have to leave this space before a year had passed. This was regardless of them being Divine Spirits or Humans.","The three of them waited for a moment for things to settle. Yang Ji and Yang Xu followed Little Eleven’s words and stayed alert. Fortunately, nothing else really happened after a few breaths had passed.","“Seems like we are in the clear now. Mo should be avoiding being close to the gate at this point in time, which is the perfect opportunity to fully open the gate.” Little Eleven said as he once more stepped closer to the Profound Source Gate. This time, to prevent any incidents, he directly stood in front of the gap and pushed the gate open.","*Rumble* once again, the world trembling tremor spread. As Little Eleven had said, nothing truly happened as he was pushing the gate open. Even when the gap was now too large for him to push any further, nothing else occurred.","It was truly anti-climatic.","However, Little Eleven’s next words sparked curiosity within all its listeners. “What is going on!?”","Hearing those words, the twins could not help but look over his arms.","Behind the gate, illuminated by the light, they saw a unique scene that they had not expected. In fact, even Yang Kai would not have predicted this scene to be in front of them.","The furthest depths of the gate was completely dark. As long as no light touched that location, it was completely dark by the abyss. This stood true to Little Eleven’s explanation of the place to the twins. However, what laid closer were the things that interested them.","They were plants! Actual plants.","However, these were not the typical plants that they could find elsewhere. The plants were pretty much all of the same colour of blackish-blue or blackish-purple. It was only with the light that their outline and slightly different colouration could be spotted. Otherwise, everything would be uniform black.","“Uncle Eleven, didn’t you say that the whole space behind the gate is just an empty space void of anything?” Yang Ji could not help but ask.","Despite this being a pressing and reasonable question, Little Eleven would also like to know what the Hell was going on.","“This was not here the last time. Something must have changed...” Little Eleven now hesitated. This was not something he thought was possible."]},{"number":6020,"title":"Chapter 6020, Strange Flower","paragraphs":["Chapter 6020, Strange Flower","Author: Silavin","[This... this is impossible. How did something like this possibly appear?] Little Eleven started to question everything, recalling all the past expeditions inside. However, nothing came up. These had truly just appeared out of thin air.","Without being able to contain himself, Little Eleven rushed into the Profound Source Gate and directly went to pick one of the flowers. The moment he touched one, a familiar feeling washed over him.","There was no need for someone else to explain it to him. He already knew what these were.","“So, that’s what it is...” Little Eleven murmured, which did not go unnoticed by the twins.","Still in front of the gate, Yang Ji questioned, “Uncle Eleven, did you figure something out?”","Little Eleven gave a slow nod and explained. “This is all made using Black Ink Strength. But, it is at the same time also not Black Ink Strength...”","Yang Xu shook her head at this contrary answer. She asked for more clarity. “So, what is it?”","Little Eleven picked out a flower and moved back to the twin. The moment he crossed the gate, he could see the flower gradually losing its original form. It was apparent that the closer he got to the light outside, the more the flower seemed to wither.","“This is made using Black Ink Strength... to create another life...” Little Eleven turned around and pointed at the ground behind the gate.","“In essence, this is no different from Black Ink Strength. But, it exists separately from Mo, as though it is another entity. This is not much different from the Black Ink Clansmen in your history lessons. As you can see, because of the Primordial Flash, the part directly in front of the gate does not have any of these plants. It is only at the periphery, with the gate being opened up, that we can see these plants.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu cutely bent their heads forward a little to get a better look at the flowers. They were certainly dark and strange looking, but at the same time, quite cool as well. Their shape was no different from the ones that could be found outside. They were not all homogenous, with some variations between them. At the same time, their placement was random, as though it was an actual flower field.","Yang Ji could not hold back his curiosity and asked, “Uncle Eleven, can I hold that for a moment?”","Little Eleven hesitated for a moment but relented. After all, they were still safe here. “Okay. Just be careful. If anything goes wrong, make sure to shout out for help.”","Little Eleven passed the withering flower to Yang Ji and cautiously watched.","The boy took it with both hands, trying to get a feel of its texture. Even when it touched his skin, he did not have the same back memories flood back into him again.","He saw that his Sister was also curious so he handed it over to her. When she felt it all over, she could not help but comment, “It really feels like a flower. The stem is tougher, the petals are softer and smoother. Just that... it’s a bit colder...”","“Yeah. But, I guess it’s colder because there is no Sun inside.” Yang Ji replied with a tilt of his head.","Meanwhile, Little Eleven questioned, [Huh? The Black Ink Strength is not affecting them at all? What is going on?]","Although Little Eleven expected things to be fine, he was still shocked to see how the Black Ink Strength from the flower had no effect on them. He questioned if it was due to the flower already withering, but that did not make sense as even the remnant Black Ink Strength outside the gate had affected them.","[The only way to test this out is for them to go in and touch the flowers inside...] Little Eleven quickly shook his head. In fact, due to these major changes behind the Primordial Source Gate, he believed it to be wise for them to retreat first. Since it was to just get a cursory check of the situation, and not really to find Mo, Yang Kai was the best candidate to do it.","[The Father should make sure it’s safe for his kids, after all.] Little Eleven mused, and was about to open his mouth when something shocking happened.","The withering flower suddenly began to expand, like a final desperate move; moving along with it were the flowers behind the gate. A torrent of black shot out from behind the gate, while the withering flower quickly tried to stretch back to the gate.","Unbeknownst to Little Eleven, it was at the instant, when the withering flower expanded, that Black Ink Strength began to affect Yang Xu. The Black Ink Strength this time was definitely more potent that the first time she had made contact with it. However, the effects on her were more muted as well. It just caused her to be disoriented this time.","Nevertheless, this disorientation was enough.","If she was still in perfect condition, she would have instinctively thrown the flower away from her. However, with her hand still held onto it, the expansion of Black Ink Strength naturally got wrapped around her fingers as it sought to escape.","As though having learned the lesson from the previous attack, the black torrent moved faster than before. It would not give Little Eleven the chance to use the Primordial Flash again.","Before Primordial Flash could activate, the black torrent made contact with the outstretched ‘withered flower’ and started to pull back. This time, with Yang Xu with it, hand stuck.","There was not even a scream from her as she got silently pulled closer into the gate. She did not even feel her feet being forced to be dragged against the ground. Not even the two arms that wrapped around her waist were felt.","Yang Ji had reacted quickly to grab onto his Sister. Unfortunately, his meagre strength was not enough to pull her free. In fact, he had made his own situation worse as he got rapidly pulled in as well.","By the time there was a bright flash, the two children were gone, with Little Eleven cursing how the situation had gotten drastically worse...","Silavin: Guys, any feedback so far? Draggy? Want more action? Want more world building? It’s okay as is?"]},{"number":6021,"title":"Chapter 6021, Released","paragraphs":["Chapter 6021, Released","Author: Silavin","Darkness soon envelops his eyes as Yang Ji could only see the faint light behind him disappear. It was no longer a matter of going back at this point. All he wished for was his Sister’s safety.","In the pitch-black darkness, there was no point looking around and relying on his eyes. He started to close his eyes and used his Divine Sense to grasp his surroundings. The most important thing right now was to avoid making contact with Black Ink Strength, lest he too got caught up like Yang Xu. If he did, he might loosen his grip and truly lose his Sister in this forsaken darkness.","His Divine Sense spread out like a tide. Unlike the outside world, this place seems to suppress it. He could feel his Divine Sense being encroached upon and get pushed back. In fact, there was a constant tingling sensation but thankfully not much else.","Unbeknownst to him earlier, a net had been formed around them. A net that kept them from escaping.","As for the surroundings past the net, there were unusual mountains and rivers. Supposed trees and grass were also in abundance, with flowers and fruits scattered about.","As for the limits of where his Divine Sense could reach, the rivers were the denotation of the boundary. The prohibitive and encroaching sensation got infinitely stronger the moment his Divine Sense got close to these rivers. He could even feel the dangers of the waters himself.","He focused on the scene ahead, and frighteningly enough, the plants in front of them seem to warp themselves to pull them forward. It was as if they were made of some kind of slimy substance. They would disfigure and pull from the front, and once Yang Ji and Yang Xu got past them; they would return to their original forms. It was through this method that their momentum quickened the deeper they went.","Yang Ji began to frown, and he immediately tapped into his Space Ring. [We need to quickly escape!]","The next instant, two crystals of blue and orange came out. Yang Ji firmly grasped onto them with both hands and the mark behind his palm started to glow.","A bright flash immediately enveloped the whole area, scorching off all the Black Ink Strength around him. Trees, grass, even the soil, none were spared. With him at the center, there was even a massive pit below. Naturally, the he and Yang Xu had been freed from their constraints as well.","“Ops.” Yang Ji quickly grabbed a hold of Yang Xu before she completely fell into the crater below.","He felt it unnerving to fall into the crater so he decided to just stay in mid-air with her in his arms.","Thankfully, the effects of Black Ink Strength did not linger on her for long as Yang Xu soon regained consciousness. In fact, she was immediately confused as she suddenly felt warm arms under her but nothing in sight. She questioned if her eyelids were opened as she tried to open them to only find that the scene before her was genuinely pitch black.","“Brother, are you here?” She asked, a little unnerved.","“Yeah. Start using your Divine Sense. No point relying on our eyes here.” Yang Ji said with a sigh.","Yang Xu did as she was advised to see a strange scene around her. She could already make sense of what had happened from fragments of her memories. Even the crater below was something she deduced her Brother had created. What made the scene strange was the crater underneath them reforming itself, as though the whole ground was alive.","However, a more thorough investigation of her surroundings was halted by her Brother.","“Since you’re fine, can you get up on your own?” Yang Ji asked, with his arms already being lowered.","“Eh? But, I’m still a little dizzy...” Yang Xu complained as she took advantage of this opportunity to wrap her arms around his neck and playfully held on.","“Just get off me already.” Yang Ji nagged as he completely took his arms off her. Yet, she clung onto him using even her legs.","“Seriously. Just get off me already. We’re in danger right now, and Uncle Eleven is no longer here with us.” Yang Ji persisted to say.","“Well, we are not in that big of a danger.” Yang Xu shook her head and explained. “If you are able to make that crater, that means that whatever they had given us is extremely effective here.”","“We don’t exactly have an unlimited amount, you know? And, we don’t really know what might happen here.” Yang Ji pointed out, believing they should remain cautious.","“I guess you’re right. But, you know, I don’t think Black Ink Strength will affect us that much if we get more exposed to it.” Yang Xu said and continued to give an account of her experience. “I don’t know why but I did feel that the effects are weakening the more I get exposed to it.”","“Hmm... Then, do you want to stay here longer to try out your theory?” Yang Ji said, believing that they should have enough resources to last long enough to test this out.","“Eh... Well, I guess it would be safer to head back to the exit fir-” Before Yang Xu could finish speaking, she frowned, and Yang Ji had already moved.","Yang Ji tried to tear open a Void Crack, but he could not do so. The best he could do was fly off, away from this place.","After all, just underneath them, the whole ground was quaking. What seemed to be sharp spikes seem to be forming, ready to strike at them. If he did not escape at this time, then when would he?","As expected, those spikes launched at him and his Sister, but they were clearly still tethered to the ground with a thin string(?) connecting the two.","They were frighteningly fast, moving quicker than them. Without the ability to tear through Space, they were truly just sitting ducks here!"]},{"number":6022,"title":"Chapter 6022, World Change","paragraphs":["Chapter 6022, World Change","Author: Silavin","“Argh! I can’t tear through Space here. The Space Principals are strange. They aren’t the same!” Yang Ji cursed as he tried to gain some distance from the black spikes.","For the twins, they had no small number of adventures with their Family to different Universe Worlds and Small Universes. However, such places all have the same World Principles within them. The World Principals here were too different from the outside world. In fact, mastery over the certain Principals outside need not necessarily mean one would be capable of manipulating Principals inside this place.","Once Yang Xu heard what he said, she was quick to react. Still on her Brother, she took out another pair of Crystals and caused another explosion.","Everything around them turned into a white flash once more, and the spike chasing after them disintegrated into white.","Then again, since this has happened once, the twins were certain this would happen again. Even if they had mountains of Crystals, if they kept this up, eventually they would run out. The best was for them to retreat back outside. However, would this strange place allow them to?","The world, seeming to have acknowledged that such means were too minor to handle the children, began to change tactics. The landscape itself started to shift, with mountains and rivers bendings and twisting.","The landmass below them started to rise in one direction. Their form no longer seemed solid, changing to something more fluid. Rivers and earth mixed into one, indistinguishable from each other. They raised to form a tsunami, wishing to engulf the two.","The twins were naturally alarmed by this.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both braced for the incoming attack. Without speaking, Yang Ji took out an Array Plate while Yang Xu took out more Crystals.","With a little bit of Qi inserted into the Array Plate, it began to spin and eight flags shot out. They each covered a cardinal and ordinal direction. A translucent sphere of around 9 metres in radius formed, enveloping the twins.","Meanwhile, Yang Xu was prepared to launch another Purifying Light once the tsunami got close enough.","However before they did anything else, the whole tsunami seemed to freeze in place and a voice came from above, at its crest. The voice was neither booming nor threatening. It was more calm and collected.","“Stop. We do not wish to fight.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu naturally looked up to see a few figures gathered at the crest. These figures certainly did not seem Human. They were Humanoid, but certainly not Humans. Some had more arms, some had longer limbs, some even had carpaces as skin.","Regardless, there was a particular figure that stood out amongst the rest. This figure definitely emitted more pressure than the rest. In terms of his aura alone, Yang Xu and Yang Ji were certain they could not best him. That was just how overwhelming his aura was.","[Isn’t he in the Emperor Realm? No, maybe the Dao Seal Realm?] Yang Ji and Yang Xu both thought. After all, they would be able to tell a person’s cultivation if they were weaker than them. Anyone Stronger had to be above the Dao Source Realm. However, this person’s aura was not overwhelming to the point of reaching the Open Heaven Realm. Then again, who knows if this figure was suppressing his cultivation?","From afar, the figure held out his fist, as an indication for his men to stop moving. He knew that if the weak were to get involved in this, their deaths would be fruitless. Such a time had long passed when the weak were used as useless cannon fodder. Now, they served a greater purpose.","Furthermore, he was personally confident in his own strength, which would be able to suppress the two children. Thus, he went down alone.","From the crest of the tsunami, he leaped down and stopped directly in front of the twins. Naturally, they both had their guards up, with Yang Xu already prepared to unleash Purifying Light.","This light used to haunt his armies in the past. Yet now, it was just a reminiscent scene. He repeated his words. “We are not looking to fight against you. Lay down your arms.”","Naturally, how could Yang Ji and Yang Xu possibly comply? If they did, they would be helpless chickens. Instead, their grips tightened on the objects they were holding.","Seeing this, the figure sighed and added. “I see that there is no helping your need for caution. In that case, I just ask that you do not unleash Purifying Light here. I am Mo Na Ye, and I believe you are the children of Yang Kai.”","Once the twins heard his name, they reeled back. Of course they would. This was the Black Ink Clansman, the Royal Lord, their Father had praised numerous times in the past. Though they were enemies, there was a sense of respect for each other as soldiers on the battlefield.","Their Father had highlighted how out of all the Royal Lords, no, Black Ink Clansmen, Mo Na Ye was special in his eyes. He was the only one with wit, cunningness and bravery. Every one of their battles were always fights inches away from death. How, like their Father, Mo Na Ye had climbed through the ranks of originally being a Territory Lord to Pseudo-Royal Lord to an actual Royal Lord. How he was the first and only to accomplish such a feat.","Though enemies, they might actually share more similarities than differences. It was just unfortunate that they never had a moment of peace to really get to know one another. Other than crossing blades, possibly, that exchange of drinks at No-Return Pass marked their only time to get to know one another.","The twins naturally heard of his eventual fate. It made it all the stranger how Mo Na Ye was currently here, still alive! Furthermore, he knew who they were!","They questioned their ears if they heard wrongly. But, his next words confirmed that this was reality.","“Yang kids, the battle against your world and the Black Ink Clan has ceased for thousands of years. Why have you come to our land?” Mo Na Ye questioned. It was not in an overbearing manner or anything. Just an actual question that showcased his curiosity.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu hesitated to explain. After all, the reason why they were here had something to do with their Uncle Eleven. They did not know if sharing this information with the enemy would be a detriment to the overall cause.","Seeing how the children were not speaking up, Mo Na Ye just shrugged and moved on from the topic. Although he did want to know, at this point, it was not truly necessary. These children would not really amount to much in a battle, and if anyone stronger crosses the gate, he would be alerted of it. Currently, no such thing had occurred so he was assured they did not exactly come with hostile intentions either. If anything, he already had a faint guess as the Holy One’s other half was detected at the gate.","To show his intentions first for them to let down their guard, he confessed. “Nothing good will come of starting a war again, much less doing harm to the children of Yang Kai. Your Father is basically the best guarantor you have so no need to be so wary.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu thought for a moment, and realised this to be reasonable. However, Yang Xu realised the contradiction. She got off her Brother and moved in front of him, directly questioning, “Then, why did you kidnap us?”"]},{"number":6023,"title":"Chapter 6023, Come With Me Or I’ll Have To Drag You Along","paragraphs":["Chapter 6023, Come With Me Or I’ll Have To Drag You Along","Author: Silavin","Mo Na Ye broke out a wide smile. Maybe he was reminiscing about the past, maybe he was humoured by the question. Regardless, he was in a good enough mood to state the reason. After all, what could two children do about it?","“What else but to keep hold of a couple of hostages?”","The twins had their eyes narrowed. It was Yang Ji that spoke up this time. “Don’t speak too soon.”","“Oh? And why would that be?” Mo Na Ye instantly asked as he smiled.","Maybe it was a false bravado, maybe it was him being convinced, Yang Ji smiled back. “Can you truly capture us without any consequences?”","Yang Ji pointed at the top, past Mo Na Ye and added. “Aren’t you in the same position as us? You brought us hostages. What’s more, isn’t this whole world our hostage?”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu had heard many things from Little Eleven. It was made clear that the world behind the Profound Source Gate was supposed to be entirely empty. Yet, why was this place now filled with life? If anything, something strange must have happened and the whole world had changed. At the same time, some things remained the same. The scourge of Black Ink Strength was still Purifying Light. The world was still empty, it was now just strangely filled with these structures clearly made of Black Ink Strength.","Though Yang Ji was just fishing for an answer, Mo Na Ye casually admitted to it, even going as far as to shrug his shoulders. “You’re right. I guess you can say that both our hands are tied.”","Yang Ji was naturally taken aback at how calm Mo Na Ye was being. Still, to express his sincerity. Mo Na Ye continued to explain their current circumstances in more detail.","“We really have no wish to be hostile with your kind anymore. Certainly, our world is lacking compared to yours, but it is slowly improving over time. Instead of committing the same mistake as in the past by pillaging, we hope to establish ourselves in this empty land. The people that I brought over are basically our version of mortals without any strength. They are just here to showcase our sincerity.”","Yang Xu and Yang Ji clearly did not buy his words. After all, what kind of sincerity could a kidnapper possibly talk about? They would be fools to fall for such sweet tongued words.","Nevertheless, since there was a show of ‘sincerity’, they might as well use it. Yang Xu stepped forward to ask, “In that case, then why not just let us go?”","Mo Na Ye shook his head as his smile widened. “The Holy One is requesting an audience with you. You are not allowed to refuse his request.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu immediately got a shiver down their spine. They naturally knew who this ‘Holy One’ was without being explicitly told. It had to be none other than the other part of Uncle Eleven, which had been sealed away behind the Profound Source Gate.","Naturally, it was part of their task to find this other half. However, they were supposed to do it with Uncle Eleven beside them. Not go at it alone.","This was supposed to be a being that was ever close to the World Creation Realm. A being only their Father was able to deal with. Even Little Eleven was not fully confident he would be able to deal with this other half by himself, which was why he normally had others go with him. Yet, this very same being wanted to meet them.","If escape from Mo Na Ye was already difficult, escape from this other half would be impossible.","Yang Xu and Yang Ji naturally wanted to refuse. In fact, Yang Ji and Yang Xu glanced at each other. Without saying a word, they already tightened their grips on the Crystals and a sudden flash of light popped off.","Unfortunately, this move was all too predictable.","Mo Na Ye had acted a moment prior.","With one hand, he reached out. A huge surge of Black Ink Strength soon gushed out. It enveloped the twins, and the Array itself.","Once Purifying Light fired off, this whole layer got scorched off, with Mo Na Ye being able to feel his hand being torched. Nevertheless, this move was enough to prevent further damage to the surroundings.","Once the light dyed down, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were greeted by the sight of nothing changing. Their faces turned grim as they did the same thing again.","Another blast of Purifying Light flashed but it was all too concealed. Once again, resulting in nothing substantial.","Mo Na Ye smirked and added. “It’s no use. Even if you keep trying to do this a million times, the result will be the same. I’d prefer for you two to come along with me willingly, but if I have to drag you there myself, I will do so.”","*Tsk* Yang Ji clicked his tongue, and Yang Xu moved to grab her Brother’s sleeve.","It was silent for a moment before the two tacitly agreed to move along with Mo Na Ye. Certainly, they could have resisted until the very end, but what would that accomplish? Were they going to exhaust everything in their Space Ring at this point in time, where the enemy already prepared any counters to their moves?","They really doubt that they would be able to escape from the ‘Holy One’, considering that they already could not escape from Mo Na Ye. Still, the best thing they could do at the moment was to find a proper opening for them to act upon. If they continued to play along, they could potentially stall for time till someone rescues them.","“Fine. We’ll go along with you. But, we will keep our protective Array up.” Yang Ji said as if this was the final line that could not be crossed.","“Naturally. We mean you no harm.” Mo Na Ye stepped aside and lifted his whole arm to gesture to them to move in that direction."]},{"number":6024,"title":"Chapter 6024, House By the Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6024, House By the Mountain","Author: Silavin","Once the twins started moving, the whole world seemed to move along with them. The tall tsunami of Black Ink Strength seemed to follow them from behind, as the onlookers from above continued to stare at these interesting Humans.","It was obvious that they were still cautious of them escaping. Otherwise, why would the way back to the gate be blocked by these obstacles?","Yang Ji felt a little disgruntled by this and asked, “We already said we will go along with you. Why do you still need to have that following us from behind?”","Mo Na Ye just chuckled as he led the way in front. “I’ve experienced so many battles with your Father. I naturally know how conniving Humans are. It’s always better to be safe than sorry when dealing with your kind.”","Yang Xu interjected, “My Brother never lies to me. Only my Father lies.”","Mo Na Ye laughed so loudly that the ground started to quiver. Even the people at the top of the moving tsunami felt odd seeing the usually solemn Mo Na Ye laugh so loudly.","Yang Ji had an odd expression on his face as he immediately asked Yang Xu through Divine Sense, “Why did you say that?”","Yang Xu, who knew that her Brother was too upright and proper if he was not being playful, explained back through their Divine Sense. “Since we are already in their hands, we might as well play along and befriend them. Otherwise, how would they lower down their guard? Mother Ru Meng has always said that those who are relaxed talk more.”","[Technically, she said those who are drunk confess their true feelings. But, no need to bother Big Brother with the details.] Yang Xu smiled in her heart, while her facial expression remained completely neutral.","“Is that so? But to insult Father like that...” Yang Ji wanted to protest but Yang Xu quickly shot back.","“It’s not exactly false right? Have you ever lied to me? As for Father, how many times have we been told he had time to play before one of our Mothers had to drag him back because he still had work to do?”","“You know that’s because he is always busy.” Yang Ji tried to defend his Father.","Yang Xu wanted to rebuke him but just kept to herself. “Hmph!” [Of course he is so busy. He has so many Wives to maintain. Although Mother never complains about it, Mother Ru Meng, and Mother Qing Luo would complain from time to time.]","Yang Ji naturally never heard about these complaints. These were normally conversations that took place when there were only girls around. With how he idolises his Father, the Mothers would naturally try their best to not talk bad about him in front of Yang Ji.","Mo Na Ye naturally noticed the two were secretly conversing using their Divine Sense. However, he was not one to worry about it. In fact, he even waited quietly until the two ended their conversation before he asked. “How is your Father doing so far?”","Although they were enemies, they did share a particular bond. It was akin to that of rivals. Although he did not have memories of how he was defeated, he knew he had lost. In fact, he had hoped that the weapon that struck him down was Yang Kai’s spear, as it would truly have concluded their bitter hostile relationship at that point in time.","Yang Xu was the first to speak. She even convinced Yang Ji to let her do the talking for now. “Father is doing well. He had restored the 3,000 Worlds back to its original state, making it thrive even better than before.”","Mo Na Ye nodded. He was genuinely happy for Yang Kai. He was also glad to hear that the 3,000 Worlds was doing better now. After all, although it was Black Ink Clansmen like them who destroyed so much of the world, they only did it out of necessity of resources. Even if most Black Ink Clansmen enjoyed seeing the cruel torture of others, and violence, he was not one of them.","In fact, such brutality seems to be more prevalent in the lower class of Black Ink Clansmen, mainly those below the Feudal Lords. The more powerful Black Ink Clansmen might host such activities, but they were mostly to motivate their men. In fact, those Feudal Lords and above tend to be more apathetic than anything, not caring about the lives of others, even their own men.","The conversation between the two continued. Yang Xu would give little updates on what happened after the war, and Mo Na Ye would continue to share what he knew about the past, and some tidbits about the current situation of this world.","These two were naturally engaging in a conversation that was trying to dig out as much information from the other person. However, both knew about it and kept their cards close to their chest.","As for Yang Ji, as the bystander, he grew bored. In fact, he was irked by this type of scheming. He knew it was not his place to judge how his Sister handled things, but he always hoped to settle things upfront if possible.","Fortunately for him, their destination soon arrived in front of their eyes. It was a mountain, but not just any ordinary mountain. The Black Ink Strength in this area was deep and vast, like this was its very source. The mountain had numerous openings, which liquid Black Ink Strength gushes out from.","When looked closely, this was where all those meandering rivers had started from.","Also, unlike the rest of the area, there seemed to be buildings around the top. Most of these buildings were unlike those found in their world. They looked a little like snail shells, with webbing around them. If Yang Ji and Yang Xu were not wrong, these were Black Ink Nests.","For Yang Ji and Yang Xu, since they could fly, they easily got to the top with Mo Na Ye. However, what surprised them at the peak was a small, ordinary looking thatched house. It was not magnificent in any way. In fact, the other ‘houses’ in the area were far bigger than this. Nevertheless, this seemingly ordinary building stood out amongst all the peculiarities."]},{"number":6025,"title":"Chapter 6025, Dao Oath","paragraphs":["Chapter 6025, Dao Oath","Author:?Silavin","Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at each other, puzzled by the sight. After all, the structure of this thatched house was really familiar. Although it was of a different colour, there was no mistaking it. This was almost a carbon copy of the small house their Uncle Eleven lives in.","Naturally, the twins were not dense enough to fail to notice that there must have been some background story to this. After all, were there really such coincidences in this world?","Mo Na Ye was respectful when he approached the thatched house. Even with someone of his strength, he would try his best to not make a sound. Even in front of the door, he would not knock. Instead, he would just kneel and wait for a response from inside.","Mo Na Ye knew that this was the courtesy expected of his kind in front of the Holy One. So, he did not expect the same from the kids. Yet, without him doing anything, Yang Xu took the lead and followed what he did, with Yang Ji also doing the same.","This one display made Mo Na Ye praise them in his heart. Though he knew Humans were sly, the gesture of them willingly kneeling to a potential enemy could not be taken lightly. At the very least, from what he remembers, Yang Kai, the Human he interacted with the most, was so prideful he would never kneel to anyone.","In truth, this was just a misconception which Yang Xu had made use of, which was more effective than she thought. After all, she and her Brother would kneel down whenever they got punished. How was this much of a difference?","Either way, for the twins, the wait was certainly not long. Almost as soon as their knees touched the ground, the door opened and a terrifying pressure emerged from within.","This pressure was incomparable to the one Mo Na Ye gave out. However, its aura also felt familiar at the same time.","A familiar child-like voice rang out, “Come in.”","“Yes.” Mo Na Ye placed his arm on his chest as he stood up, and the twins just followed along and walked behind him till they were inside of the thatched house.","The inside and outside were basically sights they had seen before. At this point, they were not even surprised. The only oddity, which caught their eye was what seemed to be another Uncle Eleven.","This ‘Uncle Eleven’ technically did not have feet, as his legs were attached to the ground. He was also completely black with a tint of purple. In terms of facial features and stature, he was basically the same as the one they knew.","Mo spoke up, welcoming his guests. “Welcome to my humble abode. It has been awhile since I last saw Humans.”","The Mo that they were speaking to seemed to have matured a lot compared to stories they heard of him. At least, he was far from what their Uncle Eleven had described him to be.","Instead of the twins speaking up to greet him back, Mo Na Ye was the one to do their introduction. “Your Holy One, this is Yang Ji and this is Yang Xu. They are children of Yang Kai, and have been brought here by your other half.”","Mo, already knowing this, just raised a hand as he gave a nod and asked the twins directly. “Just what are you two?”","This question had naturally confused the twins. How were they going to answer this?","Seeming to notice their confusion, Mo further elaborated. “My Black Ink Strength is not something Ninth-Order Masters can easily resist. My Black Ink Strength definitely still affects you two, but what are you two compared to those in the Ninth-Order Open Heaven Realm? How are you able to resist its influence so easily?”","This was another question that the twins also did not know how to answer. Was it their constitution? Or, was their Qi just different?","Yang Ji pondered for a moment, and gave an unconvincing, “I think it’s because of our pure Bloodlines.”","Mo, obviously well experienced, could tell that there was more to the story. However, if the children did not want to say it, he had no wish to force it out of them. After all, such an ability might not be replicable.","After answering, Yang Ji felt as though it was their turn to ask. So, he posed this question to Mo, “Why did you want to see us, resorting to separating us from Uncle Eleven?”","This was basically the same question he had asked Mo Na Ye – ‘why did you kidnap us’.","Mo was frank and open, not hiding anything from them. “To take in as hostages, also, to seek your help.”","“Help?” Both Yang Ji and Yang Xu exclaimed, almost unable to believe their ears. After all, why would this almighty being, maybe second only to their Father, be asking them for help?","Mo continued to explain. “Yes, I need the assistance of those who will not be corrupted by my Black Ink Strength and can use Purifying Light. Moreover, these people must be weak enough to not be detected as a threat.”","Yang Xu was the one to ask this time. “In that case, why not take Uncle Eleven with us?”","“It is not yet time to meet him.”","“Not yet time?” The twins simultaneously asked.","“I can even do a Dao Oath right now, that I, Mo, will meet him once you help me with my troubles.” Mo said, as if already prepared for this. “There, is this enough to satisfy you two?”","Silavin: I’m going to now use he for Mo instead of the previous ‘it’. There is a reason for this but I won’t get to it right now."]},{"number":6026,"title":"Chapter 6026, Dao Oath","paragraphs":["Chapter 6026, Dao Oath","Author: Silavin","Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at each other, puzzled by the sight. After all, the structure of this thatched house was really familiar. Although it was of a different colour, there was no mistaking it. This was almost a carbon copy of the small house their Uncle Eleven lives in.","Naturally, the twins were not dense enough to fail to notice that there must have been some background story to this. After all, were there really such coincidences in this world?","Mo Na Ye was respectful when he approached the thatched house. Even with someone of his strength, he would try his best to not make a sound. Even in front of the door, he would not knock. Instead, he would just kneel and wait for a response from inside.","Mo Na Ye knew that this was the courtesy expected of his kind in front of the Holy One. So, he did not expect the same from the kids. Yet, without him doing anything, Yang Xu took the lead and followed what he did, with Yang Ji also doing the same.","This one display made Mo Na Ye praise them in his heart. Though he knew Humans were sly, the gesture of them willingly kneeling to a potential enemy could not be taken lightly. At the very least, from what he remembers, Yang Kai, the Human he interacted with the most, was so prideful he would never kneel to anyone.","In truth, this was just a misconception which Yang Xu had made use of, which was more effective than she thought. After all, she and her Brother would kneel down whenever they got punished. How was this much of a difference?","Either way, for the twins, the wait was certainly not long. Almost as soon as their knees touched the ground, the door opened and a terrifying pressure emerged from within.","This pressure was incomparable to the one Mo Na Ye gave out. However, its aura also felt familiar at the same time.","A familiar child-like voice rang out, “Come in.”","“Yes.” Mo Na Ye placed his arm on his chest as he stood up, and the twins just followed along and walked behind him till they were inside of the thatched house.","The inside and outside were basically sights they had seen before. At this point, they were not even surprised. The only oddity, which caught their eye was what seemed to be another Uncle Eleven.","This ‘Uncle Eleven’ technically did not have feet, as his legs were attached to the ground. He was also completely black with a tint of purple. In terms of facial features and stature, he was basically the same as the one they knew.","Mo spoke up, welcoming his guests. “Welcome to my humble abode. It has been awhile since I last saw Humans.”","The Mo that they were speaking to seemed to have matured a lot compared to stories they heard of him. At least, he was far from what their Uncle Eleven had described him to be.","Instead of the twins speaking up to greet him back, Mo Na Ye was the one to do their introduction. “Your Holy One, this is Yang Ji and this is Yang Xu. They are children of Yang Kai, and have been brought here by your other half.”","Mo, already knowing this, just raised a hand as he gave a nod and asked the twins directly. “Just what are you two?”","This question had naturally confused the twins. How were they going to answer this?","Seeming to notice their confusion, Mo further elaborated. “My Black Ink Strength is not something Ninth-Order Masters can easily resist. My Black Ink Strength definitely still affects you two, but what are you two compared to those in the Ninth-Order Open Heaven Realm? How are you able to resist its influence so easily?”","This was another question that the twins also did not know how to answer. Was it their constitution? Or, was their Qi just different?","Yang Ji pondered for a moment, and gave an unconvincing, “I think it’s because of our pure Bloodlines.”","Mo, obviously well experienced, could tell that there was more to the story. However, if the children did not want to say it, he had no wish to force it out of them. After all, such an ability might not be replicable.","After answering, Yang Ji felt as though it was their turn to ask. So, he posed this question to Mo, “Why did you want to see us, resorting to separating us from Uncle Eleven?”","This was basically the same question he had asked Mo Na Ye – ‘why did you kidnap us’.","Mo was frank and open, not hiding anything from them. “To take in as hostages, also, to seek your help.”","“Help?” Both Yang Ji and Yang Xu exclaimed, almost unable to believe their ears. After all, why would this almighty being, maybe second only to their Father, be asking them for help?","Mo continued to explain. “Yes, I need the assistance of those who will not be corrupted by my Black Ink Strength and can use Purifying Light. Moreover, these people must be weak enough to not be detected as a threat.”","Yang Xu was the one to ask this time. “In that case, why not take Uncle Eleven with us?”","“It is not yet time to meet him.”","“Not yet time?” The twins simultaneously asked.","“I can even do a Dao Oath right now, that I, Mo, will meet him once you help me with my troubles.” Mo said, as if already prepared for this. “There, is this enough to satisfy you two?”","(Silavin: I’m going to now use he for Mo instead of the previous ‘it’. There is a reason for this but I won’t get to it right now.)","Chapter 6026 – Help Me Devour","Yang Ji and Yang Xu were both confused by this sudden request. After all, this Mo was vastly different from the stories told about him. In fact, this made them feel even more unnerved, since the being in front of them was clearly far more intelligent that what they were led to believe.","At the same time, at Mo’s level of cultivation. Rather, his own existential difference, would Dao Oaths really work on him?","Regardless, they were already in this mess. Refusing would do them no good at this point. If they showed to be too on guard, the other party would react in the same manner. Right now, having more leeway to source for information was the best thing they could do.","Yang Ji was quicker in responding, “That’s fine, but you haven’t even said what you need us to do?”","“It’s actually quite simple, really. I need you to help me collect other pieces of me.” Mo said, as he awaited their next question.","“Other pieces of you?” The twins both cutely tilted their heads and wondered what he was talking about. They had not heard of there being other ‘Mo’s in existence.","This time, it was Mo Na Ye who stepped up to explain. And, as though assisting him, the wall next to Mo Na Ye started to deform to depict a landscape on it.","Due to the lack of light, the landscape had varying gradients, structures and surfaces to depict different areas. However, such details were still in the minority. Within the frame, most of it was a monotonous flat black, with two large figures in them. It was only one particular area that clearly showed mountains and rivers, which was clearly the area they were in right now.","In this well-defined region, there was also another large figure, but it was Humanoid in shape unlike the other two large figures.","Mo Na Ye pointed to this singular figure and said, just as the twins had guessed, “We are currently here. What we require of you is to help us claim these other two territories. These two figures are the other Holy Ones.”","It seemed like even if they were enemies, Mo Na Ye still felt the need to refer to them as ‘Holy Ones’.","Yang Xu questioned, “Wait. In the first place, why do you need us for this? Both of you are much stronger than us. There is no way for us to beat the other ‘yous’”","Mo Na Ye tried to dispel her worries. “This is not about strength. Rather, it is about compatibility. In fact, right now, as things stand, we have lost a lot of our men and territory. We basically see no way to turn this around.”","Mo further added. “The other pieces of me have gotten stronger. It is unfortunate but I am not their match. Their influence and power would continue to grow if they devour more of my territory. I don’t even know how many other ‘me’s they have devoured to get this strong. So, for you two, you do not need to engage with them directly. Your job is to make it easier for me to devour their territories.”","“How are we supposed to make it easier for you? Why have you not asked my Father to help you instead? Yang Xu continued to question.","Once Mo Na Ye heard this, he chuckled. “Even if we wanted to, we dared not. Though at this point, we might not necessarily be enemies, he is too much of a risk to make contact with...”","“As for how you are going to make it easier for us, it is mainly the ability to use Purifying Light. With it, you would be able to soften up certain areas for us to take over.”","The twins looked at each other and they both gave a nod. Yang Ji stepped forward to agree to help. “In that case, we’ll help out. But, as you know, we actually need these Crystals to activate Purifying Light. Once we run out...”","Mo Na Ye shook his head, and frankly stated. “I’m afraid that we would not be able to help you replenish your stockpile when you run out. Over here, we do not have enough materials to even make more powerful Black Ink Clansmen. We certainly do not have such powerful Crystals.”","Yang Ji’s eyes narrowed and he was about to say something. However, Yang Xu cut in and asked instead. “In that case, will we be allowed to go back to replenish our supplies?”","This was the biggest thing on their minds. They needed to gauge how opposed these two were of them heading back home","Mo gave a nod and Mo Na Ye stated, “In that case, you are free to go back and replenish your supplies.”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both had loosened their expressions for a moment as this response was not something that they had expected in a million years. This micro-expression was easily caught onto by Mo Na Ye as he chuckled and further stated. “Even if I called you hostages before, do you two really expect us to keep you here forever? Yang Kai would definitely come here with a vengeance. Do you think we can afford to face his wrath when our situation is as such where we can run away now?”","“Besides, even if we do nothing, you will come back on your own.” Mo Na Ye smirked, which made the twins further questioned. “What do you mean?”","This time, it was Mo who answered them. He spoke as though this matter was of heavy importance to him. “If our side loses in this conflict, and I get devoured, the other two pieces of me will definitely be hostile against the Human Race. After all, they are the corrupted Source pieces, which have lost their sanity.”","“I do not know about the future, but you would be having another enemy in your backyard. If one day, one of them manages to reach the World Creation Realm, I believe that would spell the start of another major war. A second war with the Black Ink Clan.”","“Even if they are corrupted, they are not fools. They will definitely avoid attacking your Human Race as long as your Father is there. However, the moment he is gone, or they get strong enough to contend with him, that would be the start of another war.”","“And, your Father will certainly leave one day. For, this plane is too small for him. He would need to go to the *%$#@*!!!”"]},{"number":6027,"title":"Chapter 6027, Black Ink Pool","paragraphs":["Chapter 6027, Black Ink Pool","Author: Silavin","Mo’s words suddenly became a blur. It was not that Yang Xu and Yang Ji were unable to hear it. Rather, it just sounded incomprehensible, as though this knowledge was not allowed to be heard by them. Even Mo Na Ye could not make sense of those words.","Meanwhile, Mo just felt as if nothing was off initially. He only noticed what happened after seeing their expressions.","He did not even bother to ask them about it, since he did not know what could and could not be said at this point. Nevertheless, such details were not important at the moment. When they reached that stage, where such information could be received, they would eventually find out about what he had said earlier","As though quickly trying to move on from the topic, Mo just directed them, “The two of you would need to strengthen yourselves first. Ideally, be strong enough to completely resist my Black Ink Strength. Mo Na Ye, guide them to the Black Ink Pool to train.”","Mo Na Ye, having sensed Mo was usually sharp in his tone, immediately responded. “Yes, Holy One.”","He turned around and led the children out of the thatched house.","The twins looked back, a little reluctant to leave, since they wanted to know more about what had been said. However, from how Mo Na Ye was urging them to move, they knew better than to remain.","Once he made sure they were a distance away, Mo immediately spat out something akin to blood. He could not help but scoff, “A warning, huh?”","...","Currently, in this settlement, besides Mo, Mo Na Ye was basically the one in command. He was highly respected by everyone in the Black Ink Clan. This was not respect that stemmed from just how strong he was. That did play apart, as it was their instinct to do so. However, a large portion of how he was so respected was his intellect and kindness to his fellow Clansmen regardless of how weak or strong they were.","This was definitely unimaginable before he died. But, this was how he was right now.","Such a scene was proven by the excited waving he received from passersby. In the past, they would have been shaking in fear at a mere sight of him.","Waving? That would have been impossible. Grovelling or bowing was the most common sight when a Royal Lord met with beings much weaker than them.","In fact, the clansmen’s welcome extended even to the twins, which was quite shocking to them. After all, it was the Humans who had pushed their kind back to this desolate place. They would have at least expected some hostility from the other party, but that did not seem to be the case. At most, it was fear. Hostility did not seem to exist between them.","As the twins walked behind Mo Na Ye, he asked them. “Did this sight shock the two of you? Were you expecting something else?”","Both children nodded, which sparked Mo Na Ye to grin. “It was definitely not like this in the past. For some reason, our personalities seem to have changed over time. When I think back on it, all that hatred for the living and love for violence seemed to have been truly misplaced.”","Mo Na Ye said with a hint of pride. “Well, I’m not saying that we do not have such inclinations, but they seemed to have lessened by a lot. Now, everyone has basically become something akin to family, unlike before.”","“Why is that the case?” Yang Ji, curious, could not help but ask.","“The Holy One had said that this is due to his powers. The blessings and happiness in your world is somehow tied to how potent his Black Ink Strength is. When there are large wars, mayhem and grief, his Black Ink Strength would become so strong it would become uncontrollable. That’s why the Holy One does not act out as rashly as before...”","Mo Na Ye continued to explain how Mo’s Source had been divided into 3,000 pieces, that each piece had different levels of corruption from Black Ink Strength. The current Mo that they had just met, was one of the four surviving Source pieces. The rest had been absorbed by the remaining three – with Little Eleven being an outlier.","It was unfortunate that the remaining two hostile Source pieces had completely lost themselves to Black Ink Strength, and were now basically acting on instinct.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu naturally did not take Mo Na Ye’s words as facts. After all, they were still unaware of the whole situation. Nevertheless, Yang Xu was well acquainted with the concept of ‘in every lie, there is some semblance of truth’ from Mother Ru Meng. As for Yang Ji, he just plainly did not trust them.","Soon, the three reached another mountain top, which was in the form of a volcano. What was supposed to be lava, was filled with an extremely thick layer of Black Ink Strength Fluid. In fact, from what they could see, this seemed to be a reservoir for Black Ink Strength Fluid.","Mo Na Ye advised them, “The Holy One has instructed me to just oversee you two, and pull your two back to the shore if necessary. Other than that, you are free to dive as deep as you want.”","“What do you think?” Yang Xu asked Yang Ji through her Divine Sense.","“Not like we can run away with him overseeing us. We might as well just train for now.” Yang Ji replied also using his Divine Sense while giving a nod to Mo Na Ye.","“I’ll go in first.” Yang Ji said, as he stepped forward and soaked his feet inside.","Immediately, he could be seen frozen in place, not moving an inch. There was a grimace on his face, and some beads of sweat. His body could be seen to tense up, as his breathing quickened.","Yang Xu was on standby, in case anything were to happen.","Fortunately, it was a false alarm as Yang Ji could be seen slowly moving forward another step before stopping again.","Yang Xu stared at her Brother for a bit before calling out to him. “Are you okay?”","There was no immediate response. It took about a minute or so before he responded. “Yeah. I’m quickly getting used to this. You should come in too.”","Following him, Yang Xu also started to dip her feet inside. Immediately, a rush of emotions hit her. Instead of the images and memories like before, these were pure emotions that seemed to manifest inside of her and outside of her at the same time.","She wanted to scream but she could feel her muscles all tensed up, no longer under her control. She could not tell what facial expression she was making, but it certainly was something she could not consciously control.","A second felt like an hour, and a minute felt like an eternity.","Screams of pain and shrieks of fear could be heard, if not felt directly.","The only difference was that she was still somewhat aware of her surroundings. It was a strange feeling, as she was bordering between lucidity and confusion. For some reason, when she saw her Brother seemingly take another step forward, she started to panic.","Once a true negative emotion started to well up from within her, it felt as if the dam had broken through and a flood of something corrupting her had gotten in.","Fortunately, before that had happened, she heard a familiar voice, “Hey, are you okay?”","Soon, a pair of warm hands were tightly embracing her shoulders, giving her the warmth to wake up from this nightmare.","“Huh?” When Yang Xu regained consciousness, she immediately saw her Brother’s panicked expression. This made her heart feel warm and those negative feelings dissipated into nothingness.","“What an interesting pair.” Mo Na Ye could not help but mutter at the sight of these two."]},{"number":6028,"title":"Chapter 6028, Insane Progress","paragraphs":["Chapter 6028, Insane Progress","Author: Silavin","It should be said that even for those of the Black Ink Clan, Black Ink Strength Fluid was too potent for those that were too weak. One had to be a Feudal Lord and above to remain completely unaffected by this potent Black Ink Strength Fluid.","Nevertheless, ‘Human’ children, who were below the Seventh Order, were able to withstand Black Ink Strength Fluid to this degree. Furthermore, their resistance was improving at a visible rate. This was no longer about Talent. These two were practically monstrosities, oddities that the world did not seem to have accounted for.","When Mo Na Ye thought of how these two were the product of his greatest nemesis, oddly, he felt satisfied.","Still, he had to admit, the pace at which they were getting used to this concentrated Black Ink Strength was shocking. In less than an hour, they were fine with their waist soaked in the fluid.","From an outsider’s perspective, what they did seemed easy and fast. However, they were always pushing themselves to the point where time was just a concept for them. In fact, the only reason why they could push so fast was because the warmth of each other’s touch reminded them that they were not alone.","For Yang Ji, he admits that he felt inferior when compared to his Father, who had accomplished so many great feats. He naturally doubts if he would ever measure up to his Father. Even his Little Sister, he knew he was not as brilliant as her. Yet, could he ever bring himself to hate them? Could he truly blame them for what he lacked?","When he did not move forward and got devoured by such emotions, it would be his Sister’s tug that reminded him that they were still progressing. That they still have a long journey ahead of them.","As for Yang Xu, her worries were different from her Brother’s. She was worried that she would get left behind. In terms of talent, she knew that her Brother got her beat. She would have to work harder to catch up with him. She was also worried he would leave her eventually once they grew older and he had fallen for someone else.","When she got stuck with such worries, her Brother’s warmth reminded her of how he was always by her side. When he tugged, she had to move forward to keep up,","Maybe it was just their own experience, but there was a tendency for Black Ink Strength to enforce feelings of isolation, then hatred and violence. Their own presence helped each other get over the feeling of isolation. If one had someone else in this world, who truly loved them, could they truly hate this world?","In fact, maybe due to their young age, and lack of experience, those dark moments were few. Hardship, everyone had gone through them but they were truly blessed children of Heaven. They were born to an amazing Family, with practically a golden spoon in their mouth. They had no right to complain about their place in life, and knew better.","Those rush of negative emotions, lessened over time. Those screams of agony and voices of hatred, they were accepted and ignored. Each step was a new and more intense wave of such emotions. However, over time, they got used to it.","In fact, over time, they grew ever more grateful for what they have.","Eventually, they managed to get deep enough till their neck. At this point, something surprising happened.","WIthout waiting for them to go any deeper, Mo Na Ye had flown right above them. Due to the twins completely concentrating on resisting Black Ink Strength, his sudden physical touch made them jump.","Nevertheless, Mo Na Ye quickly pulled them out and returned back to shore.","At this point, the twins were confused as to what was happening. For all that they knew, everything had been going well. Just a bit more and they would have been completely immersed inside Black Ink Strength.","It was Mo Na Ye’s next words that made them reflect, “Why did you two rush in so quickly? Do you two think you will be able to handle it if Black Ink Strength Fluid enters your orifices? Though I said that you can dive as deep as you want, you have to condition yourselves more before that.”","In fact, Mo Na Ye had to admit that he was the one who had made a mistake. He had not expected the twins to have actually gone so deep on their first day. He had anticipated them to reach that depth in a few months, not in a single day!","At a certain point, other than being happy that they were progressing so quickly, he got worried. These two have not even used their Qi to protect themselves. They had allowed the Black Ink Strength to directly make contact with them. Even if they have cultivation equivalent to the Dao Source Realm and did not need to breathe, there was no guarantee that the Black Ink Strength Fluid would not enter their lips.","Black Ink Strength inside ones’ body would manifest differently. It would be far more potent. Worse, once inside the body, it would be impossible to take out. The twins would have to wait until their natural bodily functions flushed the material out. At that point, if they could not resist it, there was nothing he could do.","“Then, what are we supposed to do? We’ve already gotten that far.” Yang Ji asked. Technically, he and his Sister knew the answer but hoped it would not come to it.","“We don’t have much of a choice. At this point, you have to get used to digesting Black Ink Strength to proceed.” Mo Na Ye answered, which made the twins squeamish."]},{"number":6029,"title":"Chapter 6029: Instinctual Fear and Disgust","paragraphs":["“Do we really need to?” At this point, Yang Xu looked at her Brother, as though asking for help. Her big round eyes were now the sizes of plates as though begging to be excused.","Yang Ji had a multitude of curses in his mind, curses that were not vulgarities of course. He put out a strong front and calmly gave Mo Na Ye a response. “I’ll take it first. If anything happens, my Sister will be able to help me.”","Mo Na Ye gave a solemn nod. If Yang Ji had not proposed this, he would have. After all, unlike Black Ink Strength being stuck on them externally, he could not really do much if it was stuck inside their bodies. The best way to resolve it was definitely Purifying Light, something only the twins could unleash.","Yang Ji took a deep breath and moved back to the pool. This time, he did not let his feet touch the shore. He bent down and took two handfuls of Black Ink Strength Fluid.","Due to his newfound resistance, he did not feel anything strange, even when in contact with Black Ink Strength Fluid. He found it a little ironic, [Damn it. I can’t even feel anything at this point yet I have to push myself to consume you...]","When Yang Ji brought it to his face, he instinctively took a sniff. Fortunately, the liquid did not smell bad. It was just incredibly viscous, like slime. It was also cool to the touch.","Strangely, the more he thought about it, the more he realised they should not exactly be disgusted by it. After all, he and his Sister both had food personally made by Mother Shan Qing Luo. It was not an exaggeration to say that the experience itself was equivalent to a Tribulation.","This made him even more fearful. After all, that would mean this disgust and fear was without reason. When that happens, it would have to be attributed to his instincts.","At his cultivation level, which was equivalent to the Dao Source Realm, he could basically always trust his instincts. If he felt such unease, that would mean this act of consuming Black Ink Strength Fluid was dangerous to him.","Thankfully, his Sister was here. He was confident she would be able to save him if anything happened. Thus, he placed his faith in her and took a big gulp.","“Wait! Why are you taking in so much at once!?” Yang Xu chided him. If anything, they knew that they should start slow. [Why are you being so reckless!?]","Yang Ji’s face immediately had a grimace. However, at this point, he felt his mouth could no longer form words. Thus, he just forced out a smile and gave a thumbs up.","Soon enough, his body seemed to have lost strength and he fell limp.","Thankfully, Mo Na Ye was quick to act. He had already placed his arm under Yang Ji’s chest, and caught him. He pulled Yang Ji further away from the shore and let him rest.","RIght now, there was essentially nothing he could do for him. This was going to be an internal battle for Yang Ji. All he could do was to stand by the child’s side and ask for Yang Xu’s help if needed. But, was that even necessary?","Yang Xu was quick to rush to Yang Ji’s side. She clasped his hand with both of hers and sat cross-legged. She immediately went on to use her Qi and Divine Sense to check on his condition.","Inside, she found that Black Ink Strength had already started flowing inside his Meridians. It was being resisted by his Qi, but any contact made was met with brutal damage.","[If this continues his Meridians are going to be crippled!] Yang Xu worriedly screamed in her heart and tried to use her Qi to help him.","However, that was when Mo Na Ye spoke up, “What are you doing? Don’t panic. I would not have said anything if you are just going to monitor his condition. But, interfering with this process using Qi? Are you trying to make his condition worse?”","Yang Xu immediately stopped. Her hands were frozen. She turned to Mo Na Ye, with an expression that questioned what she should do now.","“Not to worry. Just wait and see for now. If it gets too dire, I’ll tell you. Use Purifying Light on him if that happens. Also, make sure that when you use Purifying Light, you only focus it on him. Else, this whole mountain might have another crater.” Mo Na Ye tried to calm her down by slowly instructing each step. It would be no joke if there was an explosion of purifying light. Since they were by a mountain, an explosion here would literally take out the ground underneath them, and cause the whole pool to spill downstream. He did not even want to consider the devastation that would cause if the Holy One does not act to prevent the worst from happening.","As for Yang Ji, he was oblivious to what was happening around him. The pain he was experiencing had basically overcomed all other sensations. He could feel his blood vessels screaming as they got torn and rebuilt over and over again. Even his Meridians were being torn and healed each second.","He was only able to keep this up due to his extremely unique and pure Phoenix Bloodline. If not for this, he would have most likely been overwhelmed by the Black Ink Strength.","Still, the rampaging Black Ink Strength was unyielding. In fact, even when his Qi was resisting the Black Ink Strength, and their tussle injured him, Yang Ji could feel the Black Ink Strength in his body not decreasing!"]},{"number":6030,"title":"Chapter 6030: Am I Going To Turn Into A Black Ink Disciple?","paragraphs":["[What is going on? Why is it not weakening at all!?] Yang Ji cursed as he sought to find a way to resist the Black Ink Strength with all his might.","Unfortunately, any resistance was met with agonising pain. His teeth were already clenched so hard that his jargulars were protruding, and only muffled roars could be heard. Yet, with all this sacrifice, nothing was being yielded.","Yang Ji could feel his body breaking down, but he did not know what else to do. The more he tried to force the Black Ink Strength out, the more he tried to repel it, or hinder it, the worse his situation got.","At this moment, he was ready to tap out. To ask his Sister to save him. However, he soon thought of a possibility. An insane one, which he would never dare try. One he could only do because he had complete faith that no matter what happens, Yang Xu would be able to save him.","With whatever remained of his consciousness, he sent Yang Xu a message through his Divine Sense.","When the girl first heard of it, she immediately wanted to slap her Brother to his senses. However, unable to bear harming him, worse, unable to bear causing the situation to be worse, she relented to his idea.","Still, she did not plan to stand by idly while he was going to do something so reckless. Yang Xu immediately turned to Mo Na Ye and said. “Take us away, where Purifying Light would not cause much harm. I believe you are able to move the environment, right?”","Mo Na Ye could tell that Yang Xu requested this not due to panic, but rational thought. So, he agreed and stated, “That is certainly the best course of action. But, I do not wish to claim credit for providing assistance I cannot do. It is not me that is capable of moving the terrain, but the Holy One.”","Yang Xu wanted to snap back, as if that was important. However, seeing how Mo Na Ye immediately took out what seemed to be a small Black Ink Clansman’s house, she just turned back to focus on her Brother.","It only took a moment before the ground beneath them started to tremble, and Mo Na Ye kept the Black Ink Nest.","In fact, trembling might be too strong a word to describe what the ground was doing. A shake was more apt. The ground beneath them seemed to have gently disconnected from the rest of the mountain, as it floated higher up into the boundless sky.","Once it was high enough, Mo Na Ye said, “This is far enough for you to do whatever you want without any restraints.”","Naturally, Mo Na Ye was under the assumption that Yang Xu would already be using Purifying Light on Yang Ji. So, what she did next confused him.","Yang Xu took out an Array Plate from her Space Ring and injected some Qi into it. Using her Divine Sense to direct the Array Plate, it activated to form a small protective Array around her and her Brother.","Once the Array had settled, that was the thing that Mo Na Ye was confused about. Yang Xu did nothing but wait and looked at her Brother.","“It’s up. You can do what you wish. I’ll make sure you are safe.” Yang Xu grabbed onto Yang Ji’s hand with both of hers. Between their palms were two already prepared Blue and Yellow Crystals. It was only once everything was ready that she spoke using her Divine Sense.","“Here goes nothing...” Yang Ji tried to force out a smile, but he initially failed to do so. It was only after a moment where his facial expression changed to reflect what he wanted to show.","The big gamble he wanted to take was letting the Black Ink Strength course through his entire body with absolutely no resistance.","Naturally, he would not have done this without a reason.","After resisting the Black Ink Strength inside of him for so long, and seeing no result was being yielded, he almost saw no possibility in them overcoming this trial. This was not a matter of not trying hard enough. It was truly impossible for him to overcome this trial by resisting Black Ink Strength.","The other option was to push the Black Ink Strength out of his system. However, if resistance was already this hard, it would be unimaginable for them to remove the Black Ink Strength from their system with their own strength. In fact, the easier option to remove Black Ink Strength from their body was to use Purifying Light.","However, the main goal of this trial was to increase resistance against Black Ink Strength, whereby it would not be able to affect them any longer. Using Purifying Light would not help them in this regard.","Now, the last thing Yang Ji believed he could do was actually let the Black Ink Strength course through him without resisting.","This decision was not without its own consequences. Still, Yang Ji believes it was better for him to go through this first than have Yang Xu blindly go through this.","Once Yang Ji’s Qi stopped resisting, the Black Ink Strength was quick to immediately rush through all paths. They travelled through his Meridians and blood vessels, quickly reaching his heart and Dantian.","When it reached his heart, Yang Ji could feel his emotions shifting. His emotions stirred in the primal sense, whereby he had no logical control over them. Unaccountable hatred, unaccountable violence, unaccountable jealousy... such emotions rushed through him. At this point, the feeling was not one of corruption. It felt as though these feelings were always there, just hidden and brought up.","The interesting thing was when the Black Ink Strength reached his Dantian. Yang Ji initially expected his Dantian to be corrupted, like what happened to Black Ink Disciples.","Black Ink Disciples were Humans that were corrupted by Black Ink Strength. It was said that they would become stronger after ‘accepting’ Black Ink Strength, able to surpass the limit of the Open Heaven Realm.","Heaven was fair though. There was still a cost to this power. Their bodies would deform, and they were akin to slaves to the Black Ink Clan.","Once they became Black Ink Disciples, it was said that they could only wield Black Ink Strength and not Qi.","For Yang Ji, he naturally expected himself to turn into a Black Ink Disciple, and have his Qi corrupted and replaced by Black Ink Strength. However, that did not happen. Instead, the Black Ink Strength seems to concentrate in his Dantain, as another sphere. It did not try to interact with the revolving Qi in his Dantian. In fact, it seemed to be actively avoiding making contact.","This strange phenomenon continued, and all the Black Ink Strength circulating in his body, even his heart, all ended up in his Dantian and settled there..."]},{"number":6031,"title":"Chapter 6031: Doubt","paragraphs":["[What’s going on?] Both Yang Ji and Yang Xu questioned what was happening. Although Yang Xu did not explore Yang Ji’s Dantian, she could still sense the Black Ink Strength in his body all being directed there.","She was already prepared to unleash a whole blast of Purifying Light, only to see that the situation had settled.","The one most perplexed by this was naturally none other than Yang Ji. He was the one who could keenly feel the changes in his body. If he were to describe it, it was as though all the Black Ink Strength wanted to do was to settle in his Dantian. It only got aggressive because Yang Ji was intentionally making it hard to reach its desired destination.","Once it found its ‘home’, the Black Ink Strength seemed to become inert. It was as though it did not want to move.","Curious, Yang Ji began to experiment with it. He circulated and manipulated his Qi to start bombarding the balled up clump of Black Ink Strength, but it did nothing. He tried to use his Qi, and focused it to form a sharp edge, to slice the ball apart. However, all that happened was the Black Ink Strength split and reformed back to its original shape.","[What the...] Yang Ji was even more confused as to why this was happening. [It doesn’t seem like it has a mind of its own. It also does not react to my Qi...]","Yang Ji could sense that this thing in his body would not harm him. However, having it there was unnerving, since he did not know what would happen if he left it unattended.","[Okay. Let’s try to remove it now. I can continue experimenting whenever I want to if I can find a way to expel it from my body.] Yang Ji concluded and tried to use his Qi to form hands to try and knead the ball of Black Ink Strength. Unfortunately, even though it was like a dough-like substance, it would always return back to its original form... which was far too big for it to fit through his Meridians.","[Are you serious!?] Yang Ji cursed in his heart and tried even more methods. He tried to slice it into smaller bits, pinch a bit off, roll it and etc. Unfortunately, none of these worked. It felt as if the Black Ink Strength was going to be stuck there.","After each failed attempt, Yang Ji became ever more frustrated. He even contemplated asking his Sister to use Purifying Light on him.","However, the idea of failure to overcome this made him reluctant to do so.","That was when his Sister’s voice entered this mind, “Brother, is everything okay?”","Even with his pride, Yang Ji did not wish to hide anything from her. First, to show that everything was fine, he opened his eyes, only to meet hers. They were slightly red, maybe signs of her tearing up. Regardless, Yang Ji did not find it appropriate to bring it up and just sat up before telling her what had happened.","After recounting what Yang Ji had tried, Yang Xu was curious as she turned her head to Mo Na Ye and asked, “What’s going on? Why is it stuck inside of him?”","Mo Na Ye was also perplexed by this. It was well known that Black Ink Strength would corrupt living beings. In fact, even non-living objects could get corrupted by Black Ink Strength. If anything, all that was on the other side of the Profound Source Gate could get corrupted by Black Ink Strength. This was the first time someone was not getting corrupted by it.","Mo Na Ye could only speculate the reason, without much basis for it. “This is something that even I cannot provide an answer for. But, I might have some guesses of my own. Maybe it has something to do with how you two are children of Yang Kai, someone who has surpassed the known limits of this world?”","Mo Na Ye paused for a bit and continued to try and further deduce the reason, “Both of you, though affected by Black Ink Strength, cannot be truly corrupted by it. Maybe, just like how the Principles of this world are vastly different from yours, your bodies operate with different Principles?”","“But, we still get affected by Black Ink Strength, and feel its effects.” Yang Ji stated, recalling how when the Black Ink Strength reached his heart, he felt a surge of dark emotions.","“You might feel it, but it has never corrupted you, right? I don’t exactly know what you /N_o_v_e_l_i_g_h_t/ have experienced, but from how I see it, whatever you’ve experienced is fleeting. If I were to give an analogy, it is like the alcohol I once drank with your Father. I can keep it in my mouth, but the taste of it would eventually weaken, so I would need another cup.” Mo Na Ye said his true feelings as an onlooker. To him, it was shocking enough for two kids, who had not even reached the Open Heaven Realm, to be dealing with Black Ink Strength directly. Furthermore, it was not normal Black Ink Strength, but Black Ink Strength Fluid, which was of an even more concentrated form.","This whole topic made Yang Ji even more curious about something more fundamental. Something he had never doubted before. No, something he had thought he already understood, “If that’s the case, what is Black Ink Strength supposed to be?”","In fact, for a large part of this adventure of theirs, even for Yang Kai and the 3,000 Worlds, what did they truly understand about Black Ink Strength? How was this world related to theirs and why did the Profound Source Gate exist?","There were so many unanswered questions which he now had, questions which he had just assumed he had answers to, since others had told him about it.","So now, with this one doubt, a myriad of questions, which might overturn their whole understanding of Mo and everything they knew, had been unleashed."]},{"number":6032,"title":"Chapter 6032: How To Control Black Ink Strength?","paragraphs":["Yang Xu, more concerned about her Brother’s well-being, quickly urged him, “That isn’t important right now. We need to get it out of you.”","Yang Ji quickly shook his head to refute her. “No, this is the perfect opportunity to test things out. If not me, then it would be you.” Yang Ji gently tapped on her hand to comfort her as he continued, “Besides, what I said earlier still stands. I don’t think I’ll get corrupted by it, so it is fine to leave it in my Dantian for now. The most pressing issue is to find out its true origins.”","Yang Ji turned his head towards Mo Na Ye, expecting him to already have an answer. However, even Mo Na Ye was pondering over this, with uncertainty in his eyes.","In fact, the Black Ink Clan had never really questioned much about their source of strength, their source of birth. After all, they all just regarded this as the substance created by the Holy One. Thus, it was a blessing for them, and a curse for the others that went against them. It gave them life, gave them power, and helped them communicate.","Was there another substance like this in the world on the other side of the Profound Source Gate?","When Mo Na Ye actually considered it, Black Ink Strength really seemed like a miraculous power. Though he produced it overtime, his was definitely not as potent as that of the Holy One. In fact, only the Holy One could create Innate Royal Lords directly, even Black Ink Giant Spirit Gods.","So far, Mo Na Ye had only thought of the Holy One’s Black Ink Strength as something unique, and unparalleled in power. He had never questioned its existence. So, when Yang Ji asked him this question, he was truly stumped. He did not know how to answer it.","While he was contemplating, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were both looking at him, questioningly. It made things awkward for him, and Mo Na Ye felt pressured to at least say something. Nevertheless, he did not hide how he too was uncertain. “Black Ink Strength is the blessing from the Holy One. We of the Black Ink Clan are beings of it. That is all that we know about it. We have never really questioned it, since questioning it might seem as though we are questioning the Holy One’s blessing.”","Yang Ji immediately sent Yang Xu a message through his Divine Sense, “That just means you know nothing as well!”","Though both twins felt the same, they did not show it on their faces. After all, Mo Na Ye could be considered their Senior. Even if he was their Father’s enemy in the past, this Black Ink Clansman still showed immense respect for their Father. The least they could do was help him save some face at moments like these.","Yang Ji just nodded his head and continued to ask, “In that case, how do you control Black Ink Strength?”","Yang Ji figured if he could not uncover the truth about Black Ink Strength, he might as well try to control the Black Ink Strength clumped up ball inside of him for now. At the very least, be able to get it out of him at will – if possible.","Mo Na Ye lifted his right hand, and Black Ink Strength flowed out of it, encasing his hand as though it was in flowing flames. Soon, he applied more force and the Black Ink Strength flame suddenly erupted to be hundreds of metres high, causing even Yang Ji and Yang Xu to shield themselves.","Thankfully, there was still the Array surrounding the children. So, the impact was not really felt.","Mo Na Ye, having seemingly known no harm would be brought to them, just explained, “I just willed it as such and the Black Ink Strength within me just moves as I willed it to. There is nothing really complicated about it.”","“Then, what about Territory Lords, what difference does their cultivation realm bring? Also, why are Royal Lords stronger than Territory Lords?” Yang Ji expressed his question very quickly after lowering his arm.","“The potency of our Black Ink Strength is certainly one main difference. Our ability to control Black Ink Strength is also different.” Mo Na Ye thought back on the difference between when he was a Territory Lord and a Royal Lord.","“There must be more to it, no? We Humans need to circulate our Qi out of our Dantian to actually make use of the Qi stored inside of us. What about you Black Ink Clansmen?” Yang Xu could not help but ask. Even though she was worried about her Brother, when he got like this, she knew he would be too stubborn to change his mind. Thus, she could only join in and try to help him quickly solve this mystery.","“We too have veins in our body that had black blood flowing in them. Same with meridians and a Dantian. In this regard, we are not too different from you Humans. In terms of utilising Black Ink Strength, I do not believe it is that different from how your kind does it with Qi. Just let it flow out of your body and it can be used.” Mo Ne Ye stated as matter-of-factly.","That statement was not wrong, since Humans too could manipulate their Qi at will once they reached a high enough cultivation realm. However, Humans needed to practise using cultivation techniques first before they could reach such a stage. It was only once they truly got familiar with their Qi and got familiar with how to control it, that it would move as they willed it to. This seemed completely different from how the Black Ink Clansmen did it, in which they seem capable of manipulating Black Ink Strength at birth.","Proof of this was how the Black Ink Clan had Innate Territory Lords and Innate Royal Lords basically knew how to control Black Ink Strength at birth. Meanwhile, Humans need to learn and improve step by step. Even Divine Beasts needed time to grow and learn how to use their Bloodline.","After hearing everything, Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt as ◈ Nоvеlіgһт ◈ (Continue reading) though they were at an impasse. If Black Ink Strength was only something a Black Ink Clansmen could manipulate, then nothing else could be done.","However, when they seemed about to give up, Mo Na Ye added, “Now, I do wonder what it is like for Black Ink Disciples. They can grow stronger with Black Ink Strength, just like Acquired Royal Lords...”","Silavin: Damn it. This is taking too long. I have so much I want to write but, due to word constraints, I’m cutting it short and splitting it into so many chapters! Argh! This is frustrating. I need to really find the time to sit down and write longer chapters so that we can move on to more exciting parts instead of lore."]},{"number":6033,"title":"Chapter 6033: My Black Ink Nest","paragraphs":["[Black Ink Disciples!] Both Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at each other. They had obviously forgotten about the key existence of those that had fully gotten corrupted by Black Ink Strength.","Still, from what they knew, those that had turned into Black Ink Disciples were doomed. From what their Father and their tutors had said, Black Ink Disciples could no longer be regarded as the same people as when they were ‘alive’. One could even call them moving corpses.","Naturally, what they had heard most about was their Father’s heroic action to end a Ninth-Order Black Ink Disciple when he was only in the Seventh-Order. Apparently, it was the first one of its kind, and was a testament to the potential of Black Ink Strength.","Mo Na Ye continued, “One thing I know for certain is that for Black Ink Strength, the source is the Master and those beneath are slaves. The Holy One is the one who blessed us, so he is our Master. As for Black Ink Disciples, we are the ones who blessed them so we are the Masters.”","Yang Ji gave a nod, and asked Yang Xu, “Don’t you think it is strange?”","Yang Xu tilted her head, not sure what her Brother was referring to.","“How is it that even after getting corrupted, Black Ink Disciples are still as capable as when they were ‘alive’? Rather than get corrupted, it is more like they get possessed, no?” Yang Ji stated.","Yang Xu nodded and stated something she recalled, “They seem to still possess their mastery of certain Daos. I recall Father saying how some of them could still manage to fix up Arrays at one point.”","Mo Na Ye gave a firm nod as he recalled those times as well. “They were certainly useful. Their potential has certainly been wasted for countless years because my people are too foolish in their approach in handling them.”","Mo Na Ye soon thought back on one issue, “But, it was a problem that you Human’s Purifying Light could turn them back to your side. Granted, they must be Black Ink Disciples that had not broken ✧ NоvеIight ✧ (Original source) through their cultivation realm. Else, they would be reduced to dust.”","“If they can have breakthroughs, that must mean they cultivate, right? How do they normally cultivate?” Yang Ji immediately went to the crux of the issue.","“They cultivate inside a Royal Lord Black Ink Nest. That’s the only way they are able to make a breakthrough.” Mo Na Ye recalled what happened in the past and explained.","“Oh?” Yang Ji and Yang Xu both exclaimed, and Yang Ji was the first to ask, “Do you have a Royal Lord Black Ink Nest we could use?”","“Erm...” Mo Na Ye hesitated for a moment and nodded.","“Ah! Then let’s go!” Yang Ji immediately stood up and helped his Sister to get up. He was so confident that he also quickly took down the Array surrounding them.","Sensing how his Sister was still worried with her hand tightly clenching around his, he gave her a comforting pat on the back of her hand.","Mo Na Ye sighed, and ‘led’ the way. He took out the miniature Black Ink Nest again, and the whole platform started to tremble.","Before it started to really move, Mo Na Ye prefaced with this, “You best not destroy anything there, understand.”","Yang Xu was the first to respond, “Of course.”","Though she said that, she was already prepared to do anything if her Brother was in any danger.","Mo Na Ye could feel his heartbeat quicken as he heard those words. It certainly did not sound as reassuring as he had hoped. In fact, it might have been better if he had not asked.","Still, the ride was quick and they reached soon enough.","It was on another side of the mountain, somewhere more tranquil. The flora around this side was more dense, with multiple fields. There were also occasional trees that stood out, making this place ever more serene. In terms of water, a small stream flowed down from the top. In terms of houses, there was a certain lack of them as only a few Black Ink Nests could be seen. However, there was one that stood out from the rest. Or more, like, there was a pair that stood out more than the rest.","This pair of Black Ink Nest were not of equal stature. One was obviously far bigger than the other, and more intricate. Even so, they were placed together so closely that it was unmistakable that this was its intent. Furthermore, the area around was fenced up, showcasing how private those that live here must be.","Still, only those perceptive enough would take note of the undertone of this. Yang Ji was sadly not one of them. Instead, it was his Sister who noticed, and she even had a grin on her face.","Yang Ji just thought that they placed those two Black Ink Nests really close.","Mo Na Ye naturally noticed Yang Xu’s reaction and just kept silent.","The platform got close to the pair of houses and just stopped there.","“Alright, we are here.” Mo Na Ye declared in a softer tone.","“En.” Yang Ji just gave a nod, while Yang Xu giggled a little.","Yang Xu helped Yang Ji fly down, not wanting him to exert too much with the Black Ink Strength still inside his body. As for Yang Ji, though he felt this was unnecessary, he still allowed her to do it. After all, receiving care from those concerned was one way to alleviate those feelings.","Mo Na Ye naturally led them to the bigger Black Ink Nest.","It was only once inside, and once he closed the entrance, that he started speaking. “This is my house. It is a Royal Lord Black Ink Nest. Probably the only one that is usable for you two.”","He was certainly not lying. Though there were other Royal Lords, they certainly would not allow Humans to enter their abode, which could also be considered their lifeline. One was their dislike of the other race, and the other was the risk of Purifying Light being released. Furthermore, these Royal Lords typically had tasks to do and were not that easily contactable.","The twins just gave a nod of acknowledgement to his words, as they busily looked around.","This Black Ink Nest was certainly much bigger than the others. However, it was not that big in Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s eyes. Though, to be fair, they had mostly lived their life in something akin to a palace.","There were multiple rooms inside, with the typical furniture in each room. There was the typical kitchen, living room, bedroom, storeroom, and cultivation room. There were also a few other rooms, which they did not really know the purpose of. However, sensing how uneasy Mo Na Ye was feeling, they did not want to probe too much.","The rooms were all quite neat and tidy, as though someone had specifically set out to clean the place. This gave Yang Ji a good impression of Mo Na Ye, while Yang Xu had other thoughts.","Mo Na Ye, not wanting the kids to overstay their welcome, quickly directed them to the cultivation room. “You can try and cultivate using that room. So, do stop wandering about.”","Yang Ji, the most eager, was the first to rush into the cultivation room. As for Yang Xu, she just followed with their hands tightly clasped together. Though, she did not forget to give Mo Na Ye a thumbs up before closing the cultivation room door.","Mo Na Ye sighed at the sight of them. He wanted to leave them for now, but could not do so since he was tasked to take care of them..."]},{"number":6034,"title":"Chapter 6034: Black Ink Space","paragraphs":["“Hey, why did you close the door? We need him in here” Yang Ji turned around to ask once he heard a *thud* behind him.","“If he’s in here, then he would stop whatever we do if it risks destroying his home.” Yang Xu said as she already took out the Array Plate and started setting up the Array around them.","“He would still be helpful if we have any questions.” Yang Ji shrugged and just allowed her to continue, without bothering to open the door.","“Maybe.” Yang Xu replied, thinking back on how most questions they had were still left unanswered. She did not believe Mo Na Ye was hiding anything from them, rather, it was the case where he truly did not know.","Yang Xu was not the only one that felt that way, Yang Ji was the same. So, they just continued to explore the cultivation room with interest.","Except for the few large indents on the walls, big enough to fit a child, there was not much else in the room. The most prominent structure was the protrusion in the middle. If the twins were to describe it, they would say that it was akin to a caldron with its lower half completely attached to the floor.","“I think this is the thing.” Yang Ji pointed to the ‘caldron’ and added, “I remember Father saying that the Black Ink Clan had something, where they pour in resources to create more of their kind. But, since he calls this the cultivation room, and seeing how they lack natural resources here, I guess they don’t need materials to cultivate?”","“Why not just try interacting with it while you try and cultivate?” Yang Xu suggested.","Yang Ji gave a nod and moved directly in front of the ‘caldron’. He sat down cross-legged and started to pour his Divine Sense into it.","However, once he did, it felt as if his Soul was taken away from his body.","By the time he regained his bearing, he was already in another space. It was dark, but not as eerie as he had expected. In fact, he felt the presence of others, but did not see them.","[So, this is what they call Black Ink Space?] Yang Ji looked around to find if there was anything else of interest here. However, there was really nothing else here. It was just an empty space that seemed to be in the shape of a sphere.","The Black Ink Space was an independent space which Black Ink Nests could connect to. Each Black Ink Nest had its own space, and each Black Ink Nest were connected to one another through their parent nest. They were so connected that Yang Ji could feel the presence of others, in their own space, without them even entering his space.","Naturally, this was amazing for instant communications that crossed the boundaries of Space. Furthermore, since each Black Ink Nest had their own space, there was a certain level of privacy for their conversations.","Yang Ji wondered for a moment on what to do next, but it did not take too long until he elicited the notice of someone.","“You’re finally here.” A familiar voice rang out, as one part of the surrounding walls condensed to form a small figure.","“Mo?” Yang Ji asked, a little taken aback. After all, the form Mo chose to take was completely identical to his Uncle Eleven.","The ‘little boy’ gave a nod to Yang Ji and he waved his hand.","Immediately, the floor had changed. The flat ground formed two bumps, which soon formed into mats.","Mo waved his hand to indicate Yang Ji to sit, as he took his own.","Yang Ji nodded obediently and sat down cross-legged. He wanted to open his mouth but Mo stuck his hand out first and addressed his concerns. “No need to ask again. I already know what you are curious about. But, I cannot answer everything right now. For now, just focus on your main goal. Focus on how to control the Black Ink Strength within you.”","“Close your eyes.”","Yang Ji still wanted to ask more, but seeing how Mo was moving on to instructing already, he had no choice but to just follow along. He closed his eyes and started to sense himself.","Strangely, even when his Soul was in this Black Ink Space, he could still feel the Black Ink Strength within his body. Typically, when one’s Soul was temporarily outside of one’s body, they would be in a vulnerable state. So, it was strange how he could not feel his actual body but could feel the Black Ink Strength inside of him.","Mo soon started to explain, “Black Ink Strength... is my or rather our entire existence. We are the embodiments of its existence. It is just as much a part of us as we are a part of it.”","There was a melancholic look in his eyes as he said that. Nevertheless, Yang Ji did not notice since his eyes were closed and he was focusing on the Black Ink Strength within him, waiting for the next set of instructions.","“To control Black Ink Strength is to be a part of it, and for it to be a part of you. This need not mean corrupting yourself to it. Rather, it is to claim a part of it as your own.” Mo said as his hand widened and Yang Ji immediately felt the Black Ink Strength within him started to squirm. Just like Mo’s hand, the Black Ink Strength inside of Yang Ji also expanded out.","“This portion of Black Ink Strength could still be considered a part of me. It not having an effect on you is a surprise in and of itself, and it is the greatest blessing you have.” Mo said with a little envy in his voice. “I will detach this portion from myself. At the same time, you are to refine it.”","With a single thought, the connection was severed and the Black Ink Strength within Yang Ji suddenly collapsed. It no longer held up its form, as though it was a lump of clay that just sat there.","Yang Ji could feel that the Black Ink Strength clump was no longer as resistive as before. Using his Divine Sense, he could now slice it apart without it changing its shape back.","He played with it for a while, and ~Nоvеlight~ was awaiting for the next set of instructions, but Mo never spoke up.","When he opened his eyes to check, he was no longer there. The space looked the exact same as before, but Mo has just disappeared.","“Mo? Are you there?” He asked, but there was no response.","In fact, he could not feel any presence, not of Mo or of any others. It was as though he had been isolated from the rest."]},{"number":6035,"title":"Chapter 6035: Twin’s Cultivation Technique","paragraphs":["“Wait. Are you seriously just going to leave me here to deal with it on my own now?” Yang Ji could not help but complain. Still, it was only a brief moment of frustration. He was sharp enough to pick up on the things Mo had said.","“Fine. I’ll solve it myself.” Yang Ji sighed.","Yang Ji thought back on the key things Mo had personally said. Namely, that ‘to control Black Ink Strength is to be a part of it, and for it to be a part of him’. Though it sounded like sophistry, Yang Ji believes there was more to this than meets the eye.","For cultivators, the normal course of making an object part of the person was to leave behind their Soul Imprint. After all, that was what they did for most Artifacts. Artifacts were connected to a person when they have a Soul Imprint on them, and wiping out the Soul Imprint would render the Artifact free for anyone to take over.","Naturally, that was the first thought Yang Ji had come to. So, he closed his eyes and tried to refine the Black Ink Strength blob using his Spiritual Energy, trying to form a connection to it, and place his Soul Imprint on it.","However, just as he was about to start, he sensed a disturbance in the Black Ink Space.","Wondering if Mo had felt guilty about leaving him on his own, he opened his eyes. However, the figure that appeared was not the person he was hoping for. In fact, he began to panic.","“What are you doing here?” Yang Ji could not help but question. After all, the person who appeared was the one who was supposed to stay outside of this Black Ink Space and make sure he did not get corrupted!","“Erm...” Yang Xu, who had suddenly appeared here, found it difficult to calmly explain with her Brother so stimulated and panicked.","Seeing how he had scared her, Yang Ji quickly apologised. “Sorry. I didn’t mean to startle you. It’s just...”","“It’s fine.” Yang Xu also quickly shook her head in understanding and continued to explain. “Mo told me to get in here. He said that you would need my help in refining the Black Ink Strength.”","“And you just believed him?” Yang Ji found it doubtful she would leave her post when his life was at risk. After all, if there was one thing he knew, out of everyone in the world, she was always # Nоvеlight # the one who was most concerned about him. Even their Biological Mother, Su Yan, was not comparable to her.","“Of course not. He made another Dao Oath that we would be safe and you would not get corrupted regardless of what you did. I mean, if he has gone so far, wouldn’t you believe him? Also, he said if I did not help you with it, you would not be able to accomplish anything.” Yang Xu sighed a little.","She truly would have preferred to ensure her Brother’s safety, but if no result yielded, then they would be stuck here for who knows how long. Weighing the options, she might as well do as Mo had asked.","“Wait... why would I need you here with me? Did Mo explain why?” Yang Ji was confused. After all, why would he need another person to help him refine something? [Did this mean my initial guess was wrong?]","Yang Xu shook her head, “I’m not too sure. He did not explain much to me. In fact, after what seemed to be sealing us off inside the cultivation room, he was in a rush to leave.”","“He sealed us outside as well?” Yang Ji asked, seeking confirmation.","“Yeah. Did he seal off this place as well? Or, was it always like this?” Yang Xu looked around and tried to sense the surroundings. However, there seemed to be an impenetrable wall around them, one which seemed to isolate them from the world.","This was strange. From what she knew, within the Black Ink Space, they should be able to connect to other Black Ink Clansmen who were also within the Black Ink Space.","Yang Ji scratched his head in frustration, and he just began to explain everything that had happened on his side so far.","Once everything was made clear, Yang Xu also began to ponder. “If it requires the both of us, then maybe it has something to do with our Cultivation Technique?”","The twins cultivated using the same Cultivation Technique. This was not an ordinary Cultivation Technique and could only be used by the two. Typically, for Dragons and Phoenixes, they would cultivate using a Cultivation Technique from their Bloodline Inheritance. They would need to focus on refining their Bloodline to make it more pure. However, for the twins, it was slightly different.","Their Bloodlines were already extremely pure. In fact, it was doubtful if it could get any purer. Furthermore, in terms of Bloodline Inheritance, they had none. At least, not from the usual way Divine Spirits get their Bloodline Inheritance, which was knowledge directly entering their minds, seeming from a distant memory, over time.","Their Cultivation Technique was more like an instinct, one which they had known seemingly from birth. It was only refined with Shi’s help.","What they had was technically a dual Cultivation Technique, similar to what the Hu Sisters, Hu Mei’er and Hu Jiao’er, had learnt. However, it was different in the fact that this Cultivation Technique was meant for them, and them alone. After all, they were a rare breed of twins, that were both of opposite genders, that were both of different Divine Spirits, with parents who stood at the apex of the two strongest Divine Spirit Clans. It was only natural that what they had was vastly different.","It was such that their Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique was born.","It was questionable if the connection they were born with got stronger with this Cultivation Technique. Nevertheless, this was the Cultivation Technique that made them very different from the rest, different from even their Half Brothers and Sisters. It enabled them to even share mastery of the different Daos and seemed to have connected their cultivation together.","In other words, if one of them breakthrough in their cultivation realm, the other would also breakthrough. If one had been enlightened, the other would also be enlightened.","This was something strange and unique about them, something which the twins took pride in, especially Yang Xu. This uniqueness was why her first thought was their Cultivation Technique.","Seeing as to how he could not think of anything else, Yang Ji could only agree with her conclusion, “Then, I guess we should try it.”","He immediately took the lead by sitting down cross-legged and pushing out his hands.","Yang Xu, having done this countless times by now, also did the same. She sat directly opposite of her Brother, faced him, and also pushed her hands out to meet his.","Once their palms connected, they immediately started to circulate their Spiritual Energy. Typically, it would be their Qi and Spiritual Energy, but in the Black Ink Space, they could only circulate Spiritual Energy.","Their Spiritual Energy flowed out from their Souls, and connected to one another through their hands. There was no conflict whatsoever. Even when their Spiritual Energies were clearly different, with opposing characteristics, when it was these two together, whatever they did was always in harmony.","In fact, their Spiritual Energy would even go into the other party’s Soul Body without resistance. This was something unheard of. Since, for others, this would mean allowing the other party to dye their Soul, essentially corrupting it. However, for the twins this was not an issue.","It was normal for them.","In fact, when Yang Xu’s Spiritual Energy entered her Brother, it had basically completely transformed to be his. At the same time, whatever he sent to her had become hers. Even if they were completely different types of Spiritual Energies, both could make use of the others’ Spiritual Energy.","At the same time, their thoughts were also transmitted to each other instantly, as though they were talking normally. It was as though time was immaterial. A full conversation between them could have taken place without one second passing.","In fact, even feelings and emotions could be transmitted, but they tend to not wish to go that far.","For now, Yang Ji was just sharing the sensation of how he felt with the Black Ink Strength in his body."]},{"number":6036,"title":"Chapter 6036: Divine Spirit Source and Blood Essence","paragraphs":["The moment all was exposed, the five senses, Spiritual Energy, and even control, something mysterious happened.","As though in a world of their own, all their senses became linked. Though they were technically only connected through their Soul in the Black Ink Space, that no longer seemed to matter. Their bodies were in perfect balance, where one could control the other. In fact, Yang Xu could control and move Yang Ji’s Qi, and Yang Ji could do the same for the Qi in her body.","This should have been impossible. After all, one’s Qi was related to one’s own power; one’s own cultivation. Being able to control another person’s Qi was no different from being able to control the other’s life.","In fact, why was Qi Deviation so feared? Because it could end a cultivator’s life. Returning back could be considered a miracle, losing one’s cultivation could be said to be a last resort, and death could be said to be expected. When someone else could control one’s Qi, was this not equivalent to experiencing Qi Deviation?","Yet, the twins could do so at ease as though Qi Deviation was never a concern for them.","Such a feat would have shocked Mo if he was present. This was definitely outside of his expectations.","No living being in existence would have thought this possible, until they met these two.","Still, for the two who could manage to pull this off, this was nothing worth mentioning. It had become so normal to them that it was like counting the number of cups of water one drinks throughout their life.","Without a word, Yang Xu could also feel the Black Ink Strength. As though in all her control, while it was still in her Brother’s body, her Spiritual Energy easily wrapped and diced the Black Ink Strength.","It was basically no different from her Brother controlling his own body.","She tried the same thing Yang Ji tried, and found that nothing really changed. No matter how she interacted with the Black Ink Strength, it remained inert.","This surprised both of them.","They ❀ Nоvеlігht ❀ (Don’t copy, read here) expected since Mo had gone so far as to isolate them, and pushed the two of them to use their dual Cultivation Technique, this would have sparked some kind of change.","“What do we do now?” Yang Xu asked, since she really did not know what else to do.","“‘To control Black Ink Strength is to be a part of it, and for it to be a part of you’. – that is the main hint Mo has given me.” Yang Ji shrugged and recalled.","When Yang Xu first heard this, she already wondered, “Have you tried your Blood Essence?”","“Blood Essence? No... I thought that since the Black Ink Strength had passed through my heart once, it should have made contact with my blood. So, I did not consider using Blood Essence...” Yang Ji stated, and he soon realised his oversight.","“Argh... how can I forget about Blood Essence?” Yang Ji lamented, frustrated at not noticing it sooner.","In terms of Blood Essence, it had long been concentrated into their Divine Spirit Sources. If Monster Beast had Monster Cores, Divine Spirits have their Source, which acts as their core. For Monster Beasts and Divine Spirits, this was their source of strength. However, for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, they were different.","Physically, they were birthed and not hatched. Like their Father and Mother, they had both Dantian and their own Divine Spirit Source. This was why though extremely young, they could transform into Humans. Rather, it was more apt to say that though young, they could transform into their respective Dragon and Phoenix Forms.","However, at the end of the day, the Dantian was only a source of power, where their Qi was stored. It could not be considered ‘them’ as a whole. However, the Divine Spirit Source, and their Blood Essence, was different. For Divine Spirits, this was no different from their existence. Even if their bones were shattered to dust, bodies immolated to ash, their Divine Spirit Source would withstand the test of time. It would be their final mark in this world, their inheritance to future generations.","So, the closest thing that was ‘them’, other than their Soul, would be Blood Essence.","Seeing things in a new light Yang Ji did not hesitate and drew upon his Phoenix Source. Very quickly Blood Essence dripped out, just two drops.","Two drops might not seem like much but these two drops contained immensely pure Phoenix Bloodline and Source Strength. These were not things he could casually give away. In fact, it would take years for him to replenish these two drops. It was only fortunate that most of his cultivation was not purely reliant on his Source. Else, he would have to enter secluded cultivation and focus getting his Source Strength back to normal.","Meanwhile, Yang Xu also acted without hesitation. She too drew out two drops of Blood Essence from her Dragon Source, and transferred them into Yang Ji.","When the twins did this, they immediately felt a waste of exhaustion wash over them. Nevertheless, they persisted and continued.","The four drops, producing cries of Phoenixes and roars of Dragons, were soon inserted into that blob of Black Ink Strength.","The process was smooth, without resistance. The blob did not even resist, and the sounds died down.","At first, the twins just watched with bated breaths. Second turned into minutes, minutes never turned into hours because they could not possibly wait that long.","“Hey, did we do something wrong?” Yang Xu asked again.","“No idea. We must have done something right.” Yang Ji concluded, convinced that this must be the right step.","Just when they were in doubt, the blob of Black Ink Strength suddenly expanded!","Yang Ji was the first to react in a panic. Using all the Spiritual Energy he could muster, he tried to quickly compress it.","Yang Xu was the same. Once she felt the pain her Brother’s Dantian was going through, she immediately used all her Spiritual Energy to suppress the expansion.","In that split second, the blob had basically turned into a balloon, expanding over the size of Yang Ji’s Dantian! If he had not reacted in time, his Dantian might have blown to pieces.","Even if only in his Soul Form, the piercing pain made Yang Ji want to shed tears. He could feel his whole body breaking out in sweat.","As for Yang Xu, she was spared after that short episode. Yang Ji was quick to react and cut off the connection of their pain senses. So, after that brief tearing pain, Yang Xu no longer felt discomfort. Nevertheless, that pain was enough to render her fearful, with her heart rate skyrocketing.","Still, with the both of them, holding the ‘balloon’, it could not expand further. Nevertheless, this was the best they could do. It was a stalemate. They had no leeway to do anything else, and Yang Ji had to bear with the pain the whole way through.","Resisting the urge to scream, Yang Ji fully devoted himself to keeping it from worsening. In the midst of all the anguish, he suddenly heard the familiar cries and roars of Phoenixes and Dragons.","Soon, very slowly, the ‘balloon’ deflated. It started to shrink as its surface started to shine with bright marks of gold and silver.","Eventually, it deflated to the point it was no longer as large as Yang Ji’s Dantian. However, the twins spared no chance. They still kept suppressing it, in case it ever suddenly expanded again. Yang Ji certainly would not want to risk it, and Yang Xu did not wish her Brother to experience that kind of pain again.","The cries and roars kept getting louder, and the gold and silver marks grew brighter.","Despite shrinking down to a size that was even smaller than when the Black Ink Strength was just a blob, even when it shrank down to the size of just a droplet, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were still on guard for anything.","Eventually, the cries and roars died down, and the droplet turned into a sphere with its marks flashing and dimming ever so slowly.","One minute passed, two minutes passed, an hour or more passed, and eventually, Yang Ji and Yang Xu, too tired to continue, stopped compressing it.","“Do you think it is okay now?” This time, it was Yang Ji who asked, holding his stomach as the piercing pain was something he could not forget. His face was still in agony whenever he thought of what had happened.","“Erm... why not check with our Divine Sense?” Uncertain as well, Yang Xu proposed as she tried to probe the inside of this sphere with her Divine Sense.","Yang Ji did the same, and their Divine Sense both simultaneously reached out. However, before they made contact, there was a *crack!*","The sphere had cracked! Furthermore, the thing that came out was something wiggly!"]},{"number":6037,"title":"Chapter 6037: The Worm","paragraphs":["There was no longer any Black Ink Strength in Yang Ji’s body. However, now, there was this mysterious creature that had come to life.","Yang Xu immediately felt her whole body turn cold as she shivered. Goosebumps could be seen all over. Meanwhile, Yang Ji was piqued by the sight. The former retreated while the latter, spurred by curiosity, approached.","The wiggly black strand seemed to want to break out of its shell, but the crack seemed a little too small. So, it just retreated back in.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu had expected it to use more force to breakthrough the shell. However, the next sound was peculiar. It was definitely different from the initial *Crack*.","“What the...” Yang Xu exclaimed in disgust. After all, after ❀ Nоvеlігht ❀ (Don’t copy, read here) that sound occurred, that thing had its head popped out. Though she had not seen its entire body, just its tail and head, she had a fair guess what this creature was.","[Why did it have to be a worm with a mouth and eyes...] She clicked her tongue.","Meanwhile in front of her, Yang Ji, was excited.","The worm was slowly biting through its shell – seeming to enjoy the ‘delicacy’. It seemed too preoccupied to bother with the two beings staring at it.","“Hey, what do you think it eats?” Yang Ji asked, genuinely curious.","“Why are you asking me that? Are you planning to keep it?” Yang Xu looked at her Brother, side-eyed. [Brother, no matter how much I love you, this is too much...]","Yang Ji, already knowing what his Sister was worried about, stated. “You know, you don’t have to be so afraid of it. It’s not even an actual Insect or an Invertebrate. It might look like a worm, but I’m certain that it is not one.”","“No no no, Brother, what are YOU talking about? It is clearly a worm, with how much mucus its body is producing.” Yang Xu rebuked.","“Look carefully! Worms do not have mouths with teeth nor do they have eyes!” Yang Ji added, trying to convince her. After all, keeping this ‘worm’ would mean it had to be inside one of their bodies. Typically, it would be fine but, due to how their Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique works, it would not be strange for that ‘worm’ to be able to move about and jump from one host to another. Even if that does not happen, as long as it was inside Yang Ji, she would be able to feel it inside of her if they cultivated and shared their senses.","Yang Xu simply could not bear the thought of this thing being inside of her. In fact, her reaction was quite mild right now because Yang Ji had stopped sharing his senses with her – due to the earlier incident. Nevertheless, if they wanted to further cultivate using Heaven Earth Symmetry, they would eventually have to share their senses.","To Yang Xu, this would be no different from two people sharing a room, when her roommate suddenly decided to take a cockroach as a pet...","“Woah!” There was a sudden exclamation from Yang Ji. Once the worm finished feasting upon its shell, it suddenly curled up. Soon, two black droplets came out of it...","“Why are you so impressed when it just took a shit in your Dantian!?” Yang Xu was almost screaming at this point.","“That’s not shit...” Yang Ji was quick to fix the misunderstanding. Not thinking things through, he quickly grabbed the two pieces and was quick to approach Yang Xu to show them to her.","Yang Xu was naturally appalled by this. Her face turned greenish black. She even tried to run away but Yang Ji was too quick. He grabbed her arm with his free hand and directly showed them to her.","“For god’s sake. Just use your Divine Sense and scan it properly.” Yang Ji insisted.","“...” Yang Xu wanted to reproach him almost on instinct. However, she held back her tongue.","*Tsk* “Fine” Seeing how Yang Ji was being that serious, with deadpan eyes, she could not help but doubt herself. She relented and did as she was told.","Her Divine Sense spread out like a wave, but upon getting close to the ‘pieces’, it hesitated to move forward. After some back and forth, she finally made first contact.","As Yang Ji had said, this was definitely not fecal matter. Though small, about the size of one’s pinky nail, these two objects had a unique aura to them. In fact, these two were perfectly identical to one another, even their aura.","In a way, these two pieces were somewhat like them. They seemed to be intricately connected, without flaw. From her Divine Sense just scanning one, she was essentially scanning them both.","Though still disgusted, even Yang Xu could not help but get curious as to what these things were. She had never seen or heard about anything like this.","However, she first had to deal with a little overly smug Brother.","“See, I told you, didn’t I?” Yang Ji could be seen grinning from ear to ear.","“Okay. Fine. I admit I was wrong okay. Still doesn’t change the fact that this is disgusting. I don’t want to touch them so can you just put them away already.” Yang Xu quickly admitted, wanting to rapidly move on from this.","However, Yang Ji’s next words disheartened her.","“I guess you did not really check it in depth. One of them is actually for you. So, you need to take one.” As Yang Ji spoke, as though to prove his point, the worm uncurled and started moving towards him – as though under his command. “It’s fine if you don’t want to host the creature, but you need to at least take this Black Ink Nest...”","“What!? This is a Black Ink Nest!?” Yang Xu repeated, unable to fully come to terms with this. After all, when have Black Ink Nests been so small? Even the smallest ones she had seen were the size of a palm. She had never seen or heard about it being this small! Worst of all, pooped out by some creature!"]},{"number":6038,"title":"Chapter 6038: Breaking Free","paragraphs":["“Argh. Stop being so picky about every little thing. Just take it into your Dantian already.” Yang Ji was starting to get annoyed at this point. Though he could understand why she was disgusted, they could not possibly keep going back and forth on this.","Yang Ji did not need two Black Ink Nests in his body. Furthermore, since this creature no longer had any connection to Mo, and was created by both their Blood Essences, it definitely would not harm them.","“Can I not...” Yang Xu seems to be giving a last bit of resistance. However, seeing how Yang Ji was not relenting, she knew it was no use.","Still, seeing how he was forcing his Sister, Yang Ji gave in a little. “Fine, fine. You don’t have to touch it, okay? I’ll just help put it in your Dantian for you...”","“En...” Since he was going so far for her, Yang Xu could not really refuse at this point.","Since the matter had been settled, Yang Ji was the one who took the initiative to stop the Cultivation Technique, and left the Black Ink Space. Once back inside the cultivation room, he could not help but take note of his surroundings.","His Sister was sitting cross-legged, with her hands stretched out to hold his. She still had her eyes closed, but it was certain she would awaken soon enough.","As for the cultivation room, like Yang Xu had said, it was truly sealed off. The door was no longer there, and there were just smooth walls all around them. The whole room now looked so uniform that Yang Ji was having trouble telling where the original entrance was.","He actually took awhile to get a feel of his surroundings, all while waiting for Yang Xu to wake up. However, nothing happened.","[Oh, I see.] Maybe it was due to their unbreakable bond, Yang Ji quickly realised what Yang Xu was doing. [That sure is sly of you, Sister.]","She planned on staying in the Black Ink Space, where she could easily cut off most of the senses to her body. That way, she could remain oblivious to what her Brother was going to do to her body.","Yang Ji just let out a soft chuckle and he opened his mouth. He stimulated his Qi, and had it wrapped around one of the micro Black Ink Nests in of him. Very quickly, he expelled it out of his mouth.","This was a brute force method expelling something out of one’s body. It was unfortunate, but they were unable to manipulate Space Principles here, and the Black Ink Nest was not an Artifact that had been refined. Thus, Yang Ji had to physically remove the Black Ink Nest from his Dantian.","Naturally, he was considerate to make sure it was cleaned before he helped insert it into Yang Xu’s Dantian.","He took out some water from his Space Ring, and gave it a rinse, before inserting it into her lips. Typically, it would be impossible to guide an object into someone else’s Dantian. It was only due to their Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique, that he faced no resistance when his Qi was inside her body.","Once the micro Black Ink Nest was settled in, only then did he wake her up.","“It’s done, you can come back now.” Yang Ji told her using his Divine Sense.","Hearing his call, Yang Xu immediately sprung to life. She touched her lips and shivered a little.","Yang Ji rolled his eyes at this, and just moved on to more important topics. “Hey, do you know how we are supposed to get out?”","Yang Xu shook her head, trying to not think about the matter anymore as she replied, “Not really. He never mentioned anything about getting out. Still, there must be a way. If Mo had truly isolated this place from the outside world, that means even he would not be able to sense what’s going on inside. Following that logic, we must be the ones who take the initiative to get out of this isolated space.”","“Haa... easier said than done. This whole place looks the same to me. I can’t even make out the indents on the walls due to this barrier. I can’t even tell where the original entrance is.” Yang Ji scratched his head as he sighed. He walked up to the closest barrier wall and with all his strength, swung his fist, *boom!*","A loud sound was made, but that was all. The barrier was still pristine, without a flaw, with the only reminder of the attempt being the pain in his knuckles.","“We definitely can’t break it down.” Yang Ji shrugged, trying to play it cool even when he was in pain.","“Maybe, we give the worm a try?” Since their own strength would clearly not be enough, Yang Ji quickly suggested this new found specimen.","“...” Yang Xu gave a nod, and took some distance away. She too came to the same conclusion.","Yang Ji tried to use his Divine Sense to probe it within his Dantian. The little critter was still curled up. Unsure how he could communicate with it, Yang Ji just tried to send it a message through his Divine Sense.","“Hey, can you help us lift this barrier? Erm, please?”","To his astonishment, the worm had responded!","It unravelled itself, and seemed to groggily look around. As though it was a part-time shift worker clocking in, it slowly lifted its body to complete its task.","Seeming to perfectly understand what Yang Ji wants, it travelled out of his Dantian. Surprisingly, it did not have to go through any Yang Ji orifices. Instead, it seemed to be able to pass through the barriers of space, and appeared outside of him in an instant.","It was floating mid-air, looking around at its surroundings, trying to take everything in.","When it noticed its target, it seemed to heavily judge the barrier that had caused it to work ‘overtime’, It looked back at Yang Ji and Yang Xu with its bead-like eyes, as if questioning them, ‘you two woke me up for this?’","No even needing an answer, the worm turned back and slithered onto the barrier. With its mouth, it started to nibble on it.","As though knife through paper, the barrier was unable to put up the least bit of resistance against its teeth.","A tiny pencil dot hole soon turned into a fist-sized one. The fist-sized hole soon turned into a basin sized hole. The little worm just kept eating, without any regard for anything else. It was unbelievable how something smaller than a pinky had enough capacity to devour more than a hundred times its size.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu just watched, wide-eyed.","It was only once the hole became big enough to fit two adults that the worm stopped.","As though clocking out of work, it was quick to rush ‘home’. Disappearing into Yang Ji’s Dantian before he could even ask it a question.","In fact, it had already curled up inside the Dantian, and seemed to be – what Yang Ji could only assume – to be sleeping","“Is it just me, or does this thing have an attitude?” Yang Ji could not help but look at his Sister and ask."]},{"number":6039,"title":"Chapter 6039: Two Pieces Meet Up","paragraphs":["Underneath the veil of worldwide darkness, a figure could be seen roaming about. He looked to be a boy, around eleven or twelve years old.","He was none other than Little Eleven.","Currently, in front of him were droves of Black Ink Clansmen, all of whom were on their knees, welcoming him.","“Welcome back, Holy One!”","Naturally, Little Eleven had not expected such a sight. In the first place, there should not have been anything here. Yet, there were both flora and fauna here. Though, it had to be stated that there were no actual animals except for the Black Ink Clansmen in front of him.","Underneath Little Eleven’s feet, there was a radius of clear open void. It was apparent that he had been reabsorbing the Black Ink Strength surrounding him. Those that were sent to welcome him naturally dared not step close to this space, much less dare to cross the Holy One in any way.","Seeing these familiar figures from his memories, Little Eleven could not help but recall the past. He had never truly known all of them in person. Still, they were his people. They were also the people he had fought wars for him, tossed aside like nothing – lives, valueless to him.","If regret could kill, he would be dead a trillion times by now. Still, what was done, was done. He need not ask for their forgiveness, nor would they even have the intention to. After all, in their eyes, he was their sole purpose in life.","In their eyes, his desire was worth everything while their life, nothing.","It was not that they could not forgive him, but rather they did not have the capability to forgive him. They never saw his actions, his tantrum, as wrong.","Just as he was about to move forward, the closest part of the ground, made of Black Ink Strength, shot up. Soon, a figure that was similar to his own, appeared in front of him. Except for the fact that he was entirely black, with tints of purple on him, and lacked feet, Little Eleven would have been convinced he was looking at a mirror.","“Greetings, My other half. Or, should I address you by what you go by now? Little Eleven, right?” Before he even fully formed, there was already a voice that echoed out of it. Once he showed his face, a smile immediately appeared.","“How?” Little Eleven was completely bewildered by the sight. Nevertheless, he stood on guard, ready for a strike.","It had to be said that this was pretty much the first time Little Eleven had come face to face with Mo like this. In the past, if there were any powerful accomplices that followed Little Eleven past the Profound Source Gate, Mo would always be in hiding.","Judging by the number of Black Ink Clansmen behind Mo, and how he was so confident as to appear directly in front of him, Little Eleven knew that Mo had the upper hand. Thus, it was only natural for him to be on guard. In the first place, if he was that confident about take Mo down on his own, he would not involved others in this affair.","Still, Mo seems to have no inclination to start any conflict. He just peacefully held up both hands and said. “I’m not here to fight you.”","Like anyone could believe what an enemy was saying. Little Eleven’s eyes narrowed as he became even warrier.","Seeing how everything he planned for was going in the opposite direction, Mo quickly changed the subject. “I believe you are looking for the kids-?”","Little Eleven immediately shot a glare, and cut him off. “What have you done to them!?”","Little Eleven brazenly took a step forward, and the Black Ink Strength on the ground all collapsed, absorbed into him. The radius of the void around him blasts off to increase by a few metres.","The sudden change caused Mo to even shift back a few metres.","This time, Mo was quick to state, hoping to not get mistaken as a villain. “Look. I’ve done nothing to them. They are with me and are in perfect health. In fact, what can I possibly do to those two monsters?”","Seeing to agree with Mo’s last statement, Little Eleven then asked. “In that case, why did you bother separating us? You blatantly kidnapped them.”","Mo scoffed as he stated, a little annoyed. “If I did not separate you two, would I have gotten the chance to talk to them? Would I have gotten the chance to talk to you?”","Mo could see Little Eleven frowning and he continued. “I doubt that would be the case. You label me as the villain. A target to be subjugated. If I were to let you three continue on without separating you, were you not going to just continue cleaning this whole place of my existence?”","Mo took a breath as though calming himself down. “Every little bit of Black Ink Strength you absorb or destroy is strength that I lose. Right now, I have no intention of allowing myself to be weakened. I have my own responsibilities to uphold. A fate which I want to change, which you ran away from.”","Before even giving Little Eleven a chance to speak, Mo quickly summoned up a screen. Anything on it lacked the variety of colour. However, there were clear outlines and gradients of black and purple, which helped make out what was on the screen.","Little Eleven could see the twins on it, with the familiar figure of Mo Na Ye behind them. Currently, this was when those two were already soaking their feet in Black Ink Liquid.","Initially, Little Eleven wanted to jump forward to help them. However, upon looking at the situation with calmer lens, he realised that nothing drastic was happening to them. At most, they would frown – and that was it. Seeing how the corruption was {N•o•v•e•l•i•g•h•t} just superficial, he relaxed a little.","He looked at Mo, and asked. “What is it that you want then?”","Mo, seemingly having been waiting for this moment for a long time, finally sighed. “To get us all back together as one. That is my main goal.”","Little Eleven looked at him strangely. He had expected some form of threat from Mo. After all, he had the twins there, and there was obviously a Royal Lord just standing behind them. Nevertheless, the first out of him was Little Eleven’s own goal – to basically get every piece of himself back.","However, there were lingering questions in Little Eleven’s mind. “If that’s the case, why do you need to convince me? Just do it through force.”","Soon, another two screens appeared from the ground. This time, they depicted two areas. On the ground, there was a split between them. A clear line denoting separation existed between the two. Yet, it was clear that this line was moving, as patches of the ground seem to be fought after.","There were even Black Ink Clansmen there, one side was more Humanoid, while the other two, more Beast-like.","They were fighting each other for what seemed to be earth, with some scraping out the dirt to bring it over onto their side.","Seeing these scenes, Little Eleven seemed to have realised. “You’re trying to stop yourself from getting devoured by our other selves?”","Mo nods and said, “Now you see why I would not be able to do anything to you three? Besides us two, there are two others. If we are to describe ourselves as ‘more Human’, then those two are the pure representative of the raw corruptive power of Black Ink Strength.”","“Us two, ‘more Human’?” Little Eleven gave a look as though he wanted to reject the notion. However, before he could, Mo added, “Over the past few thousands of years, I’ve managed to regain myself, and pry off some of the influence of Black Ink Strength. Else, do you think we could have a civil conversation like what we are doing now?”","Certainly, that was one aspect which confused Little Eleven. Nevertheless, he already had a theory as to why this was the case. However, for now, that was not important.","“So, you need our help in dealing with them. So, a truce, is it?” Little Eleven folded his arm and asked, still not willing to lower his guard.","“No, not exactly. I’m willing to forfeit myself, for us to be united again.” Mo openly said.","This made Little Eleven raise his eyebrow. After all, that was not a decision that could be taken lightly. Forfeiting oneself would mean giving themselves away, letting their consciousness be stripped. It was no different from death.","In short, Mo was saying he was willing to die for his own goal, that who was in charge did not matter to him. As long as all the pieces were reunited, it did not matter.","“Why go so far?” Little Eleven could not help but ask. After all, he had expected great resistance from Mo. Being dealt this easy victory made all his prior preparation feel like all his effort had been mocked.","Mo was genuinely surprised to hear this. He thought for a moment. However, a playful smile came onto his face, “I thought you wanted to reunite because you knew. But since you don’t, there is no point explaining to you. You can just find out once you remember everything from me.”"]},{"number":6040,"title":"Chapter 6040, Small Fry","paragraphs":["Chapter 6040, Small Fry","Author: Silavin","Once broken free, the twins were able to easily leave the room. There was no other hindrance to their path out, as though they had passed through all requirements to continue and were simply waiting for the next round to start.","In fact, the twins could not help but wonder what happened to their surroundings. This Black Ink Nest, which was supposed to be Mo Na Ye’s home, had seemingly transformed into something completely different.","The whole space had changed. It no longer bore any resemblance to a home. Rather, it felt like the whole interior of the Black Ink Nest had been modified into a giant Array, with the cultivation room at the centre.","This was extremely peculiar, since there was a saying that only Humans could create Arrays and Artifacts, because only they could comprehend the Dao of Arrays and the Dao of Artifacts. Typically, for most people, seeing the Black Ink Clan setup an Array would be a strange sight. However, for the twins, this was not the case. After all, they did not believe in that saying. Their personal experience proved that saying to be false.","To them, the most important thing was what had happened to Mo Na Ye, and his home. They were also curious how much time had passed.","Spreading out his Divine Sense like a tide, Yang Ji scanned the whole Black Ink Nest, and noticed no one was there. In fact, no one had stepped in here for what seemed to be a long time. “He’s no longer here. Do you think he moved out?”","“Since he’s not here, you want to try and escape?” Yang Xu asked, checking with her Brother. Though, the question seemed redundant to both.","Yang Ji slowly shook his head, and confirmed their thoughts. “I doubt we would be able to escape. Mo would know where we are as long as we are within his territory. Besides, we promised to help. I don’t really feel good to back out of our words.”","Yang Xu gave a silent nod of agreement. She too felt the same. It was just that, whatever Mo wanted their help with would have been much easier if their Father was here. Technically, going back and asking for his help was an option.","However, if her Brother wanted to continue on and do this themselves, she was fine with it as well.","Yang Ji took the lead to exit through the door, leading to the outside world. There, he found the whole scenery to be the same. He once again scanned his surroundings with his Divine Sense, and finally discovered life in the Black Ink Nest next door.","Seemingly to have noticed his presence, the opposite Black Ink Nest’s door suddenly opened and there, Mo Na Ye came out.","The man was certainly dressed, and had a gentlemanly grace to him. His hair was more well kept, and he seemed to have donned something more formal – at least, it was something more formal in Yang Xu’s eyes. Their fashion trends here were definitely more different from those back home, since the material they could use was different as well. In fact, even the slightly ignorant Yang Ji could tell something was different about him.","Mo Na Ye seemed a little flustered as he appeared. He was certainly not expecting the twins to come out at this time. There was a natural trace of disappointment in his eyes, which he quickly tried to hide.","Yang Xu naturally noticed, but she kept quiet, [Seems like we ruined his little session?]","Pitying him a little, Yang Xu was the one who stepped in to speak, before her Brother said something that might be insensitive. “We’re done with removing the Black Ink Strength from my Brother’s body. Is there anything else we need to do?”","Mo Na Ye gave a small sigh, as though indicating, ‘I knew you two were monsters, but could you have taken a few days to do it?’","He turned towards the little girl and said, “In that case, now, it is your turn.”","Yang Ji quickly interjected, “My Sister does not need to do it. I’m certain she would not get corrupted even if she drank Black Ink Liquid.”","Mo Na Ye had one of his eyebrows raised as he asked, “How are you so confident?”","Yang Ji smirked as he declared, “Because, we got a new helper.”","Soon, Yang Ji summoned out the little worm.","Technically, he tried to call it awake, but the little worm would not respond. So, Yang Ji, without much of a choice, forcefully expelled it from his Dantian.","The little worm was confused. While it was taking it much needed beauty sleep, it suddenly got expelled out of its home. It looked at Yang Ji with grievance in its beady eyes, as though asking him, ‘I’ve already done my work for the day. What else do you want from me!?’","Yang Ji held the little worm in his hand and presented it to Mo Na Ye. “The little guy should be able to consume Black Ink Strength.”","Hearing it getting called ‘little guy’, the little worm immediately bit onto Yang Ji ‘s thumb.","*Ouch!* Yang Ji cried out. “What was that for!?”","Yang Xu, who had stepped back a couple of feet at this point, questioned, “Maybe it is because that thing is a girl?”","“Okay, okay. Little girl. Fine. Are you happy now?” Yang Ji said and the little worm finally released her grasp on his finger. Like a Young Lady, she even seemed to have made a ‘humph’ in front of him.","Mo Na Ye took a closer look at the little worm, and felt an instinctive urge to prostrate before it. This sensation felt similar to looking at the Holy One. Yet, it was also different at the same time. He could not quite describe it, but he could tell that his Black Ink Strength would certainly be rendered mute before this little thing.","Seeming to sense what Yang Ji said was right, Mo Na Ye gave a slight nod as he gulped, trying his best to stay calm.","However, when the little worm had her eyes set on him, he could feel a slight shiver down his spine. It was akin to that of a prey meeting its natural predator. This had nothing to do with their difference in strength. This was just an instinct.","The little worm eyed him, and as though throwing a slight tantrum, it slammed its tail on Yang Ji’s palm repeatedly, as though questioning, ‘you woke me up for this small fry?’"]},{"number":6041,"title":"Chapter 6041, Capillaries","paragraphs":["Chapter 6041, Capillaries","Author: Silavin","Yang Ji could not help but have his eyelid twitch. The small fry this puny thing was referring to was none other than a Royal Lord! A Royal Lord who was almost three times his size, and probably a million times her size.","Yet, this little thing had the gull to show such an attitude!?","However, what surprised him was how the Royal Lord showed acceptance at this treatment, without a word or expression of complaint. He just gave a nod, and accepted what Yang Ji had said earlier, that his Sister need not go through the same experience he did.","Seeing how things have already progressed, and they tacitly agreed on this same point, Yang Ji just straight-forwardly asked, “Does this mark the end of our training?”","Mo Na Ye gave a slow nod. Realistically, there was nothing else for them to train for at this point. Other than increasing their own cultivation, these two children could not get any more resistant to Black Ink Strength. No, rather than call it ‘resistant’, it was more accurate to call it ‘ravenous’.","In fact, trying to increase their cultivation here would be ill-advised. The World Principles here were vastly different from the outside world. There was naturally World Energy here, but not the same World Energy as the one in the outside world. For Humans, this place would seem like an empty void. However, that was far from the truth. IIt was just that they could not perceive these other forces at play, which made this whole space seem like an empty void.","In short, this truly marked the end of their training. There was nothing else he could do for them.","With narrowed eyes, and a deep understanding of what they needed to do next, Mo Na Ye said. “Do give me a moment. I just need to change and we will head off to the next area for the actual task.”","Mo Na Ye quickly went back in and changed. When he came out, he was wearing the same suit he wore when he met them.","When he came out, his eyes seemed to have also changed. Gone was the relaxed and more open expression he had. Now, he had eyes of determination, with a singular goal in sight.","The twins just waited for him, waited until he declared with a heavier tone, “I’m done. Now, we are off to the battlefield.”","“Huh? Battlefield?” Yang Xu exclaimed, as her eyes narrowed.","Yang Ji was the same. Though he expected there to be an eventual battle, he did not consider there to be a war ongoing.","“Yes. I’ll explain while we move. The trip there will take a long while.” Mo Na Ye said as he took out and then kept his Small Black Ink Nest.","He led the twins to the same platform they had used before, and once they got on, it shot through the sky.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could feel the ground underneath them push them up, to the point it was hard to stand; and after a few seconds, they felt their feets disconnect from the ground, only to return back thanks to Mo Na Ye’s support.","As for the little worm, she did not return to Yang Ji’s Dantian and just loitered about outside in his clothes. Would be troublesome to go in and out of the Dantian, after all.","This time, this piece of land was no longer connected to the ground. It was launched directly into the sky, precisely into a river made of Black Ink Strength.","*Spash*","When the twins could finally feel solid ground beneath their feet, the land underneath them had finally landed on top of a river, creating a huge splash.","Yang Ji noticed that the ‘water’ was less viscous than the one they dipped their bodies into, and it flowed much faster thanks to that.","In fact, it was not an exaggeration to say that this river was a rapid. In seconds, they had crossed more than ten kilometres due to the force. They were only able to stay on thanks to their powerful, cultivated Physique.","Mo Na Ye, seeing how the twins did not need his support, let go. He raised his arm and introduced. “Welcome to the Holy One’s Capillaries. Technically, only Feudal Lords and above are allowed to ride on these Capillaries, since those weaker might not be able to hold on. I initially thought I would have to support you two for the whole trip, but I have certainly underestimated you two.”","Mo Na Ye continued, “The Capillaries are connected to all regions under the Holy One. They go forward in one direction, and back in another connecting path. Right now. The site we are headed to is one of the fronts. But not to worry. For all your activities there, I’ve been tasked to protect you two.”","“Woah!” Yang Ji and Yang Xu both exclaimed, having fun with the ride. Though they could use Space Principles in the outside world, riding at such a high speed was an experience all on its own.","Even when enjoying the ride, the two of them still paid a lot of attention to what Mo Na Ye had said. So, Yang Ji was the first to ask, “In that case, what are we supposed to do there?”","Mo Na Ye nodded his head, as that was the next topic he was going to talk about. “Both of you will be using as much Purifying Light as you can over there. The only main thing to look out for is our allies. I do note wish to have any of our people fall due to our own allies.”","Yang Xu tilted her head and asked. “Wait a moment. If the enemies are going to be Black Ink Clansmen, how are we even going to tell them apart?”","Mo Na Ye shook his head and directly said. “No need to worry about that. You will definitely know it once you reach the place. It is really just that easy to tell. ”","“Erm, okay.” Yang Xu tilted her head, wishing for more answers. But, Mo Na Ye just added how personally seeing it for himself was more than any words in the world.","Mo Na Ye also added, “Also, try not to damage anything that is within our territory.”","Yang Ji was the one to respond this time. He just questioned, “How are we supposed to tell?”","Mo Na Ye gave back the same answer again, “You will know.”","“...” The twins wanted to ask for more details, but since Mo Na Ye had said as much, they just left their curiosity to unravel at the actual place itself.","As for the little worm, she had already started sleeping in Yang Ji’s inner chest pocket. To her, these minor matters were not things she needed to concern herself with."]},{"number":6042,"title":"Chapter 6042, Two Meances","paragraphs":["Chapter 6042, Two Meances","Author: Silavin","The distance from where they originally were was considerable. It took them more than a whole day of travel before they could hear the panic voices of ‘their’ people.","Yang Ji sends out his Divine Sense, concentrating it in the direction of the sound, to discover multiple people frantically rushing about. Due to the darkness around him, he could not visually see into the distance. However, he could sense that something was off with how they were acting.","Mo Na Ye was naturally the first to notice the strange condition at the frontlines. His expression turned dark as his eyes narrowed. Unable to hold back, or delay for another second, he warned the kids, “Hold on tight. I’m speeding up.”","Yang Xu and Yang Ji immediately felt their hearts jump into their throat. They quickly got on all fours, using their Qi to hold onto the piece of ‘earth’ beneath them.","Their instinct proved correct as in the next moment, they sped off even quicker than before. They whizzed past the air so quickly that those sounds of panic turned muffed, and any speech between them would be impossible.","Behind them were the remnants of Mo Na Ye’s power. Once the Royal Lord rooted himself into the ground using Black Ink Strength, a black jet flashed out from the arms directed behind him.","In seconds, they have covered what would have been minutes. Furthermore, they need not even step out of the ground beneath them. Mo Na Ye took complete liberty to swift his body lower and make the whole site leave the Capillary.","Before they knew it, they had already flown over the sounds beneath, and into enemy territory.","*Bang!*","The ground beneath them had crashed, with Mo Na Ye taking precaution to use his Black Ink Strength to wrap around the kids before it did.","This could be said to be one reason why Mo had them train, so that Mo Na Ye could use his powers on them without them getting affected by it.","The second would be what faced them next.","While still trying to catch up with the changes of event, Yang Ji and Yang Xu both took in a large breath. Never had they missed their ability to tear through Space as much as they did now.","Through their Divine Sense, Yang Ji asked, “You okay?”","Yang Xu had many things to say, but she chose to keep them in at this moment, as they regained her bearings. “Yeah...”","“*Huuu...* Me too, thankfully...” Yang Ji showed a face of relief that the whole ordeal had been over. However, that quickly shifted as he felt the ground tremble.","“Wait. What’s going on?” Shocked, Yang Ji asked Mo Na Ye as he immediately grabbed his Sister as they both retreated to the air, hovering about ten metres from the ground.","“We are in enemy territory. It is devour or be devoured here.” Mo Na Ye said as he joined up with the twins and pointed to the platform they were on earlier.","The detached piece of land, made of Black Ink Strength, had started showing signs of cracking. From these cracks seeped through another power, also Black Ink Strength. However, this Black Ink Strength seemed to be eroding the piece of land, slowly breaking it down as though digesting it.","It did not take long before what they once stood on had completely disappeared, enveloped by another type of Black Ink Strength.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu were both taken aback by this sight. But, they were quick to realise that this must be what the war had been about – devour or be devoured. It was pretty much the same reason why their Uncle Eleven had come.","In too much of a rush to care about their thoughts, Mo Na Ye pointed to behind them, where they had come from. “We are at the backlines now. Perfect for you two to start. Like mentioned before, I’ll keep you two safe. Just keep blasting your Purifying Light on the ground.”","That statement had snapped them out of their thoughts as they gave a firm nod.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both took action. In a flash, Blue and Yellow Crystals appeared in their hands. They both clasped them together in the palms, as a bright light leaked through the gaps between their fingers.","A little weary, Mo Na Ye even took a few paces back, which proved fortunate he did.","After all, in the next moment, two bright flashes that enveloped the world flashed out. They enveloped the twins and everything around them.","Naturally, that meant two large craters on the ground, even when they were a distance away. However, Mo Na Ye was not spared from the blast...","However, due to his position, quick reaction, and cultivation, Mo Na Ye was spared from any serious injuries. Just some minor burns.","The twins opened their eyes and saw their handiwork, a little proud of themselves.","As for Mo Na Ye, he was grateful that he had sent them deep into enemy territory. If these two menaces had been at the direct frontline, who knows how many Black Ink Clansmen they would have accidentally killed?","“Do the two of you only know how to envelop yourselves in Purifying Light?” Mo Na Ye had his eyebrows wrinkled as he asked. Though, when he thought about it, he had never seen the twins do anything else but blast out Purifying Light in all directions.","Needless to say, his guess was spot on.","“If not around us, where would the light go?” Yang Xu questioned back. After all, the blast would naturally just envelop them. This was not so much how they willed it to be, but just how it normally worked.","Truth be told, the twins had never really practiced how to use Purifying Light. They just knew how to unleash this power using the Sun and Moon Marks on their respective hands.","To be fair, they were not trained on how to use it because Little Eleven saw no need for them to do so. After all, except for those that were made up of Black Ink Strength, Purifying Light had no effect on them. In other words, blasting it all around them would do nothing to Little Eleven nor the twins. Furthermore, with how many Crystals the twins had received, spamming Purifying Light could be said to be an encouraged course of action.","Since the natural way Purifying Light was used would envelop its caster, the way the twins used it could be said to be perfect. They were practically walking geneades, and each cast would both protect them and attack their enemies.","If Mo Na Ye knew about this, he would certainly curse the other Holy One. Though, such thoughts were prohibited, and they were quickly wiped from his mind.","He could only sigh as he advised, “During the war, your Father had managed to concentrate the Purifying Light into different shapes. Blasting it all around you is too much of a waste. From now on, try to concentrate on only blasting what is in front of you. That way, you won’t take down our allies as well...”","Yang Xu gave a nod, while Yang Ji covered his mouth and chuckled a little.","After all, Mo Na Ye’s current appearance was a little ridiculous, since bits of his clothes had been burned off, with his hair also messy and puffed up.","Silavin: Okay, most of the setup is done. Onto the war."]},{"number":6043,"title":"Chapter 6043, Space Principles","paragraphs":["Chapter 6043, Space Principles","Author: Silavin","*Rumble*","Without any time to clean up, Mo Na Ye could sense a huge wave of enemies approaching from the frontlines. Though not maximised to its greatest potential, the Purifying Light release would still be deemed the greatest threat here, and he had already anticipated this would happen.","He took out his Small Black Nest to order those from the frontlines to retreat while he charged out to the front. It was his optimistic hope to have the enemies pincered, but he would rather prioritise the lives of his men now with how unskilled the children were.","This change in priority clearly highlights the change in the present Black Ink Clan compared to the past, where lives were just numbers. Mo Na Ye personally was thankful that this had changed.","Still, his war-like demeanour had not changed as he charged out to the front, taking on any enemies that came his way.","“Follow me from behind and just keep blasting Purifying Light. Keep practicing! Don’t worry about me.” Mo Na Ye roared as in his hand formed a sharp javelin made of Black Ink Strength. When the twins sensed it for that brief moment he held onto it, they could have sworn it was no different in hardness to Eighth-Order Metal Ores.","Once Mo Na Ye threw it, it flew so fast they could have sworn it had disappeared for a moment.","*Boom!*","The very next second, the javelin struck the ground and blew up, creating a massive creator.","It was an explosion made purely from the potential energy within the javelin.","Mo Na Ye had to tweak the way he fought here. He was no longer dealing with Humans, after all. When he fought against Human, the corruptive effects of Black Ink Strength was something that the enemy feared. However, when dealing with his own kind, such effects played a minor role.","His own people, or those hailed from the Holy Ones, were all influenced by Black Ink Strength. However, such influences were limited to their mental and emotional state. It would not be enough to kill them. Therefore, in duals between Black Ink Clansmen, fights were mostly done through physical means. Black Ink Strength might supplement as weapons, or footholds, but they could not be used the same way as when dealing with Humans.","Naturally, with how tough those hailed from the Holy Ones were, Mo Na Ye knew that one release was not enough.","Each time he pulled his arm back, another javelin would form and he would toss it again. He did so repeatedly, creating tremors while running forward.","*Boom! Boom! Boom!*","The twins behind followed suit and ran, also releasing Purifying Light whenever they could. However, tried as they might, most ended up the same, with the light enveloping them.","Ironically, while Mo Na Ye was dealing with the enemies, all they did was practice. In fact, they had not even hurt a single fly. All they were doing was terraforming the land to create more meaningless craters. They could not help but wonder if they were even necessary.","As for Mo Na Ye, who was at the front, he would always keep his distance from them. Otherwise, he too would get burned by the light. Still, there was another reason why he remained at the front, a distance away from them.","“Quickly! Set up your Defensive Array!” Mo Na Ye roared and in his hands quickly formed a long spear this time.","Rather than throwing forward, he held his weapon tightly with both hands as his feet dug into the ground. The very next instant, he leaped, flying so fast the twins did not even manage to catch where he went.","The next thing they knew, a huge blast, stronger than all the previous ones, erupted a distance away from them. The wind pressure from it was so strong, they could feel their bodies getting pushed back even from this distance.","Yang Ji was the one to react. He took out an Array Plate and immediately injected his Qi into it.","A Protective Array was formed, a barrier to shield them from the elements. However, even this was not enough to prevent worry from eating away at them. After all, every wind blast was accompanied by overt ripples on the protective barrier.","Though Yang Ji and Yang Xu knew the Protective Array would still hold, the aftermath of a true exchange between a Royal Lord and an enemy of his equal was nevertheless just as terrifying. This was a battle they knew they would not be able to participate in.","It made them all the more question why they were brought here.","Still, they knew they had a task to do.","An irreplaceable task. This was why, despite their low cultivation realm, they were still tossed to the frontlines.","“You think you can do it?” Yang Ji asked, as he gave a forced smile. Despite wanting to seem calm in front of his Sister, cracks still showed.","“Not without being able to concentrate the Purifying Light blast into a beam...” Yang Xu replied, as she also forced a smile.","“Then, you have a clue how we can concentrate Purifying Light into a beam?” Yang Ji asked, a little hopeful.","Yang Xu gave a small nod, “We can’t manipulate it using our Qi or Divine Sense. Purifying Light just passes through everything.”","Yang Ji, seeming to get what she was hinting at, suddenly added with her at the same time.","“”We need to use Space Principles.””","Yang Xu gave a nod. That was the conclusion she had come to. After all, since Mo Na Ye said that their Father could do it, it had to be something that their Father could do at that time. Though they did not know the full history of the war, they knew that their Father had only mastered the 3000 Daos close to the end of the war. Yet, Purifying Light was introduced quite early on once he joined the cause. It had played a pivotal role in the war, and Artifacts were built to help aid the Humans in their crusade.","However, Mo Na Ye had specifically said that their Father was able to manipulate Purifying Light. This was without an Artifact. That could only mean one thing – if Qi and Divine Sense did not work – he had manipulated it through using Space Principles.","Unfortunately, this was where they were stumped. The twins could not currently manipulate Space Principles while in this world. The World Principles here were just too different from the outside world.","That was when Yang Ji got a brilliant idea. “Maybe she knows how to manipulate Space Principles here?”","“She?” Yang Xu tilted her head, slightly confused.","“You know, the little worm.” Yang Ji said while already reaching out for his inner chest pocket.","“Why would she know anything?” Yang Xu could not help but step away as she questioningly asked.","“Well, she isn’t an Artifact that is tied to my Soul. Yet, she can enter and exit my Dantian as she pleases. Isn’t that something akin to teleportation – like, how we travel through the Void?” Yang Ji stated as he used his index finger to poke her awake.","Yang Xu gave a contemplative expression. She certainly could not deny that it was a possibility. She had been so used to seeing Artifacts coming out of a cultivator that she forgot living creatures were not supposed to be able to do that. In fact, unless they had a Small Universe, cultivators could not possibly store living creatures within their bodies. However, she and her Brother were only in the Dao Source Realm. They definitely did not have a Small Universe in their body. Yet, this thing could go in and out of her Brother like his flesh did not even exist, and settle in his Dantian.","The little worm seemed reluctant to awaken at first. However, with all the constant poking, she eventually relented and woke up with tired eyes.","Maybe because she had been sleeping for so long, she seemed like she was in a receptive mood.","Yang Ji quickly asked her, “Hey, little one, can you tell me how you manage to manipulate the Space Principles here?”"]},{"number":6044,"title":"Chapter 6044, Difference Between Realms","paragraphs":["Chapter 6044, Difference Between Realms","Author: Silavin","The little worm thought for a moment. She seems to contemplate what to ask for in return.","Strangely, though seemingly powerful, she did not extend her Divine Sense to communicate her will. In fact, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not sense her cultivation. Though, that would not be too strange as this little thing had just been ‘born?’ ‘created?’ just days ago.","Instead, after a brief moment, the little worm seemed to have made a decision and started to open its small mouth. From it, black flames started to spew forth. However, these were not ordinary flames. They bore no heat, and only seemed to reassemble flames in appearance.","Whether heat was lacking due to them not meaning to hurt anyone was unimportant at this moment, as these flames were created to form words in front of the boy.","‘Soul replenishing Pills’","“Huh? You want Pills that replenish the Soul?” Yang Ji asked in confirmation, and Yang Xu took out a few bottles from her Space Ring.","These Pills were made by their Mother Ning Chang. Though they were not her children by blood, it could be said that Ning Chang was the one of those who pampered them the most. If she was not refining Pills, she would always be on their side. Even when she was pregnant, she would alway spare time to play with them. Even after her first child was born, she still provided them with the same amount of attention. In fact, Ning Chang was like this to all the children.","Out of all the Mothers, Ning Chang was definitely the most liked among the children. If not for how gentle and accepting she was, there were always the insurmountable Pills that she always gave them.","It had to be noted that these Pills were always those of the highest grade, with many of them having Pill Veins. They were priceless outside, but she would give her children Pills like they were food – not candy because that was just how much she gave them.","At some point, the material use became so much that other Alchemists of High Heaven Palace wanted to raise a complaint to the Sect Master, Yang Kai. However, what could they do when she used the proceeds of the Pills she sold outside to purchase materials for the Pills she made for the children?","Naturally, that meant that the twins had plenty of Pills, especially those that healed. With how fast their injuries heal, they did not ever need to use such Pills. Yet, these Pills had accumulated over time, with Ning Chang’s excitement to always give them something each time they saw her. Eventually, bottles became mountains...","And since they were twins, and the oldest of all the children, Ning Chang probably gave them the most Pills out of everyone...","In short, they were not short on Pills. Taking out these few bottles of High Rank Seventh-Order Divine Soul Restoration Pills would not make their inventory seem any fewer.","Yang Xu quickly opened up a bottle and a scent that invigorated one’s Soul immediately spread out. The little worm naturally noticed this first as she immediately turned towards Yang Xu. However, instead of pouncing and taking whatever she wanted, the little worm seem to have some grace and awaited for the transaction to be approved. Stll, her eyes certainly glowed with a strange light, as though she was looking at a golden goose.","This actually made Yang Xu raise her eyebrow. “Say, why do you need these Pills for? Your Soul couldn’t have been damaged since you were just born.”","The little worm gave a small scoff, as if to say, ‘what does a little girl like you know?’","Naturally, the twins could not read her mind, and could only await her response in gestures or words. So, the little worm’s reaction did not garner any reaction from them. Still, Yang Xu for some reason felt an instinctive urge to crush this little shit.","Still, Yang Xu did not act on instinct and awaited the little worm’s response.","More black flames came out, ‘I need them for my own use.’","“So, in short, you are unwilling to say, huh?” Yang Xu’s eyes sharpened. However, that was when Yang Ji stepped in.","“Okay, I think that’s enough. We don’t have time to deal with this right now. If you want to hide things from us, fine. All of us have our own secrets. Our most pressing thing right now is to survive. If we can’t use Space Principles, if a second Royal Lord comes, we are dead.” Yang Ji coldly stated, as if to stop the sparks between a worm and a little girl from further intensifying.","“Fine. Here you go.” Yang Xu did not want to quarrel with her Brother here. She also did not wish to get close to the worm so she used her Qi to direct the Pills out of the bottle, towards the little worm.","The little worm, seeing how they had backed off, gave a nod of acknowledgement. This was her way of showing some semblance of respect to the two who respected her boundaries.","She opened her mouth and took in the massive Pills into her body with a few gulps.","Seeming to be satisfied, the little worm flew towards Yang Ji’s forehead and rested her tail in between his eyebrows.","Immediately, fragments of knowledge started to engrave themselves in his mind. He felt a pang of pain and his hands moved up to clench his head. However, it was as quick to end as it had begun.","Soon, he commented with light in his eyes, enlightened by it. “I see. So that’s how it is done...”","The little worm, seeming a little proud of what she had done, was turning her head towards the girl. She was awaiting the scenario where the Little Sister would also ask her to teach. In return, she could ask for more Pills. However, that did not happen, as Yang Xu immediately showcased mastery over using Space Principles here.","Yang Xu spread her delicate fingers, but the space between them seemed to distort. Eventually, it cracked, creating a spider web-like crack in the air.","Yang Xu smiled and then looked over to the little worm, as if mocking, ‘think you were going to take advantage of me huh?’","The little worm looked away and scoffed, obviously unamused by this turn of events. In her mind, she was confused how Yang Xu had already mastered it so quickly.","It had to be said that the application of Space Principles was difficult as it was related to the Dao of Space – one of the most esoteric Daos. Still, the twins already had great mastery over the Dao of Time and the Dao of Space. It was just that this place had different World Principles. Thus, they could not fully apply what they knew to manipulate the Space Principles here.","Still, it was not like the two places had completely different World Principles. There were some similarities. The main difference being that over here, the World Principles were more obscure, with a mix of Spiritual Energy mixed into it. It felt like the World Principles here were each a world of their own, with a ‘Will’ of their own.","Still, these ‘Wills’ were weak. Yang Ji and Yang Xu just had to infuse a certain level of Spiritual Energy, and willed their Divine Sense to do the action in that area of Space before trying to manipulate the Space Principles there.","It was certainly tougher to manipulate Space Principles here. However, it was still manageable for the two.","That being said, typically, it would take a lot more time to master it. Much less, without the little worm’s guidance, it should have been impossible to notice this difference. Thus, the little worm was confused how Yang Xu was able to accomplish this feat without her input.","Though frustrated, the little worm did not show it. She still had her pride to uphold. If she wanted to show any frustration, she would do it in her down space. In other words, Yang Ji’s Dantian.","Since there was nothing left for her to do, the little worm slipped away from the twins. Not even bothering to bid farewell. She just disappeared from sight once the twins were not looking at her. Right now, all she wanted to do was to cultivate with the Pills she had just gotten.","Meanwhile, Yang Xu looked at Yang Ji and asked, “Don’t you find that thing suspicious?”","Yang Ji rolled his eyes, and replied. “Of course I do. But, it is a fact that we currently need her. Though I have no assurances, I don’t feel like she bears any ill-intent. So, I’m just going to remain hopeful. Eitherways, I have you to help me if I get into trouble right?”","Yang Xu pouted and gave a nod. She thought of how sly her Brother was. [When he puts it like that, I can’t really complain. How unfair...]"]},{"number":6045,"title":"Chapter 6045, The Beam That Marked The Start","paragraphs":["Chapter 6045, The Beam That Marked The Start","Author: Silavin","*Boom! Boom! Boom!*","While they were conversing, the sounds of explosive clashes seemed to be getting closer. This would mean that Mo Na Ye was being pushed back.","“Seems like we don’t have much time. You got this?” Yang Ji asked.","“Of course.” Yang Xu responded as she took out two Sixth-Order Crystals this time. [Best to start with something small.]","Since she did not know what extent the Space Principles she employed could perform, she started with the lowest grade of Crystals. She held them in both hands, the right at the top and the left as the bottom. When she started to activate Purifying Light, her hands were gently spaced apart, with the two Crystals floated up, in between her cupped hands.","Yang Ji could see that in between her hands and the Crystals, the Space within started to distort. Eventually, from the side, it would have seemed as if there were no Crystals at all.","Since the Purifying Light explosion was going to spread out in all directions, and they had no control over it, they just needed to change the definition of ‘all direction’. Yang Xu was demonstrating this first hand, with the Crystals only visible from the front. In any other direction, one would not be able to see the Crystals between her small hands.","*Ziiii* At the very next moment, a thick laser beam was released. It was about the thickness of a fist, and it shot straight through, cutting down anything in its path. Like always, the Protective Array did not hinder it, as it passed through and struck the ground at full force.","Like oil and water, anything the laser touched seemed to split apart. Though, it was more accurate to say that they immediately disintegrated upon contact.","Yang Xu just moved her arm a little, and the laser beam slid through the ground, creating a large cut in it.","Once the energy of the two Crystals had been exhausted, the beam ceased and the Crystals broke down into dust. Yang Xu, not wanting to dirty her hands, simply sent whatever remnants were left to the Void.","“Oh? This place is even connected to the Void?” Yang Ji exclaimed, with a small thought in mind. [I wonder if that means we can go back home through the Void?]","“No. The Void here is strange. This is not the usual Void that we know of.” Yang Xu, seeming to have read his mind, answered. She looked further ahead at her handiwork, amazed at the destruction.","There, in front of them, lay a flat land with a deep ravine. It was so deep, that even at their distance, their Divine Sense could not perceive its bottom.","This deep ravine stretched into the distance in a straight line, creating a sight as though the ground had been slashed by a Deity.","Yang Xu, amazed at what a pair of Sixth-Order Crystals could do, exclaimed, “I did all that? It wasn’t even that difficult.”","“Oh? You mean to say that you would be able to do it with Ninth-Order Crystals as well?” Yang Ji asked. He too wanted to give it a shot.","“I’m not so sure about that. We need to try it out to be sure. Brother, why don’t you give it a go?” Yang Xu asked in return.","“Sure-” Yang Ji smiled and excitedly took out two Ninth-Order Crystals before speaking. However, before he could do anything, his words were cut off by the quaking ground. It felt as though the whole world was awakening from their eternal slumber!","*Rumble*","Yang Ji immediately turned to look around. With the Array Plate in his other hand, he looked towards his Sister and moved his chin to indicate what they needed to do.","She jumped up into the air, to the top of the Protective Array, and scanned her surroundings.","“What the. There is something coming out from the ground!” Yang Xu exclaimed as she could see something moving in the ravine she had created. It was huge, far bigger than them by thousands of times. Still, in the crack within the earth, it seemed to be moving unfettered.","What it was, Yang Xu could not tell – it was simply that big.","“Why don’t you try blasting it?” Yang Ji joked.","“Are you crazy? How in the world are we going to take that thing on?”","Yang Ji shook his head. The way he saw it, if that thing was their enemy, they would eventually need to overcome it. Moreover, they were now in enemy territory. Mo Na Ye was engaging with a Royal Lord, blocking their route to escape back. Furthermore, Mo Na Ye took the fight to the enemy to make sure there was some distance from them. Worse, they would have to get past enemy lines to return back. In short, what else could they do but fight?","Certainly, being able to use Space Principles again meant that they were able to escape most situations. However, they were still restricted in its use. Yang Ji estimates that they would be doomed if they met a Territory Lord.","He turned to her, floated up and passed her the Array Plate, saying. “Alright. It’s fine if you don’t want to do it. But, I want to give it a shot.”","Yang Xu took the Array Plate and injected more Qi into it, strengthening the Protective Array. She sighed. She knew at this point, there was no changing his mind. Though reckless, she had to admit he was capable. All she could do now was to ensure their safety while he focused on attacking.","*Rumble* The trembling of the ground intensified, and a small portion of the gigantic figure could be seen erupting from the ground. It had an elongated body, similar to that of a maggot, with multiple legs of dozens. Each ‘foot’ looked like hands, with nails that were closer to claws.","On the small portion that was exposed, on its sides, were gigantic bumps. Occasionally, black gas would leak through, if not a liquid that poured and hardened once it touched the ground.","Its head, which was at the peak, lacked eyes. However, there were gigantic jaws that seemed capable of tearing countries apart.","By all accounts, this creature was disgusting to look at. It was more unfortunate that the twin had to use their Divine Sense in this place, getting a ‘clearer look’ of it.","Yang Xu gulped when she first saw that thing. As for Yang Ji, he gave a long exhale and made the same pose as what Yang Xu did earlier. This time, he directly used Ninth-Order Crystals.","“Die!” Yang Ji roared as an even more intense laser shot out. This time, it was the thickness of an entire torso.","As his arms trembled from containing the force, the beam struck true to its target.","*Rarrrrrrrrr!* An unholy screech rang out as the creature felt its body being pierced through. Its skins and flesh served no function in protecting it, as the searing pain tore through it like molten steel. The pain erupted from the point of impact, spreading outward in violent waves that sent violent convulsions through its massive frame. Each pulse of agony brought fresh torment, as if liquid fire had been injected directly into its nervous system.","Under the unbearable pain, the beast’s massive body began to betray it. The precise control it once commanded dissolving into erratic spasms as the earth it hid under was torn asunder.","Land, the size of cities, was uprooted, and cracks spread out throughout the land.","The Purifying Light scorched through its body. Yang Ji intended to slowly move the laser towards its head. However, due to its spasm, he missed, creating a horizontal line out rather than slicing it into two.","*Rarrrrrr!* Another screech came as it fell to the ground, escaping its torment. Seemingly a little elated, it took a second to regain itself. Still, this was not over – far from it. This beast soon turns to face the source, towards its tormentor, emitting killing intent that could crush bones into dust.","As for the twins, they felt cold sweat dripping down their backs.","...","On that day, a white light shone, seemingly piercing the Heavens. With this dark world as its backdrop, even from afar, all could see it. Some felt fear, some felt interest, some felt hope, and some felt grief.","Be that as it may, this marked the turning point. The war between the three remnants had reached its peak, and a new factor had come in to turn the tide.","All three, along with their Royal Lords, looked towards the sky as the gears of change had finally started to move."]},{"number":6046,"title":"Chapter 6046, Fatal Blow","paragraphs":["Chapter 6046, Fatal Blow","Author: Silavin","The supposed wound that they dealt was slowly stitching back together. Like threads, a black liquid seeped out from its wound and slowly hardened to create a new layer. This procedure repeated as the opening seemed to gradually become smaller.","Seeing this scene, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not help but worry if their attack had not done anything. In fact, they might have just enraged this beast, causing their downfall.","As this monster faced them, these two tiny beings, the difference in their size was only further highlighted. It was fortunate that the Protective Array was up. Otherwise, with how much killing intent was being pressed down upon them, the twins might have crumbled to their knees.","Yet, despite its overwhelming advantage, the monstrosity chose not to get any closer.","Its instinct was screaming warnings at it – these two absolutely could not be underestimated. Despite their small stature, that one attack had nearly ended its life. However, there was also another compelling force inside of it. A drive to want to destroy everything. A madness that it could not contain.","A madness which drove it to continue its slaughter.","Ignoring its injury, the monster concentrated all its energy towards its jaws.","A black ball of concentrated Black Ink Strength gathered, charging up for a full release.","At this distance, it could not possibly miss!","Not even a second later, a black beam fired, completely opposite to the white beam from before.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu wanted to react but they had failed to do so. In fact, they had not thought it would release a counter attack so soon.","The black beam struck true to its target. It struck the Protective Array surrounding the twins.","Ripples formed on the thin barrier around them, as small web-like cracks spread out. The force of the beam also pushed them back, further into enemy territory.","*Crack* A sound of something cracking could be heard. It came not from their bones but the Protective Array around them!","Yang Xu saw this and immediately panicked. She injected more Qi into the Array Plate. Even if they were not afraid of Black Ink Strength corrupting them, the force of this beam was certainly something they could not possibly take on. A direct hit might as well have been fatal. She could not help but call out to Yang Ji, “Brother, do something!”","Yang Ji took out two more Ninth-Order Crystals. Once more, he clasped them in his hands and released another beam of Purifying Light!","The white and black collided. One filled with vibrance while the other filled with agony. The former was about the thickness of an arm, while the latter was as thick as a Human body.","One would have expected a battle between two great powers. However, that was far from reality. Purifying Light sliced through the black beam like it was nothing, shooting straight through. This time, it was the monster who did not have time to react.","Despite the increase in distance, this beam was more concentrated that the last. Unbeknownst to the monster, it had travelled inside its own attack almost unnoticed. When it finally noticed something was off, it was already too late. The beam had already shot through its head.","Unhindered by the mass in front of it, the beam shot through all ‘organs’ it faced, exiting out of the back of the monster.","However, Yang Ji felt this was not enough. With a flick of his wrist, the beam shot down, slicing through space like a blade.","The monster, unable to even so much as raise a roar, got split in two. Its regeneration, no matter how effective, failed to cease its demise. There, it collapsed to the ground, unable to raise any resistance.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu saw the result with wide eyes. Though they had expected the might of a Ninth-Order Purifying Light to be effective, they had not expected it to be this effective. Furthermore, the ground beneath, where the monster stood, had a deep cut as though the abyss had been created.","Both twins could not help but wonder how far this beam had shot to. If it had even reached back to Mo?","Still, it had to be said that at this point, Yang Ji had given his all to condense the Purifying Light into that single dense beam. It was no thicker than an arm, but it had sapped him of so much energy, he felt faint.","Yang Xu had noticed and quickly held her arm out to support him.","However, Yang Ji, always the one to put up a front, said, “I’m fine. No need to worry.”","He closed his eyes, took a deep breath, and did one circulation of Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique. Warm Qi immediately flowed from his Dantian through his whole body, making him feel completely refreshed.","He turned around and smiled back at her, “I have you with me, after all.”","Yang Xu rolled her eyes at him. However, the joy in her eyes could not be hidden.","With the Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique, they two were as one. Qi sharing was the most basic of applications. In a way, what Yang Ji said was just facts. Though, what one wants to hear was entirely different.","Yang Ji looked towards the monster that had just fallen and indicated to his Sister, “Hey, let’s go forward to take a look.”","“En” Yang Xu gave a nod. However, this time, before she even began to take another step forward, she already took out a pair of Blue and Yellow Crystals. This time, she had prepared Ninth-Order ones, in case something unexpected were to happen.","With Yang Xu leading the front, along with the Array Plate one on hand and the Crystal on the other, they ‘soon’ arrived at the monster.","‘Soon’ being a couple of minutes of flying at their fastest speed. They were not able to tear through Space to the outside while in this Protective Array. Within it, they were still able to do it. Furthermore, that was just how far that monster had pushed them back with its one beam attack.","Not waiting to even lower the Protective Array for even a second, Yang Xu had led Yang Ji to fly over.","Taking in its grandeur, even if just a pair of gigantic carcasses, Yang Xu could not help but ask, curious, “What cultivation realm do you think it was in?”","At their current cultivation realm, they could not even begin to fathom what kind of monstrosity this thing was. Unlike Mo Na Ye, who they were previously aware of from their Father, and thus knew of his cultivation realm, this was an entirely new unknown entity.","“Maybe a Feudal Lord?” Yang Ji guessed, though he was questioning his Sister in his mind. [What are you asking me for? Neither of us would know. We don’t know anyone who is weaker than a Royal Lord...]","“Not a Territory Lord?” Yang Xu asked in return, also doubting.","“Well, we both know that it is at least not a Royal Lord. It must be weaker. For now, how about we leave it as that before we ask Mo Na Ye?” Yang Ji said as he moved closer to the thin protective barrier, trying to get a good look at the carcass."]},{"number":6047,"title":"Chapter 6047, Ambush","paragraphs":["Chapter 6047, Ambush","Author: Silavin","As Yang Ji was about an arms’ length away from the protective barrier, they could hear a sudden scream.","“Get away!”","The next moment, they tried to look up, to the source of the voice, they sensed something flash by.","*Boom! Boom!*","It was too fast for them to even perceive. Before they could even react, two explosion came. One was behind them and one was directly in front of them!","Right now, in front of their eyes, the carcass had splatted and dust bloomed all around. Something had crashed down upon it with such velocity, nothing of it had remained. Even those crystalised bits, hardened from the monsters’ liquid, shattered into dust. The impact was so bad, the shockwaves pushed the protective barrier back a few metres.","As for the thing that landed behind them, it did not cause that much destruction. It had crashed faster than the one in front, but that was all.","Nevertheless, due to the protective barrier suddenly being pushed back, Yang Ji, who was facing up at the time, had his chin struck back by the barrier. He got thrown back along with the barrier, landing quite a distance away from where he originally stood.","As for Yang Xu, who was at the centre, she too got pushed back.","Her grip on the two Crystals tightened even further as she awaited the dust to settle.","The one behind cleared up first. It was a familiar weapon, something akin to a javelin. Judging from that voice they had heard, it must have been thrown by Mo Na Ye.","As for the one at the front...","Though its figure had not been exposed, it had flashed forward. Cutting through the dust, heading straight towards them.","From the short moment they could catch its figure, they could see a large being with four arms. Each arm seemed to have been covered with a thick exoskeleton, with hands the size of watermelons. It had a pair of thick, well defined legs that had more joints that a Human’s leg. Its feet were claw-like, sharp to the point not even metal would be able to put up any resistance.","Its torso and head seemed to be combined, with no neck, but it had a thicker exoskeleton around these vital areas that stopped around its waist.","As for its face, it was strangely Human-like, with a pair of eyes, ears, nose and mouth. However, they were oddly spaced, giving one the sense of seeing something alien.","This monster rushed out in an instant and using one of its four arms, it delivered a devastating punch.","In the face of its fist, even the protective barrier could not hope to hold up. In fact, the barrier shattered at the moment of contact, as if it could not even hope to put up any resistance.","Unhindered, the punch went through. Its target, the one operating the Array, and was on the verge of launching another blast of Purifying Light – Yang Xu!","Caught off guard, Yang Xu had no time to react. This attack came at her too quickly.","It was Yang Ji, who was just in front of her, who managed to react. He had moved beforehand once he felt something was off. In fact, earlier than when this monster had started its charge.","Unfortunately, he was too weak. The gap between them was too much to overcome. He knew that all too well. So, he instinctively sought not to clash against this monster but to prevent his Sister from getting hurt.","He turned around and dashed towards her. At the same time, he manipulated the surrounding Space Principles, all focused around Yang Xu.","Behind her, a Void Crack appeared. However, she seemed to not be moving. It was uncertain whether she was in too much of a shock to react or otherwise.","However, Yang Ji took no chances. He directly pushed her into the Void Crack, along with himself.","*Cii*","Once they both disappeared inside the Void Crack, Yang Ji originally thought that they were safe. However, he soon felt his left arm was strangely warm.","As he registered the warmth in his left arm, his senses gradually sharpened. The warmth was not comforting – it was spreading, wet and alarming. He looked down. There, he saw nothing but blood seeping down. What was supposed to be his hand had disappeared, and all that was left was liquid red.","The sight did not immediately connect with sensation. There was a strange disconnect between seeing the blood and feeling the injury. Then, the pain arrived. It was not a sudden jolt, but a rising tide. It started as a dull throb and quickly intensified into a searing heat that radiated from what remained.","The warmth of his own blood contrasted sickeningly with the cold sweat breaking out across his forehead. His breathing became shallow and rapid as shock began to set in. However, the circumstances proved too dire for him to fall right now.","He first cut off Yang Xu’s senses from his. The least he could do was to not let her notice for now.","He did not even make a sound. He just clenched his teeth from the searing pain and focused on the task at hand. [I can’t lose consciousness here damn it! I can’t!]","However, how could his Sister not notice? She had personally seen the moment his hand got taken from him before the Void Crack closed. Even the warm sensation was seared into her heart as the feeling suddenly got cut off.","She bit her lip, frustrated that she failed to protect him, while he had gotten injured in her place.","She wished she could cut the enemy into a thousand pieces, but she knew that she was currently too weak. Else, why would they have to hide in this eerie void?","Right now, all they could hope for was to escape. They were definitely not a match against that thing.","Unfortunately, even that proved difficult as two robust hands suddenly punched into the Void.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could feel their hearts leap into their mouths as the supposedly closed Void Crack had started to be pried open.","Thankfully, Yang Xu had already been primed with the Crystals this time. Though afraid, anger won out as she initiated a concentrated blast of Purifying Light.","The beam struck true to its target. The monster lost its grip and got pushed back.","Yang Ji, not waiting for another second, once the Purifying Light beam ended, he immediately manipulated Space Principles into sealing off the Void Crack.","Seeming as though the danger had passed, Yang Xu immediately called out, “Brother!”","However, Yang Ji struck out his right hand, indicating to her to stop. This was clearly not over yet.","Compared to the large monster they had first dealt with, this one was far tougher. The earlier blast had only blown it back but had not killed it. It might be injured, but Yang Ji knew that even with injuries, the gap in their strength was far too wide. It could still easily kill them.","If Yang Ji was not mistaken, this must be the strength of a Royal Lord!"]},{"number":6048,"title":"Chapter 6048, Retreat","paragraphs":["Chapter 6048, Retreat","Author: Silavin","A Royal Lord, a being that fought on par with Ninth-Order Open Heaven Realm Masters. For Yang Ji and Yang Xu, there was already a huge chasm between them and Open Heaven Realm Masters, what more someone on par with those of the Ninth-Order!","Masters of this cultivation realm were the main pillars of every Sect. Even in High Heaven Palace, there were not many of them. Not even all their Mothers were in this Realm. From what the twins knew, only their Biological Mother, Su Yan, was in the Ninth-Order.","If someone were to ask them if they could ever compete with their Mother, they would absolutely say no. This was even with her going easy on them, and with them being able to apply Bloodline Suppression.","Right now, they had no way of dealing with a Royal Lord. Their only saving grace would be their mastery over the Dao of Space, but even that was not foolproof against such overwhelming force.","Certainly, at that level, breaking open the barriers of Space should be an easy feat. So, the twins were far from safe even if they hid out inside the Void.","As for Purifying Light, the result had already been shown earlier. Yang Xu had blasted the enemy with Ninth-Order Crystals but it was not enough to kill it. In fact, that blast was a lucky shot. If that Royal Lord had been more alert, and was not busy tearing open the Void Crack, it would not have been caught by that attack with its speed.","Aware of how grave the situation was, Yang Ji could never allow himself to let down his guard. The searing pain on his left arm just served to remind him of how he needed to stay on his toes.","He quickly pressed down his pressure points to stop the bleeding and looked towards the Void Crack with eagle-like eyes, narrowed as though he was trying to peer through it. He kept staring as he told Yang Xu, “We need to get out of here. We cannot afford to engage with that thing.”","Yang Xu nodded and started to manipulate Space Principles. She was trying to create a path for them to move through. Unfortunately, this was not like their world. Moving through the Void here felt like moving through Tar. It took quite some effort just to move a couple of metres.","Thankfully, judging from the more clustered Space Nodes here, these few metres would be hundreds of metres outside. It might be a small distance in comparison to their world, but here, it was still faster than if they flew.","Yang Xu continued to push through the Void, and Yang Xu followed behind with his back turned towards her. Naturally, this was for the sake of their own safety. After all, though the Royal Lord could break through the barriers of Space with their own strength, that did not mean they would be able to find them so easily.","Right now, the easiest way for the Royal Lord to go after them was to break open where the Void Crack was. Though sealed, how could Yang Ji’s seal possibly defend against a Royal Lord? Yang Ji just hoped what he did would slow it down, even a second would be great.","Time trickled by as seconds turned into minutes.","Eventually, Yang Ji and Yang Xu arrived at a nearby Space Node, and Yang Xu asked, “Should we take a peek at where we are? We are quite a distance away at this point.”","Yang Ji was a little hesitant. That was to be expected. After all, he did not know the capabilities of this Royal Lord. If they could hide out in the Void, that would be the safest. However, at this distance, they would have travelled outside of where their Divine Sense had covered.","Typically, at their cultivation realm, their Divine Sense would cover a massive area, far larger than they could teleport to. They would be able to identify Space Nodes from the outside, and use it as a guide to where they wanted to go.","But here, it was different. Their Divine Sense was also being restrained. So, they definitely could not sense too far a distance. At this point, if they continued forth in this strange viscous Void, they might really get lost. However, if they do tear open a Void Crack, they would be exposing themselves to the risk of getting detected. In that case, all the distance they had covered would be for naught.","Yang Xu naturally knew all of this beforehand, and asked him for a decision.","“Check it.” Yang Ji said with a sigh.","“En” Yang Xu nods and with a slash of her hand, *Cii*, a Void Crack was torn open. She knew the task – the moment she tore it open, she was going to close it back up again. For that brief breath that it was open, both were going to do a quick scan of the area.","Yang Xu did a quick grasp with her hand and the Void Crack was sealed once more.","Both heaved a sigh of relief that the Royal Lord was not around. Also, from the Space Nodes, they could tell that they were so far heading in the right direction. They strayed a little off course but it had not been too severe.","“That was clos-” Just as Yang Ji was about to complete his sentence, a *Piang* sound broke out.","It was from the very spot they had just opened a Void Crack at. When he looked towards the source, he could see something sharp penetrating through. He could not make out what it was as only five centimetres had been exposed. Nevertheless, he was not going to take the risk.","Yang Ji immediately took Yang Xu’s hand and they both desperately tried to push through the viscous Void to get away. Unfortunately, the harder they tried, the greater the Void resisted their advance.","*Clack* Another sound came, and this time, the seal on the Void Crack had been completely undone.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt their heart drop at that moment and their already frantic movement became even more panic-stricken.","A sigh soon broke out, “stop panicking. I’ve driven it away. So, come out.”","There, a familiar face appeared right at the Void Crack. Yang Ji and Yang Xu had never seen a face they wished so dearly to see, but at the same time, not look at. Mo Na Ye was not ugly by any means, just that his innocent smile was so sinister looking, the twins would rather not look at it.","The twins immediately took a deep breath to calm down and Yang Xu asked, “So, is it safe for us to go out now?”","“Relatively.” Mo Na Ye was not going to lie at this point. They were technically still in enemy territory. Furthermore, with how grand of a display the twins showcased earlier, it would not be surprising for them to face more enemies. Regardless, it was best for them to move together.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both looked at each other and gave a nod. Yang Xu was the one to take the lead this time, and she went out first. Yang Ji soon followed suit and exited the Void Crack.","Like what they had sensed earlier, they were a distance away from where that gigantic monster was taken down. In fact, with their Divine Sense, they would barely detect it from this distance. As for their surroundings, it was a dull flat land, one which seemed to span infinitely. There were no trees, no nothing – desolation would be a fitting description for this place.","Mo Na Ye took out something hanging from his waist. It was the left hand that the Royal Lord had severed. Unprotected by Yang Ji, exposed to the elements, it had already turned pitched black, as if completely infested by Black Ink Strength.","Mo Na Ye apologised, “I failed to keep you two safe. For that, I apologise.”","He handed over the hand to Yang Ji, but instead of putting it back on, the boy stored it inside his Space Ring. He took a look, saw Mo Na Ye’s strange expression, and felt like he had to explain, “I’ve already stopped the bleeding. Even without a hand, it won’t affect anything. I’m not planning to fight with my fists. We are also out in the open right now. I can’t focus on recuperating at this point, right?”","Mo Na Ye relented, “You’re right. The situation here is far stranger than I thought. I did not expect to meet another Royal Lord here of all places. But, I do have to thank you two. Without that beam of Purifying Light, I would not have been able to get behind it and dealt a powerful blow, piercing through its torso.”","“So, is that Royal Lord dead?” Yang Xu asked, glad the enemy got bested. At least she had contributed in getting revenge for her Brother.","“Unfortunately, no. For those of the same cultivation realm, it is extremely hard for us to kill them. A battle for days might not even settle it. Still, with the injuries it had sustained, years of recuperation would be necessary. Right now, it would not pose much of a threat to us. But, this Royal Lord is certainly one I have never seen before.” Mo Na Ye worriedly said.","“We should return back to the frontlines while we can.” Mo Na Ye stated and used his Black Ink Strength to wrap around those two. Since they had already built up a resistance, the twins just felt like a cloth had wrapped around them – a cloth that pulled them into the air faster than the speed of sound.","They moved up so fast, so high, that the twins began being unable to sense where the ground was.","Unable to get what Mo Na Ye said out of her mind, Yang Xu asked, “You mentioned that the situation is strange. What’s so strange about it?”","Mo Na Ye’s eyes narrowed as he explained, “Royal Lords are beings the Holy Ones create. But, in this world devoid of everything, each one of us takes tens of thousands of years to create. Not even ten thousand years had passed since I was brought back to life so how is it that they have created another Royal Lord but not us?”","“And you’ve seen all their Royal Lords?” Yang Ji asked, a little sceptical.","“Of course. Except for if a Holy One intervenes, the only person that can deal with a Royal Lord, is another Royal Lord. So naturally I’ve seen the other two Royal Lords.” Mo Na Ye said with worry in his eyes. It was obvious that this matter was of vital importance."]},{"number":6049,"title":"Chapter 6049, Blockade","paragraphs":["Chapter 6049, Blockade","Author: Silavin","The implication of a new Royal Lord appearing was apparent. There might be more hidden behind the scenes, yet to make an appearance. Worse of all, it was still a mystery as to how a Royal Lord was produced so quickly.","“Are you certain that the other Mos can’t sacrifice something to speed up the creation of another Royal Lord?” Yang Xu speculated.","“Absolutely not. If it were so easy to create a Royal Lord, the Holy One would have been able to escape the Primordial Heavens Source Grand Restriction from its very inception. Creating a Royal Lord is equivalent to cutting off part of his cultivation. He can always recultivate it back, but it takes time. The only possibility is...” Mo Na Ye spoke with a voice that became graver by the second. “Unless the Holy One has a supply of Elements that he can consume...”","“Wait! But our world is safe. It’s impossible for them to have...” Yang Ji abruptly cut in, thinking it was an impossibility.","However, Yang Xu corrected him with an anxious voice, “No Brother. It might really be possible. Just, not our world... but another world...”","“Ah!” Yang Ji exclaimed in pure astonishment. The possibility had been in his face the whole time. In the future, their Father did say that he would be leaving to explore more worlds to keep his word of saving a friend?","Currently, construction of the ship that their Father and Mothers were going to board was already underway. They spared no expense to get the best available materials for it, due to the predicted long voyage. It was already enough proof that there were worlds outside of what they knew, outside of the 3,000 Worlds.","What they remained unaware of was that this dark desolate space had connections to other worlds.","“But these are all just speculations. Still, I hope that isn’t the case...” Mo Na Ye said as he did not need the twins to get worried over this. In any case, they should not be the ones dealing with the Royal Lords – he should be the one to deal with them. Still, as the only Royal Lord on this side, he swore that he would make sure they were kept safe from harm.","Soon, out on the horizon, they could see a massive army marching ahead, about to clash with another. The army closest to them was definitely made up of repulsive creatures. Most were insect-like, with a few gigantic ones which reminded them of the first monster they had encountered.","As for the other side, they were more familiar. Though they might not be considered beautiful by Human standards, they certainly looked more Human-like. They also had more proper formations, unlike the other size, which were sporadic with their placements.","The contrast of the two sides was so stark, Yang Ji and Yang Xu need not even think to know which side they were on.","Like a hive mind, the moment Yang Ji and Yang Xu could sense them, the enemy army also seemed to have sensed them. Instantly, without even caring about the army in front of them, they turned around.","Sensing so many eyes suddenly turning towards them, the twins felt their scalp go numb. Worst of all, all these eyes were lifeless, as though they were void of emotions. They simply stared at them, as though their target had finally been found.","Seeing this for the first time himself, Mo Na Ye frowned. He could feel something ominous was happening. In the next instant, he had received news from the Small Black Ink Nest that the other frontline was being pushed.","Suddenly, the ground trembled. Mo Na Ye could sense the power swirling beneath him!","[Damn it!] He cursed in his heart, but knew that nothing could be done. After all, he was here.","*Boom!* A wall explosively rose up, cutting them off from their path back. It stood erect between them and the enemy army. It was unlike anything Yang Xu and Yang Ji had seen before. In fact, it was a mountain, so tall and wide that it stood like a wall even if they were kilometres aways.","Then, it happened. The walls developed slits, which opened up to show millions of eyes. Like the army before, these eyes were lifeless as they looked around before landing on their target.","The sense of disgust and oppression from these eyes was worse than the army earlier. If one stared too deeply into them, it would feel as if their Souls would get sucked in, trapped in the torment of desolate eternity.","At this point, Mo Na Ye had to stop, lest he get too close to it. Even he felt his body turn heavy at the sight of these eyes.","He wanted to speak, to warn the twins. However, he was not even given the chance to breathe. The next instant, arms upon arms formed from below and in front of them. It was grotesque, as even fingers could grow out arms if not eyes. They stacked upon each other, reaching out towards the twins as though trying to claim their prize.","However, how could Mo Na Ye possibly let it approach them? He immediately flew up with the twin in tow. With a mountain this large, he did not know how high he needed to fly, but he knew they would get caught if he did nothing.","Obviously, retreating back was not an option. If anything, that seemed to be what the enemy wanted. Predictably, the only option for him was up and to the sides.","At this point, even if afraid, Yang Ji could not remain idle. With so many arms coming towards them, he took out multiple Crystals in one go, all in the Sixth-Order this time. As for Yang Xu, as though reacting to what he was doing, took out another Array Plate and more Crystals.","Yang Ji was the first to fire. With a clench of his right fist, the Crystals, all initially floating in mid-air, suddenly disappeared. Then, he released his fist, and multiple ripples appeared around them, which was followed by thousands of beams that shot out.","The breams, even if inaccurate, would always find something to strike. This was not due to Yang Ji but rather Yang Xu. If her Brother missed, Yang Xu would manipulate the Space Principles surrounding the beam to redirect it to a target.","In fact, even if the beams sliced through an arm, Yang Xu would redirect it back to hit another arm. She would continue maintaining this until areas where her Divine Sense could no longer reach.","With this bombardment, the sky was like a fireshow, with breams spreading and soon criss-crossing one another, bouncing off invisible walls – back and forth.","If Mo Na Ye had not been solely focused on escaping, even he would have stared at the scene in wonder.","Like knife cutting through butter, everywhere the beam passed, an arm or two would fall, down into the darkness below.","The millions of eyes were simultaneously forced to wince from the Purifying Light. And by the time they fully opened back up, the swarms of arms that were supposed to be flooding towards the twins seemed to have stopped.","It was not that they were no longer growing, but rather Yang Xu had basically manipulated the beams to eventually form flat screens that prevented them from further proceeding!"]},{"number":6050,"title":"Chapter 6050, Another Array?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6050, Another Array?","Author: Silavin","*Ciiii* Sounds of scorching could be heard as wave after wave of arms made of Black Ink Strength was incinerated into oblivion. Even so, the Purifying Light screens were getting dimmer with each wave – eventually exhausted of power.","To maintain its strength, Yang Ji continued to consume more Crystals to launch out more beams, which Yang Xu took to manipulate into screens. Even if one screen faltered, there was a second layer already prepared.","With the twins working in tandem, sustaining this was not an issue. In fact, Mo Na Ye could entirely focus on flying up, above the mountain, thanks to the twins.","However, how could the enemy not foresee what the three were trying to do?","Right in front of Mo Na Ye’s eyes, the mountain grew even taller. Every metre he covered, it would grow by two. The peak, which was so close before, was now distancing!","Furthermore, to slow him down, more arms grew from above. Now, the back, front and top, were all blocked.","Even when he changed direction, to move to the side, it would be no different. The mountain would length, increasing its width, continuing to trap them behind it.","“If we can’t go around, then let’s go through!” Yang Ji said as he had already prepared Ninth-Order Crystals to blow through a hole. So far, they had been on the defensive, and had only used Sixth-Order Crystals. They still had not used Ninth-Order Crystals.","After all, the power of Sixth-Order Crystals were much lower than those of the Ninth-Order, allowing the twins to easily manipulate the shape and direction of the resulting Purifying Light. However, that was not the case of the Purifying Light created using Ninth-Order Crystals. The power of it was so much that Yang Ji was only confident in making condense till the thickness of an arm – with all his strength. However, for Sixth-Order Crystals, he was more than confident in consuming over a hundred Crystals at once and making beams as thick as his hair.","Yang Ji was about to charge up for a release, but Mo Na Ye suddenly stopped him and retreated back. “Stop!”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could both feel their necks stiffen as they tried to maintain their posture while suddenly changing direction. They were about to open their mouth to ask what was going on when they heard a loud, *Boom!*","The sound was so loud their eardrums itched. However, they did not have any time to focus on such trivialities as the mountain in front of them was trembling as though it was about to collapse.","The millions of eyes and arms on its walls seemed to have been shaking by this. The eyes all seemed to narrow as the arms immediately stopped pursuing the twins and retreated.","For a moment, the trembling had subsided, possible due to the one manipulating all this Black Ink Strength to reinforce the mountain. However, the trembling never ceased.","Eventually, a crack on the mountain began to form. Arms upon arms moved to reinforce this crack, hugging each other, overlapping on top of one another, as though what was behind should never be allowed to break free. However, all this effort was in vain as something sharp broke out, and soon, liquid began to pour out.","The liquid did not seem to be affected by the arms, as it simply spread out to cover them. It did not seem to do much else.","Mo Na Ye’s expression at this moment was one of hesitation, while the twins were confused by this sight. Though, they did not remain confused for long as Yang Xu was sharp enough to pick up the pieces and understood that this was their ‘reinforcements’.","After all, it was only their allies on the other side. Besides, if the thing preventing them from returning was trying to resist, then it should be their ally.","Yang Ju soon realised this as well, and he began to sigh with relief.","As for Mo Na Ye, he seemed to come to terms with what must be done and he rushed forward. He abandoned all sense of preservation and simply flew at max-speed, towards the crack.","Initially, Mo Na Ye’s actions seemed fine with the twins. After all, if the crack were to break open, then they would have an escape route. However, with each passing moment, their heart rate was raised further. No matter how close they got, the crack did not seem to be widening. In fact, nothing had changed since Mo Na Ye had started charging forward. Worse, he was not even preparing to break open the Crack using a spear!","[Is he planning on breaking it open with his body?]","The twins could not help but think, realising that at this speed, even if they used their Qi to protect themselves, they would still be flattened.","As his heartbeat raced, Yang Ji instinctively started to prepare the two Crystals he took out.","Just seconds away from crashing, Yang Ji had activated Purifying Light.","However, before he did, the liquid that had escaped from the crack, and had already spread out around the crack, suddenly changed to form a strange pattern. This pattern was obtuse and mysterious, and it began to glow with a mysterious dark light.","Before Yang Ji had realised it, the Purifying Light concentrating in his hand had been removed, and the scene before him had completely changed.","His Divine Sense seemed to have been cut off, limiting it to only a few metres around him. However, even from what he could sense, everything was distorted beyond recognition.","By the time Yang Ji’s Divine Sense could come back into function, he heard a loud “Boom!* off in the distance.","“Wait. What just happened?” Yang Ji asked, turning towards his Sister. After all, before his Purifying Light blew up, he could clearly feel his Sister had manipulated it away. He knew her better than anyone – she would not have done that without a reason.","“That was a Teleportation Array... made of Black Ink Strength...” However, Yang Xu replied with a shocked expression, unable to comprehend the existence of this Array. Since they could still hear the explosion, that meant the Teleportation Array had not been a long-distance one. Still, the fact that there was a Teleportation Array at all meant that the Black Ink Clan had someone who could comprehend the Dao of Space.","“A Teleportation Array?” Yang Ji’s eyes widened, He tried to process what had happened. Indeed, only a Teleportation Array could have sent them away across Space without them knowing.","They had encountered an Array outside of Mo Na Ye’s home before, which someone had to have set up. This Teleportation Array just proves that someone within the Black Ink Clan was proficient in the Dao of Arrays, and even the Dao of Space.","The twins looked at each other, both in shock. They were trying to comprehend what was going on, were the history lessons all wrong?","As for the true relic of the past, Mo Na Ye, who was just following orders being relayed from the Small Black Ink Nest, he breathed a sigh of relief. If he had resisted the Teleportation Array, he and the kids would have been stuck there, and he would have to bear the major brunt of the Purifying Light explosion. Though it might not kill him, he certainly did not wish to get injured."]},{"number":6051,"title":"Chapter 6051, Finally, Safety","paragraphs":["Chapter 6051, Finally, Safety","Author: Silavin","“Sir, are you okay?” An unfamiliar voice soon rang out from the side.","Mo Na Ye and the twins had been transported to the backlines, and there was currently a whole army ready to defend them. They were in a field, with a mass of people surrounding them. The voice came from a male Black Ink Clansmen, whose aura was the second strongest here – first being Mo Na Ye.","“I’m fine, Mo De Kai. Look at the boy first.” Mo Na Ye stated as matter-of-factly. For them, the twins were the top most priority. Yang Ji had lost his left hand, so he needed attention first. As for Yang Xu, though she did seem tired, she did not sustain any injuries – a testament of both her caution and her Brother’s eagerness to keep her safe.","This was the first time Mo De Kai saw Humans. He could not help but wonder how alike they were to the Black Ink Clan. Though the Black Ink Clan were not exactly Humans in form, they share many similarities. In fact, it could be said that their appearance was based on Humans.","It was just that they had certain imperfections or ‘upgrades’ like horns or more arms. Their skin colour also tended to be different due to the Black Ink Clan association with Black Ink Strength.","Nevertheless, the power within their bodies could not be anymore different. So, though Mo De Kai noticed that Yang Ji was missing his hand, his first thought was to create another one using Black Ink Strength. Even if it would not be comparable to one’s naturally born hand, it was better than nothing, right?","When Mo De Kai made this proposal, Mo Na Ye immediately sighed. “Sorry. They do not know much about the Humans. Though he is a Territory Lord, he did not take part in the war. He doesn’t know what effects Black Ink Strength has on Humans”","Yang Ji immediately waved his hand as he stressed, “There is really no need for you to help me with my injuries. You already got my hand back. That’s more than enough for me.”","Yang Xu added, further emphasising, “Yes. My Brother will be able to heal on his own. We have enough Pills with us. No need to trouble yourselves with this.”","Mo Na Ye, though still concerned, could only give up at this point. He gave a small nod and agreed, “In that case, I’ll lead you back to rest. Since you are injured, best to heal up first before you head back out. The Holy One also wishes to meet with you.”","“Mo De Kai, is there a suitable place for these kids? They would most likely need a few weeks to recuperate.” Mo Na Ye turned to the Territory Lord and asked.","“I’ll immediately clear out a Black Ink Nest for them.” Mo De Kai gave a salute and responded as though he had been given a vital task.","“Please follow me.” Mo De Kai said as he gestured to them, and Mo Na Ye tilted his chin to ask the twins to follow.","As the two moved through the field to the camp, all sorts of stares were directed at them. Though they had ignored them at first, it was hard to when these eyes also began to whisper amongst themselves.","There was both a trace of excitement and fear in their voices. Excitement since some had never seen a Human before. Fear since they could tell that the terrifying beam of light that shot through the sky must have been their doing. That beam was so foreign, and its aura was so threatening that they knew they would fall if it was directed at them.","Strangely enough, there was no hostility in their gaze. Even if certain Black Ink Clansmen had taken part in the war during that bygone era, none held hostility towards the twins. This was not out of fear of their Father, Yang Kai. Likewise, they did not seem to have the same aggression as what the twins were used to hearing.","[They are really different.] Yang Ji could not help but think. This was truly different from his history lessons and stories told by his Father.","It had to be said that his Father, Yang Kai, had once infiltrated their ranks. At that time, he was treated like a slave, and he had to fight for his Master in arena battles. These slaves were naturally Black Ink Disciples, Humans corrupted by Black Ink Strength. Though they gained greater power, they were beholden to the every whims of the Black Ink Clan.","Yang Kai had described the Black Ink Clan as people who held no regard for their own kind, as they would kill their own at a whim. The area, though filled with Black Ink Disciples, also had Black Ink Clansmen participate in it. Furthermore, the arena was the main highlight as entertainment for the Black Ink Clan.","Even though certain Humans were deprived to the same extent as well, the Black Ink Clan was different in that everyone enjoyed such activities.","Looking at the peaceful scene in front of them, at how disciplined they were, with Black Ink Clansmen properly greeting each other and smiling, the twin’s previous perception of them had been completely smashed to pieces.","Right now, they were no different to Humans. Yang Ji and Yang Xu even began to wonder if these people could be integrated back in the 3,000 Worlds.","However, they knew that was still not possible as the core of the Black Ink Clansmen, Black Ink Strength, was a power that could not dwell outside the confines of the Primordial Source Gate. Unfortunately, despite how Human-like they might be, due to this sole difference, they could never be integrated into Human society. No, they could not even be exposed to Humans.","As they walked through the camp, besides the Black Ink Clansmen crowding around them, leaving them a path to walk through, there were a few Black Ink Nests behind them. Appearance wise, these were different to the Black Ink Nests like Mo Na Ye’s home. The Black Ink Nests here all looked the same, and had few decorations on them. Obviously, they were the living quarters of those present.","Soon, seeing how the twins were a little uncomfortable, Mo De Kai broke up the crowd, “Nothing to see here. Everyone, move back to your stations. For those on rest, return to your barracks.”","The crowd, upon hearing this command, quickly became silent. They gave a small salute and immediately went on their way. It would be a lie to say they were not interested in the children. However, commands were commands – they had to abide by them.","The rest of the path was relatively calm in comparison. Seeing as Mo De Kai had given the rest a warning, the other Black Ink Clansmen did not dare bother the twins. At most, they would just give glances.","When they arrived at a particularly large Black Ink Nest, Mo De Kai led them in and announced. “This will be your living quarters for now. You can freely use it as you please. Just don’t use that beam inside. I doubt the structure will be able to handle it. Sir will be quite busy maintaining the frontlines while you rest, so if you have anything you need, you can direct them to me–”","There was a slight pause before Mo De Kai gave a firm nod. He seemed to have received a directive from somewhere – most likely from a Small Black Ink Nest he carried around.","“Understood. Any requests you two may have need not be directed to anyone. The Holy One says that he will be able to speak with you so long as you are in here.” Mo De Kai looked at the twins as he said this. Though his facial expression remained stoic, there was envy in his eyes.","“Erm... okay. Thanks.” Yang Xu said as she immediately started looking around the place. It felt a little discomforting to know that they were being spied upon. Still, she had to admit that it was convenient for them to stay inside as they too did not want to go out and be the centre of attention again like earlier.","Mo De Kai gave a final salute and left.","As for the twins, they were in this room alone, just like when they went to Mo Na Ye’s place.","However, the interiors were much simpler than before. Likewise, though it could be said that this place was larger than the other Black Ink Nests, it was certainly a lot smaller than Mo Na Ye’s house.","There was a room with two simple beds, and the rest were the familiar furniture like tables, chairs, shelves, etc. It actually resembles more a home than a barracks, which was peculiar as the table and chairs were outside the other Black Ink Nests. Still, the twins did not question much as they headed to the bedroom.","However, before they did, a figure had appeared behind them."]},{"number":6052,"title":"Chapter 6052, Reunion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6052, Reunion","Author: Silavin","Instead of raising their guard, the two felt a familiar aura. It was strong, unimaginably so. Yet, it was not in any way hostile to them.","The two children could already guess who it was without turning back.","It was none other than Mo.","With this whole land being made of him, it was not surprising for Mo to be able to appear and disappear as he pleased. So, though he had suddenly appeared, the twins were not that surprised – they even had a heads up though they had anticipated a proper meeting and not a sudden visit.","When they turned around to see Mo, they found the sight of him to be baffling. There, Mo stood, with an appearance that was slightly different. Like before, his feet were attached to the ground, and he was a completely black entity with the tint of purple. It was just that his facial and stature seemed more defined for some reason. Furthermore, the facial expression he wore this time was different.","The last time they met him, he had this cold indifference to him that was hard to remove even when he was requesting their help. It was an indifference of a higher-being – not so much that he was trying to be rude. In fact, the twins would not have noticed unless they contrast the one before them and the one from their memories.","The Mo before them was far warmer. Though his eyes remained the same black with glowing purple irises, there was a slight warmth to them.","The first thing that was muttered from Yang Ji was, “Uncle Eleven?”","This was the first impression that he got. Though no longer looking Human, those warm eyes reminded him of the Uncle that took care of them.","Mo, no, Little Eleven broke out a smile. He was happy that they could still recognise him even after taking on this form.","Seeing Little Eleven break out into a smile, the twins immediately knew their instinct was right. Their Uncle had successfully assimilated with Mo.","They did not know when this had happened, but it was a great thing for them. After all, this was their original goal in coming here. Though they now know that there were more fragments that needed to be assimilated, their first step was a success.","Curious, Yang Ji asked, “Uncle Eleven, what happened?”","Though they were happy, they were at the same time disappointed. After all, they were brought here to help him out. Yet, before they could do anything, they were kidnaped. In fact, when they thought about it, they were no different from being burdens.","Little Eleven placed his hand up and shook his head. “I’ll tell you in time. Right now, there is something more urgent I need to deal with.”","Little Eleven did not waste anymore words and immediately appeared right in front of Yang Ji.","Little Eleven reached out and gently placed his palm on Yang Ji’s abdomen. There, a mysterious force was injected into Yang Ji, one in which would reach his Dantian without harming him.","In fact, Yang Ji had not felt anything but a warm palm land on his abdomen.","However, this mysterious force had startled the little worm inside his Dantian. It had enraged her.","As this mysterious force spread through the Dantian and was about to reach the little worm, she retaliated. She forcibly pushed back against this force and rushed out.","Little Eleven, who could feel his probe being pushed back, immediately snorted. He lifted his hand away and clenched his fist.","All around the originally plain looking living room now appeared to be symbols and lines. They instantly formed upon Little Eleven’s Will. This whole Space, this whole Black Ink Nest, was all entirely in his control.","The twins stood there rooted. They were not sure what was happening. All they knew was an Arrayshad formed around them. Naturally, this further proved that it had been Little Eleventh who had rescued them earlier, since he was probably the only one in this world who was proficient enough in the Dao of Arrays to create them in a flash.","Yang Ji could feel a subtle Space Fluctuation in front of his abdomen, and suddenly, the little worm came rushing out.","She did not even bother to scan her surroundings as she already knew the target of her rage. Her haughty eyes seem to portray absolute confidence as she dash forward.","Little Eleven, already seeming to be prepared for it, pushed his palm out. Immediately, the Array around the room lit up, and barriers were erected between them, surrounding the little worm.","However, it was apparent that the Array’s barrier meant nothing in the face of this tiny creature. With a small chomp, she easily bit through that layer and proceeded to charge forward.","With a swift move of Little Eleven’s hand, the symbols and lines around the room changed. A different Array was formed to isolate the little worm. However, she yet again repeated the pattern and easily broke through the Array.","Seeing this, Little Eleven did not panic. In fact, he had already predicted this would be the case. He just formed more Arrays, each different from the last. The room would dim and glow with each change, with a small figure pushing forward each second.","This proceeded with more than a hundred Arrays broken, until the little worm showed difficulty in certain types. Eventually, figuring it out, Little Eleven had the little worm come to a sudden stop. His eyes narrowed and he moved forward to erect a second Array on top of the first one.","From what it seemed, the only Arrays that worked on her were Soul and Illusion Arrays. Other Arrays simply did not work. Even Space Arrays to teleport her back did not work. It was a true mystery why only these two kinds of Arrays were effective on her.","“Uncle Eleven, is she dangerous?” Yang Xu was the first one to break the silence. Through this period, Yang Ji and her had been keeping quiet, watching the whole battle unfold. She did not understand what her Uncle Eleven did to make that little worm so angry, but she trusted him over some worm.","Little Eleven opened his mouth but felt great difficulty in trying to explain. In the end, he could only shake his head and vaguely say, “It depends.”","The twins narrowed their eyes.","Little Eleven gave a sigh and asked Yang Ji, “Can you recall her?”","Yang Ji scratched his check in embarrassment. After all, he technically did not know how to control her. She moved on her own, and only abided by his order as she pleased. Whenever she left his body, it was technically by her own Will, and willingness to help him.","“I can give it a try but she might not listen to me.” Yang Ji said, willing to give it a try.","Little Eleven seemed to understand something and then gave a nod. Though he had hoped Yang Ji had control over this variable, it was understandable if he could not. After all, this little worm’s existence was something that defied common sense.","So, Little Eleven contemplated. If anything, the priority was to enable the twins to reign her in. They were the only ones who had a link to her very Source, so they were the only ones who could tie her down in the truest sense. Even for him, with the power of Mo, he would not be able to stop her without his ability to create Arrays. In fact, if considering who was the most dangerous being to the Black Ink Clan, it would undoubtedly be this little worm – not the twins who could cast Purifying Light."]},{"number":6053,"title":"Chapter 6053, He is Gone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6053, He is Gone","Author: Silavin","With a few hand signs, the Array around the round had changed. Its effective radius had stretched out to encompass the twins inside. However, the two remained unaffected by the Soul and Illusion Arrays, Little Eleven just wanted them to be inside to recall the little worm.","So, lighted symbols appeared beneath their feet, protecting them from the larger Array. In a way, this was also to shield them from being able to see what the little worm was experiencing, which Little Elven, the one operating the Array, had a clear view of.","For the little worm, trapped within the Illusion and Soul Arrays, there were scenes of her past. This was not as effective as a direct Soul Search, which would injure the other party since it required the invasion into their Knowledge Sea, but it would do. Little Eleven did not wish for her whole history. He merely wanted to prove if his conjecture was correct.","As for why Little Eleven did not want the twins to pry at this time, he believes that they should remain uninvolved in them.","The twins looked around and saw that they were now in the Array. Now, Yang Ji had a clear path to reach the little worm and recall her.","As Yang Ji moved towards the seemingly frozen little worm, floating in mid-air, he first ordered, “Come back.”","Upon receiving such an order, no reaction came. It was as though the little worm had not heard him – which was the case since she was still trapped under an Illusion.","That was when Little Eleven added, “Just take her back in your Dantian and lock her inside. Don’t let her out unless necessary.”","Though Little Eleven had not said much, not being able to recall her upon command, even if she was unable to hear it, meant that Yang Ji had little to no power over her. For example, Artifacts could be recalled upon command. They might be restricted but they would still respond in some way upon being called. This was due to their connection being through the Soul.","Since she could exit and enter Yang Ji’s Dantian at Will, Little Eleven naturally assumed that their connection was something similar. Now, he even doubted if Yang Ji could actually restrain her inside of his Dantian.","Yang Ji gave a nod and used Space Principles. The Space around her distorted and she disappeared in the distortion to appear back inside Yang Ji’s Dantian.","However, the moment she was moved out of the Array, she was free from its effect. She immediately noticed how she was back inside her ‘home’, and tried to rush out again.","Yang Ji quickly circulated the Qi in his Dantian to block off her escape, but it seemed to not work as the little worm easily left and continued to rush ahead.","Unfortunately for her, she got trapped in the Array again.","This time, Little Eleven directly talked to her, without the twins hearing in, “I’ve seen through your memories. As the guardian of these two, I cannot let someone as dangerous as you, who should have already crossed over, roam with them without assurance. Your body has been formed from them, yet you share almost no ties. You do not obey their orders and act as you Will. What is your purpose?”","The little worm just gave a cold scoff, refusing to answer.","Little Eleven’s eyes sharpened and he spoke to the twins, “Yang Ji, take her back in. This time, I will make sure she does not have the ability to escape.”","Yang Ji gave an obedient nod. Though he did not quite understand why his Uncle Eleven was being so harsh on this little worm, he believes he must have his reasons. He also believes Yang Xu would approve of it since she detested the little worm’s attitude.","Once again, Space around the little worm distorted and she disappeared. However this time, the moment she got sucked in, Little Eleven stuck out his palm and placed it on Yang Ji’s Dantian. Dark symbols immediately formed, all around his front, back and sides. All Yang Ji felt was a tickling sensation all around him, despite this seal being made from Black Ink Strength.","Once everything was done, Little Eleven waited for a few seconds before retracting the Array outside, returning the room to normal.","However, unbeknownst to him, the little worm was smirking while in Yang Ji’s Dantian...","Watching as Little Eleven stared at his abdomen for a few seconds before waving his hand, Yang Ji asked, the most pressing question in his mind. “Uncle Eleven, how?”","Little Eleven gave a heavy sigh, and he turned towards the twins, showing a forlorn look. “Mo let me take over.”","This was the easiest way for him to express it. He did not wish to say that Mo wanted his consciousness wiped off, choosing a release from life.","Little Eleven’s trip here was to assimilate with Mo, and get his powers back. Though assimilation meant that they would be one, it did not mean that the other would stop existing. They would be a part of him, like before. However, this fragment of Mo seeked termination. Worse of all he was actually holding back the other two fragments.","Essentially, Little Eleven should not have needed to bring the twins in. In fact, the past times, when Mo was avoiding him, it seemed to have been on purpose. As for why, the answer lies in the twins. Or more specifically, the twins and that little worm.","As for the mastermind behind this, it was none other than Yang Kai. Other than him, who could have coordinated with Mo till this degree? Other than him, how would everything have flowed so smoothly?","Regardless, Little Eleven believes the objective of their Father had been accomplished with the birth of that little worm.","After all, once he took over, the other two fragments of Mos would definitely not be able to make any real waves – with him having mastered different Daos while he was living as a Human. So, as a fighting force, the twins were essentially not necessary. He believes he alone could hold the fort.","As for Yang Kai, that manipulative bastard, Little Eleven swore he was going to get even with him!","However, right now, his task was to explain to the children, and placate them of this farce.","To move on from the topic of Mo, Little Eleven quickly looked at Yang Ji’s hand and sighed. He asked, “Are you able to regrow it back? Need my help?”","Yang Ji gave a confident nod, “I just need sometime. No need for you to trouble yourself Uncle Eleven.”","“Alright. In that case, I should send you two back home. Your mission has already been accomplished.” Little Eleven shook his head. He knew Yang Ji could regrow his limb after sometime, as this was part of his nature as a Phoenix. However, since the boy wanted to be independent, then he would abide by his wish.","However, Yang Ji seemed reluctant to leave. After all, though they have faced grave danger, this was the first time they had truly been on an adventure. They had even trained to resist Black Ink Strength, and learn how to fight here.","Little Eleven noticed the reluctance in his gaze and added, “I took you two here when you two were only at the Dao Source Realm. Honestly, with all the tools in your arsenal, you should be safe here. But, at your current Cultivation Realm, you would not be able to help out much at this time. Won’t it be better to come back once you reach the Open Heaven Realm, where you can use the Royal Lords here as your practice partners?”","Little Eleven tried to make a logical appeal, but Yang Ji was still reluctant.","That was when Yang Xu stepped in to try to convince him, “Brother, I do want to return home. We still need to heal up and I think Uncle Eleven is right. We are still too weak. Mo Na Ye has been dragged around by us through this whole period. He can’t keep babysitting us. He needs to protect the frontlines.”","“But...” Yang Ji wanted to refute, but at this point, it would truly be selfish of him. So, he just accepted the verdict with a sigh. “Okay, fine...”","Little Eleven gave a nod and his eyes immediately darted to one corner of the room. There was obvious annoyance in his voice as he spoke, “I’ve already helped you deal with this. Come out and bring them back.”","Upon those words, the space which Little Eleven was staring at started to distort. From it came two familiar figures, a man and a woman.","The woman had a cold aura to her, as though everything in the world could be frozen by her sight. However, upon seeing the two children, there was immense warmth in her eyes. She was like an ethereal fairy, as though nothing in this world could smudge her.","As for the man, he had a heroic aura to him. He had a dashing look, but one would not say that he was extremely handsome. He also had a smile on his face that irked Little Eleven to no end..."]},{"number":6054,"title":"Chapter 6054, Yang Kai Had His Reasons","paragraphs":["Chapter 6054, Yang Kai Had His Reasons","Author: Silavin","Naturally, the two were Yang Kai and Su Yan.","Little Eleven had only noticed them after he had assimilated with Mo. He did not know when they had come, but he knew that they had been watching the twins before they had gone to the battlefield.","It was most likely the case where all the other Mo fragments knew of the twos’ presence, which was why they avoided a full-force siege. One had sent out additional trump cards like that new Royal Lord, but they had not personally shown themselves.","In fact, Little Eleven believes Yang Kai was already here, before he assimilated with Mo. After all, the assimilation process was not immediate and during that time, his domain would be vulnerable. Despite this, there was no attack from the other two sides.","Yang Kai, seeming to be able to read into Little Eleven’s thoughts, gave an awkward smile. As for Su Yan, she took no time to rush up to her children to give them a big hug. She had watched everything unfold, but could not do anything to help because Yang Kai had stopped her.","Back before the Royal Lord had taken Yang Ji’s hand, she was moments away from unleashing all her might to confront it. Yang Kai had to step in at the time to stop any energy fluctuations from her, else the twins would have spotted them.","Despite showing a cold front, Yang Kai had his fist clenched till his knuckles turned white. He had also wanted to act out but he chose to be objective there.","In fact, he had expected the little worm to intervene for the children’s sake, but she did not. Perhaps she had sensed them, or perhaps she understood the true strength of the twins. Regardless, even in that precarious situation, the little worm did not do anything to protect her ‘host’.","Seeing as even that did not force her out, Yang Kai did not believe they could do anything else. He could try to wait it out further, and have the children be in even more dangerous situations to have the little worm act. However, seeing Su Yan’s frosty eyes the moment he tried to stop her from helping, and his own palm, which had his nails dug into, he knew that was impossible for them to tolerate anymore than this.","To be fair, Yang Kai sort of knew this would have happened. After all, the Yang Family tradition of raising their children like Cuckoo Birds has ended in their generation. Even if Yang Kai wanted to toughen his children up, would his Wives let him? He was certain his bed would be cold for the next few decades if he were to forcibly impose. What more, when his Mother, Dong Su Zhu, vehemently objected to it, who else in the Family could oppose her?","As a Mother, Dong Su Zhu had suffered greatly when forcibly separated from Yang Kai when he was sent to High Heaven Pavilion. Her Son had been forced to go through such hardship, how could she let her Grandchildren suffer the same fate?","With her spearheading the opposition, even the Yang Family Elders had to lower their heads.","However, the merits of facing and overcoming hardship could not be undermined. Even if the women within the Family did not like it, the children had to grow in harsher environments to polish themselves and grow to be independent. They could not always be sheltered throughout their lives.","So, a middle-ground had to be reached. The children would have to experience the outside world, and learn independence. From now on, they need not force them into another Sect, and the parents were allowed to watch over them.","With Yang Kai and his Wives abilities, this would not be a problem (in most cases).","There were issues though. For one, the Yang Family, despite wanting to keep a low profile, had far reaching influence and resources. Most cultivators know of them, and naturally, the eldest of Yang Kai’s children, twins at that, were sure to be recognised. Even if they wore disguises, and competed for resources, their Phoenix and Dragon Forms or their mastery in the two extremely abstruse Dao of Space or Dao of Time, if exposed, would make their identity obvious. But the most important reason was: ‘is there even a need to do so?’","The basis of the Yang Family’s Cuckoo tradition was to make use of the resources of other Sects, to raise their young using these resources. However, they were born and raised in High Heaven Palace, with their Sect Master being the only World Creation Realm expert. They were incomparable to other Sects. In terms of cultivation resources, which place could compare to their High Heaven Palace?","Furthermore, all of Yang Kai’s children were monsters in their own right. Their cultivation speed far surpassed their own Father. With their Eldest, Yang Ji and Yang Xu, being monsters within that pool of monsters. They were already in the Dao Source Realm before they turned thirteen, what kind of concept was that?","In a way, deciding on their ‘training ground’ was tough. Regardless of the limited resources of the place, these two would certainly outgrow it within a couple of years (at worst) to a couple of months. Even if Yang Kai had wanted them to experience an independent life, they realistically could blow through most issues through brute force if necessary. Though their cultivation could not be said to be at the highest, they could already defeat opponents above their cultivation realm. In fact, Yang Kai was quite confident that if those two worked together, with all their Artifacts and Pills, and shared mastery over Daos, only those above Half-Step Open Heaven Realm could oppose them.","Those monstrous twins had even progressed so much in the Dao of Space that even Yang Kai found it hard to hide from their notice – something Yang Kai was both proud of and embarrassed about. This was not Yang Kai being inapt. Rather, it was their exceptional ability to sense Space Fluctuations.","That was why, in the outside world, during this period, Yang Kai had never appeared close to them. He was always a few steps behind them, monitoring them through other third parties. It was only after the two entered the Profound Source Gate that he could follow them more closely.","Also, though it had decided upon that they would go past the Profound Source Gate for training, this space was truly strange, with its whole existence shrouded in mystery. Yang Kai had tried to uncover its secrets before, but the truth remained obscure.","Even when asking Mo, he could not receive any answers. There was a Restriction placed on him, one which disallowed him from speaking about its history. Naturally, Yang Kai had both explored and questioned those with ancient memories.","Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer seem to have no recollection of how the Profound Source Gate came to be formed, nor when this place was created.","Shi also did not know, since Mu was the only one out of the ten of them that went past the Profound Source Gate. From his recollection, Mu did not explore that place for long, and did not seem to be aware of its secrets.","However, Shi did once tell Yang Kai that the twins might be able to uncover some of the truth behind the Profound Source Gate. This was due to the special existence of their Cultivation Technique, which even he was unable to fully comprehend the mysteries behind it. Certainly, he did help refine it, at least those parts of the Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique which he could understand to make it simpler. However, a large portion of it still remained a mystery.","Like the Profound Source Gate, which had mysterious ancient markings on it that they could not comprehend, this Cultivation Technique was similar. Thus, Shi could not help but draw a connection between the two.","Yang Kai was initially reluctant to have them go beyond the Profound Source Gate, but with him alone having no clues – trying multiple times to explore it, with nothing substantial coming up even after weeks of exploration, he eventually had to pin his hopes on the twins.","Furthermore, they just so happen to need a place to train, and Yang Kai could follow them to keep them safe. So, with the idea of killing two birds with one stone, Yang Kai set out to arrange everything.","As for why he did not deal with the other Mo fragments, that was because he believed it was up to Little Eleven to deal with them. Since they could no longer cause any harm to the 3,000 Worlds, it was best to leave this for Little Eleven to deal with his own karmic ties. Also, if Little Eleven could get back all the power of Mo, Yang Kai believes he could act as another vanguard for the 3,000 Worlds once he goes off to venture outside the 3,000 Worlds.","So far, this whole trial has been fruitful: his children have basically grown immune to Black Ink Strength; he had uncovered hints of more ‘gates’, most likely connecting to other places besides the 3,000 Worlds; Little Eleven had assimilated with one of the three major Mo fragments, with the ability to still use the Dao he had mastered as a Human; and the strangest thing of all was the existence of that worm.","Yang Kai was certain that Little Eleven had an inkling as to what it was. Otherwise, Little Eleven would not leave it with the twins. However, there was no point in asking him since the Restriction would now affect him like it had with Mo.","Regardless, Yang Kai believes it was time to end the trial – not because Su Yan had been giving him frosty glares after Yang Ji got injured, certainly not."]},{"number":6055,"title":"Chapter 6055, I Will Support You From Behind","paragraphs":["Chapter 6055, I Will Support You From Behind","Author: Silavin","Su Yan was busy holding Yang Ji and Yang Xu in her left and right. She hugged them for a good minute before being satisfied enough to let go.","She immediately looked to Yang Ji’s hand and asked, “You must have been so scared.”","Truth be told, Yang Ji was really scared for his and his Sister’s life at that moment. However, putting up a brave front, he just smiled and shook his head. “Mom, it wasn’t that scary.”","Su Yan, seeing some of her Husband’s stubbornness in their boy, just gently shook her head and said in a gentle voice, “Hand.”","Yang Ji seemed to become very obedient at this moment as he raised his injured arm and took out the hand in his Space Ring.","Su Yan gently held the two and seemed to signal to Yang Kai with her colder than usual eyes.","Yang Kai quickly moved closer, as if by divine providence, and he quickly spread his hand out. Soon, Time Principles started to spread, with profound characters that seeped out and covered the two items in Su Yan’s hand. Yang Ji’s injured arm, and his hand, were soon both enveloped in a gentle light.","Beneath this power, the two entities started to merge into one. As time flowed backwards, all injuries were replaced and the hand was once again back to its original position.","The gentle light and characters soon retreated, disappearing into nothingness as Yang Ji gave his hand a few squeeze. It truly felt as if the injury had never been there.","“Okay, he is fine now.” Yang Kai said in relief. As a Father, though he knew his own capabilities, he still could not help but worry.","“En” Yang Ji nodded with a hint of embarrassment. After all, he was already 12, a grown boy, the eldest of his Siblings. Yet, here he was, still being coddled by his parents. Also, though his injury might seem serious to most, he really could recover on his own.","“Okay, all good now.” Su Yan gave a gentle smile and then turned to Little Eleven to give a slight bow. “Thank you very much for taking care of my two children. I hope we will be able to see each other soon.”","Little Eleven simply gave a wave and thanked them back, “No, they were the ones helping me here. Unlike someone else.”","Su Yan, with her smile still on, “Not to worry. We will help you.”","Yang Kai who heard that, could not help but have cold sweat pour down his back. He wanted to say something but he was very ‘timely interrupted’ by Yang Xu, who tugged at his sleeve. “Hmm? What is it?”","Yang Xu made gestures as though asking him to ‘come here’, and Yang Kai bent down. In a quiet whisper, Yang Xu told Yang Kai something in secret, going as far as to distort Space around them, before handing over a Space Ring.","Yang Kai, as though having received a mission, gave a nod, agreeing to her request. “Okay. I’ll pass this to him.”","Yang Xu gave him a small peck on the cheek and quickly ran to Su Yan’s side.","Su Yan then gave Little Eleven a nod prompting him.","Seeing as all matters had been dealt with, Little Eleven raised his hand again and another Array was formed on the wall. This time, it was a Space Array, meant to lead them back to the Profound Source Gate.","Now that the path has been established, Su Yan took her two children by their hands and walked into the Space Array, completely vanishing from the room.","After the three had vanished, Little Eleven relinquished the Space Array and turned towards Yang Kai, asking directly. “Will you be helping me or not?”","Yang Kai shook his head. “I’m not. This is something we believe you need to handle on your own, as Little Eleven, as Mo.”","“Even if this place is proven to be connected to other worlds?” Little Eleven asked.","“Yeah. I can always come back once you deal with the other fragments.” Yang Kai added with a sigh. He too would like to explore the mysteries of this place. But right now, the priority would be his children. Exploration, which might take an unknown amount of time, would be unfair to them in their growing years.","Yang Kai added, “But I will support you from behind.”","Yang Kai took out a Space Ring and tossed it to Little Eleven. When Little Eleven checked what was inside, he was shocked. These were materials from the Fifth-Order and above. Materials of all Five Elements, including Yin and Yang. The implication of this was obvious, Yang Kai was going to support him in building up his own army. Or even, his own population here.","“Well, at least you have some conscience.” Little Eleven kept the Space Ring and helped Yang Kai open another Space Array to leave. However, Yang Kai shook his head and told him, “I still have some unfinished business here. My Daughter left me something to do.”","Little Eleven asked, “Oh? What is it?”","“A meeting with an old friend of mine.” Yang Kai said with a soft smile and just disappeared in front of him.","Seeing as Yang Kai was acting all mysterious, Little Eleven just shrugged and sank back to the ground, also disappearing from the room.","***","The next time Yang Kai appeared was outside another large Black Ink Nest. This one looked similar to the one Yang Ji and Yang Xu were in, just bigger. Naturally, his old friend was inside, with Mo De Kai updating him about the children.","“Since the Holy One wishes to speak to them in private, then we can leave them in his hands. For now, return to your post. The enemy lies seem to be acting up again.” Mo Na Ye said with a stern expression.","“Yes!” Mo De Kai cupped his fists and left the Black Ink Nest, leaving Mo Na Ye alone with his thoughts.","However, before Mo Na Ye could sit down on his chair, a familiar voice could be heard behind him.","“I’m surprise you are still alive. Could have sworn I killed you”","Naturally, the one who said this was Yang Kai. He had waiting until Mo De Kai left, waited until Mo Na Ye was alone before he showed himself."]},{"number":6056,"title":"Chapter 6056, Drinks After A Long Time","paragraphs":["Chapter 6056, Drinks After A Long Time","Author: Silavin","Mo Na Ye, never expecting to see Yang Kai here. His eyes widened in disbelief as he needed a moment to calm himself. Still, seeing that typical grin of his made him relive those past headaches.","He could not help but ask back, “What are you doing here?”","Yang Kai grinned with pride, “As a Father, I have to fulfill what my Daughter requests of me.”","“In this regard, I really have to thank you for taking such good care of them. I didn’t expect you to be such a good caretaker.” Yang Kai chuckled after seeing this new side of Mo Na Ye.","Mo Na Ye shrugged, “They are just a couple of kids. They were quite well behaved, which makes taking care of them much easier. Though, I doubt you have much to do with that.”","Yang Kai scoffs but chose not respond to the jab for some reason, [They are my children. Who do you think they take after? Of course they are well-behaved because of me.]","Yang Kai just took out a Space Ring, the one Yang Xu gave him, and passed it over the Mo Na Ye, “I’m here because my Daughter wanted you to have this.”","Mo Na Ye’s eyebrows were raised as he accepted the ring. Since it was said to be a gift from the girl, he saw no reason to be on guard and checked its contents. There, he found a few sets of Ninth-Order Materials and even a written message.","The message was carved on a jade plaque, seemingly hastily made using her Divine Sense.","When Mo Na Ye read it, his face turned a little red, as he gave a thunderous laugh, which boomed through the whole room.","‘Dear Uncle Mo Na Ye,","Thank you for helping me and my Brother. I wish you have a happy marriage and bear plenty of children!’","Yang Kai even gave a teasing smile and gave his early congratulations, “Congratulations. A child will be born soon. So, who is the lucky woman?”","Mo Na Ye took a while before he could regain his cool as he answered. “No one you have met before.”","Yang Kai gave look, as though waiting for the ‘groom’ to introduce him to her. However, Mo Na Ye, seeming to want to keep his private life distant from his past dealings, chose to forgo the introductions. He simply wished for his private life to be left out of all these dealings.","Yang Kai, seeming to have realised Mo Na Ye’s intentions, just changed the subject, “Anyways, since my Daughter has given you a gift, as her Father, I can’t really do nothing, can I?”","Yang Kai summoned out a dozen Soul Rending Thorns from his Knowledge Sea. These were Artifacts crafted by Grandmaster Ma Fan using a piece of his Soul, which was now in the World Creation Realm. Though disposable, each one could easily eliminate a Royal Lord. Yang Kai was only able to create them thanks to his Soul Warming Lotus, which would passively help his Soul recover with time.","In the past, Yang Kai had been the only one who could use them, since they had to be used in tandem with a Secret Technique. However, with some progress in both his and Grandmaster Ma Fan’s mastery over the Dao of Artifacts, these Artifacts have been made more versatile. In the future, he plans to make sure all his children have a set of a thousand. However, for now, he was still gradually crafting more.","Seeing these dozen Soul Rending Thorns appear caused Mo Na Ye to feel his Soul tremble. This was despite them not even being aimed directly at him. Mo Na Ye could tell that each one of these were a priceless treasure, items which could overturn the whole tide of battle in a single instant.","He could not help but feel nervous accepting them. However, Yang Kai spoke up as if to ease his tension. “If you feel that it is hard to accept, I am open to trade them for information.”","Once he heard that, Mo Na Ye immediately recalled certain scenes in the past flash, and felt regretful in needing to ever make a deal with Yang Kai. Still, he calmed himself. After all, their position now was different and Yang Kai was no longer their enemy. So, whatever deal he proposed would not be too lopsided. In fact, if Yang Kai had wished for it, with his current cultivation, he could have easily eliminated the whole Black Ink Clan.","Looking from another perspective, Mo Na Ye realised that Yang Kai was genuinely trying to help him, and was offering a deal to ensure Mo Na Ye could keep his pride.","[If things are like this, I can’t really refuse, can I?] Mo Na Ye gave a nod and stuck out his hand, “Sure.”","Yang Kai gladly passed the Artifacts to him. He soon took out a jug and he pointed out, “Would you like to talk here, or, talk outside?”","Once Mo Na Ye saw the jug, he could not help but break out into a smile, reminiscing the past. “Let’s head out. I know a spot.”","***","Yang Kai and Mo Na Ye exited through a Void Crack, traversing what took Yang Xu and Yang Ji over a day to cover, to a familiar spot. It was on the peak, where Mo’s hut was. Over here, they would be able to see the familiar housings for most of the residents.","“Here?” Yang Kai questioned, and Mo Na Ye affirmed.","“There is no place better for a drink.”","Yang Kai agrees with him and takes out a set of table and chairs from his Space Ring, along with multiple jugs full of alcohol. He popped open a jug and push it to Mo Na Ye.","Mo Na Ye caught it in mid-air and gulped a mouth-full before commenting. “It has been such a long time.”","Yang Kai popped open another jug and took a mouth full as well, before commenting, “Yeah, the last time we shared a drink was back at No-Return Pass. Thousands of years have passed since then...”","“Yeah...” When looking back on the past, Mo Na Ye could not help but feel mournful at the losses. In the past, he would have never felt this way, since to him, lives at that point in time were valueless. As long as those could help him serve his objectives, sacrifices meant nothing.","However, now, the whole Black Ink Clan has changed. Lives were more precious than ever. Even Mo Na Ye, was seeking to protect those weaker than him, and even wishing to have his own ‘children’ if possible.","In this regard, he had to admit, Yang Xu was certainly sharper than her Brother. Though he wanted to keep the children away from his private affairs, the girl was sharp enough to see through him and provide enough materials for him and his Wife to produce offsprings.","“So, how did someone who was dead come back alive?” Yang Kai once again asked this question, which he was bewildered by. He could have sworn he had killed Mo Na Ye with his own two hands that day.","“I am the Mo Na Ye that you know, at the same time, I am also not him.” Mo Na Ye seemed a little melancholic as he said that, thanking another gulp before continuing. “I have no memories of my death. My last memory stopped at our final battle, when I last sent out a message to the others, before No-Return Pass fell. I do not remember how my life had ended, but I already had a good guess that I had died in your hands.”","“But make no mistake, I do not resent you for my death. Nor do I hold any hatred for the Humans now. In fact, when I look back on our battles, I have to thank you. You were my perfect rival. You bested me when I was at my very best. There was nothing more that I, as a warrior, could ask for.” Mo Na Ye said in a somber voice, before continuing, “I do not know how I return back alive. It could be that my memories were retained with the Holy One, allowing him to bring me back. Yet, I too question if I am the same person you clashed with in the past.”","Yang Kai’s eyes widened. This was both an amazing discovery, and also a tragic one. Amazing that their kind might have the chance at resurrection. Tragic because this meant that the target of hatred for the 3,000 Worlds would never cease unless Mo, now Little Eleven, ceased existing.","The blood spilled during that era was far too much for some to overcome. That was why Little Eleven had been kept safe within High Heaven Palace, with his existence hidden from the world.","Thankfully, there were only a few who knew about the situation here, and Yang Kai was confident he could help keep this a secret. What more, the Profound Source Gate was far beyond reach of others, which helped separate the 3,000 Worlds from their old nemesis.","“You’ve changed. You were never someone to speak of sentiments.” Yang Kai said with curiosity.","“It is not just me. The whole Black Ink Clan has changed. Everyone here desires peace now. We also no longer have any wish to return back to the 3,000 Worlds.” Mo Ne Ye added.","“What changed? The environment?” Yang Kai asked, though, he had his own guesses.","“We change with the Holy One. His emotions have settled, so we have settled. But, if you want to ask me why that is the case, you best ask the Holy One himself.” Mo Na Ye also wondered about this point. However, he instinctively did not ask Mo. He felt like he would not get the answer even if he had asked, so he refrained from doing so.","At the same time, Yang Kai just gave a nod, as if he had already expected the answer. If anything, Mo Na Ye did not seem to know much, only accepting the current situation like it was natural. Still, from Yang Kai’s point of view, this peaceful Black Ink Clan was far better than the one the 3,000 Worlds had to deal with.","Since Yang Kai now knew that most of his questions would only be responded with vague answers, he just took his time to leisurely drink with this old rival of his.","Both men laughed and joked as they reminisced about the past. Bickering and forfeit drinks were plentiful, as they drank ‘way into the night’. Though, in this world, where there was no night and day. So, they only stopped when Mo Na Ye drank, for the first time in a while, till he dropped.","Yang Kai, feeling satisfied, left Mo Na Ye on the table, with a Space Ring filled with alcohol.","However, before Yang Kai left, he sent a message to Little Eleven using his Divine Sense. He soon ripped open a Void Crack and disappeared..."]},{"number":6057,"title":"Chapter 6057, Wives Council","paragraphs":["Chapter 6057, Wives Council","Author: Silavin","While Yang Kai and Mo Na Ye were busy catching up, Su Yan had already brought her kids out of the Profound Source Gate, and back to the World Tree. Naturally, she sent her regards to Zhang Ruo Xi and the two Seniors, Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer. All three were naturally glad to see that the children were safe upon their return.","Zhang Ruo Xi naturally had questions about the state of the world behind the Profound Source Gate, but Su Yan just redirected her to ask Yang Kai instead, as he was certainly much more knowledgeable about such matters, and the twins were merely being dragged around by the circumstances there.","Still, Zhang Ruo Xi was actually glad to not see Little Eleven with them, since that indicated that he had accomplished his goal. Though she still had to remain here, not just to keep Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer company, but also as a guard; the post was not as vital as before. After all, with Little Eleven guarding what was behind the Profound Source Gate, she need not always be here.","They certainly could not move Sun’s Burning Light and Moon’s Serene Glimmer’s True Bodies out of this region as it was far too big, but with Zhang Ruo Xi, she would be able to help safely bring their consciousness around to explore the 3,000 Worlds.","As for the World Tree, the old wizened face clearly showed relief. However, in front of the World Tree were two familiar figures, drinking.","These two figures were a Human and a Black Panther.","Naturally, they were Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow.","Even after drinking for quite a few days, they still remained sober, and immediately identified the three that had just been transported here.","Fang Tian Ci was the first one to ask, “So, it’s done?”","Su Yan just gave a small nod and did not say a word. She looked at the World Tree, as though asking it to transport them away. However, without words, just from her eyes alone, the World Tree seem to already know of the location.","The World Tree gave a sigh and with a wave of its branch, the three had been transported away.","*Haaa...* Unexpectedly, the one who first broke the silence was Thunder Shadow. His sigh was heavy and he drank another gulp of alcohol.","Though he was happy the twins had returned safe without harm, seeing as Little Eleven had not returned with them was a huge sign that he would no longer be joining them. Thunder Shadow could not help but feel that the small hut within their Forbidden Area would remain empty from now on. It was a melancholic feeling. He was glad that Little Eleven had moved on to take his next step in life, but also a bit reluctant as a good old friend would no longer be around.","Fang Tian Ci shared the sentiment. Though they were tasked to keep watch of Little Eleven at the start, they were by no means enemies. In fact, they could be considered to be Fellow Brothers after spending such a long time together.","However, with the person they had to keep watch over was gone, they themselves would have to start on their new journey as well.","Naturally, everyone knew that Little Eleven was not dead. But, they would not be able to see him in the foreseeable future for a long time. From now on, after this, Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow would step ahead and travel out past the 3,000 Worlds. They would be the forerunner, exploring the unknown before Yang Kai.","Right now, this drinking session also marked the last time the two Brothers could see each other in a long while. Who knows? This might really be their last time seeing each other.","Although they could choose to travel together, which would be safer, they much prefer to cover more ground by independently moving. Besides, this was a way for them to return to being independent after thousands of years.","They naturally promised each other that they would reunite after every hundred years, using the World Tree Saplings. By then, the one with fewer tales to tell would be the one providing the drinks!","Now, the final one they were waiting for was their Eldest Brother. Once he came and bid them farewell, they planned to leave.","***","The place where the World Tree had transported Su Yan and the two children was within High Heaven Palace. However, this area was exclusive, in which Yang Kai was not allowed to enter. In fact, most of the adult men of the Yang Family were not allowed to enter this space.","This area was a cluster of small palaces, with a woman taking up a single palace. There was a common courtyard amongst these palaces, which already had a large table and multiple chairs in place.","The place was serene with sunlight filtering through twisted branches, casting ethereal patterns over the table and seats. Mist rose, veiling the setting in mystery. As for the trees, they would remain silent sentinels, as the women chatter. Bell-like voices would ring out from time to time, even more graceful than the gentle splashing in the accompanying pond.","This was none other than the place where the Wives Council was. In short, all of Yang Kai’s Wives were here. The palaces were smaller here mainly because this place was made just as a retreat for them.","The other women who frequented this place would be the maids and their Mother-in-Law. However, even the maids were special as only the most trusted were allowed entry into this place–like Bi Luo.","Here, all conversations were free to be spoken about, free of judgement. The only ones they had to be wary of were probably the children, but normally, more sensitive topics would not be discussed in their presence.","The moment Su Yan appeared, everyone present could feel her aura. Most of the other Wives instantly made their way to the courtyard as though this whole matter had been decided upon, that a gathering would be held the moment their Eldest Sister had returned.","Even Dong Su Zhu, who was alerted by Su Yan’s presence, quickly abandoned cooking to her Husband, who was wide-eyed with confusion, and rushed to the courtyard."]},{"number":6058,"title":"Chapter 6058, Secret Message","paragraphs":["Chapter 6058, Secret Message","Author: Silavin","“Yang Ji, Yang Xu!” The first to come screaming in excitement was Shan Qing Luo. Though rushing, she still exudes unparalleled charm. If men were here, they would naturally be mesmerised by the sight. But for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, they wanted to hide at this moment.","Shan Qing Luo came down and swooped the two into her bosom, tightly nuzzling her cheeks against their heads as though that was the most common of greetings.","As for the twins, they had to fight for breath under those two bosom...","This always happened when their Mother Shan got a little too excited after not meeting them for a while. Out of all their Mothers, she was the most expressive and the most touchy. Though the twins had gotten used to such occurrences, Yang Ji, having grown up, wished she would stop since it was slightly embarrassing to still be nestled in his manner.","In fact, Shan Qing Luo did not let them go until all their other Mothers had gathered.","“Qing Luo, I think that’s enough. Are you planning to suffocate them to death?” A melodious joking voice came. It was from none other than Zhu Qing.","“En, we haven’t even seen them yet and here you are, already taking up all their attention.” Ji Yao, added.","“Alright. Alright. I just couldn’t help myself when my Children are finally back.” Shan Qing Luo gave a small sigh and released her hug. When she put them down and her eyes met with their adorable eyes, she immediately wanted to give another hug. However, reminding herself to be restrained, she just settled with a peck on their forehead before backing off.","It took a moment before the twins could gather their bearings. However, once they did, they quickly greeted each Mother in order, “Yang Ji and Yang Xu greets Mother Ning Chang, Mother Qing Luo, Mother Yue, Mother Qing, Mother Yao, Mother Ru Meng, Mother Hua Chang and Mother Ling Wan.”","This greeting was basically a well established line at this point, with the twins saying both of their names instead of individually.","The Mothers all gave a nod and Yu Ru Meng turned to Xia Ning Chang, indicating with her eyes, ‘since we are about to have some serious discussions between us, it would be best to move the children away for now’.","Xia Ning Chang gave a nod and was about to bring up that she would take the children away when another loud shout came, quite familiar to earlier.","“Yang Ji! Yang Xu! My Grandbabies are back! Come! Let your Grandma see both of you!” This time, it was Dong Su Zhu who came rushing in. Since she was in the furthest region from this place, she took the longest to get here–also with her cultivation being the lowest. However, her enthusiasm to see her Grandchildren was unmatched. At this point, even mountains could not stop her.","Dong Su Zhu immediately came in and the first thing she did was check their clothes and hair, then their skin to see if they had sustained any injustice! There, she immediately noticed a problem, on Yang Ji’s sleeve, there was blood!","She immediately questioned, “Who hurt you? Come, tell your Grandma. I’ll help you two teach them a lesson.”","Being the ‘obedient’ children that they were, the twins instantly greeted their Grandmother first before anything else. “Yang Ji and Yang Xu greet Grandma.”","“Good good good. Now, tell me who is the baddie who hurt you so that I can go teach them a lesson.” Dong Su Zhu urged once more, with eyes ready to seek justice. In her eyes, these two good children could never do no wrong. After all, they were always so obedient in front of her. Sure, Yang Ji might be a little mischievous from time to time, but he would always listen to her and Yang Xu was exemplary at always meeting her expectations. Even the other Grandchildren might not necessarily be as well-behaved as these two.","However, before the twins answered, Su Yan gently cut in. “Mother, Yang Ji and Yang Xu have just gotten back and are quite tired. I will share what happened with all of you. For now, we should just let them rest.”","Xia Ning Chang took this opportunity to add. “En, I’ll take them away first. Eldest Sister, you can tell me about everything later.”","“Alright. I understand, but you need to tell me every single detail, got it?” Dong Su Zhu easily relented since it was Su Yan who spoke.","Su Yan gave a nod, and Xia Ning Chang took the opportunity to grab the two children by the hand. She led them away to a corner, where they would not disturb the meeting.","However, before the twins left, Yang Xu gave an ‘inconspicuous’ thumbs up to Yu Ru Meng, and then a fist.","At that point, Yu Ru Meng gave a small nod, with luscious lips that formed a smile, but her eyes definitely held fury.","***","At this point, the Wives Council had basically been assembled, except for Xia Ning Chang. However, that was not an issue as Xia Ning Chang did not hold as much interest in these gatherings. She would often just keep quiet and listen to what was being talked about if she was present. Also, when she met up with one of the other Sisters, she could always ask them about what was being discussed. In a way, that could function as a conversation starter for her.","So, out of all the Mothers, she was normally the one to take care of the children while the others were busy.","While Su Yan was sharing what had happened during the twin’s trial, many Mothers could be seen wincing. They knew that the trial would be dangerous but not to this extent.","Dong Shu Zhu could be seen with a pale face, as she regretted not forcibly cancelling the whole trial, using all her might.","Even the more cold Ji Yao could not help but have some of her aura leak, causing the surrounding temperature to pullment, which was contrasting to Zhu Qing, who would increase the surrounding temperature with her leaking aura.","Typically, anyone would feel their skin burn or freeze if they were around these two women when they leaked out their aura like that. However, since everyone present had high cultivation, this was not that big of an issue.","At this moment, some were glad that none of the other children were here.","Qu Hua Chang and Tao Ling Wan were both biting their lips.","As for the two most cunning of the bunch, Shan Qing Luo and Yu Ru Meng, the former was frowning while the latter was smiling. However, both of their eyes had unmistakable fury in them. They were certainly not going to let this matter rest.","“We need to quickly decide on how we will deal with this!” Zhu Qing straightforwardly said, slamming the table, which was rare for someone like her. However, no one corrected her. Instead, the all gave a nod in response.","“There is no need to rush. Our precious Daughter has brought us time.” Yu Ru Meng smiled, but her eyes were certainly not smiling.","“Oh? Was that what those hand signals meant?” Shan Qing Luo asked.","Naturally, all the women, with their high cultivation, had noticed those hand gestures. It was just that they did not question it, since it was obviously meant for Yu Ru Meng.","Yu Ru Meng smiled, choosing not to elaborate on it too much. After all, this was her little ‘secret code’ with Yang Xu. Though those observant enough would be able to deduce what Yang Xu was telling her, she would still like to not leak it out.","“Just know that our Daughter wishes for her Father to be punished, and that he would not be coming back for at least a day.” Yu Ru Meng said with narrowed eyes."]},{"number":6059,"title":"Chapter 6059, Mother Knows Men Best","paragraphs":["Chapter 6059, Mother Knows Men Best","Author: Silavin","“Oh? There’s such a thing?” Shan Qing Luo commented with a grin. “Seems like our Eldest Daughter is someone who bears quite the grudge. Guess it’s normal for her considering what happened to her beloved Brother. I wonder who she learnt it from?”","Naturally, Shan Qing Luo’s eyes were on Yu Ru Meng, who shrugged. “Like you’re one to talk. Pretty sure her cunningness has much to do with you as with me. Besides, not like any of us here thinks it’s a bad thing for her to be like this.”","The rest nodded on that point. Certainly, Yang Xu being more aware of her surroundings, and also more adaptive to situations, helps them. Compared to Yang Ji, who idolises his Father, it was better to have a Daughter who they could easily talk to.","The only concern they had was that this Daughter of theirs seemed to only have eyes for her Twin Brother. In fact, her Father was probably worth a toenail as compared to her Brother. She would gladly throw her Father to the wolves, knowing fully well he would make it out fine, if it meant her Brother would be kept safe.","It was for this reason that all her Mothers could only shake their heads at how Yang Xu was acting.","Still, they all agreed on one point–this whole ordeal should not repeat itself. Though the whole situation was in context to how strong Yang Ji and Yang Xu were, it was remarkably dangerous for them to be sent to the Black Ink Clan. The Mothers had expected some level of danger, but not to this extent.","Who could possibly accept having their children, who were only around twelve, fight off against a Territory Lord and a Royal Lord? They were not even in the Open Heaven Realm! They were only in the Dao Source Realm!","This was far too much, even for someone like Su Yan, who leaned more towards supporting her children’s independent growth. Certainly, Yang Kai was there, and had been a safety net for the twins. However, that safety net was not absolute, not when the region they were sent to was still full of mysteries. Proof of that was the peculiar little worm that stuck to the twins, which even till now, no one present knew of its origins.","All Mothers present were concerned not only for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, but for the other children as well. This matter could not be allowed to repeat itself.","Currently, Yang Xu has bought them precious time to decide on how to handle things before Yang Kai returns to soothe things over with them.","“In that case, what sort of punishment should we deliver? Pretty sure that rascal wants something more than a slap on the wrist.” Zhu Qing asked, still musing over the fact that Yang Xu was acting so resolute. In her mind, disappointing that girl was not an option. As a fellow Dragon, she naturally had to support this Daughter of hers.","Surprisingly, it was the quiet Tao Ling Wan who raised up her hand to caution. “Actually, the children have been asking when they can see their Father. It has been more than a week since some of them last saw him. I don’t think we can go too far with whatever we want to do, and upset them. The children are still young and impressionable. They need to take priority over whatever we do.”","Su Yan gave a nod in agreement, “Yes. The children are the main priority. Even if I want to teach him a lesson, we cannot use the children against him.”","Dong Su Zhu soon gave a knowing smile. She was glad that her Son had all these wise Wives with him. Knowing men and their weaknesses, Dong Su Zhu openly stated, “Of course we can’t have my precious Grandchildren suffer because of that naughty boy. Don’t worry, we will let them spend as much time with their Father as possible. In fact, they will surely enjoy their time with him.”","“Oh? Mother, you have an idea?” Shan Qing Luo curiously asked.","There, Dong Su Zhu gave a knowing smile, a little excited for the upcoming event.","...","In the meantime, while the Mothers were discussing, Xia Ning Chang took the twins out of the palace complex. Both kids, on her left and her right, were retelling what had happened. Yang Ji would elaborate with great fervor, while Yang Xu would occasionally step in to correct him on different points.","As they walked, occasional soft bell-like laugher could be heard coming out of Xia Ning Chang’s soft lips. She would attentively listen and just gently ask what happened next, seemingly eager to know what her precious children had been up to while they were away.","It had to be noted that the children made no mention of the actual dangers they encountered. Instead of mentioning a Royal Lord, they would just describe how the opponent looked and what they did.","This was a deliberate action on their part, without needing any prior agreement. Out of all their Mothers, Xia Ning Chang tended to be the one who worries for them the most. Even if Yang Ji was dense, their Mother, Su Yan, had advised them not to make Xia Ning Chang worry unnecessarily.","They could still recall how in the past, when one of their Siblings got sick, their Mother Ning Chang had locked inside her Pill Room to refine an excessive number of Pills in panicked desperation. The result was naturally a mountain of High Grade Pills when only one was needed. Furthermore, the Pills used up rare ingredients, so much so that Hua Qing Si, the High Heaven Palace Manager, had a hard time replenishing the stock.","For that to never happen again, the Family had basically separated Xia Ning Chang from anything that might cause her to worry.","Thus, Yang Ji would just mention all the interesting and fun bits, removing most of the dangers they had faced.","When Xia Ning Chang heard of the familiar name of ‘Mo Na Ye’, her face turned solemn for a moment before relaxing after realising that the man meant no harm towards the children.","She walked them all the way to their other Brothers and Sisters, who were currently in another palace, the Starry Sky Palace. There, all Siblings would live close to one another.","As expected, the moment Xia Ning Chang stepped into the palace, many other children had rushed out to greet her in excitement. After all, this was the Mother who would always give them delicious Pills for being good children.","In total, Yang Kai had ten children, with Yang Ji and Yang Xu being the oldest of the group. Each Mother basically had one child except for Su Yan, who bore twins. Out of the eight children, currently, only five had come out.","Two had not begun to walk yet, and the oldest besides the twins was busy, in close door cultivation.","“Big Brother, Big Sister.” The other Sibling the twins were closest to was Xia Ning Chang’s Biological Daughter, Yang Ling. She was so close, that out of the five, she has given priority to the Twins rather than her own Mother."]},{"number":6060,"title":"Chapter 6060, Starry Sky Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 6060, Starry Sky Palace","Author: Silavin","“Ah, Yang Ling!” Yang Ji immediately reacted by giving her a big hug. Similar to Xia Ning Chang, Yang Ling tended to be quiet most of the time. However, she sheds off her shyness when it comes to those closest to her, namely the twins and her own Mother.","Meanwhile, Yang Xu just gave her a small wave.","“Big Brother, Big Sister, where did you two go? It has been very boring without the two of you...” Yang Ling complained while in Yang Ji’s arms, looking up at him.","Out of all their Siblings, Yang Ji could not help but pamper her. At just around six years old, she was just too cute. Her big round eyes, well rounded squishy cheeks and innocent demeanour made her the center of attention–even if the girl did not want the attention.","Even if she was spoiled, that had not ruined her. For some reason, the little girl had always been down to Earth, demanding little. Even in terms of attention, she would willingly give way to those younger than her.","Out of all the children, she was definitely the one who took the greatest care of others.","Yang Ji hesitated to say. After all, Xia Ning Chang had asked the twins not to divulge what had happened to the other children since it was a really dangerous place, one in which the children need not know about right now. Even so, Yang Ling’s innocent round eyes made him feel guilty if he were to lie.","“Sorry Yang Ling, we went out with our Mother to see the Phoenix Clan.” Yang Xu was spared from those eyes and quickly explained. Though not directly stared at, even Yang Xu knew how potent that innocent gaze was.","“Ah? Did you have a good time there? Was it nice? Can I go with you next time?” Yang Ling adorably asked.","“Sure, we will ask our Mom if we can bring you there.” Yang Xu could only say as much to placate her.","“Yay~”","Even her cheer was cute as it was soft and she snuggled against Yang Ji.","Then, a shout suddenly came.","“Ah! You brats are finally back, huh!?”","It was the familiar voice of the man who had chased them back then. It was none other than their Uncle, Yang Xiao.","He had almost instantly appeared beside them and glared at them, seemingly wanting to teach them a lesson.","Naturally, another voice came in, it was their Aunt, Yang Xue. “What are you shouting for you idiot? Do you want to wake up the other kids?”","However, before Yang Xiao could enact any justice to the Twins, his ear received its just deserts as Yang Xue immediately pulled it as she reprimanded him. “I just got those two to sleep, and here you are making so much noise.”","“Ahh...”","Xia Ning Chang noticed the two and giggled. She immediately stepped in to placate Yang Xue. “Sister-in-Law, we need to keep quiet.”","“Ah... right... I’ll let you off this time, but only this time.” Yang Xue shrugged and then let go, allowing Yang Xiao to finally rub his freed ear. This action was only made more awkward when the other little kids giggled at him.","However, the next target was naturally the Twins. “As for you two, to go off for so long. Come with me.”","The other children, seemingly knowing this commanding tone, all looked away.","As for the Twins, they had no choice but to agree since Mother Ning Chang was still smiling at them. “Don’t worry. I’ll go with you.”","“Okay...”","The Twins began to start walking to a location without being told, as though repeated countless times. In fact, Yang Xue need not even look at them to know where they were going as she said to Yang Xiao, “Look after them while we are away. Since you’ve made so much noise, if any of the younger ones wake up, it’ll be your job to pacify them.”","Yang Xiao could only nod. What else could he do but nod?","However, Yang Xue paid special attention to Yang Ling, as she gently said to her, “Sorry Ling’er, I know you miss them a lot and want to spend your time with them but Auntie has some very important business with them. I promise they will spend the whole day with you after this, okay?”","Yang Ling just gave a cute obedient nod, as though all was forgiven. “En.”","“Good girl. Okay, for now, can you help take care of the others? I’m sure you know your Uncle by now.” Yang Xue said, which caused Yang Ling to giggle and Yang Xiao to point at himself and question to himself, ‘wait, what did I do wrong?’","However, it was not like he could rebut at this point. After being with Yang Xue for so long, he knew better than to open the can of worms.","Yang Ling just gave a nod and quickly moved to grab two of her Younger Siblings’ hands, leading them away. Despite not being the oldest out of the five, she was the most well regarded one. Also, since their Aunt had basically put her in charge, like usual, the rest just followed her lead to the palace courtyard to play with Yang Xiao trailing behind.","***","Where Yang Ji and Yang Xu went was Yang Xue’s own home within the Starry Sky Palace. Naturally, with Yang Xue’s cultivation, and being Yang Kai’s own Biological Sister, she could have her own palace, but she chose to stay close to her Nieces and Nephews.","Of course, since Yang Xue wanted to live here, Yang Xiao had to follow.","It could be due to her past, where most of her childhood was trapped within the Flowing Time Temple, that she chose to stick close to her Family now. Also, her own Brother was not present most of the time, during her childhood and after when she was an adult, which might have added more to the feeling of reluctance to stay away from her Family.","That being said, it was a little suffocating for her to live with her ‘still active’ Parents. So, she opted to live next to her Nieces and Nephews. For some reason, with these kids, everyday was interesting. They were all developing so fast that it was hard to believe, be it cultivation or just growth in general.","Naturally, after spending so much time with the children, she had gotten used to their habits. Likewise, they had gotten used to how hers as well.","When she was about to punish them, they would typically do so in her hall, the Xue Hall.","(Silavin: It means Snow Hall, but can also mean Blood Hall, since the pin yin is the same)","Right now, the Twins were obediently sitting on two mats, awaiting the judge to enter the room. However, right now, both were not worried in the slightest. After all, their Mother Ning Chang would be here with them.","With her here, there was no need to fear!","*Dong*","The door to the room opened, and footsteps entered. There two women stepped in, and they sat across from the Twins. However, before either of them spoke, the room behind was already shut with Yang Xue’s Divine Sense.","Soon, the door glowed with marking, and an Array had been activated. It was an Isolation Array, to prevent outside disturbances. Typically, Yang Xue would activate it when she was cultivating. She would rarely activate it when there were children inside.","So, when she activated it, the Twins could not help but be a little nervous.","“Now, no one can disturb us. So, tell me, what happened to your Uncle Eleven at the end? Also, when was the last time you saw Fang Tian Ci and Thunder Shadow?”"]},{"number":6061,"title":"Chapter 6061, Inquiry","paragraphs":["Chapter 6061, Inquiry","Author: Silavin","They first eyed Xia Ning Chang, who gave a soft sigh and stressed, “I knew you two were hiding something from me. Everything you’ve told me on the way here has left out so many key details. I know you two are worried about me, but I am still your Mother. Regardless of what had happened, I also need to know.”","Xia Ning Chang rarely seeked out answers from her Children like this. After all, she could always find out from the other Mothers or her own Sister-in-Law. However, this time, it was different. She could clearly sense how angry Su Yan was when she had returned with the Twins.","Though she knew the answers would fall onto her lap eventually, since the other Mothers would inform her of it, for the first time in a long while, she felt like she could not help but get involved in this. At the very least, she wanted to find out what the Twins went through from their own mouths.","She could have asked all these questions earlier, but she doubted they would tell her. So, she got her Sister-in-Law involved in this as well–who would definitely also love to hear just what had happened.","At this point, the Twins knew that there was no point hiding anything.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both took turns narrating what had happened, everything from start to finish. No details were missed.","This time, through their story, Xia Ning Chang’s expression would change drastically from worry to relief, back to fear and reproach. The same could be said for Yang Xue, though she was not as expressive–her face remained neutral throughout but her eyes spoke volumes of her inner turmoil.","...","“And that’s how we returned” Yang Ji ended the tale with that.","Yang Xue heaved a heavy sigh before directly scolding, “Why didn’t you two immediately run away when faced against a Royal Lord or a Territory Lord!? Did you think Artifacts and Pills are going to save you two against them!?”","In response, the Twin could only offer silence. Truth be told, they had really done the unthinkable. Yet, if one were to ask whether they would do the same thing again, they knew in their hearts of hearts that they would.","For some reason, unbeknownst to the Twins themselves, during those dangerous moments, they had not felt like they would really die. Still, those feels had not been realised nor articulated, so it remained a mystery why they had felt like that.","Seeing how the two of them were not offering even the shortest word in response, Xia Ning Chang just sighed and tapped on Yang Xue’s shoulder, “Calm down.”","“But Sister-in-Law!” Yang Xue was basically ready to flip the table at this point. However, seeing how the usually worried Xia Ning Chang was remaining strangely calm, she too started to mellow down.","Xia Ning Chang just shook her head, and she moved to the Twins and hugged both of them. “I’m just so glad that both of you are safe. Just promise that you won’t do something so dangerous again, okay?”","The Twins hugged her back and gave obedient nods.","It took awhile before Xia Ning Chang willingly let them go. “For now, please play with Yang Ling. She misses you two a lot. While you two were away, she kept asking where you two were.”","Yang Ji immediately responded, “En.”","After all, even without her saying this, they would always make time for Yang Ling.","“Okay, go off for now. We adults have something to discuss.” Xia Ning Chang said as she turned to look at Yang Xue, who gave a sigh and unlocked the Isolation Array.","The Twins looked at each other for a moment, and quickly ran out. After all, since Mother Ning Chang had given them permission to leave, that meant that they would not need to face any punishment today. In short, strike when the iron is hot and quickly get out!","Once the two left, Yang Xue reactivated the Isolation Array and she questioned, “Sister-in-Law, you are too soft on them. What if-”","“What if they actually died there, right?” Xia Ning Chang softly said as she slowly shook her head, wishing that thought never appeared again. No Mother’s heart could bear to see the grave of her Children.","Still Xia Ning Chang shook her head and said, “It’s not really their fault. They were put in that situation. Also, you know whose fault this mainly lies with. There is no point in getting angry with them.”","Yang Xue sighed, “Fine. Seems like Brother will be in for a whole storm once he gets back.”","Xia Ning Chang gave a nod in agreement. After knowing all that had transpired, she knew Yang Kai was going to face the wrath of her other Sisters. Still, she warned Yang Xue about their utmost priority, “But, I am worried about that ‘little worm’ in their story. Have you ever heard of such a thing?”","Yang Xue shook her head, “I don’t know but I think Brother definitely knows a thing or two about it. Let me go and check on this with Wu Kuang. Maybe he knows something about it. I’ll also ask Yang Xiao to ask the Divine Spirits.”","“In that case, I’ll try to refine a Pill to expel it if possible...”","Both women were definitely worried. However, showing such emotions to the children would only make things worse. Especially for Xia Ning Chang–she knew her tendencies were what made the Twins hide details from her. So, now she tried her best to hide such feelings, making an effort to only show it to the adults.","Regardless, the details about the little worm had unnerved her and Yang Xue, to the point she immediately made the Twins leave so that they could decide on their next step.","***","It was already the next day by the time Yang Kai had returned from the Profound Source Gate. He naturally travelled through the same route Su Yan and the Twins took and got to the World Tree.","There, he saw his two other Selves already drinking, and already knew their intention.","Without any words, the two raised their cups to Yang Kai in greeting. Yang Kai just shook his head, and sat down in front of them, also taking out another cup and a few bottles of alcohol.","At this point, no words were needed. They just drank and drank.","They would take turns pouring for the others, savouring the scent and flavour of each gulp.","Once all the alcohol was gone, all three just stood up.","“I’ll be heading East.” Thunder Shadow said.","“And, I’ll be heading West.” Fang Tian Ci declared.","Yang Kai simply cupped his fist towards the two of them.","However, before the Man and Panther left, they warned, “Big Brother, do take care once you get back. Eldest Sister-in-Law did not look too happy when she returned.”","Yang Kai sighed, as though already knowing the storm that was to come. “Thanks, I know. Quite sad that you two are leaving me during my time of need.”","Thunder Shadow joked, “You’ll survive.”","Fang Tian Ci just shook his head, “I guess that’s what you get for making use of our Niece and Nephew.”","Yang Kai sighed again. “You say it as though this is all my fault. I was doing this for the sake of everyone’s future.”","Fang Tian Ci just shook his head, “This is this, that is that. I’m so glad I didn’t get married.”","Thunder Shadow shared the same sentiment, “En, after watching Big Brother, I think single life is best for now.”","“Wait. Then what about me? I’ll never get to see any Nieces or Nephews then. You two don’t want to have any, Yang Xue and Yang Xiao also don’t want to have any.” Yang Kai was a little frustrated at this point. He was the only Father here. How was it that none of his ‘Siblings’ wanted Children?","“You have already done our share.” Fang Tian Ci only said as much and disappeared, as though he wanted to cut out any argument.","Yang Kai clenched his fist and then turned towards Thunder Shadow.","“Err... see you.” Thunder Shadow’s eyes darted around. He also wanted to say he agreed with Fang Tian Ci’s sentiments, but at this point, would he dare to say that?","He too quickly disappeared, obviously thanks to the World Tree.","At this point, it was uncertain whether they had coordinated with the World Tree to say this last bit before immediately getting teleported away, or they had quickly asked the World Tree to send them away once they said enough.","Regardless, Yang Kai could only put both hands on his face as he awaited what would happen to him once he got home..."]},{"number":6062,"title":"Chapter 6062, How to Appease Wives","paragraphs":["Chapter 6062, How to Appease Wives","Author: Silavin","The saying ‘happy Wife, happy life’ was true. As a married man now, Yang Kai already knew a storm was coming for him. However, he was still a man with great consciousness. He knew that this matter was for him to deal with, and him alone. So, he did not ask the World Tree for anything, just to lead him back home. After all, he did not want any third-parties to get caught in the crossfire.","The World Tree, also a being with great empathy, chose to transfer him over to a location a little further from High Heaven Palace–instead of directly to his Wives. That way, Yang Kai could make any necessary arrangements if need be.","With gratitude in his heart, Yang Kai quickly made way to the shopping districts.","The conundrum he faced now was how to please his Wives so that they would lessen his punishment.","Why only ‘lessen’? Because he had multiple Wives!","Even if he had managed to please one, the others would hold the line!","Pleasing them all was as hard as scaling Mountain Tai. In fact, Yang Kai felt that pleasing them all was harder than his fight against Mo.","He was not like his Father, Yang Ying Feng, who could sometimes get away with it using the ‘oldest trick in the book’. Of course, even for his Father, the back pain the next day could also be counted as a form of punishment.","However, that would be impossible for Yang Kai. Rather than let him ‘sacrifice’ his body, it was more likely he would spend the nights cold and alone. Even his children would most likely not be allowed to accompany their dearest Father.","Regardless, right now, the only thing he could do was to quickly purchase goods to lift their mood, and hope that it would be enough to appease them.","Yang Kai mentally noted down what each one liked. However, even this had issues.","For example, for Pills, Yang Kai was certain that none of his Wives would be satisfied with Pills since Xia Ning Chang would refine them whenever she had time. In fact, rather than an occupation, she would do so even as a hobby.","So, none of his Family members lacked Pills–from beauty Pills to cultivation Pill, they had them all. So, Pills were already out of the question.","Artifacts were certainly an interesting option, as one could never have enough Artifacts. However, what kind of Artifact was also another issue.","To meet these women’s eyes, who already stood at the peak of the 3,000 Worlds, ordinary Artifacts would not do. Certainly, if they were to have some form of sentimental value, that was a different thing entirely. However, Yang Kai’s Wives would certainly know his plan.","[Little Senior Sister, Su Yan, Xue Yue, Yu Ru Meng and Ji Yao are not really concerned with material goods. Shan Qing Luo... would probably prefer something more perverse... Zhu Qing would be happy with something to help further purify her Bloodline. Qu Hua Chang tends to like Artifacts that are beautiful and Tao Ling Wan would prefer more simple looking Artifacts....]","Five out of the nine had already been judged to be really hard to please. Despite this, Yang Kai would still have to try his best. He would also need to pick one item for all nine, since he had to be fair about it.","Creating those Artifacts himself would certainly add some sentimental value to it. However, he was certain that the longer he delayed going back home, the worse the outcome would get. So, a quick trip to the Auction Houses around High Heaven Star City was needed.","However, unbeknownst to Yang Kai, it seemed like this plan of his had already been seen though...","***","“Palace Mistresses, a mysterious man has entered the High Heaven Auction House. He is wearing a mask and is purposefully hiding his cultivation, as you have expected.” A voice could be heard through a Transmission Token.","Hua Qing Si, the Palace Manager, soon rubbed her forehead and replied. “Understood. Just keep an eye on him and inform me of any purchase he has made.”","Hua Qing Si sighed once more before turning to the women in front of her. The two Palace Mistresses of High Heaven Palace, Yu Ru Meng and Shan Qing Luo.","After the Wives Council meeting, these two had immediately sought for the Palace Manager.","After being married for so long, they naturally knew what Yang Kai would do. However, this time, there was really no escaping the punishment since even their Mother-in-Law was fully on board with it this time.","They knew he would try to appease them, but could mere material goods truly make up for everything?","No! Of course not! Besides their own personal rage, they were now determined to crush the ‘Cuckoo Yang Family’ tradition!","What about training for the Children? They could still do that in High Heaven Palace! There was no need for them to risk their lives like Yang Ji and Yang Xu.","So what if they were not going to be as strong? Would it matter if they were dead? To the Mothers, they did not need their children to hold up the sky! As their Mothers, they would be the ones to hold up the sky for them!","Even if they were gone, they had their Sister-in-Law to hold the fort. What more, the whole backing of High Heaven Palace would be with their Children. Conceit and arrogance was a worry, but they believe that the Children had been taught well enough to not fall into those traps. Besides, could they truly be arrogant when monsters like Yang Ji and Yang Xu were always beside them?","Right now, the Wives Council had already agreed on a direction, and all Wives of the Yang Family had already set out to do their own task. Since this was going to be an entire policy change within the Yang Family, everyone was going to take part, even Yang Xue.","Naturally, they also dragged third-parties into this as well, since they knew better than anyone else that to truly change a tree, the whole earth underneath needed to be changed.","“As expected, Sister Ru Meng, you were right. He actually went to the High Heaven Auction House first.” Shan Qing Luo giggled as she tossed a Space Ring filled with Heaven Opening Pills to Yu Ru Meng.","Yu Ru Meng gladly accepted the Space Ring with a smile after winning the bet, “Thank you, now I have more money to treat Ai’er and Little Mei’er.”","Shan Qing Luo rolled her eyes at the blatant attempt to win over her Daughter’s favour and asked, “We are not supposed to play favourites. You can’t just treat only our Daughters.”","Yu Ru Meng just giggled without replying.","“Anyways, what now? Do you not plan to go after him?” Shan Qing Luo, seeing as Yu Ru Meng was not going to change her decision, just ignored it and moved on to the main topic.","Yu Ru Meng shook her head. “Why should we stop him when he is going to give us gifts? Besides, the Wives Council would uphold whatever had been decided upon. Even Sister Su Yan, Sister Ning Chang and Sister Ling Wan are angry, you know?”","Shan Qing Luo sighed, “Yeah, it is really rare for them to be so angry.”","Hua Qing Si, a little nervous but curious, asked, “Will the Palace Master be okay?”","“Hahaha. It’s not like we are going to eat him. But, I do think that you should spread news about our Husband trying to buy many presents for his Wives and Children.” Shan Qing Luo laughed upon hearing her being so worried.","Yu Ru Meng then quickly added, “Also, make sure he cannot touch the High Heaven Palace Treasury and do enjoy a long vacation after having worked so hard for so long.”","At this point, since the Palace Mistresses had already made the decision, a decision even the Palace Master would not be able to overturn by himself, Hua Qing Si just carried out those orders with a heavy heart. [Sorry Palace Master, but I will not be able to help you...]"]},{"number":6063,"title":"Chapter 6063, Heavenly Demon Queen?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6063, Heavenly Demon Queen?","Author: Silavin","In the next two days, Yang Kai quickly rushed all over not only High Heaven Star City, but the whole of Star Boundary.","This was a task he had to do personally. If he asked someone else to help him buy the goods, and his Wives found out about it, he did not know how much it would backfire. Instead of risking his hide, he might as well just do it all himself.","Even if High Heaven Star City was the most prosperous area in Star Boundary, due to it having connections to the 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises, there might still be other treasures not found here. So, Yang Kai tried his luck at multiple locations, regardless if he had to travel from the Northern Territory to the Southern Territory–distance did not matter.","Since he was a Great Emperor of Star Boundary, he could instantly teleport to wherever he willed himself to be in, so long as it was still within Star Boundary.","Even amidst the worry that he still has not collected enough ‘gifts’, he knew he needed to return by now. After all, counting the time he separated from Su Yan and the Twins, it had already been four days, two of which were fully dedicated to purchasing these ‘gifts’.","***","Within a room, decorated with drawing, Artifacts and Pills, were three children, peacefully asleep.","Yang Ji had woken up with a familiar sensation. Unbeknownst to him, while he was asleep, Yang Xu had taken one of his arms as her own pillow. However, this time, even the other arm felt like it had been locked in a vice grip...","When he turned his head to the other side, he saw Yang Ling, using his arm as a bolster.","He could not help but wonder, [Are my arms so soft that you two want to use me as a cushion? Seems like I have to start doing some muscle training!]","Naturally, Yang Ji was misunderstanding. Yang Xu aside, it was not rare for Yang Ling to sleep next to her Siblings. It was just that Yang Ji and Yang Xu rarely slept due to their cultivation realm, that he had forgotten how Yang Ling would normally cuddle with someone while she slept. This time, she merely wanted to spend more time with those two who had left High Heaven Palace for so long.","So, once Yang Ji and Yang Xu went to sleep after they played, Yang Ling had come to join them after she was tired.","Then, there was a sudden voice in his head.","It was a voice he had never heard before. This voice was feminine and seemed to be more mature. If any man had heard it, their hearts would most likely start racing. However, Yang Ji was not a man yet so it just sounded like any Auntie to him.","“Oh? You’re finally awake. Did not think that someone of your calibre would need sleep. Though, I guess playing with your Siblings is quite exhausting, and adding everything you’ve experienced in the Source World. To think you would use Space and Time Principles to play hide and seek...”","“Huh?” Yang Ji exclaimed, confused where this voice came from.","“Emm?” His sudden jump had caused Yang Xu to also slowly mummer in her sleep, seemingly about to wake up.","“Oh? You still haven’t figured out who I am? I’m in your Dantian.” The voice, seemingly amused, chuckled.","“Little worm?” Yang Ji immediately focused on his Dantain.","Seemingly having been insulted, the voice shot back, “How rude of you to call me a worm! I might have tolerated it before but you are going to call me by my title, Heavenly Demon Queen from now on, you got that?”","Yang Ji felt like he was being unjustly accused. After all, what was wrong with calling a worm, a worm? Though he already knew beforehand that she was not a worm, her appearance was similar to one. Furthermore, his Sister was the one who placed that label on her. He merely called her that since it was easier for everyone. However, because this complaint sounded like his own Mothers’, he just accepted it without saying more, “Okay, okay.”","From his own experience, when women start to nag, it was best to just keep quiet and quickly move on from the topic–a life lesson he learnt from Uncle Yang Xiao!","As expected, since Yang Ji was being so ‘amicable’, the Heavenly Demon Queen was forgiving enough to let the matter go. In fact, she even expressed justification on Yang Ji’s part, as though she was the defendant, prosecutor and judge. “Well, I will be magnanimous and forgive you for this transgression, I can understand since I am in this unsightly form temporarily. I can also empathise with your Sister, and forgive her too.”","At this point, Yang Ji thought that the conversation was over. However, the Heavenly Demon Queen pouted and complained yet again, “Why aren’t you showing your gratitude? I have forgiven you, the least you could do is respond with gratitude.”","Yang Ji felt like he was going to have a headache. What gratitude? He did not feel like he was in the wrong in the first place.","Thankfully, before he needed to speak, Yang Xu had already started rubbing her eyes as she woke up and groggily looked at her Brother, “Morning. What time is it now?”","“Not sure, I also just woke up and haven’t moved from the bed because of you two...”","“Two?” Yang Xu questioned and got up a little and exclaimed, “Oh? Yang Ling,” before lying back on Yang Ji’s arm.","“You’re awake already, can’t you get off me?” Yang Ji, seemingly completely forgetting about the Heavenly Demon Queen, just focused all his attention on Yang Xu.","“Since she is not up yet, then I’ll just stay here.” Yang Xu giggled and rubbed her head on his arm.","Yang Ji just sighed. Then, as he willed it, he freely manipulated Space Principles. Under his fine control, Yang Ji had left the bed and was now on his feet. Meanwhile, the arm that Yang Ling had been hugging was replaced with one of Yang Xu’s arms.","In short, he had teleported Yang Xu to his position while he himself had got up.","This was immaculate control over Space Principles. It was absurd that such power was being used to move children around. Yet, here it was being done freely, without worry where one mistake could have casted Yang Ji or Yang Xu into the Void.","However, it had to be said that if Yang Xu had resisted it, Yang Ji would not have been able to teleport her to replace him so smoothly.","Still, Yang Xu just pouted and whined, “We hardly sleep anymore. Couldn’t we have just remained in bed for longer?”","“If you want to stay in bed, then just stay there. I want to go out to see what’s going on outside. I can sense our Mothers are moving about. I wonder what is going on outside.” Yang Ji said while already moving towards the exit.","“Wait...” Yang Xu naturally wanted to go with him. She too had felt that there was far more commotion amongst the adults than usual. She had her own guesses as to why. However, when she turned to look at how peacefully asleep Yang Ling was, she just sighed and relented. She could not bear to wake her up.","After all, what was also the reason why Yang Ji had moved her to replace him in the first place.","Yang Ji, upon hearing that sigh, just waved his hand and disappeared from sight by tearing through the Void.","The next moment, he was already above the Starry Sky Palace, looking down on everything from above.","Below, he could see some of his Siblings running about, playing like usual. However, a few of them were missing. Not accounting for those that were still asleep or could not walk, two were not in Starry Sky Palace. As for the adults, he could see a few of his Mothers moving about the palace grounds, gathered together. However, two adults seemed to be missing, who were always here–Yang Xiao and Yang Xue.","[Oh? Where did they go?] Yang Ji wondered and expanded his Divine Sense to cover an even wider area. He expanded his search to the whole of High Heaven Palace.","[Ah. Yang Ai and Yang Mei are with Mother Ru Meng and Mother Qing Luo. They seem to be enjoying themselves. Though, Mother Qing Luo seems to be pouting and complaining. But, I still can’t find Aunt Yang Xue and Uncle Yang Xiao... maybe they’ve left High Heaven Palace?] Yang Ji was starting to get the itch to leave and look for them. After all, it was a little boring staying in the palace.","However, before he had any other thoughts, a voice spoke to his mind once again. “I’ll be magnanimous and forgive you for ignoring me if you grace me with subsistence appropriate for my status.”"]},{"number":6064,"title":"Chapter 6064, You Use A Lot of Hard Words","paragraphs":["Chapter 6064, You Use A Lot of Hard Words","Author: Silavin","“Subsistence?” Yang Ji tilted his head at this unfamiliar term.","“Do you not need to take in food?” The Heavenly Demon Queen seemed a little surprised at first. After all, even children would know about food, right? However, upon remembering that people at his cultivation realm truly did not need food, she just sighed in her heart, not expecting much. [He requires sleep but not subsistence? This jest is too much.]","“Oh, you’re hungry? Here.” Yang Ji seemed to have realised something and took out Open Heaven Pills. Open Heaven Pills were both a form of currency and cultivation material for cultivators. Technically, children who were weaker in cultivation like Yang Ling would not carry them unless they reached the Emperor Realm, since such potent materials would be more detrimental to them than helpful. Yang Ji and Yang Xu were just exceptions in this case.","Still, the food that the Heavenly Demon Queen was seeking were not these Pills. She wanted a proper meal after so long...","“This is not even food...” The Heavenly Demon Queen would have slapped her own face if she had arms. “Does your family not have meals to socialise?”","“Meals to socialise? You mean eat together? Ermm... I don’t think so. Most of us don’t really get hungry, and sometimes people need to enter secluded cultivation. So, we don’t really eat together. Also, even if I don’t eat these Pills, Mother Ning Chang will just keep giving us more.” Yang Ji said as matter of factly. He seems to be suggesting for her to not be humble and just take the Pill.","How could the Heavenly Demon Queen not understand his underlying words? She was not even trying to be humble. She just wanted to eat a proper meal for once, after so long.","“Then, can you bring me to a culinary establishment to get food?” The Heavenly Demonic Queen said, more direct this time. [It is evident that this boy requires forthright communication...]","“Culinary establishment? You know, you use a lot of hard to understand words. But I guess you are asking for a restaurant right?” Yang Ji at least managed to deduce this.","“Exactly. A restaurant.” The Heavenly Demonic Queen thought for a moment and then gave a slow nod. Though she did not wish to lower herself down, it was evident that it would be hard for the boy to understand her if she kept speaking in her usual manner.","Still, she could not help but add, “Also, do not chastise me when you are the one with paltry vocabulary. Do they not educate you?”","However, obviously, such terms flew over Yang Ji’s head as he ignored it. It was not that he did not know she was faulting him. He could have guessed as much even if he did not understand her words. He was just following one of Uncle Yang Xiao’s teachings: ‘Listen to me Yang Ji, if a woman scolds you, just stay silent. It would be best if she moved on from the topic. If not, try to be the one who moves away from the current topic.’","Such great ‘wisdom’ had certainly proved useful. Indeed, the topic easily shifted as Yang Ji just continued, “But if you want to go to a restaurant, we need to wait for Yang Xu and Yang Ling to wake up. I can’t go off without them.”","“But surely that ignorant Sister of yours does not wish to associate with me.” Remembering what had happened before, the Heavenly Demon Queen brought up this issue.","“It’ll be fine. Yang Xu always listens to me. Also, if I don’t say anything beforehand and leave without her, she would pout for the rest of the day. I also think Yang Ling would like you. She adores wo– animals like you.” Yang Ji smiled.","“Oh? That little one had such discerning eyes? Very well, I do hope to meet such beings who appreciate me.”","Yang Ji just gave a small nod and then soon disappeared into the Void to reappear back inside his bedroom.","His appearance was soon accompanied by a voice.","“If she could talk, why didn’t she talk to us in the first place?”","The first voice that came was Yang Xu, who already knew of the whole situation. After all, Yang Ji could immediately share his thoughts, emotions, and even cultivation with Yang Xu. Even his memories could be shared with her; such was the power of the Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique.","So, there was no need to elaborate. Yang Xu immediately understood the situation. In fact, it was because she understood that her attitude towards the Heavenly Demon Queen became colder. After all, who was this little vixen who was trying to treat her Brother like her servant?","If Yang Xu could, she would tear that worm apart. However, she knew that Yang Ji saw her as an interesting pet. So, she would let this slide for now.","Regardless, the more pressing matter was going out. There was no need to make a fuss here right now. She could deal with this worm at another time.","Yang Ji just looked at the Heavenly Demon Queen, awaiting her answer.","Seeing how an answer was needed, she casually went out of Yang Ji’s Dantian, which shocked the Twins.","“Wait. How are you able to come out so easily!?” Yang Xu immediately raised her vigilance. The Arrays placed on Yang Ji seemed to have become nonexistent. These were Arrays that Uncle Eleven had placed! They were not something that even Yang Xu and Yang Ji would easily destroy.","“Oh? Those restrictions. They only work mono-directionally, to contain this Queen in one vessel. But, can this Queen not transverse through two vessels?” The Heavenly Demon Queen said this as though in triumph; as though she was showing off.","After all, she had basically outsmarted a being that was close to the World Creation Realm, and an actual World Creation Realm expert. Such a feat certainly deserves praise.","“Wait... two vessels? You mean you came out of me!?” Yang Xu now felt all dirty inside.","“Indeed.” The Heavenly Demon Queen did not refute and just said as much.","“I no longer feel the Arrays on me. I guess you must have gotten out of Yang Xu and consumed them?” Yang Ji this time focused on where the Arrays were supposed to be to find his body completely free of them. It had to be said that Little Eleven would naturally not impose Arrays that would hinder a child’s body or make them feel uncomfortable. Furthermore, he would hide them since they would look like tattoos and would raise questions.","Little Eleven did not want to play a part in negatively influencing the children, especially not when Yang Ji would sometimes bath with his Younger Siblings. Also, since the matter with the Heavenly Demon Queen was sensitive, it was best to prevent onset questions from appearing.","The Heavenly Demon Queen, in her small form, gave a small nod. It looked cute to Yang Ji, but looked utterly repulsive to Yang Xu.","“As for my articulation, that I cannot say.” The Heavenly Demon Queen was personally fine with telling them more, but she could already feel this was touching upon the World Restriction–the same restriction that prevented Mo from speaking more."]},{"number":6065,"title":"Chapter 6065, Heavenly Demon Queen’s Power","paragraphs":["Chapter 6065, Heavenly Demon Queen’s Power","Author: Silavin","At this point, all the noise had disturbed the precious princess sleeping. Yang Ling’s eyes struggled to open. But when she did, she saw that she was no longer embracing Yang Ji, but Yang Xu at her thighs.","Yang Xu, sitting up on the bed, was obviously fuming while disgusted. Naturally, Yang Ling’s eyes followed hers’ and it landed upon a curious being that had taken its place on Yang Ji’s shoulder.","The creature was long and seemingly hairless but had two round eyes that held a hint of loftiness.","Being the first time Yang Ling had seen such a creature, her tired eyes soon turned excited as she exclaimed, “What’s that!?”","The Heavenly Demon Queen was obviously pleased with this little girl’s insightful and curious eyes. It was certainly better than the hostile eyes the other girl wore or the ‘so be it’ eyes her main host wore.","The Heavenly Demon Queen was quite quick to act. She immediately shot through space, quickly arriving next to Yang Ling. It was similar to tearing through Space but also different.","However, she had forgotten that the one next to Yang Ling was Yang Xu. How could she possibly let this disgusting creature approach her like this? Once Yang Xu sensed that Space had distorted, she immediately manipulated Space and Time Principles to freeze. Then, at where the Heavenly Demon Queen would appear, she had already swung her hand, reinforced with Space Principles, creating a solid block in her hand.","*Pa!*","The sound of something being struck rang out. However, the Heavenly Demon Queen had not truly been struck. Instead, the solid block formed by Space Principles on Yang Xu’s hand had been the one that got damaged instead. In that block, there was what appeared to be a small hole.","“What!?” Yang Xu cried out, but all she could hear was a scoff from her opponent.","“Ridiculous. If even a being like your Uncle proves incapable of containing this Queen, how presumptuous of you to think you would fare any better?” The Heavenly Demon Queen mocked while landing on Yang Ling’s open hands. As though showing off she had accomplished her goal.","“Damn it! You! How could you break through my Space Principles so easily?” Yang Xu seemed to be unable to admit defeat. She had already started to condense Space again to form a hand to grab a hold of the Heavenly Demon Queen. However, that proved futile once more as it was easily bitten through.","“What you have mastered is but a mere paltry glimpse into the true Dao of Space and Time. You know not about the true role of Space Principles. Indeed, that man who is your Father has surpassed the limits of this world. But, what of it? Do you think he reigns truly supreme in this Realm? And you two, though talented here, you two are but younglings who have not truly stepped out into the wider world. Yet, here you are, already in disbelief that someone else might be able to trample over you?” The Heavenly Demon Queen spoke in a regal manner. At this point, other than mocking them, she was trying to educate them to the reality of things.","“Enough of your presumptuous challenges. I seek substance, and we must definitely bring this young one along.” She pointed her tail at Yang Ling while looking at Yang Ji, completely ignoring Yang Xu and whatever expression she was making.","“Eh? Me?” Yang Ling pointed to herself, confused as to why this small being, who she was seeing for the first time, was so fond of her. They had not even talked, at most, they had only made physical contact.","“Don’t belittle yourself. This Queen has approved of you. Naturally, you would need to attend.” The Heavenly Demon Queen had jumped off Yang Ling’s hand, as though she was done confirming something, and had already moved next to Yang Ji.","However, how could Yang Ji be like her and ignore his Sister?","“You expect us to leave after you made my Sister like that?” Yang Ji scolded.","“Stop it, Brother.” However, Yang Xu had cut him off. His protectiveness would not work here, and she knew it. At this point, it was clear that the Heavenly Demon Queen was a being far stronger than them. Though her origins are a mystery, and Yang Xu found not just her form but her attitude to be repulsive, she chose to swallow those feelings down. [If she wanted to harm us, she could have done so way earlier. But she did not... Brother, there is no need to fall out with such a being and endanger yourself.]","The Heavenly Demon Queen seemed to have read her thoughts and praised while smiling. “Though our association may be less than harmonious, I do acknowledge your sharp mind. Sharper than this Queen’s main host at least. Your vigilance is warranted, but ultimately misplaced.”","How could Yang Xu believe her words at face value?","Yang Ling, sensing the tension in the air rising, and just wanted everyone to get along, said with an adorable stammer. “B-be nice!”","Yang Ji, seeing how even the shy Yang Ling had spoken up, took it upon himself to stop everyone. “Enough. As promised, we will head out to eat. Any more fighting would just waste time.”","“Hmph”","“En”","Yang Xu snorted and started to move on ahead while the Heavenly Demon Queen, who just wanted to get to a restaurant already, just remained quiet. Meanwhile, Yang Ji and Yang Ling just breathed out a sigh of relief.","*Snap* With a snap of his fingers, Yang Ji once more teleported back up to the sky. However, this time, he had brought along with him his two Sisters.","As they floated high up above, he asked, “It’s been so long since we last went out to eat. Any place you want to go?”","Yang Xu shook her head while Yang Ling raised her hand.","“I want to go and eat at the Recalling Dreams Pavilion. Is that okay?” Yang Ling asked, with some hesitation.","“Recalling Dreams Pavilion?” Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked at each other. They had obviously never heard of this restaurant before. Then again, they had never really sought out restaurants, and every time they snuck out, it was mostly to explore or play.","“En, it’s Aunt Qiu Yi Meng’s restaurant... Mother brought me there a few times before, and the food there is really good.”","“Oh? Aunt Qiu Yi Meng? Hmm... it had been quite a while since we last saw her. Might be fun to see her again.” Yang Ji said with a nod, which was easily agreed upon by Yang Xu.","Though they did not know the location, with their powerful Divine Sense, they did not even ask where it was. They just scanned the whole High Heaven Star City, splitting the task of searching left and right of the city to each other.","Each signboard was checked, and within seconds, Yang Ji found it.","“Oh? It’s over there!” Yang Ji pointed at the location with excitement. Then, at the next moment, he snapped his fingers but nothing happened. He snapped again and exclaimed. “Eh?”","Yang Xu, seeing the confusion on his face, swung her whole arm this time, intending to tear into Space to create a Void Crack. However, though Space did indeed tear right before their eyes, it was quickly mended back, and restored to its original form.","“Attempt once more with more force. I’ll aid you this time.” The Heavenly Demon Queen, who had kept silent this whole time, suddenly spoke up.","Yang Ji gave a nod, and this time, with two arms, he forcibly tore Space apart, creating a bigger Void Crack. Naturally, like before, it started to mend. However, this time, the Heavenly Demon Queen charged forward and quickly bit at the edges.","With each chomp, the mending seemed to have stopped. It was until she did a loop that it stopped entirely. Nevertheless, she warned, “Enter at once, before it seals itself.”","The Twins both looked at each other and gave a knowing nod. Yang Xu charged forward first, while Yang Ji took Yang Ling’s hand and ran in.","Once all three Children entered, the Heavenly Demon Queen scoffed and entered as well.","***","Meanwhile, inside her room, Su Yan’s closed eyes fluttered a little. When she focused her Divine Sense at the Void Crack that her Children had passed through, she muttered, “To even be able to stop me... who is at the Ninth Order... just who are you? Still, those two naughty Children should be able to tell that it was my doing but they still went ahead and left...”","Naturally, Space would not mend so quickly unless it was done by an Array or by someone else. Su Yan was the one who purposefully closed all those Void Cracks and sealed the Space around Starry Sky Palace.","Her target was not the children, but their Father. Who knew when he would be back, trying to sneak in? Nevertheless, she happened upon an interesting sight.","The first time Yang Ji tried teleporting out, her interference was not on purpose. However, noticing the familiar little worm with them, she intentionally blocked their other attempts.","If she had used her full strength, the Twins would naturally not be able to tear through Space. So, she merely mended the Space once it was torn.","Unexpectedly, that mysterious being had managed to stop her from mending Space. Though she did not know the extent of the mysterious being’s power, it had led her Children to go through the Void Crack, essentially disallowing Su Yang from further interfering. After all, if those three were inside the Void, and she messed with it, who knew where they would end up?","So, seemingly before the Heavenly Demon Queen needed to expose more of her strength, she hid behind the well-being of the Children.","Still, since the Void Crack was there, Su Yan easily deduced where the Children went. She naturally got up and left to keep an eye on them, sending a message to Xia Ning Chang, Qu Hua Chang and Tao Ling Wan about the situation before she left."]},{"number":6066,"title":"Chapter 6066, Recalling Dreams Pavilion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6066, Recalling Dreams Pavilion","Author: Silavin","*Ci*","A Void Crack opened in the sky and the three children ran out, followed by an inconspicuous figure. Naturally, due to the intense Space Fluctuations, they drew attention from the streets below.","However, as though in their own world, they did not hear the muttering of, ‘who is that?’, ‘how can there be such young experts over the Dao of Space, and etc.","It was naturally for the Yang Family children to not be recognised outside. After all, most of their time was spent within the Starry Sky Palace. Even when travelling outside with their Mothers, they tend to keep a low profile. This was basically the common preference amongst their Mothers.","However, Yang Ling was not as unaffected by the stares of onlookers as she quickly hid behind her Big Brother.","Meanwhile, the Twins did not really care about the onlookers. Rather, they were worried about the power that had worked hard to prevent them from escaping.","“You don’t think...” Yang Ji looked at Yang Xu and the latter just gave a nod.","*Haaa...* Yang Ji sighed and looked back at the Void Crack, which had already started to mend and disappear. “But why would Mother try to keep us in the Palace? She’s never tried to do this whenever we try to escape.”","“Why don’t you ask her?” Yang Xu cast a sidelong glance at the obvious culprit.","The Heavenly Demon Queen just ignored the question and flew around to give a few small sniffs. “Why fret over such insignificant matters? The establishment beneath us is waiting.”","[Well, if Mother is worried, then she would turn up soon enough. With her powers, she definitely knows where we are. Might as well wait for her in the restaurant first.] Yang Ji gave it a brief thought and then gave a nod, which Yang Xu immediately understood.","The three soon flew down and landed just outside of Recalling Dreams Pavilion’s front door.","As though signifying great prosperity, the doors were made of a dark Fifth-Order Material, lined with a hint of golden coloured Seventh-Order Materials. Even the signboard outside was made of Seventh-Order Yang Element Materials, which gave anyone who saw this sign a warm feeling.","Naturally with such a lavish exterior, the service provided was not lacking either. Just before the front door, there were two figures. These two were the servants meant to greet their customers.","Typically, there were four, but two had gone inside. They had recognised that three figures had appeared above their establishments from the commotion of the onlookers on the street. When using their Divine Sense to check, they naturally noticed Yang Ling.","Though she and her Mother were not frequent customers, they were one of the rare VIPs. These two happened to have greeted Xia Ning Chang and Yang Ling before, and recalled Qiu Yi Meng treating them with both great respect and great warmth.","Naturally, they quickly went in to alert Qiu Yi Meng of Yang Ling’s presence.","The two outside had already been briefed on what to do, and they immediately bowed to greet the children and guided them in, no questions asked. A private room on the second floor had even been booked without the children needing to request for one.","The room they were led into was more opulent than the first floor, with Eighth-Order Materials easily being seen, used as decorative pieces and lightning. There was even an Isolation Array, to keep the truly room private, one which not even Eighth-Order Open Heaven Realm Masters could break through.","In fact, this room was no different from another Small World, with its initial size being far bigger than what it was outside, in an open field with mountains and rivers around them. Other than the door leading back, and the flooring with tables and chairs, it would seem as though they had been transported back to nature.","The Heavenly Demon Queen nodded approvingly at this, as though this much were to be expected.","As for Yang Ji, Yang Xu and Yang Ling, they were taking it in stride. They did not even realise how expensive such a room must be.","The two guides soon bowed and mentioned how the owner would like to meet them, and how the owner would help to serve them from here on out before leaving.","“Yay! Did you hear that? Aunt Qiu Yi Meng is coming!” Yang Ling got a little excited.","“That’s great. We finally got to see her after so long. I wonder how she has been?” Yang Ji played along and gave a high-five.","*Crik* Speaking of the person, a fabulously dressed woman soon opened the door and came in. She had flowing hair, well defined features and was in a complementary purple dress, which highlighted her beauty. Her beauty was almost on par with their Mothers, and must have moved the hearts of countless men. Yet, she remained steadfast in just wanting one man.","She was the Matriarch of the Qiu Family, owner of Recalling Dreams Pavilion and many more businesses, along with having an identity of being a Core Disciple of High Heaven Palace. Her achievements in business and other fields would have granted her the identity of Elder, but she had not reached the Open Heaven Realm yet. Thus, she could only remain a Core Disciple for now.","Still, the Open Heaven Realm was not far from her. She had recently broken through to the Dao Seal Realm. With all the businesses under her, she had the wealth to accumulate the resources she needed with a snap of her fingers. She merely had to stabilise her current cultivation before taking the next step.","She was grateful for all the help Xia Ning Chang and the others had provided her. Technically, most of their meetings at this restaurant were an expression of her gratitude for the Pills and assistance she had received from Xia Ning Chang.","As for Yang Kai’s children, she had met them before. She basically saw them as her own children. So, she was more than happy to see three of them come today.","Despite her busy schedule, in maintaining all businesses, cultivating, and the Qiu Family, she immediately made time to see them.","So, her typical serious demeanour had disappeared in that instant, replaced with a blooming smile that showed even in her eyes. “Yang Ling. Oh? Yang Ji and Yang Xu are here too? What a surprise. How have you all been?”","“Aunt Qiu Yi Meng!” The three greeted, with the Twins merely bowing while Yang Ling had run up to her to ask to be carried.","“You are as adorable as always.” Qiu Yi Meng pinched Yang Ling’s plentiful and soft cheeks, and carried her, with the little girl wrapping her arms around Qiu Yi Meng’s neck.","Then, Qiu Yi Meng soon noticed there was another presence. “Oh? What is this? Your pet?”","*Hmph!* “This Queen answers to no Master! Though you may own this exquisite venue, courtesy should not be so readily abandoned.” The Heavenly Demon Queen scoffed and complained. However, even she knew that she does look like their pet at this moment, so her words would fall on deaf ears.","“Hmm?” Qiu Yi Meng gave a curious glance to Yang Ji, who just nods and explains. “She calls herself the Heavenly Demon Queen. Well, she is something like a pet.”","The Heavenly Demon Queen wanted to lash out. But, she knew at this point, holding any other identity would just cause more issues to Yang Ji, so she chose to let this slide. Nevertheless, she still gave a glare, showing her misgivings.","[Haa... pleasing women is so hard... Father, how do you do this?] Yang Ji felt a little sympathy for his Father at this moment. Still, he knew what he had to do. “Auntie, can we eat? I’m really hungry.”","Naturally, that was a bold face lie. Someone in the Dao Source Realm hungry? How was that possible?","Still, Qiu Yi Meng did not question this and just gave a graceful smile. “Of course. I’ll go order your food right away. What would you like?”","At this point, she took out four Jade Tokens from her Space Ring, which contained the list of items they could order. It had to be noted that this list was different from what was offered on the first floor, with many of the food items here being treasures for one’s cultivation.","As a Proprietress, she naturally served many customers before. Though she had never seen such a being like the Heavenly Demon Queen before, she immediately knew how to treat her from those few statements of hers. So, she also provided her with a menu, as a show of respect.","“Come, let’s sit down first. Yang Ling, you’ve tried a few of these dishes for yourself. Why not recommend Yang Ji and Yang Xu a few dishes?” At this point, Qiu Yi Meng had already moved to one of the chairs, pulling Yang Xu along as if to guide her to a seat.","Thus, the five there naturally began chatting. As per usual, the children bore no hesitation in asking what each of the listed menu items was, and Qiu Yi Meng answered all their questions with eagerness.","Naturally, Qiu Yi Meng had questions of her own, they were in relation to their Siblings, Yang Kai and his other Wives.","Without any filter, the children answered all her questions without hiding anything. Even Yang Xu did not hesitate to answer. Though Qiu Yi Meng did not feel like she was yet worthy of being with Yang Kai, she still continued to strive to keep up. It could be because of this resilience and loyalty in her that some of the other Wives had even approved of her.","Nevertheless, such matters would have to wait till she steps foot in the Open Heaven Realm. The same could be said for Hu Mei’er and Hu Jiao’er, who were also in a similar position to her.","After the children ordered their meals, Qiu Yi Meng stepped out first to place the order with the chief. Once she closed the door to the private room, a familiar figure greeted her. Naturally, it was Su Yan.","Su Yan had followed the children here, and was waiting till the door to the private room was closed before appearing.","Qiu Yi Meng was naturally shocked by this. She froze for a moment before greeting, “Welcome, Sect Mistress.”","“En” Su Yan gave a nod, but corrected her. “We have both known each other for so many years. Like Sister Ning Chang, just greet me as Sister.”","The meaning behind her words was clear. Qiu Yi Meng thanked her, “Thank you Elder Sister.”","Su Yan gave a small smile, and turned her head toward the door. “How are the children doing?”","With that short statement, Qiu Yi Meng already understood that the question posed was mainly asking about that strange entity that appeared next to the children. After all, the children could not be doing any better.","“Sister, my cultivation is lacking, so I am unable to see through what she is, but she calls herself the Heavenly Demon Queen. The way she speaks is quite odd, as though she is not from here. Also, she was the one who ordered the most out of all four of them, with most of her meals also being the most expensive.” Qiu Yi Meng said, trying to think of all the information she could gather from that brief meeting.","Still, that was enough for Su Yan. After all, she herself could not see through what the Heavenly Demon Queen is, so how could she have expected Qiu Yi Meng to do something she was unable to?","“It’s fine. Do you have a way for me to see what they are doing?” Su Yan calmly asked.","“Sorry, but our rooms are private and we have no way to check on how our customers are doing. Though, Sister, with your cultivation realm, I believe you should be able to forcibly perceive what’s happening inside.” Qiu Yi Meng said. After all, as one of the top experts in the Dao of Space, the Isolation Array here should not pose any problems to her..."]},{"number":6067,"title":"Chapter 6067, True Dao of Space","paragraphs":["Chapter 6067, True Dao of Space","Author: Silavin","At the same time Su Yan was fretting over how she could look after the children, the four in the room were chatting away while waiting for the food. Though, only two of them were looking forward to it. It had been so long since Yang Ji and Yang Xu ate a meal that they forgot the cravings of a different taste. Still, seeing Yang Ling excited was more than enough to fill their stomachs.","Though, that changed once the door opened and the aroma of delight spread out.","Despite not needing food, the complex aroma that spread out from different dishes had even caused Yang Ji’s stomach to rumble and his mouth to start watering.","“Foods’ here.” Qiu Yi Meng walked in with an array of dishes floating behind her. Naturally, they were all being delicately lifted up using her Divine Sense.","Each child had their own main dish. Furthermore, there were multiple side dishes as well, all for them to try. Even those that the children had not ordered were there. This was, after all, Qiu Yi Meng’s way of doting them.","Only the Heavenly Demon Queen had more than one main dish.","Sniffing the aroma, seeing the delicacy she had ordered finally in front of her face, despite her haughtiness, even the Heavenly Demon Queen showed eyes of unconcealable desire. She could not wait to wolf down everything. The only thing preventing such an uncivilised act was her ‘high station’ in life.","“Woah. Aunt Qiu Yi Meng, there is so much more food now then when Mother was here!” Yang Ling exclaimed with her eyes glittering as she looked at the dishes in front of her.","Qiu Yi Meng chuckled. She could never bring in so much food with Xia Ning Chang around. After all, knowing that such items were a treat to repay for whatever Xia Ning Chang had done for her, she would always be humble and order one item for herself. If Qiu Yi Meng had tried to order more food, Xia Ning Chang would obviously say that she would be full with this one order.","“You are all growing, so you need to eat up.” Qiu Yi Meng said, and then pointed out, “This is made from a Divine Phoenix Duck. It has a trace of Phoenix Bloodline in it. Yang Ji, you should try this. As for Yang Xu, you definitely need to try this Blossoming Flood Dragon Egg.”","Each of these meals would have cost millions of Open Heaven Pills. Yet, here they were, all lined up for the children to eat.","Upon Yang Ji trying his first bite, only then did the Heavenly Demon Queen also take her first bite.","However, the difference in how they ate was vast. Despite her size, the Heavenly Demon Queen still managed to consume her meal far faster than Yang Ji, who was savouring each bite. Even if she tried to be dignified, one would not be able to separate her conduct from that of a starved man finally having their first meal after a month.","This naturally did not go unnoticed by Yang Xu, who was also taking delight in her main dish, the Lava Dragon Fortune Feast bite after bite. “Despite acting all high and mighty, you are eating like a beggar. No one will steal your food.”","Such sharp words naturally embarrassed the Heavenly Demon Queen. Her little face blushed a little, but she still rebuked. “You are the one that’s uncouth. Where I hail from, it is considered the height of courtesy to honor the culinary master’s craft through vigorous and wholehearted appreciation of their creations.”","“Just blabber from a beggar.” Yang Xu rolled her eyes.","“You!” The Heavenly Demon Queen was ready to pounce at that moment, but she was held back by Yang Ji.","“Enough. If both of you keep quarreling, everything would get cold. Do you want to waste this delicious meal?”","Yang Ling added, “Sister Yang Xu, don’t bully her.”","Yang Xu and the Heavenly Demon Queen just gave a snort and returned back to their meal. Still, interestingly, the Heavenly Demon Queen now took smaller bites, trying to restrain herself. While, Yang Xu took bigger bites.","[Ah, kids.] Qiu Yi Meng’s eyes were smiling as she saw this scene play out. In all honesty, she could not really see this mysterious being as anything dangerous. Haughty, certainly; strange, definitely, but dangerous... that she doubted.","If anything, the Heavenly Demon Queen seemed like any other child who just wanted to fit in. Qiu Yi Meng did not know about her background but this was her assessment of her so far. Still, since Su Yan was worried, she thought to give her an update first so she excused herself from the room once more.","Seeing that Auntie Qiu Yi Meng left the room once more, Yang Ling pondered for a moment and asked, “Brother, Sister, where should we go next?”","Yang Ji tilted his head for a bit, wondering where they should go next. However, in all honesty, he doubted that they could go anywhere seeing how their Mother should have been here by now. Due to their last adventure, they certainly would not be allowed to go anywhere far.","That was when the Heavenly Demon Queen said something that could not be taken back. “We may return to seek out your Uncle Eleven at any moment you wish.”","“What are you talking about? We are so far away from the Profound Source Gate. There is no way we would be able to go there without help from Uncle World Tree.” Yang Xu’s eyes narrowed as she said.","Perhaps in a good mood from the meal, or perhaps in a mood to rebuke Yang Xu, the Heavenly Demon Queen, “Why do you presume we need a gate to cross over to the Source Realm?”","“How else can we get there then?” Yang Ji was the one that asked this time.","“When your mastery over the True Dao of Space achieves the requisite level.” The Heavenly Demon Queen added.","“True Dao of Space? How is that any different from the Dao of Space?” Yang Ji asked, bewildered. He was certain he had never heard of this term before except through the Heavenly Demon Queen’s mouth. It was odd how similar this term was to the Dao of Space.","“Your knowledge of the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time is paltry to the True Dao of Space and True Dao of Time. The Dao of Space that you have perceived mastery over is but a small part of the True Dao of Space.” The Heavenly Demon Queen added, “Given the modest extent of your current mastery, you remain confined to traversing solely within the boundaries of your own Realm, the so-called ‘3,000 Worlds’ yet you lack the requisite mastery to venture forth into foreign Realms, needing structures like the Profound Source Gate.”","“So, it’s just another level for us to reach?” Yang Ji gave a nod, quite nonchalant about this news. Yang Xu was less calm, but upon hearing that it was just another cultivation level she just needed to reach, she calmed down.","Yang Ling was probably the only one who lacked the confidence to ever touch upon such a mighty Dao. So, she was the one that started to worry. “How hard is it to get good at the True Dao of Space?”","It had to be said that Yang Ling had not even started exploring the Dao of Space. So, news that there was another thing called the True Dao of Space was a little disheartening for her. After all, she was already working hard to catch up to the Oldest Brother and Sister, but no matter how hard she tried, she could never keep up.","“Like I said, refrain from belittling yourself. Your talent lies not in the True Dao of Space and True Dao of Time but in something far more interesting.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated, but did not go into the topic any further. After all, she sensed that the Isolation Array was weakening.","As she had predicted, *Crik* the door opened once more. However, this time, Qiu Yi Meng did not return alone. She entered with Su Yan.","“Mother”","“Mother Yan”","The children greeted her. Only the Heavenly Demon Queen remained passive, and gave a nod in greeting.","“En.” Su Yan’s calm and gentle voice spread. “After this meal, we would need to head back. Your Father has returned.”","“Oh? Father is back?” Yang Ji was the first to get excited by this news.","“Yes, over the next few days, we will all be very busy.” Su Yan added, still calm as always. Maybe unintentional on her part, but she was staring at the Heavenly Demon Queen while she said that. “So, finish up your meal and we will leave at once. Also, Sister Qiu Yi Meng, would you like to join us later?”","When Qiu Yi Meng heard that, her heart immediately skipped a beat. She was excited at the thought of spending time with the children and Yang Kai. However, when she thought about how her cultivation realm still had not reached her goals, she shook her head. “It’s fine, Sister Su Yan. I’ll be busy during this period. It’s best for you and the children to enjoy yourself without me.”","Seeing how Qiu Yi Meng had her own plans, Su Yan did not force the issue. “In that case, do tell me when you have the time.”","“Of course.” Qiu Yi Meng gave a nod, and sweetly smiled.","“For now, why don’t you sit down and eat with us? We’ve ordered quite a lot of food. If you’d like, I can order more food.” In gratitude, Qiu Yi Meng said, as she took Su Yan’s hand to the table. She took out a seat from a Space Ring and had her quickly seated.","“It’s fine. I’ll just have some of the side dishes.” Su Yan hurriedly added. It was hard to refuse with Qiu Yi Meng being so excited as the host.","Qiu Yi Meng soon started suggesting the different dishes to Su Yan, explaining their origins and the chief intentions. Such details were not even said to the children, since she did not think that they would care much about it. However, Su Yan, being an adult, and knowing the nature of such ingredients, would certainly see their appeal.","“En, delicious.” Su Yan commented as she took her first bite out of the Divine Phoenix Duck.","Seeing how their own Mother loves to eat this dish, Yang Ji added, “Mother, in the future, why don’t we come here more often?”","Hearing this, Su Yan looked at Qiu Yi Meng, who already agreed to it without her needing to say a word. Seeing that, Su Yan agreed to it despite having reservations.","While all this played out, the Heavenly Demon Queen grew abnormally quiet once more, seemingly alert as she ate her meal.","Since their Father has returned, that means she would eventually have to meet him. Though she might be immature, she was not a fool. Who would allow a mysterious creature, who they do not know the origins of, to be with their children?","Despite this, she also knew that this was a hurdle that she would need to overcome sooner or later since she could not really leave the Twins.","As for Yang Ling, seeing how the conversation about the best cultivation path for her had stopped, she seemed a little downcast. She wanted to ask the Heavenly Demon Queen more about what she had not said.","However, it seemed that the Heavenly Demon Queen had no intention to continue the conversation for now, even with Yang Ling’s cute pleading eyes. So, Yang Ling could only dejectedly continue eating her meal."]},{"number":6068,"title":"Chapter 6068, Could Not Say Much More...","paragraphs":["Chapter 6068, Could Not Say Much More...","Author: Silavin","Yang Kai had been worryingly pacing around, within the Restricted Area where Fang Tian Ci, Thunder Shadow and Little Eleven had lived in not too long ago. If any of his Wives saw him, they would assume that one of them was giving birth again.","He had relegated himself here because he did not want to get exposed to any of his Wives yet. Out of all places on Star Boundary, this was the most unlikely spot for any of them to visit, and was the most secured from third parties due to the Restrictions placed.","Though he had mastered all Daos, it seemed like his Dao of Women was lacking, as he did not know how to better his current situation.","He had been trying to deduce which Wife to approach first. He had brought all the gifts he could get, but now was the task of actually trying to placate them.","His go to would be Su Yan, since she could be considered everyone’s Senior, and was the most calm when dealing with things. Her word was basically law amongst his harem, with all the others listening to her. It could be said that this was due to both her position as being the First Wife, and her collected attitude when discussing matters, truly never using her position to sway the other Wives.","Therefore, if he could manage to placate her, it would be him winning half the battle already. As for the others like Yu Ru Meng and Shan Qing Luo, these two were the hardest to deal with. Yang Kai never personally seeked them out for favours like this. They held the strongest grudge, and would egg on the other Wives to punish him. In the harem, they were basically the counter balance to the forgiving Little Senior Sister and Tao Ling Wan, ensuring he would not cross the line.","Typically, if he could not seek out Su Yan, he would seek out Little Senior Sister and Tao Ling Wan, since they were the most forgiving. However, he could not find them at their usual locations.","Since he was a Great Emperor, naturally, his senses of what was happening on Star Boundary was but a thought. Yet, he could not find Little Senior Sister and Tao Ling Wan. This hinted that the two were either not on Star Boundary or were some Restricted Area that warped the Space Principles of Star Boundary, which would be too numerous to check through. After all, the whole High Heaven Palace had powerful Restricted Areas that he could not so easily peer through.","Why would they make such powerful Restrictions? Because there were nine other Great Emperors besides him.","Out of curiosity, Yang Kai had even looked for his Mother, but she was apparently gone too. Naturally, his first assumption was that Little Senior Sister and Tao Ling Wan were with his Mother, and that any of the other Wives he could not immediately spot would be with her.","The same could be said for his Little Sister, Yang Xue, who he too could not sense. Yang Xue was also an option, but she too mostly listens to her Sister-in-Laws and her Mother...","Despite all the rest being hidden, Yu Ru Meng’s and Shan Qing Luo’s positions were painfully obvious. They were moving around, shopping. It was as though they were telling him, ‘hey, we are here.’","As for Su Yan, though he could sense traces of her from time to time, since she was the one who seemed to be the most enraged by this whole affair, Yang Kai believes it would be wise to avoid meeting her directly for the time being.","[If I drag this on for longer, it’ll only get worse. At least Yu Ru Meng and Shan Qing Luo brought Yang Ai and Yang Mei along... surely they would be more forgiving when in front of our Daugthers...] Yang Kai sighed. The easy path had been blocked for him. It was obvious the Wives had agreed that he would meet with the two toughest ones first.","Adjusting his clothes one last time, and checking his Space Ring to ensure all the ‘offerings’ were in order, he disappeared from the site.","***","Yang Kai had transported himself to one of the busiest streets in High Heaven Star City.","The next scene in front of Yang Kai’s eyes was two country-ending women playfully smiling as though they had expected him. Even if they had not mentioned a word, their eyes were saying, ‘finally, you are here!’","However, the sound he heard next was not from either of these two women, but from the two adorable girls beside them, holding onto their hands. “Pa Pa!?”","Yang Kai’s appearance had been quite subdued, since he had used his powers as a Great Emperor to transport himself here. Yet, that could not hide his overwhelming presence and face.","The moment onlookers heard the excited exclamations of the two little girls, they turned their heads for a second to see the Palace Master of High Heaven Palace, the hero who saved the world, the strongest expert in existence right in front of their eyes!","Immediately, some onlookers froze from shock, some knelt down in reverence, and some started to pray–maybe to hope that their descendants could enter High Heaven Palace or they would receive his blessings.","Nevertheless, they all greeted, “We Greet Palace Master Yang!”","Such a shout inevitably drew even more attention, and crowds began to form. Even from the second floor windows, there were people who rushed over to stretch out their necks to catch a glimpse of him.","“En.” Yang Kai was already somewhat used to this at this point. But, he was like his Wives, and very much preferred to keep a low profile if possible. He just returned a nod at them and then quickly wrapped him, his Wives and children into an isolated Space, disappearing from the crowd.","“Pa Pa is so popular.” Seeing how everyone was looking at her Father, Yang Ai commented, which drew Shan Qing Luo to giggle, “He sure is. Your Father is the most popular man in the world.”","“En.” Yang Ai gave a nod, as she looked around, and noticed how everyone else had started to turn their heads to look around for them, “Why is everyone turning their heads, looking around? Can’t they see us anymore?”","“Silly girl. Of course not. Your Father made it so that they can no longer see us.” Shan Qing Luo moved forward and patted her head.","“Oh!” Yang Ai exclaimed as she raced to her Father and said, “Pa Pa is amazing.”","“Yes, yes, he is amazing. That’s why he has come here to help so many people.” Yu Ru Meng was the one who spoke this time, with a smirk.","“Woah.” Yang Ai seemed to be impressed, as her dazzling eyes turned towards Yang Kai.","“... Yeah, I’m here to help everyone.” Yang Kai could already feel an ominous foreboding. Yet, in front of his Little Princesses, how could he possibly refuse? [Damn it. So this was their trap!?]","“En, Yang Ai, Yang Mei, don’t you two find staying at Starry Sky Palace a bit boring? Don’t you want to have more friends?” Shan Qing Luo looked towards Yang Kai for a second and then towards the two children and asked.","“Erm... it does get a little lonely if Oldest Brother and Oldest Sister are gone. Brother Yang Hao also always focuses on cultivating, and doesn’t play with us anymore. Yang Ni and Yang Yue are too small to play... so it is mostly us five.” Yang Mei said in a soft voice, a little sad.","Even if they were Silbings, there was a huge gap between them and Yang Ji and Yang Xu, so the Twins typically did not bring them along when going out for fun adventures. At most, they would play in Starry Sky Palace, but they would not leave its confines. Yet, the Twins would sometimes go off for a day or more, and only return to tell the rest of their adventures.","It had to be said that out of all the children, only Yang Ji, Yang Xu, Yang Hao were old enough to leave Starry Sky Palace without needing their parents to accompany them. Yang Ling, Yang Zhi Rao were old enough to leave Starry Sky Palace with Yang Ji and Yang Xu accompanying them.","As for the rest, they were still under six years old, so adult supervision was a must.","“En... we are still too weak to play with them...” Yang Ai said dejectedly.","At this point, all three Parents could not help but sigh. Though it was great to have talented children, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were truly too exceptional. They had cast a shadow in everyone else’s hearts. That was why Yang Hao, the third oldest, had been so diligent in cultivating that it had become a borderline obsession.","None of the children were untalented. In any Sect, they would be labelled as cream of the crop. It was just that if they compared themselves to Yang Ji and Yang Xu, the gulf between them was truly too disheartening. After all, even adults would have their Dao Hearts shaken upon finding out about the Twins’ cultivation progress, what more these innocent children who did not have an accurate gauge of what was normal.","Despite this, it was not like they could hinder Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s cultivation. It would be unfair to them.","Yu Ru Meng gave a forced smile this time, quite rare for her, and said, “That’s why, we are going to make a place where you can get a ton of friends. So, even if your Brothers and Sisters are busy, you will still be able to play with others.”","“But Mom, I don’t want to play with other people...” Yang Mei said, a little uncomfortable with the idea of playing with strangers.","“Not to worry. Your Father will be there to take care of you.” Yu Ru Meng’s eyes turned sharp as she turned to Yang Kai, “Dear, can you please take down this barrier so that I can announce something?”","From what had been said, Yang Kai could already guess what was coming. However, could he refuse at this point? As a Father, could refuse her in front of his two Daughters?","“Fine...” Yang Kai said as he just awaited her next words.","The isolated space that protected them from all the others slowly disappeared, showing Yang Kai again.","Naturally, the onlookers were kept safe. Even if they were close to the distorted Space, no harm would come to them as Space distorted back to normal.","Having the Space around them change like this naturally bewildered many. Even if one knew that Yang Kai had manipulated Space Principles, they would find the sensation shocking. Yet, before they could grasp their bearing, an explosive news ran out.","Yu Ru Meng, as if waiting for this, stepped forward, “On the orders of all Palace Mistresses of High Heaven Palace, High Heaven Palace will now be establishing the High Heaven Academy! Children above 2 years old but under the age of 15 can enroll, and have a chance to be taught by the Teacher and Principal, the Palace Master!”","At this point, there was so much Yang Kai wanted to say. However, the words ‘orders of all Palace Mistresses’ meant that this had already been decided upon, and there was basically nothing he could do about it...","[Well, at least it is not that bad.] Yang Kai comforted himself. Though, what chaos he would face would need to be seen."]},{"number":6069,"title":"Chapter 6069, Announcement To The World","paragraphs":["Chapter 6069, Announcement To The World","Author: Silavin","Yu Ru Meng’s voice seemed to have resonated throughout the world. It was not just High Heaven Star City, the whole of Star Boundary seemed to have heard this news.","This was naturally not because she had used her powers to spread the news. Rather, it was because the Wives had already prepared for this news to propagate the instant it had been announced.","Such preparation was by no means easy. They had dispatched High Heaven Disciples to spread the news to the 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises first. After all, High Heaven Palace taking in so many seedlings would be crossing the line, no matter how one looked at it. So, arrangements had to be made prior, to ensure they do not step on anyone else’s toes.","Naturally, the Wives did not just want the children from the Cave Heavens and Paradises. They wanted those from normal Families, with potential as well. For this, they employed the help of the Great Emperors:","Duan Hong Chen, the Bustling World Great Emperor;","Zhan Wu Hen, the Iron Blood Great Emperor;","Gu Qing Feng, the Wondrous Pill Great Emperor;","Mo Huang, the Martial Beast Great Emperor;","Hua Ling Long, the Flower Shadow Great Emperor;","And Li Wu Yi, the Space Traveller Great Emperor.","When each Great Emperor had been approached and requested to help, they each gave different responses.","For example, Duan Hong Chen found it interesting and was eager to start travelling the world to announce the news. Though, it was unknown if he had been eager because he wanted to use this opportunity to tease his Disciple, Wen Zi Shan. After all, who would not want to quickly have a Godson to pamper? As for Gao Xue Ting, Wen Zi Shan’s Disciple and Wife, her reaction to the news was certainly interesting.","It could be said that on that night, their marital bed was noisier than usual.","In contrast, Zhan Wu Hen and Mo Huang were much more muted in their response. However, seeing how this would strengthen and improve Star Boundary as a whole, they supported it. However, Mo Huang stressed that the Academy needed to have Beast Taming as a part of the curriculum and Zhan Wu Hen stressed that Body Tempering. Naturally, to this, the Wives agreed, since they would much prefer all Children to be exposed to many different Daos while they were still young.","Gu Qing Feng and Hua Ling Long were helpful, since the former was Xia Ning Chang’s Master and the latter was someone Yu Ru Meng understood very well. After all, Yu Ru Meng had once disguised herself as the Flower Shadow Great Emperor’s Disciple. So, naturally, Yu Ru Meng knew how to ‘push and pull’.","Still, Hua Ling Long did not refuse as she personally found this project to be interesting. If she could pick out a few budding flowers from the batch, she found it all the more worthwhile.","As for Gu Qing Feng, seeing how this was one of the rare requests that Xia Ning Chang had come up with, he gave it his all to fulfill it. Such was a Master’s adoration for his Disciple.","Then there was Li Wu Yi, the Space Traveller Great Emperor. Thanks to the expansion of the bottleneck of Starboundary, Li Wu Yi had finally become a Great Emperor. After all, he used to be the foremost Pseudo-Great Emperor, behind Yang Kai. So, such a station was only natural.","This title, ‘Space Traveller’ was given by the Star Boundary’s Will. When Jiu Feng, a woman who had Phoenix Bloodline, heard of this title, she immediately thought back on how he would try to peek and escape. Naturally, she could not help but tease him to no end.","Still, how he got the title was for Star Boundary’s Will to decide, whether it was through such constant activity remains a mystery.","Regarding Li Wu Yi, technically, the Wives did not approach him first. Rather, it was Mo Huang who approached him and told him about it.","Typically, Li Wu Yi would be uninterested in such events. After all, he had no children of his own, and the only little one he had taken care of was Mo Xiao Qi, who was way older than sixteen. However, he had already reached the Eighth-Order Open Heaven Realm. Though he had taught the Dao of Space to others in High Heaven Palace, he had not officially taken in a Disciple.","Why not just take in any Disciples from High Heaven Palace?","Most children in High Heaven Palace were affiliated with the Sect from birth. Their parents were from High Heaven Palace, and the children as well. Their understanding in the Dao of Space had been influenced by Yang Kai, since their parents had most likely been raised in one of the Sealed Worlds or his own Small Universe. Normally, this would be fine, but as his own personal Disciple, Li Wu Yi would like to pass down his mantle in its entirety, with him building up their foundation.","As for those that entered from the outside, they would typically be a little older, above twelve years old. For Li Wu Yi, this was a little too old. He much prefers to see children around three, to raise them with his Dao of Space.","As for why he does not take in people into his Small Universe, to raise them, he did not see his Small Universe as being perfect enough. Though Small Universes could hold living beings, that did not mean it was suitable to raise people inside of it. The lack of Daos inside would hinder one’s progress. Besides, what could beat Star Boundary’s environment? Raising others inside when there was Star Boundary would be starving them of true opportunities. Such actions go against his own principles.","Thus, Li Wu Yi saw this as a major opportunity. Because High Heaven Academy was going to be different from High Heaven Sect. Certainly the two were still affiliated, but they were entirely different entities otherwise.","A student need not be inside of High Heaven Palace when they joined High Heaven Academy. Anyone could join. It would be open to all, regardless of one’s talents. Furthermore, one’s background did not matter to the academy. In short, they could be affiliated with a Cave Heaven, and still be allowed to join the academy. After graduation, these students would then be sent back to the Cave Heaven, to further their education and cultivation.","In fact, other Sects or individual experts, could come to the academy and choose who they would like to take under them, and if the children were willing, they could immediately leave the academy.","Furthermore, High Heaven Academy was made not just for cultivators, but they wanted to also have Mortals in mind. After all, there was still a subset of people who could not cultivate but they could do something more in their life.","However, it should be stressed that one’s background was to be kept secret in the academy. After all, this was a place for children, and not for politics. An even playing field should be kept, and one’s background should not be used to suppress another.","Such was the idea of the Wives, to allow their own children to get a sense of how they were placed in society, without the status of High Heaven Palace’s Princes and Princesses, attached to their names.","For Li Wu Yi, who was admittedly being overly picky, saw this as a great opportunity and for once, promoted himself as a teacher to the academy.","...","Therefore, once Yu Ru Meng made the loud announcement, which could be heard throughout all of High Heaven Star City, Star Boundary itself reacted to her.","Up above the skies, words began to form. After all, this was an announcement to the whole of Star Boundary from six Great Emperors!","Even for cities other than High Heaven Star City, from this day onwards, all would know that High Heaven Academy was being established, and that everyone within that age bracket could join.","Naturally, this caused a huge stir. Even Yang Kai did not expect that his Wives would create such a huge commotion, and that other Great Emperors had also agreed to announce this.","This meant that the whole of High Heaven Palace had agreed to this proposal.","In fact, more than what Yu Ru Meng had announced, the details on how it would run was stated there for all to see and scrutinise. Mortals and cultivators would intermingle in the academy, Secret Realm would be built to house the academy, and the Secret Realm would be connected to all cities around Star Boundary. Even the curriculums and holidays had been listed, along with the major events each year.","It had such a long list of things that it would have been hard for anyone to remember everything. Yet, thanks to the Great Emperors using Star Boundary’s Will, anyone who saw this news up in the sky would remember the details clearly, no matter if they had the memory of a goldfish.","This was naturally not for cultivators, since cultivators had excellent memories, but for Mortals, since one of the express purposes of High Heaven Academy was to introduce Mortal students, and some parents were not literate, so making them understand was necessary.","Also, with this, all questions in the hearts of the surrounding people were all answered, and they need not bother Yu Ru Meng and Shan Qing Luo with questions. Furthermore, the Wives need to really tell Yang Kai much, since he had already figured out what his next task was.","[It’ll open in a month? Do we even have a Secret Realm ready to take so many people in?] Yang Kai naturally took everything in and looked at his Wives.","Of course, Shan Qing Luo and Yu Ru Meng just smiled knowingly.","[So, I’ll have to build the Secret Realm... within a month at that...] Yang Kai sighed. However, in his heart, he still felt a little relieved. After all, with this, it should help calm everyone down."]},{"number":6070,"title":"Chapter 6070, Main Hall","paragraphs":["Chapter 6070, Main Hall","Author: Silavin","“Eh? We are going to school now?” A girl questioned, uncertain if she heard correctly.","“Yeah, why do we have to go to school?” It was a boy that questioned this time.","These two had seen the announcement in the sky. Naturally, deducing the age range and who was setting it up, they naturally came to the conclusion that they would be tossed into the academy.","However, this also did not make any sense to them, as throughout their cultivation journey, they did not really need anyone to serve as their Master. The way they cultivated was far too different from others, and they technically had no Master to speak of. As for pure knowledge, like history and language, they had their Mothers, ’Aunts’ and ‘Uncles’ to teach them. So, was going to High Heaven Academy really necessary?","“Oldest Brother, Oldest Sister, you don’t want to go to school?” An innocent voice played out from the side. After all, if the boy and girl were to go to school with her, they would certainly be able to meet more often, no?","“No... it’s just...” Yang Ji soon found himself unable to explain... If it did, it would be a little too much. The same could be said for Yang Xu.","“These two simply refuse to be shackled by the bounds of mediocrity, little one. After all, for existences of their caliber, descending to the level of the commons would merely impede their brilliance.” A womanly voice casually stated, as though it was a matter of fact. Naturally, as though she could see through Yang Ling’s worries, she added before the little girl got teary-eyed.","“But this sentiment applies to you as well. Such a common establishment would do nothing in polishing the raw precious jewel that is yourself.” The Heavenly Demon Queen added, as she turned towards the little girl and stated.","The children had already left the Recalling Dreams Pavilion, returning back to Starry Sky Palace when the sky lit up with words.","After their quiet meal, their Mother Su Yan had received a notice and had to rush out, so she quickly sent the children back home first using Space Principles. Through this one meal, it also seemed as if she had gained a little more trust in the Heavenly Demon Queen–at least enough to leave her with the children unattended to.","At the time, the children could not help but notice how their Aunt Qiu Yi Meng was getting a little excited as she moved with their Mother to go somewhere else. Then, before they knew it, they were transported back home and the sky lit up.","They naturally knew that this whole episode had something to do with them, since they perfectly fit in the age range and were part of High Heaven Palace. Not to mention, their Father would be overseeing the whole High Heaven Academy. It would be strange for them not to be forced to enroll at this point, since their Father was in such a post.","Also, with their Father overseeing the place, certainly, escape was impossible...","It was already hard enough to get out and not be caught by their Mothers, but their Father? Forget about it.","Their feelings were in great contrast to Yang Ling, who looked forward to spending more time with everyone. After all, if their Father had to stay in one place, would that not mean she would have more opportunity to meet him? Furthermore, there were going to be classes besides cultivation. Surely she would be able to join Yang Ji and Yang Xu in those, right?","As for the Heavenly Demon Queen, such a facility seems interesting as to find out the situation of the world here. But ultimately, useless overall. In her view, rather than limit the children with those of inferior knowledge, these adults might as well seek the truth of the world.","“Oh?”","It was then that their Sect Token started to vibrate.","These Sect Tokens were relatively small, about the size of a thumb. They were made of material that resembled jade and contained a trace of their Divine Sense and that of the Palace Master. For many, these tokens hung by their waist. Some place them in their chest pocket or create a necklace out of them. Nevertheless, these tokens could not be forged without the Palace Master’s permission.","They served as identity plates as well as communication devices in the 3,000 Worlds. Though, communication was only limited to within the Sect.","The three sent their Divine Sense into the Token to receive the message and they all had strange looks on their faces.","“All Disciples are to gather. A massive task is about to be issued by the Palace Master.” Yang Ji read it out loud, since the Heavenly Demon Queen would not be able to read it.","“En, there should not be a place for the High Heaven Academy yet. So, Father must be asking for help.” Yang Xu stated her deduction.","“Then, we must definitely help, right?” Yang Ji said as there was a sparkle in his eyes.","“Of course.” Yang Xu similarly opened her eyes wider at those words, which contain another meaning.","“Given your daily confinement to that locale, one ought to construct accommodations befitting oneself, no?” The Heavenly Demon Queen seems to have gotten the gist of it and fully agreed with their thoughts.","“Let’s go!” As for Yang Ling, she just saw this as something interesting to do with her Siblings. “Oldest Brother, are we going to call the others?”","“Hmm... why not. Might as well gather everyone and go to the Main Hall.” Yang Ji gave a nod and he grabbed Yang Ling’s hand, teleporting away the instant he did so.","As for Yang Xu and the Heavenly Demon Queen, they could easily sense the Space Rift Yang Ji tore open and transverse through it themselves. Though, they certainly would have preferred it if he did not leave them out like that.","...","The Main Hall of High Heaven Palace was a unique space that was no different from an Independent World. The interior was far larger than its exterior, and it could house millions of Disciples. There were even private rooms in the Main Hall, in case they have people that wish to keep their presence unknown.","Initially, Yang Kai wanted a simple Hall, but when practicing the Dao of Artifact Refining on a building, he went a little overboard. It could be said that for an entire year, he did not even see his Wives and was holded up creating this Main Hall, with multiple functions.","Seeing the stage from ten kilometres was hard for those with weaker cultivation, right? No problem, Yang Kai came up with screens and speakers by focusing on the Dao of Sound and the Dao of Light.","Was it not a waste for this huge space to only be used as a hall where people gathered to be announced?","No problem, why not make it into an Auction house from time to time as well?","With such ideas that kept popping up, Yang Kai could have been done within a month, but he kept adding functions that eventually stretched the project to a year.","Typically, his Wives would not mind since secluded cultivation itself might take decades. However, some were pregnant at the time, and even if they did not reprimand him for being so engrossed in something, his Mother certainly would.","Currently, in this overdone Main Hall, millions of Disciples were seated comfortably, awaiting for the Palace Master to appear.","There were a mix of expressions on their faces, as some of the younger ones who fit within the age range were wondering if they would be allocated to High Heaven Academy instead of sticking with their current Master in High Heaven Palace. There were also those older, who were not impacted by this new news, who simply wore solemn expressions. The oddest ones were probably couples with children of their own, who were wondering if their children would be placed in High Heaven Palace or High Heaven Academy.","Up on stage, the Elders and those above were already there like: Hua Qing Si, Bian Yu Qing, Yu Chang Dao, Nanmen Da Jun, Zhao Ya, Zhao Ye Bai, Xu Yi and etc.","Even some of the Palace Mistresses were already seated like Su Yan, Xia Ning Chang, Zhu Qing, Qu Hua Chang and Tao Ling Wan.","Their children, in the meantime, were placed in one of those private rooms.","It had to be mentioned that even Yang Hao, who was in secluded cultivation, was called out for this gathering. After all, this whole event also concerned him, so he too needed to be present. In fact, Zhu Qing, his Biological Mother, had specifically set out to call him over before the rest. So, by the time Xia Ning Chang had moved to gather all the children into this room, Yang Hao was already here.","“Ah! Yang Hao, long time no see!” Yang Ji immediately exclaimed after seeing his Little Brother for so long.","“Oh? You’ve grown taller.” Yang Xu next spoke up.","“Big Brother Hao.” Yang Ling greeted.","Meanwhile, some of the other children hesitated a little before greeting him. “Big Brother Hao...”","Yang Hao was the third child, so he grew up with Yang Ji and Yang Xu. In a way, they were quite used to his cold and aloof demeanour, which was quite an interesting contrast to his Mother, who was quite fiery and passionate. Though to be fair, his coldness was actually due to how his mind only focuses on one thing at a time, and he was actually pretty absent minded most of the time.","This was something obvious to Yang Ji and Yang Xu, but to the others, who rarely see him because of how often he spent in secluded cultivation, along with his quite thick eyebrows and never smiling face, he just seems fierce.","“Geez. Smile a little, will you?” Yang Ji rolled his eyes and he moved over to pad Yang Hao on the back.","However, all he received was an ‘En’, and a smile that seemed really forced due to how little Yang Hao did it.","“That’s better. So how far are you now?” Yang Ji asked, though admittedly, that smile had probably caused a few of their Siblings to step away some more.","“Still at the Saint King Realm... a little more before the Origin Returning Realm... Big Brother how...” Yang Hao stated, a little deflated. But before he could say more, the screen in front of everyone flashed and a few familiar figures had appeared.","Naturally, it was their Father and other remaining Mothers coming up onto the stage!"]},{"number":6071,"title":"Chapter 6071, Palace Master’s Speech","paragraphs":["Chapter 6071, Palace Master’s Speech","Author: Silavin","At the moment of their appearance, all noises ceased. It was to the point a pindrop could be heard.","That was just how much respect all the Disciples of High Heaven Palace had towards the Palace Master. Not only was he the Founder for many of their Ancestors, with them being born and raised in his Small Universe, but he was also the one who had saved the world from the Black Ink Clan.","On such a day, where they could finally see the hero of the world firsthand, many went silent to catch every word of his.","This was only natural. After all, such a grand gathering hardly ever happened. Furthermore, this was actually the first time many of them were seeing the Palace Master delivering a speech in person.","Contrary to the tense atmosphere, where one awaited Yang Kai’s words with bated breath, the man himself was tense for another reason.","As he had expected, his Wives seemed to have already planned everything out: from the size of High Heaven Academy to each facility’s staff. Even the resources had been ironed out. However, it was apparent that the bulk of the cost of this whole venture would be on their shoulders.","In other words, High Heaven Palace would not be allocating resources directly to this venture. Rather, Yang Kai and his Family would be the ones sponsoring this venture. Even for Secret Techniques in High Heaven Palace that could be given to High Heaven Academy, they needed to be paid for. It would not be a donation.","There were a few reasons for this.","Since High Heaven Academy was not strictly tied to High Heaven Palace, they should not allocate existing resources to High Heaven Academy. This would be unjust, as they would be taking resources from the current Disciples of High Heaven Palace to provide them to High Heaven Academy. Even if High Heaven Palace was wealthy, it was not like their resources were unlimited.","At the same time, to maintain the fact that High Heaven Academy was a neutral space for education, they should not be biassed in accepting donations from outside sources, which includes High Heaven Palace.","They definitely did not want to be tied down to certain demands from a Sect, just because they ‘donated’ a precious Secret Technique to the school. So, a fair trade to settle matters openly would be best.","They might also have teachers from different Sects, with different agendas, but such risks could not be helped. They could merely manage it such that nothing detrimental falls on the children. Also, such exposure might actually be great for the children in terms of exposing them to a variety of lifestyles and belief structures.","For Yang Kai, all these arrangements made sense. It was just that he could feel his Space Ring bleeding.","He was not a materialistic person. He was willing to spend if needed, and give away rare precious treasures to those he loved. Yet, he could not help but feel the heavy burden this whole school would take on him...","In fact, his heart had already fallen when he gave his gifts to Shan Qing Luo and Yu Ru Meng, only to have them say that these would be great for the new school...","Since the resources would be provided by the Yang Family, this included his Wives. In short, they too were going to help him carry the burden. However, this also meant that his plan to appease them with gifts had fallen short...","Though, admittedly, he knew that placing his hopes on such gifts were futile in the first place.","Right now, as he stood before millions of Disciples, he could feel their smiles from behind him, like cats watching a mouse. As for his Mother, he certainly dared not look at the daggers she was staring at him with. It was as though she was screaming, ‘You dare do that to my precious baby Grandchildren!?’, with her eyes.","Even his script has been prepared for him beforehand. That was just how thorough they were...","“Disciples of High Heaven Palace, today marks the formal establishment of High Heaven Academy. A bastion that will forever shake the foundation of the 3,000 Worlds.”","“The grand announcement has been made, with all sectors of Star Boundary and beyond having heard of its grandeur. For those still unaware, here is a token with all the details. Use your Divine Sense. We will wait for thirty breaths.”","Yang Kai confidently took out a prepared token and lifted it up midair. Soon, countless Divine Sense flooded out, scanning the token. Even for those who had read the announcement in the sky at the time, they still read it again. After all, they feared they might miss out something so they scanned the token.","After thirty breaths, Yang Kai continued.","“The location has been decided. It will be within High Heaven Star City. I will be creating a Secret Realm to house High Heaven Academy. But, I would require the assistance of the Disciples here to help create it within a month.”","Next, Yang Kai took back the token and released an Artifact this time. This was an Artifact that was typically used during such grand gatherings. Activating it, a hug display, over a hundred metres tall and over two hundred metres wide, appeared in the air. On it was a large list of items, each with a price tag.","However, this price tag was not based on Open Heaven Pills, nor were they based on the Merit system in High Heaven Palace. This was another independent system created, with the currency being used called Credits.","There were items like World Beads, Open Heaven Pills, Tai Yi Soul Cleansing Water, Yang Kai’s own Protective Taslimen and so on...","Naturally, all these items listed had to be from Yang Kai’s own collection, or that of his Wives. There was a range from basic items that cost only ten Credits, like an Open Heaven Pill, to expensive Artifacts like World Beads, which came at the billions of Credits.","“To earn Credits, one would need to contribute to the foundation of High Heaven Academy. You may trade in copies of your Secret Techniques, Artifacts, Pills and so on. Their value will be fairly assessed, and you will gain Credits upon a successful transaction. Do note, certain items will not qualify to be traded, as they will not help our future generation. Items like Open Heaven Pills, Artifacts that require one to be in the Open Heaven Realm to use and so on. Keep in mind that these will be used for children.”","“If not, you can also help in terms of labour, helping us build up the future of the next generation.”","Yang Kai looked around to check everyone’s expressions. At this point, there was clear excitement in their eyes. After all, it could be said that the items on sale were relatively cheap for their price. If Open Heaven Pills were the baseline of ten Credits, then Artifacts that should cost tens of millions were basically on offer, costing less than half their usual price.","Furthermore, throughout one’s cultivation journey, who did not have Artifacts or Pills that they had outgrown? Many might keep them for sentimental value, if not never bothered to sell them. However, now, was this not a golden opportunity to get rid of what they no longer needed for something better?","In short, this was too good an opportunity to give up on, and everyone knew that (except for Yang Kai’s children). Their eyes were gleaming with excitement.","“For helpers, a variety of tasks are available for you to pick up.”","Then, the screen flashed and changed once more. This time, there was a list of jobs that the Disciples could pick up, each yielding different amounts of Credits per task or per hour.","Even this was a luxury, as even someone doing clerical work was going to be rewarded 10 Credits an hour, which was an Open Heaven Pill an hour. This was a huge contrast to the same task that would reward three Open Heaven Pills a day!","There were even tasks that would yield tens of thousands of Credits each hour, like Array creation!","It was fair to say that this was an event no Disciple would want to miss. After all, this was only open for a month or so.","“Those that wish to take up a task, speak to the Palace Manager and Vice-Manager. As for those that only wish to trade, you can use the Exchange Hall. It will be available through this period to process all transactions.”","“You only have a month, so make best use of it.”","Yang Kai ended the speech on that note. He gave a nod and Hua Qing Si, the Palace Manager took to the stage to wrap everything up.","In fact, once his speech had ended, Yang Kai immediately tore Space to quickly leave and set up the foundation for the Secret Realm. After all, without it, nothing else could start and a month’s time was already stretching it thin.","Of course, the main bulk of everything had already been said by him. Hua Qing Si was there to answer questions if needed and to direct the Disciples in the finer details–like where they could take up tasks, and etc.","Overall, the atmosphere was exuberant, with many Disciples wanting to immediately rush over to the counters outside the Main Hall and immediately start taking on tasks.","This was obvious once the whole speech ended, with the Elders and Palace Mistresses leaving first. The Disciples immediately rushed out, with some heading to the Exchange Hall first, while others heading to the counters first.","As for the children, they were not really all that impressed. After all, what did this have to do with them? There was no Artifact that they really wanted, nor Pills.","In a way, though Yang Kai and his Wives had ‘tried’ not to spoil them, living in Starry Sky Palace, within their own little bubble, it had made their common sense skewed. Right now, invaluable treasures were nothing in their eyes, as Open Heaven Pills were merely snacks for them.","In short, they did not truly understand the value of each Open Heaven Pill, or how hard it was to earn one. However, this was to be expected, since they were all still really young. The three oldest, Yang Ji, Yang Xu and Yang Hao–12,12,10 respectively, who were free to go out whenever they wanted, never bothered to spend any of their Open Heaven Pills. Likewise, they never needed to earn any Open Heaven Pills with Xia Ning Chang around.","At the same time, the Twins had no interest in shopping, while Yang Hao only concentrated on cultivation. Though to be fair, they had been provided with all they could ever need, so why would they need to shop for items?","If the three oldest were like this, then the rest, who could not even go out alone, could not have been much better, right?","So, naturally, the question that popped up in their mind was: [So, why were we brought here?]","And as if to answer that question, the Wives, who had disappeared from the stage, had just entered the room."]},{"number":6072,"title":"Chapter 6072, Creating Matter Out Of Nothing","paragraphs":["Chapter 6072, Creating Matter Out Of Nothing","Author: Silavin","The first to enter was Zhu Qing, who turned to Su Yan behind, “So, only Yang Ji and Yang Xu? Are you sure? Won’t it be hard on the others?”","Shan Qing Luo added, “Not like the other little ones would be of much help at this point. But, they will each have a role to play later. We agreed to have him divide his time equally right?”","Ji Yao’s calm voice entered, “En. Right now we are just setting the foundation. The faster we get this over with, the more time he will be spending with the rest.”","“Yang Ji, Yang Xu, come with me. As for the others, follow your Mothers back to Starry Sky Palace for now. Each of you will have your own tasks to do, and your Father will join each of you later.” Su Yan gave a soft nod and lifted her hand. With that one small movement, the Twins gently floated to her side as the other children watched.","However, before anything else happened, the Heavenly Demon Queen spoke to Yang Ji and Yang Xu through their Divine Sense. “Bring that little one with you.”","‘Why?’ Yang Ji wanted to ask, but Yang Xu had already spoken up without questioning it too much. “Mother, is it alright if Yang Ling comes with us?”","The other Mothers immediately looked at each other.","Shan Qing Luo shook her head, since it would be unfair if they took only Yang Ling along. It would also be unfair to the rest if she was the only one without strength and was allowed to go.","Meanwhile, others were also showing reluctant expressions.","Favourism was normal, since they were still Humans. But, they could not possibly let it be so evident, right? As Mothers, it would be hard to explain to the rest why Yang Ling was allowed if she could not help out.","Su Yan gave a soft sigh and shook her head. “Yang Ling will be with Sister Xia in the Starry Sky Palace. They would be busy refining Pills.”","Seeing as she got rejected, Yang Xu simply gave a nod and did not question it any further. As for Yang Ling, she initially got a little excited, but was let down by the final decision.","“Hey, why did you agree to ask?” Yang Ji asked Yang Xu through their Divine Sense and she immediately replied, “because Yang Ling wants to come with us. Also, aren’t you curious why she is paying so much attention to Yang Ling?”","“I guess I am, but isn’t it because Yang Ling likes her?” Yang Ji asked, and Yang Xu refuted, “I don’t think it is quite as simple as that. She mentioned something about Yang Ling, but was cut off because Mother entered the room.”","“Now that you mention it, even I am curious about it now.” Yang Ji added.","“Well, we can’t do much right now. Our Mothers are against it so we can only wait. You can ask her for the reason in the meantime. I doubt she would answer if I were the one to ask.” Yang Xu shrugged.","“I refuse.” Seemingly able to hear their conversation, the Heavenly Demon Queen immediately said to the both of them. “Speaking of another in their absence is far too uncouth. If you so desire to hear it, then gather without the adults.”","“And, listening in on others is not uncouth?” Yang Xu rolled her eyes.","“What remedy exists for these unwelcome vocal manifestations that impose themselves upon me without invitation?” The Heavenly Demon Queen replied back in an unbothered fashion.","“You!” Yang Xu wanted to curse but was cut off.","“Okay, see the rest of you later.” Su Yan said and the Space around her distorted, with her and her two children’s figures disappearing from the scene. However, it was not just those three, all the other Mothers and Children also got transported away at the same time by her manipulation of Space Principles.","By the time Space around them returned back to normal, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were already in the sky, far above High Heaven Star City. Below, they could see the whole city, which was magnificent as it was wide. Yet, despite its grandeur, there was a single figure that stood out even amongst the most magnificent palace complexes.","It was their Father, who, at a corner of the city, was exuding a heavy pressure to all those around him.","Thankfully, it seemed like the streets around him were empty, as an evacuation order had been sent out earlier.","Yang Kai was solely focused on three streets. The buildings of these three streets had all been bought by ‘him’, and everything was to be transformed into the new school. Overall, it covered about ten square kilometres, which was large to many but still too small for the scale of the school his Wives had in mind.","In other words, he needed to create an even larger space, around tens of thousands of kilometres, within this area.","This would be an easy feat for any Open Heaven Realm Master who was extremely proficient in the Dao of Space. The difficulty came with the requirement that individuals must be able to enter and leave without suffering any side-effects.","It needed to be said that for people to move through different Spaces, there was bound to be disorientation to some degree. After all, they would be moving through the Void in most cases, similar to how most Transport Arrays functioned.","Typically, for cultivators of certain strength, this would be fine. If not, they would wear protective Artifacts to shield them from such effects. Even so, there were cases where cultivators would feel sick and weak for an entire day.","Meanwhile, High Heaven Academy was expected to welcome regular Mortals. Their Physique was already weak to begin with. Could they truly bear the brunt of such a harsh travel route? Furthermore, most would not be able to afford such Artifacts on their first trip. Though subsequently High Heaven Academy would be giving out Artifacts to all students to function as their identity, but that merely minimises the problem rather than solves it.","Yang Kai had to realistically solve the problem at its root. Transport Arrays were still necessary, but he would need to fix the warps in Space that caused such discomfort. To do that, he would need to create them in a way that does not move through the Void.","“Let’s set up a Protective Array first, to prevent anyone from accidentally entering.” Yang Kai muttered as he tossed out a few Eighth-Order materials around in a pattern, and drew out a basic Protective Array to keep outsiders out.","Next, with the aid of Star Boundary’s Will, Space within the Protective Array started to visibly compress. It was evident, as the buildings that were present started to shrink smaller and smaller, till they were almost indistinguishable from toys, till they could no longer be seen anymore. In fact, what appeared to be a scene of buildings and streets, turning into nothing but darkness.","At this point, Yang Ji and Yang Xu were just staring and learning. Naturally, they could feel from the changes in Space Principles that this darkness was not the typical Void that they were used to traversing. Rather, it was merely empty Space, from the lack of any material around the region. The buildings and streets had merely been shrunk down.","From what Yang Ji and Yang Xu knew, this was similar to the Artifact called Floating Mountain, which Uncle Li Wu Yi made. The difference being that the Floating Mountain would require one to wrap Space to enter, while this allowed one to walk into it to enter. That was why Yang Kai had erected the Protective Array first.","Next, Yang Kai entered the Protective Array, and Su Yan, judging that it was time, also followed behind and entered without resistance. It was clear that Yang Kai had set the Array up, knowing their presence.","There, their next sight changed drastically. They had naturally shrank. In front of them was a space filled with nothingness. The only thing that helped them realise this was not the Void was the complete lack of Void Turbulence. At the same time, when they turned behind, they could see gigantic structures that would take them an hour to climb. Even what they would consider as pebbles outside were now hills to transverse over.","It was overwhelming in a way, and also interesting at the same time. Yang Ji naturally looked towards an insect on a wall, and even that was far bigger than him.","Yang Kai, who immediately noticed, turned back to ask, “The view outside is better, you know?”","“Nothing is better than seeing it first hand.” Su Yan answered, giving Yang Kai no space to refuse.","Yang Kai sighed and looked towards the Twins and explained. “I’m going to start adding the foundation for the place, since it is so empty.”","Then, Yang Kai closed his eyes and started to focus.","He pictured a scene in his mind, one where the ground was filled with earth, deep and unending, with caverns to explore, with jagged ravines carved dramatic pathways through the landscape, their edges softened by cascading vegetation that tumbled toward mysterious depths below. An endless bottom that could not be broken, and space for future Arrays.","Once he opened his eyes Yang Kai placed his hand down and lifted it.","The empty world was soon filled with light, so blinding that it would put the Sun to shame. Yet, from its mere presence, something that transcends the Principles themselves was formed.","The light itself soon dissipated and in front of the bare darkness that sought light, it was now filled with unending earth, no different from the lands outside. Yet, these lands were mysterious. They were similar but different to what was outside. In all appearances, one would not be able to tell. However, for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, who had great mastery over the Dao of Space, this new earth was something obviously foreign.","They mimicked the real thing, close to perfection, but were still not the real thing in itself. Nevertheless, they would function no different from the real thing, so did that really matter?","Yang Kai looked at the brown scene in front of him. So far, even with visions of vegetation, life did not sprout from nothingness. Though he was in the World Creation Realm, able to create matter from nothing, that did not mean he was a master of life.","Still, it was enough to impress his two Children.","“Woah! It suddenly got filled up. Is this what it means to reach the World Creation Realm?” Yang Ji exclaimed.","Su Yan added, “En, even I would not be able to create something from nothing as freely as this. Your Father is amazing isn’t he?”","“En.” Yang Ji and Yang Xu gave strong nods, holding expectations to one day reach that realm.","However, they could hear a voice of degreement, a familiar voice."]},{"number":6073,"title":"Chapter 6073, Space Array","paragraphs":["Chapter 6073, Space Array","Author: Silavin","“You innocent little ones remain blissfully unaware if such trifling displays should stir your wonder.” The Heavenly Demon Queen added, unimpressed by this scene.","“What are you talking about? Father is creating an entire world right in front of us. If that isn’t amazing, then what is?” Yang Ji rolled his eyes, sharply pointing out the flaw in her argument. “Even those in the Open Heaven Realm are unable to do something like this, unless they part with a part of their Small Universe, which comes at the great cost to them. Even if we master the Dao of Space, we would not be able to create something from nothing. But Father is doing just that from his own Will. I don’t think you fail to see that!”","The Heavenly Demon Queen gave a scoff, “So those realms within a few of your kind are distinguished as Small Universes. Flawed worlds conceived from the materials of this one.”","“Discourse with one such as yourself is fruitless. Just know that worlds born without life at the start are flawed. This world requires the tempest of time to breathe life into it. It is not a True World in the truest sense. Yet still, this creation serves its appointed design, and to those of unrefined eyes, it shall bear no variance from a True World in its manifestation. Upon this point alone, do I grant my acknowledgement.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated and no longer wished to explain further.","Still, her words did spark interest in Yang Ji and Yang Xu. They could not help but ask their Mother, “Mom, why is there no life here?”","Instead of Su Yan answering, it was Yang Kai who overheard them and answered, “Life takes time to sprout. It is not done in an instant. But no worries, in one month, this whole place will be a paradise of green. Right now, all it takes is just the passage of time to pass by. But before that, I still have to set some things up.”","Yang Kai then took out a small sapling. It was none other than a World Tree clone. Since this was going to be an independent Space, though still connected to Star Boundary, it would not receive as much of the blessings of the World Tree as outside. The only way to solve this was to plant a World Tree clone here, so all children would be blessed.","It should be noted that Universe Worlds, like Star Boundary and Myriad Monster World, were filled with people due to the blessings received from the World Tree clones–Star Boundary especially. The reason for this was due to how the blessings would not only affect the parents, but would be more effective when passed down to children born here. So many couples, those wealthy enough, would strive to settle down in Star Boundary to receive such blessings.","However, those weak and poor, outcast and uneducated, would never receive such a blessing with the current system, whereby everything was monopolised by the powerful and wealthy.","Since his Wives wished for a better system, a more fair system, as their Husband, who had also strived through adversity from the bottom, why would he be against this? He would also like to give opportunities to those who lacked them, and allow those diligent to go further in life.","With this one sapling, though they might not be able to completely eliminate that gap, they would significantly narrow it down. As long as parents were willing to put their children in High Heaven Academy, there was a greater chance for them to prosper, and an even greater chance for their Grandchildren to prosper.","Yang Kai placed it down at the centre of this place, which was a tall mountain, already laced with channels for the river beds. There, without a single trace of water, the sapling took root and immediately began to grow, little by little.","Next Yang Kai looked to the sky and he clasped his fist. The supposed sky above, bright and radiant from the Sun’s rays, soon darkened with massive clouds that covered the world.","Yang Kai soon turned to the three behind him, and said, “Next is to speed up time, for the cycle of life to begin. With Yin and Yang already in existence, with Fire provided in abundance, Earth and Air created from my Will, and with Wood and Metal by time, this world would be complete. We should leave now and let nature take its course. I plan to speed time up by a hundred thousand times before the rest arrives. I hope this has been educational for you two.”","From beginning to end, this had taken about two hours. The basic foundation of the world has already been established, but Yang Kai still has much to do, more things to adjust, like natural Formations of mountains and rivers and the Space Arrays themselves for others to enter. However, he could not possibly allow his children inside a Space with such drastic time dilation.","“En.” Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt amazing at the power his Father possessed. With a wave of his fingers, mountains and rivers were carved, with a thought, lightning and rain was called upon. Still those words from the Heavenly Demon Queen nagged at them. In the end, it was as she said, that time still needed to pass for the world to become complete. In that case, was this world really not a True World?","The Twins seem to be deep in thought, as though they were comprehending the mysteries her Husband had performed. So Su Yan excused them, “I think they have realised a few things. That has already made this trip worthwhile. For now, we will wait outside while you work inside then. But, since we three are here, I would like to ask what kind of design you plan for the Space Arrays. I want these two to have something to do while we wait for you outside.”","That had been a tacit agreement that their Children were not allowed to enter and Space that distorts time. So naturally, the Twins would be kept out of this place before time began to speed up, and would only be allowed to enter once time had been set to normal.","The reason for this was Yang Xue and Yang Xiao, who had lost their childhood while trapped in the Flowing Time Temple. There was also a little bit of their own selfishness at play since Su Yan and the rest wanted to raise them till adulthood for as long as possible.","Yang Kai gave a nod and produced three tokens from his Space Ring. Using his Divine Sense, he carved out the base design of the Space Array on it, and sent it over. There were even instructions written on it, detailing what material should be used for each component of the Array.","Su Yan saw it with a glance and gave a nod, understanding everything. As for the Twins, they were still a little lacking, so they would need guidance on it.","“Okay, you three should leave first. I’ll connect the Array once I’m done with the basics here.” Yang Kai said as he reached out and a portal opened up behind Su Yan and the Twins.","Once outside, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not help but stare at the portal closing and the whole interior of the world changing from one instant to the next. After all, one second outside was more than a day inside. Though there was no day and night, rain would appear and then disappear in the blink of an eye. Even their Father was merely afterimages inside, along with the mountains and rivers that could form and disappear in the next instant.","Still, the one thing that was noticeable was the constantly growing World Tree clone, and the original barren soil which soon sprouted patches of green, till it was covered. Even the mountains, fully greyish or brown, soon had green or white.","The only time they had seen such a sight was within their Father’s Space-Time River, but that was only a glimpse while this was playing out right in front of their eyes.","Su Yan allowed them this moment before speaking, “Want to surprise your Dad?”","Yang Ji and Yang Xu looked back and gave a nod. Of course they do. Who would not want to surprise their own Father?","“If we can create these Space Arrays during this time, don’t you think he would be impressed?” Su Yan added and the eyes of the Twins already gave her the answer.","So, out on the empty street, she took out a table and a few chairs, and set it up for them to have class.","For some reason, once they were out of the Protective Array and got seated, the Heavenly Demon Queen also took the liberty to get out of Yang Ji, and appeared right on top of the table, as though there was nothing wrong with her being here.","It might be the case where Su Yan had already met her first hand, and accepted her existence, that was why she felt comfortable to come out. Nevertheless, she seemed quite comfortable here.","As the Heavenly Demon Queen had predicted, indeed, Su Yan did not do anything to her and just left her be, as she solely concentrated on teaching the Twins.","Su Yan would explain what certain parts of the Space Array meant, and how this combination worked to enforce the other function. At the same time, the Twins would ask questions, pretty much fully focused on the lesson, all while the Heavenly Demon Queen just silently appraised the Space Array.","Also, as though everything had been prepared beforehand, Su Yan even took out empty Array Plates, which she had Master Ma Fan craft prior. It had to be said that this was a lesson she had wanted to teach them for quite a while, so lesson materials had been prepared beforehand. These empty Array Plates were basically a base, made just for them to fit the Array on top of it to be used.","Naturally, it was not going to be effective as an Array Plate made for a singular function, but for educational purposes, nothing could be better. Also, like Yang Kai when he first touched upon Space Arrays, Su Yan’s mastery over the Dao of Spirit Arrays was lacklustre, but she was basically one of the best when it came to the Dao of Space. Therefore, she could teach the concepts of the Space Array.","The Twins would place different materials, engrave lines, and fill these lines with different materials to form the Space Array. However, as expected, the first time yielded no success.","Still, they had the whole day to keep testing, so they did, while they continued to converse in their minds, testing out different theories, perfectly in sync.","Strangely, while they did this, the Heavenly Demon Queen just watched on in silence. Even if she had anything to say, she knew that this was for the Twins to figure out, that guiding them too closely would be detrimental to their growth. After all, even Su Yan, once she explained everything, merely sat back and watched as the twins fiddled with their Array Plates, and would only answer when the Twins had a question.","In fact, Su Yan was actually building out the basic structure of the Array outside while the Twins were seated. After all, she already knew what needed to be done from the instructions Yang Kai had given her through their Divine Sense before she left."]},{"number":6074,"title":"Chapter 6074, Enrollment","paragraphs":["Chapter 6074, Enrollment","Author: Silavin","On the first day, the world was formed with greenery ever present.","On the start of the second day, the world created was connected to the outside world, with masses moving in and the construction beginning, with two of the Space Arrays being made by Yang Ji and Yang Xu.","On the third day, Arrays experts moved. Those proficient in the Dao of Space had set off to other Universe Worlds, and even Yang Ji and Yang Xu were deployed (with Su Yan overseeing them of course).","On the fourth day, the children started to work as well. The Young Masters like Yang Hao and Yang Zhi Rao, who were more in tune with martial cultivation, would work hard on construction and the Young Mistresses, if they had certain inclination to Artifact Refining or Array Formations, would help out with those various aspects. Naturally, Yang Kai would take turns with them and accompany them while they worked. Truly being a Father on rotation.","On the fifth day, centres for enrollment and hiring would be set up in the various Universe Worlds. Naturally, these were to be manned by High Heaven Palace Disciples. Teachers from all walks of life would be welcomed, though the stringent tests that High Heaven Academy put up for them were not few, with many having to later travel to High Heaven Palace for the final vetting.","On the sixth day, they started designing and weaving the school uniforms. All children took part in this, except for Yang Ji and Yang Xu since they were away. The design for the boys was simple, a white robe with blue highlights with the words High Heaven Academy behind, placed vertically (凌霄院). The boys just gave a nod and said that the design was good and moved on, even Yang Kai gave his approval with relative ease. However, the females were broken up into camps regarding their uniform. Some wanted it to be mostly blue, some wanted it to be a one piece dress, some wanted it to have a floral pattern...","The battle was just as intense as any other, with his Daughters pointing and pouting if rejected, with their Mothers approving and disapproving designs. They had to cycle through about a hundred different designs, with the final decision laying with Yang Kai...","If he could, Yang Kai would rather they make the decision themselves, since he was hardly interested in clothing. Still, it took the whole day, and through all the designs, they settled on a two piece uniform robe with blue highlights, with the skirt being blue, and even adding a phoenix pattern for the girls, with the same vertical (凌霄院) on the back.","However, to make it matching to the too simplified male uniforms, they made the boys’ pants blue as well, and had a dragon pattern sewn into it.","As expected, the boys readily agreed, just wanting to get this over with and so, the tough sixth day had passed.","On the seventh day, plants, animals and Monster Beasts were brought in. Monster Beasts would be allocated an entire mountain range, sealed within an already prepared Array Formation to separate them from the children. They were meant for the Dao of Beast Taming. As for the more ordinary animals, they were spread around the fields and lakes, just kept out of construction zones. The plants brought in were all different, some rare others common. They were here to mainly educate the children about the different types of plants. Naturally, anything dangerous would be planted in a different location.","...","Each day, there was always something different being established or brought in. Each day, High Heaven Academy was gradually coming into shape. Eventually, an entire month was over and the grand opening took place, with all the students, their parents and teachers invited.","It did not matter if they were cultivators or not, all were welcomed. Even teachers, with heads full of white at seventy years old, were invited. Maybe, from where they had been, the journey here to the campus itself seemed so mystical that they could hardly believe their eyes.","So, there was a wide array of expressions, from those that were used to such sights and those who found it to be miraculous. Regardless of their background or upbringing, High Heaven Academy had exceeded all expectations as there was one common expression filling their eyes, which was great astonishment.","Even those that lived a life of luxury since birth would have never seen the sight of land plagued by Demonic Energy or Monster Energy so close to their dwelling place, yet completely isolated. What more, an actual World Tree clone just for one Secret Realm...","Also, regardless of their cultivation realm, be it parents or children, unless they were in the Emperor Realm or above, they would all be suppressed to be no different to ordinary mortals here. Their Qis could not be mobilised unless in specific areas of the school. So, even cultivators were surprised by this place.","On this day, all were gathered in the Grand Hall of the school, which did not pale in comparison to High Heaven Palace’s own Main Hall. It was so massive that millions easily fit in it with more space available. Still, the thing that attracted everyone’s eyes was not the setting but the person hosting, the eternal hero, now Principal of this great school, Yang Kai!","His presence, appearance and demeanour, like the lord ruling Heaven, bore down on the onlookers as they could feel their hearts beat at his every word. This was despite his words being gentle, saying a speech that was not even prepared by him, but by Xue Yue...","“I would like to express my gratitude to all guardians who have entrusted their children to us. Through the next few years, all your children will be staying with us, but rest assured, we will take care of them like our own. The parting will not be eternal, as they will be able to return with you twice a year for two months in total without cost so, all can be rest assured.”","Yang Kai waved his hand and a screen appeared, showcasing images of the dormitories the students would be staying in, and the meals they would eat. He then explained how the children would live each day, and how the classes had been structured.","For cultivators, the current classes were made based mainly on the Dao they pursued, and split up further according to their cultivation realm. So, there was only one class for those that pursued the Dao of Space, due to the low number of students, but multiple classes for those that pursued the Dao of the Sword, split according to each student’s cultivation realm.","For mortals, their classes were split mainly based on their current education level and then age. For example, those illiterate would be grouped and then further split up based on year. They would also have a chance at cultivating, all materials given would be equal, regardless of talent. If they managed to become cultivators before the year ends, then they would be moved to classes for cultivators. If not, they could try again next year. However, the priority for their education would still be things that would be helping for their mortal lives.","Naturally, for each student, before they officially enrolled, they had been tested prior. So, such allocations were made possible.","Currently, in the Grand Hall, the students were all already seated in their respective class, with their overall teacher in charge seated just in front of them, and the parents arranged to seat behind the students.","At this point, while Yang Kai was talking about the class allocation, many parents and students looked to their left and right, seeing how the children had been arranged. There were certain classes that were smaller than the others, but in most cases, it did seem like the number of mortal students was higher than the number of cultivator students.","This was natural. After all, High Heaven Academy provided mortal students with far more benefits than the cultivator students, who most likely hailed from relatively well-to-do Families. Therefore, many cultivators chose not to send their children to High Heaven Academy.","Nevertheless, Yang Kai and High Heaven Palace’s fame was not to be underestimated. After all, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could sense quite formidable auras amongst the students here. There naturally were also those from the 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises, whose auras stood out amongst their fellow classmates.","Nevertheless, Yang Ji and Yang Xu still stood out amongst everyone. Even within their class of twenty students, which had been modified to teach both the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time, due to the limited number of students who could comprehend the Dao of Time, they could see familiar faces from the Phoenix Clan and Dragon Clan. However, due to the purity of their Bloodline, the other children felt a sense of oppression whenever they looked at the Twins.","The most interesting thing yet, since they were in a combined class, they had two form teachers. One was Uncle Li Wu Yi, and the other was Uncle Xu Yi, who was Yang Kai’s Third Disciple.","“Brother, is it me, or are people staring at us?” Yang Xu could not help but ask, sensing stares from a lot of parents.","Silavin: Though I wanted to go into detail of what each child does with Yang Kai, I think it would be too much seeing how there is only one chapter a week. I also wanted to start the school arc sooner."]},{"number":6075,"title":"Chapter 6075, Worries of Parents and Children","paragraphs":["Chapter 6075, Worries of Parents and Children","Author: Silavin","“I don’t know. Maybe because we are Father’s children? I don’t think I’m handsome enough to get that kind of attention. Or maybe they are just looking at you cause you are so cute?” Yang Ji theorised.","Yang Xu blushed a little and corrected, “Brother, stop belittling yourself. You are handsome enough. I can already see some girls stealing glances at you from the corner of my eye. Also, I don’t think it is because of Father. They are paying attention to the both of us, but not to Yang Hao and the rest. It’s so strange...”","“What else could it be but your transcendent cultivation realm? Though masked, do you believe you Twins could conceal such matters from the eyes of true experts?” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated as if it were a fact. “Even if not your cultivation realm, your Bloodline already seizes much attention.”","“Check the other little ones that surround you. How do they compare to you two?” The Heavenly Demon Queen asked, and Yang Ji swept his Divine Sense to their surrounding classmates.","“Oh? The highest here is in the Transcendent Realm, that’s two Major Realms below Yang Hao, who is in the Saint King Realm.” Yang Ji gave a baffled expression and then swept his Divine Sense to the other classes as well. “Eh? The highest is only in the Saint King Realm?”","As Yang Ji swept through class by class using his Divine Sense, the Heavenly Demon Queen had her eyes narrow for a moment before returning to normal. It was so fast that neither Yang Ji or Yang Xu noticed despite her being in Yang Ji’s Dantian. It seemed like she had spotted something peculiar, but she chose not to voice it out just yet.","In fact, the person that drew her attention had also frowned at that moment but remained perfectly composed.","Instead, even without knowing all the cultivation realms of this plane, she retained her usual composure and continued to explain to these ignorant children, who were so sheltered they did not even know that Dao Source Realm experts like them, ignoring age, were already rare.","“You two have yet to bash under the stars and still remain sheltered. Even I, who am not from your plane, could tell how exceptional you two are at a glance. Those onlookers must surely be pondering in their hearts what manner of prodigies you two might be. They likely question whether there was some error in the age verification process, given that you two were permitted entry.”","“So, compared to other children, we are just that strong, huh?” Yang Ji seemed to be in thought for a moment, “We already know that we were strong amongst our Siblings but the result here is a little disappointing. I heard from our Mothers that there are going to be prodigies from the other Cave Heavens and Paradises. I guess they did not send their best...”","Yang Xu agreed with his view. “Yeah, if they had sent their best, I’m sure they would be much stronger.”","Though the Twins had convinced themselves of this, the reality of it was that for most prodigies, it would take more than a hundred years just to reach the Origin Returning Realm. For the true cream of the crop, with close to unlimited resources, they might take fifty years or more to reach the Dao Source Realm. Yet, they Twins were expecting such a feat to be accomplished before a child reaches sixteen of age. Still, it was true that most of the best from the Cave Heavens and Paradises were not sent here.","If heard outside, the ludicrousness of this idea would have made many Masters spit out blood if they were made to expect their Disciples needed to reach such heights at such an age.","This was highlighted by how shocked the other children’s parents were. They would exclaim, with their Divine Sense with each other.","“How is this possible!? Who raised those children!?”","“Dao Source Realm before sixteen!? Wait, they haven’t even hit puberty yet!”","“Dear, should we withdraw Jun’er? I’m afraid these two might become a Heart Demon for him...”","“I heard that they are the Palace Master’s children. It would be great if our Son can get close to them.”","Such conversations were frantic, with Divine Senses shooting back and forth between parents, and acquaintances. That was just how shocking the existences known as Yang Ji and Yang Xu were.","It got so out of hand that the children, due to their low cultivation, started to feel the pressure of all those Divine Sense messages being sent. It reached a point where Li Wu Yi had to step in, silencing them all with a blast of his own Divine Sense.","“Silence! If there are any questions, we will address them after the Palace Master’s lecture.”","The pressure from an Eighth-Order Open Heaven Realm Master was not to be underestimated. Once that clear message was delivered, all parents quietened down. Though it did not fully eliminate all those Divine Sense flying about, that was more than enough to allow the children to breathe easier.","Li Wu Yi gave a sigh and wondered to himself, [I would have reacted the same way if I did not know the Twins prior to this. Why did they even want to enroll them? These two are monsters who do not even need teachers. How do I even teach them?]","Lu Wu Yi then turned his head to another class. It was also another class but this one was solely focused on the Dao of Space, and it was taught by Jiu Feng. There, she was grinning, wishing him good fortune with those two.","Yang Kai soon ended his speech, and he directed the students and teachers to leave in preparation to arrange the children in the dormitories.","As for the parents, they could stay in the Grand Hall and ask questions. Yang Kai and the teachers would be able to answer their queries.","Naturally, once the children left, questions started to pop off from the parents. Especially cultivator parents. For the mortal parents, most were just happy that their children were accepted here and could have an opportunity to cultivate. What more, most were afraid to speak up, since the people that they were speaking to were the illusive cultivators, who could kill them with a wave of their hand. Under such circumstances, how would they dare to raise their voices to question anything?","Thus, Yang Kai answered all the queries coming out from the cultivator parents. Though, as expected, a large majority of them were related to Yang Ji and Yang Xu since most details had already been disseminated prior, with facility tours available after the children have settled down in their dorms.","Nevertheless, sensing that he had not once addressed a question from a mortal parent, he sent a message through Divine Sense to Xue Yue, and had them go over to address them if possible.","As for the questions related to Yang Ji and Yang Xu, Yang Kai naturally admitted that they were his oldest children, with a hint of pride on his face.","“Yes, they are currently twelve and they have reached the Dao Source Realm, as many have noticed. They are proficient in the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time. Right now, we just want them to socialise and have friends rather than focus on cultivating.”","“Wait, so they are already proficient in two Daos? Have they reached Grand Mastery!?” A woman from the Yin-Yang Cave Heaven asked.","“Yes. So, they are qualified to be teachers themselves but we really just want them to make friends.” Yang Kai felt a strange premotion when it was a woman from Yin-Yang Cave Heaven that asked this.","“Palace Master, is it fine to enroll more students?” A Father from the Great Battle Cave Heaven asked. Unlike those that had their Dao Hearts tremble and were afraid for their children, he would much prefer prodigies from his Cave Heaven come and sharpen themselves using this whetstone called Yang Ji and Yang Xu.","“General enrollment happens every year. But, since this is the first year and I believe many potential students have yet to enroll, we will give everyone another month. After that, we would not accept any new students till the next year.” Yang Kai stated and gave a nod to Shan Qing Luo, who moved to arrange things.","“As for those who wish to withdraw because of my children, please feel free to do so. We merely hope for the best for the children. You can look for my Wife, Xia Ning Chang outside the Grand Hall later, she can help you arrange things.” Yang Kai could feel frightened gazes so he mentioned this before needing any parent to speak.","At that point, a few parents silently left and waited outside the Grand Hall, since they had already made up their minds. As for other a few others, some still had not made the decision yet.","“Palace Master, if we wish to donate certain Secret Techniques and have the teachers teach our children, how do we go about it?” One Father asked, even preparing a manual in his hand.","“You can talk to the form teacher of the class later and tell them about it. We leave it up to their discretion. Some Secret Techniques might not be suitable for the form teacher to teach. So, you would need to speak to the teacher individually. This way, the Secret Technique need not be spread to the academy, and you can have the teacher swear to secrecy.” Yang Kai explained.","“Palace Master, will there be any bias against our children if they ever get bullied by your own children?” One concerned Mother asked. After all, the ones in power here were those from High Heaven Palace. Bias was definitely a thing, and as a Mother, she could not help but worry.","“Judgement would be left to the World Tree, not us. The World Tree clone here will be able to perceive and record any happenings in this small space, and would act as a neutral judge in any case that is brought up. There is no need for any parent here to feel fearful for their safety as well, since the World Tree clone would act to protect the children.” Yang Kai explained.","“Okay, let’s take the final question before we go for the facility tour.”","“Palace Master, when do you think is the appropriate age for your children to have grandchildren?” That same woman from the Yin-Yang Cave Heaven asked this but before Yang Kai could answer, the whole Grand Hall could feel the temperature drop, needing Xue Yue to reflectively protect the mortal parents.","As for the woman from Yin-Yang Cave Heaven, the Void had immediately claimed her, and Su Yan gave a sharp glare at the other Mothers from Yin-Yang Cave Heaven."]},{"number":6076,"title":"Chapter 6076, Dormitories","paragraphs":["Chapter 6076, Dormitories","Author: Silavin","For cultivators, each class was allocated two dormitory buildings, one for each gender. The dormitories were located a little more distant from the school. At least, they were further away compared to the dormitories for the mortal students. After all, for cultivators, they would need more space for themselves when training, and they could travel further distances at an extremely fast pace compared to mortals.","Therefore, cultivator dormitories held a far larger area but were also quite a distance away from the school itself. Unlike the dormitories for mortals, each cultivator would get their own room, as secluded cultivation was to be expected. As such, their dormitory rooms would be reinforced with an Isolation Array and tougher materials like Divine Metals.","Moreover, the dormitory rooms had different grades to them as well, to spark competition amongst the students. For the Time Space Class 1, the best rooms naturally went without saying to the two best students, Yang Ji and Yang Xu.","As Yang Ji and Yang Xu moved through the dormitory buildings, due to the number of students here and their distance from Li Wu Yi, they spoke to him using their Divine Sense.","“Uncle Li Wu Yi, why have you become our form teacher? Didn’t you say that you have nothing to teach us?” Yang Ji said words that really pierced into Li Wu Yi’s heart.","Li Wu Yi had definitely said those words a few years ago, when Yang Kai had asked if he could take the Twins as his Disciples. After all, he was a Family friend, and someone Yang Kai respected. At the very least, from Yang Kia’s point of view, it was better to have a Human who mastered the Dao of Space through insight rather than a Divine Spirit that mastered it through their Bloodline act as their Master.","Unfortunately, Li Wu Yi keenly knew that such a relationship was impossible. He could not be a Master to these two children. It was not that he did not have anything to teach them. Rather, he simply could not see himself being their ‘Master’ for long, as he was certain they would surpass him on their own, even without him.","Furthermore, Li Wu Yi has his own criteria for his Disciples. As such, he had refused Yang Kai’s request, giving the excuse that he had nothing to teach them.","Still, to think that Yang Ji would say such words to him, as though slapping him in the face...","“You brat. You think you’re so amazing that you know everything about the Dao of Space? I just said that to give you some face. You better prepare yourself. Tomorrow, I’ll make sure I drill you with knowledge till your head goes numb.” Li Wu Yi gave a huff, thinking to ignore them for now.","Li Wu Yi focused on the other children as he approached their dormitory buildings., “A little more and we’re there.”","Their dormitory was quite isolated from the other buildings, with trees all around. In fact, it was probably the building furthest away from the school, at the highest altitude on top of a mountain. From here, they could easily see the school, though it would be the size of a stretched out thumb despite the school’s massive size.","Li Wu Yi had purposefully travelled all the way here without bending Space, since he was sure some students would need to walk up and down the mountain until they got adept enough at manipulating Space Principles.","Nevertheless, with the whole class gathered, he pointed at the compound, with two tall buildings facing each other. Each building was four levels high, built in a traditional style and in between them sat a large stone platform. There were other structures as well, but the two tall buildings stood out as the most inconspicuous.","There were various flora surrounding the place, with a garden equipped with stone tables and chairs. The compound had the sign, ‘Time Space Class 1’ written on it, and the left building had a ‘女’ sign on it that denoted it was meant for the girls and the right one had a ‘男’ sign denoting it was for the boys.","At this point, due to the distance they travelled, some of the kids could be seen panting. However, there were also those that had not even let down the least bit of sweat. Such a difference had made their inadequacies obvious, causing some of the children to get frustrated.","Despite how each of them felt, Li Wu Yi had them line up on the stone platform, according to their seating arrangement in the Grand Hall, and called out the name of each student.","“Zhang Fei, male building, room 1-A.”","“Li Ying, female building, room 1-A.”","“Kai Kai, male building, room 1-B.”","...","Names were called out one by one, and Li Wu Yi had them step out to collect a jade token. These jade tokens were the keys to their rooms.","It was clear from those that were being called out, from how they were sweating and panting, that these children were most likely the weakest out of everyone present. They had used Qi, and still barely caught up to the group.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu did not know if they were judged based on how well they performed from the trek, or from solely their cultivation realm. Nevertheless, the difference in strength between each student was being showcased right in front of everyone.","...","“Xin Yee, female building, room 2-A.”","“Huo Chong, male building, room 2-A.”","...","Next were children who seemed relatively fine. They had beads of sweat, but were not panting. They were clearly another class of their own compared to the previous batch.","As the names were called out, it seemed like a large majority of the students here would be placed in rooms 2-something. In fact, all the other students were called out and placed in room 2-something, even the Saint King Realm student was also placed here.","Next came to be a surprise to everyone. Everyone else but the twins had been called, however, once the next name was called, it raised eyebrows.","“Yang Xu, female building, room 4.”","...","The students all looked at each other, baffled. After all, 3 was skipped and then suddenly 4? Furthermore, there was no alphabet behind the number!","Immediately, this raised murmurs. Despite not stepping out, all the students could tell who ‘Yang Xu’ was. The pressure she exerted on them unconsciously was too apparent.","“Wait, why is she the only one in 4?”","“Shhh, quiet, can’t you sense how powerful she is? Also, she is not the only one at 4. That boy next to her definitely will also be placed at 4.”","“I know she is strong but, isn’t this too unfair?”","Such murmurs continued. They could keenly sense that Yang Xu was in a class of her own. Yet, some could not accept that the difference was this stark.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could hear all the murmuring. However, they two just felt annoyed by it more than anything. After all, it was not like they asked to be placed in room 4.","Li Wu Yi, hearing all the murmuring, could not keep it in any longer and spoke up, “Silence. The rooms are classified under your mastery over the Dao of Space or the Dao of Time. It is not based on pure cultivation.”","Xu Yi also stepped up to explain further, “The higher the floor, the higher the room number, the stronger the Array inside that helps the student study the various Daos and for general cultivation. For the current batch, I believe that there are only a handful of students that can use the third floor. So far, only these two are qualified to use the fourth floor.”","“Do not rush. Even the sweetest of nectar, when too potent, will become poison. If you all study hard, I believe most of you will be qualified to use the rooms on the third floor next year.” Xu Yi added.","However, upon saying all of this, the two teachers were still waiting for her to step out. That was when Yang Xu made a request to them through Divine Sense.","“Uncle Li Wu Yi, Uncle Xu Yi, I don’t want to be in a different room from my Brother...” Yang Xu said in a disheartened tone, but her words brooked no refusal.","“Yang Xu, we have already expected you to say that. But, this is also a request from your Mother, Su Yan. She hopes that you will grow independent of your Brother. You are already twelve years old. Isn’t it time to stay in a room of your own?” Xu Yi was the one who replied, as he was closer to Yang Kai’s Family than Li Wu Yi, and was also the one who had received Su Yan’s request.","Li Wu Yi added, “What’s more, it would be unfair for the rest if you were to be able to sleep in the male dormitory, while all the female students are only allowed into the female dormitory. We obviously also can’t allow your Brother to enter the female dormitory, right?”","“No! I don’t want to! How is that fair? I cultivate better with my Brother with me! How can you separate us!?” Yang Xu pouted and stomped her feet, which seemed strange to the other students since it seemed like she had suddenly done that out of nothing.","“But from what your Mother has said, you don’t need your Brother with you when you cultivate.” Xu Yi sighed in his heart, [Mistress, why didn’t you explain it to them? Why leave it to us to explain...]","At this point, Yang Ji cut into the conversation, also through their Divine Sense but only to Yang Xu. “Yang Xu, if you still want to stay together, why don’t we just combine both rooms together?”","“Huh? We can do that?” Yang Xu raised a questioning look, but only spoke to her Brother this time. After all, both of them had never done this before.","“The Heavenly Demon Queen said it can be done, that it would be good if we have more space in our room.” Yang Ji this time said directly to her.","“Are you really sure?” Yang Xu this time asked the Heavenly Demon Queen with a sharp gaze.","“It is but a paltry task for me.” The Heavenly Demon Queen scoffed, rolling her eyes.","Yang Xu thought for a moment and just suddenly stepped out to go to the front and return. She moved so fast that the students around them only saw her afterimage, with a jade token already taken from Li Wu Yi’s hand.","Still, seeing how Yang Xu had not raised a fuss and had accepted the arrangement, Li Wu Yi quickly sealed the deal by calling the next name.","“Yang Ji, male building, room 4.”","Similar to Yang Xu, Yang Ji also quickly moved forward and returned. He raised no fuss and just accepted the jade token.","At this point, Xu Yi had his eye brow raised. From what he knew and expected, the Twins should have caused a greater fuss. However, he chose to keep silent since he did not want these two to cause anymore trouble.","He motioned to Li Wu Yi, and the latter quickly sent the kids to their rooms, before any more noise could be made about the matter."]},{"number":6077,"title":"Chapter 6077, Difference in Rooms","paragraphs":["Chapter 6077, Difference in Rooms","Author: Silavin","Li Wu Yi took the boys to the male building, and Xu Yi took the girls to the female building.","As expected, the size of each room differed based on the floor. For the first floor, it was a normal single room but with a small area for the person’s amenities. Those rooms on the second floor had even more space, two rooms worth. One room functioned as a living room, and the other, the bedroom.","It was naturally a wonder for those children when they saw these two rooms. After all, even if they were of a wealthy background, it was rare to have a room with so many Arrays in place. So many in fact, that their jade token was written with instructions...","Still, Li Wu Yi and Xu Yi went through how each room on each floor would look like, despite no one living on the third floor. After all, they wanted the children to see the goal they should strive towards.","On the first floor, there were ten rooms, five rooms on the second floor, three rooms on the third floor, and only one room on the fourth floor. It was fortunate that the class only had twenty students, with a balanced number of girls and boys, and that they did not need to compete for rooms on the second floor. It was unlike other classes, where they might be holding a small competition for the rooms on the second floor right now.","Both teachers stressed how the key difference between the rooms was not the amount of space allocated, but rather the Arrays inside. For example, the basic Spirit Gathering Array was more potent the higher the floor, with Grades reaching up to the Origin Returning Realm for rooms on the third floor. However, most importantly was the Insight Array, which one could use to study the depths of that specific Dao within their room.","It had to be said that these Insight Arrays were all made by Yang Kai, using the Space-Time River. Each student could pursue deeper insight into their Dao when within this Array. There were 3,000 Daos within each Insight Array, but the Arrays were limited based on the floor and the compound. It was the separation of beginner, intermediate and advanced knowledge, not allowing the children to dive into too many different Daos, limiting their study to just one. After all, for each Dao, one could not rush and had to take things step by step.","Contents that were too difficult might lead one to missing the fundamentals and straying away from the Dao itself. At worst, it might develop into a Heart Demon, at best, the student needed to be corrected by a teacher.","However, it had to be noted that for each class, the Insight Array’s contents might be different. It depended on the teacher. Yang Kai had allowed the teachers to set their own insights into the Insight Array. After all, though his insights might be deep, he was at the end of the day not the one teaching the students. It would be best for the teachers to come up with the contents themselves, and teach according to what they felt right. In a way, this could be said to be a tailor made education system.","For Time Space Class 1, Li Wu Yi had imparted his insights while Xu Yi avoided doing so. After all, from Xu Yi’s point of view, he learnt everything from his Master, Yang Kai. In short, he believes the insights Yang Kai had to the Dao of Time was much more profound than his, so he would not overstep his Master’s teachings. Likewise, Li Wu Yi wished for a Disciple, and wanted them to learn from him starting at the very basics.","Naturally, that also meant that Li Wu Yi was actually focused on selecting his Disciple from those on floor one.","As the teachers and the students moved floor by floor, they eventually got to the fourth floor. It could be said that their class was probably the only one that had students on the fourth floor.","As expected, since there was only one room on the fourth floor, that means the whole space, no, the whole floor, had been made into their room. If one were at awe with the luxury of the third floor, the luxury of the fourth floor would have made their eyes green with envy.","This space, equivalent to ten room’s worth, had its own cultivation room, bath spring, sparring room, study room, gravity room, and more...","It was better than any house. One could basically live inside and never come out.","“This is all for one person!?” One of the students muttered, envious.","“Argh! The difference is too much!” One of those living on the first floor could not help but get angry.","Li Wu Yi and Xu Yi, would agree with the students. After all, the fourth floor was made truly different from the other floors. Typically, showing this floor was to make the students shrive for the fourth floor. But in this case, the other students knew Yang Ji and Yang Xu had them beat, so it was not even a competition for them. This was just showing them something unattainable, while stroking their desires.","However, there was a reason why the teachers wanted to show them this room. After all, the Arrays here were made far more potent than what could be experienced on the third floor.","The teachers lead their own groups into the cultivation room. There, they had three students on the platform and they activated the Spirit Gathering Array at its lowest setting. Immediately, despite the three students being prepared, they felt a rush of World Energy entering them. After a minute, their faces could be seen to turn red, and beads of sweat were rolling down. After just two minutes, the teacher quickly shut off the Array, but its effects were clear for all to see.","Without explaining much, they moved onto the bath spring. Here, without needing them to even step into the bath, the teachers had handpicked the strongest of the groups (excluding the Twins). The teachers had them place one hand into the pool and start cultivating.","The moment the students placed their arm in, they felt a biting sensation. However, that biting sensation got stronger, and soon it felt like their whole arm started to burn...","From the girl’s side, the girl immediately pulled her hand back in shock. That arm was unable to stop trembling.","However, from the guy’s side, the boy named Lei Ao, was trying to preserve through. He knew what Li Wu Yi was trying to tell them by having such a demonstration. However, he was unwilling to accept it. He, a prodigy from his Sect, praised and envied by all, was now being said that he was nothing but second rate compared to those Twins. How could he possibly accept it!?","Li Wu Yi sighed, “The young need to experience reality to learn. If you wish to continue, then go ahead.”","Even medicine, when too potent, becomes poison. This was a live example of this for everyone here to watch. Yet, despite the dangers, Li Wu Yi was not joking. He truly would not make a move to save this young man.","“Arghhh!!!” Soon, Lei Ao could visibly see his arm start to enlarge, with hideous bumps on it. The pain at this point had spread not only to his shoulder, but to his whole body. His eyes turned bloodshot as he stared at Yang Ji. [I don’t believe we are that different! I don’t believe it!]","However, at some point, Yang Ji sighed and he snapped his fingers. He did so before Lei Ao had blood pouring out of his orifices.","Lei Ao was immediately teleported away, next to Yang Ji, who was already prepared to support him.","Li Wu Yi, who seemed unbothered by this, addressed the others. “I believe all of you are aware that too much of a good thing can be poison, right? Do understand that despite this room seeming to be unnecessarily luxurious, it is actually too dangerous for all of you to use it. This is just what it means to be on the fourth floor. This is why we have different classifications. If you like to improve your living conditions, you only need to do one thing: train hard. That’s it.”","Li Wu Yi added while lifting Lei Ao using his Divine Sense, “All of you, go to your rooms to rest for the day. I’ll need to send this kid to the infirmary to get treated. Your parents might also visit you later.”","The boys, upon seeing how Lei Ao had ended up, gulped and gave a nod before quickly shuffling to their rooms downstairs. At this point, they held no desire for the fourth floor. Their own rooms seem pretty good.","Yang Ji, who sighed this time, asked, “Uncle Li Wu Yi, why didn’t you save him?”","Li Wu Yi just chuckled, “Oh? You really don’t know, or are you just asking to clarify your guess? Your Sister would have figured it out by now.”","Yang Ji had a guess as to why. His Uncle was trying to make Yang Ji appear in a positive light in front of the other children, since they seem to be frightened of him and Yang Xu. “But, that was too dangerous. He could have gotten seriously injured.”","Li Wu Yi knocked Yang Ji’s head, “You think I didn’t notice you trying to save him? I would have made a move if you didn’t do anything. For now, just stay in your room and abide by the rules set by your Father and Mothers. You are not allowed to go to the female building, understand?”","“Yeah yeah yeah. Quickly go and get him treated.” Yang Ji rolled his eyes at the nagging and started pushing Li Wu Yi out.","“You! *Haaa...*” Seeing how this ungrateful rascal was throwing him out, Li Wu Yi sighed and moved, flying away with Lei Ao in tow.","Yang Ji quickly closed the door and locked it. Then, before he could say anything, the Heavenly Demon Queen came out. “Your side has been delayed by a single whelp. Your Sister has grown weary of waiting. Come, let us begin.”","“How should we start?” Yang Ji asked, and the Heavenly Demon Queen asked back, “Why resort to such crude methods as tearing Space apart and journeying through the Void? Does true refinement not lie in wielding dominion over Space itself, bending it to facilitate one’s transit? What are the distinctions between your capabilities and those of the World Tree? Pray tell, what fundamental differences preclude you from replicating its extraordinary feats?”","“Erm... I don’t know.” Yang Ji scratched his head and Yang Xu cut in, her voice resonating in their minds, “Just get to the point already!”","“Stay your haste, for enlightenment takes time. Take heed that your present methods rely most heavily upon the Void for your transits. I bid you turn your efforts toward the pure control of Space itself.” The Heavenly Demon Queen rolled her eyes. This was after all, something completely foreign to these two children.","“So, I am to just control Space, without moving through the Void...” Yang Ji seemed to have entered deep contemplation with those words. He then just sat down on the stop, cross-legged.","Even on the other side, Yang Xu felt something and sat down cross-legged as well.","In the meantime, the Heavenly Demon Queen smiled and took the opportunity to move out of the room, where even Arrays could not hinder her."]},{"number":6078,"title":"Chapter 6078, Pure Control of Space","paragraphs":["Chapter 6078, Pure Control of Space","Author: Silavin","“Pure control of Space...” Yang Ji muttered as he tried to wrap the very fabric of Space to his own will. This time, he merely opted to twist Space itself.","Space Principles undulated as the Space around him began to tremble. Without the Protective Arrays enclosing this place, the fluctuations would have definitely stiffed massive reactions amongst his classmates. Yet, all outside remained silent while all within his room remained in complete chaos.","As though everything in front of his eyes were cloth, walls began to warp. There were creases all over, with spots that clearly stretched. All this was merely him manipulating Space Principles to wrap Space.","However, at a certain point, those creases in the fabric of Space tore open, and a Void Crack leading into the Void was open. Similarly, those areas stretched would also tear open, with more Void Cracks filling the room.","Yang Ji saw this and immediately frowned. If he were to describe the sensation, it was akin to him merely using his hands to pull apart a piece of cloth, only to have it tear right in front of his eyes. He had hardly used any strength, and Space itself had been torn apart.","“Has Space always been this fragile?” Yang Ji muttered, which was easily heard by his Sister, in her own room. Despite there being Arrays isolating them, they still could communicate effortlessly. This was all thanks to the mysterious Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique.","“Brother, I think it is because we are too used to tearing Space apart...” Yang Xu said with a frown as well. Her own efforts were proving to yield the same results.","Yang Ji thought back on how their Father and Mother taught them how to manipulate Space. It was truly the case where the first step was the tear open Space, to understand the power of the Void. In fact, most of their understanding of Space had been intrinsically linked to the Void.","Yet, right now, they were trying to control Space, without the Void. In terms of fundamentals, they were sorely lacking when the Void was omitted from the process. In a way, they were true beginners in this.","“You might be right. But to think that a small warp could tear Space to this extent...” Yang Ji sighed.","He waited for a moment, and the Space around him was once again restored back to its original form.","Curious, he tried again and failed.","Tried again and failed.","Regardless of how delicate he tried to warp Space, it always had one outcome: it would always lead to the Void.","With both Brother and Sister working together, they each tested and theorised their own understanding of Space. Due to them being in different rooms, it further helped in their understanding of Space.","From what Yang Xu could feel, she could tell the Space around her was a little tougher than that of her Brother’s. If her Brother merely needed two fingers to twist Space apart to create a Void Crack, she needed to twist her wrist to create a Void Crack.","It was through such small discoveries that the Twins were getting twice the results with half the effort. Naturally, their understanding of Space rapidly increased. However, it still did not change the fact that all their attempts to warp Space had failed.","After four hours of trial and error, Yang Ji asked, “Each Space is different, with different thresholds. We have searched through our rooms to find the toughest spot to wrap Space, but even that tears apart. Heavenly Demon Queen, are there any more clues you can give us?”","As Yang Ji had suspected, despite the Heavenly Demon Queen not being inside of him, she could still hear him and Yang Xu. It was truly a strange connection they shared.","“Am I to serve as your perpetual instructor? The seeds of wisdom have been adequately sown. True enlightenment of this nature must blossom from within through your own earnest cultivation.” The Heavenly Demon Queen gave a huff. [These children are too used to swift attainment. Who amongst this realm could fathom the boundless depths of a True Dao in such a brief span of time?]","“Brother, no need to bother yourself with her. Haven’t we figured stuff like this out ourselves countless times?” Yang Xu rolled her eyes. She definitely did not want to rely on this worm to teach her. However, there was something that bothered her, “Why do I feel like you are at some distant location? Brother, is she not with you?”","“No, she went off, outside my room. I didn’t really focus too much on her, since we’ve been focused on cultivating.” Yang Ji stated this openly, which threw Yang Xu into an alarmed state.","“You just let her leave like that!? What if she harms someone?” Yang Xu immediately chided him.","However, the Heavenly Demon Queen corrected her, “I am cognizant of your diminished regard for my character, yet even I must protest such calumnious slander. Your esteemed Brother deems me sufficiently trustworthy to traverse unaccompanied. Furthermore, what conceivable purpose would I serve in bringing harm to any soul within this realm of yours?”","“You also need not harbor any concerns regarding my conduct. Let it be known with utmost certainty that I shall never cause calamity upon either of you, nor upon those whom you hold dear.” The Heavenly Demon Queen scoffed. “A person of particular fascination has captured my attention, one which has escaped detection even by your Father’s formidable perception. Rest assured, I shall remain but a humble witness here, merely pending confirmation of my hypothesis.”","“So, you went out to stalk someone?” Yang Xu’s eyes narrowed.","“By strict definition of the term, that is correct.” The Heavenly Demon Queen felt the statement was off, but for some reason, Yang Xu gave a nod, as if in understanding for some reason.","*Knock knock knock*","Before they knew it, the Twins had their room doors both knocked at the same time.","“Sister, you too?” Yang Ji asked.","“Yeah. I wonder what it’s about.” Yang Xu stood up and walked towards the door, opening at the exact same time at Yang Ji.","To their surprise, there was no one there. However, upon opening the door, they could see that there were already students gathered at the platform, on the ground floor.","“Oh? A day has already passed. I did not even realise it... guess it’s time to gather.” Yang Ji said, as both he and Yang Ji leaped from the fourth floor down to the ground floor, quickly joining the gathered students.","Naturally, their actions sparked a lot of attention. However, no one said two words about it. Only Li Wu Yi reminded, “Okay, seems like the last pair has finally arrived. A reminder to everyone here, if you are going to enter secluded cultivation, remember to tell us first before you enter your room to activate the Isolation Array. Also, turn your room number over. Since today is the first day, I will not deliver any punishment. But going forward, I expect everyone to act in accordance with the rules.”","Li Wu Yi specifically eyed the Twins when he said the last part. However, knowing them, he kept his expectations low.","“Since we are already running late, I will be teleporting all students to the classroom. But, that’s only for today. From tomorrow onwards, you would need to travel down yourselves.” Li Wu Yi said and with a wave of his hand, students on the platform were instantly transported away. He even took it upon himself to transport Xu Yi to the classroom.","There, class officially starts.","...","And that was also where class ended.","However, not like it mattered because to Yang Ji and Yang Xu, they hardly remember what was being mentioned. Instead of listening to Li Wu Yi on his first lecture, they had been talking to each other the whole time. After all, this class was truly too rudimentary for them.","Also, since the Twins were not making a ruckus, and seemed to be awake, though staring blankly forward like their Souls were away, Li Wu Yi just let them be. After all, even he knew that the things he was teaching them were a little too basic. He was already happy that they were not sleeping in his class.","Li Wu Yi had given much thought on how he could teach them. Unfortunately, he could not come up with much. The Twins were on their own path, and he, as their teacher, found it hard to actually teach them when their bar was already so high. In fact, it was more accurate to say that the Twins were at a level where they could hold discussions about the Dao, rather than him teaching.","At the end of the first day of class, Li Wu Yi could feel it keenly that these two were not going to fit into this class, like their Parents had hoped. So, he eyed Xu Yi, but the man only returned with a shake of his head.","[So, you are out of ideas too, huh?] Li Wu Yi gave a sigh in his heart as he finally asked, “Any final questions?”","At this point, for the other students, the contents of his class was already far more than enough for most of them to ruminate over for a month. Some, who already understood, could take this as a refresher. However, many had plenty of questions to ask. Surprisingly though, the first ones to raise their hands were not these students but the Twins.","[Huh? They were listening? Or were they just waiting for the class to end to ask me something?] Li Wu Yi thought and then said, “Yang Ji, since you were the first one to raise your hand, then I’ll answer your question first.”","Yang Ji straightforwardly said the thing that he and Yang Xu had been pondering over since yesterday, “How does one control Space without the Void?”","Li Wu Yi was taken aback by this question. Like he thought, the Twins were at a level where they could have a discussion about the Dao of Space. However, at this point, this question was not really helpful to the other students in the class and in fact could be a detriment if they focus too much on it. So, he directed them to talk after class and gave the opportunity to the other students."]},{"number":6079,"title":"Chapter 6079, The Mysterious Boy? Man?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6079, The Mysterious Boy? Man?","Author: Silavin","Once the class ended, the students dispersed. Since they were all cultivators, after their daily lesson, it would be free time for them. They could look for Secret Techniques in the Heaven Records Pavilion, go to the Battle Arena if their fist itched, or go to the Heaven Exchange Hall to shop. Naturally, this was also the best time for students to get to know one another.","However, two students remained in class, with two teachers overseeing them at this moment. They were not being punished, but from the expressions of the two teachers, one would be uncertain about it.","The class isolated as well, preventing any sound from leaking, as though no one wanted any secrets to leak out.","Li Wu Yi sighed and said, “I know that class is boring for you two, and realistically, it would be hard for the other children to keep up with you two. So, in the future, if you have such questions, it is best for you to speak to me through your Divine Sense. I don’t wish for the others to get confused by your questions.”","“But, on the topic of controlling Space without the Void, I do not think that is possible. All things exist in the Void, but that is not the case for Space. The Void is everywhere, and contains everything.” Li Wu Yi said his own theory of Space and its Principles. Naturally, even Xu Yi was interested in this topic, despite his focus being in the Dao of Time.","Yang Ji gave a nod, it was unclear if that was in regards to the former statement or the latter statement. Still, Yang Ji just said his own thoughts, “If the Void contains everything, then how do we go to the world behind the Profound Source Gate through it?”","At this question, Li Wu Yi and Xu Yi had their eyes widened and their ears perked. After all, how did this young boy know about the Profound Source Gate and the world behind it? That was a secret that was kept, which few knew about.","Of course these two would be surprised, as what happened to Yang Ji and Yang Xu a few months prior had not been spread, and few knew about it. Nevertheless, Li Wu Yi could now only thank his own insightfulness in isolating the classroom before they had begun talking. He initially only did it to prevent students from overhearing and leading to confusion in their Dao, but this was something even more vital to keep secret.","“How did you...” Still Li Wu Yi could feel a headache coming as he continued, “Never mind. Since you are already aware of that world, then I will frankly say that I do not know. All I know is that it is a different world, unlike ours. It might exist in the Void, and that we merely have not uncovered another route to get to it.”","After all, no one could claim that they fully explored and understood the Void. Thus, it stands to reason that they might really be able to transverse through the Void to get there.","However, as though overhearing the conversation, despite the barrier isolating the room, the Heavenly Demon Queen’s voice broke through into the minds of the Twins, “Do not deceive yourselves. That place exists beyond the Void itself.”","The Twins did not understand how she was able to hear their conversation, but it also did not seem too odd for them. So, rather than badger about it, they focus on the meaning behind those words instead.","However, before they could ask Li Wu Yi another question, the voice came out again.","“Your teacher has nothing more to offer you–no insights, no revelations. The path forward belongs to you two alone to forge. Enough deliberation. Come to me at once. I require your strength.” The Heavenly Demon Queen urged, and the Twins immediately felt something was off. After all, this was the haughty Heavenly Demon Queen speaking. When had she ever asked for help?","“What’s wrong?” Seeing the Twins had their expressions so drastically change from that of deep thought to confusion in one and worry in another, Xu Yi could not help but ask.","“Uncle Li Wu Yi, I think that’s all the questions that we have for today.” Yang Ji quickly said.","Li Wu Yi just gave a nod, “Alright, it is your first day anyway. Best if you can get more time to mingle with your classmates.”","With a snap of his finger, the barrier was removed and the Twins were free to leave.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu immediately nodded at each other and quickly disappeared from sight, leaving the classroom with only two adults.","“Aren’t you going to go after them? It is clear that they are up to something.” Xu Yi asked as he used his Divine Sense to perceive where those two might have gone.","“We are not their baby sitters. Besides, where else can they go? This whole space is created and sealed by their Father. It’s safe here. If you want, you can go after them, but I believe you will be found out soon enough.” Li Wu Yi said, knowing full well the capabilities of these two children. After all, even Yang Kai had to keep a distance when trailing them.","Xu Yi shrugged. He believes that since his Master was here, nothing could go wrong.","...","The Twins need not ask for the Heavenly Demon Queen’s location and just knew of it. In just a blink of an eye, they had already appeared close to her.","They could have immediately arrived before her, but Yang Xu was cautious and opted to appear a distance away.","However, the sight before them was... baffling. After all, the Heavenly Demon Queen was not in any danger.","In a small alleyway within the school, where there was a clear lack of people, the Heavenly Demon Queen was hovering in the air. In front of her was a child, not too much different in age from them. This child was kneeling with his head on the floor, arms out as if in complete submission.","Though they could not see the child’s face, from his hair alone, he obviously did not bother to groom himself. Still, at least he did not appear like a beggar, though that might be because of the new attire he had received.","“Hey, what the heck are you doing bullying someone?” Yang Xu naturally berated her the first instant she saw this scene through their Divine Sense.","“Bully?! Preposterous! I raised not a finger, spoke not a threat! The moment this man perceived my presence, he threw himself to the ground in terror! Is it my fault then?” The Heavenly Demon Queen’s eyes narrowed as she replied. Naturally, this conversation was not heard by the boy grovelling. So, she ordered, “Stand up at once. A mighty being grovelling, do you have no shame?”","The boy immediately stood up and wore a sneaky pleasing grin. If one were to describe such a face, the word ‘puchable’ would come to mind. However, he tried his best to appease the being in front of him, as though she were his only pillar in the world, “Beautiful Sister, why has someone so mighty and beautiful come to see an insignificant ant like me? I dare not take on the grace you have given me...”","Even with his fist cupped, and head down, he could still sneak in a few glances, as though gauging the Heavenly Demon Queen’s reaction.","Seeing how she was unmoved by his words, he continued, “May I ask what a great figure like you might want from a humble being like me?”","Ignoring him completely, the Heavenly Demon Queen stood silent. However, in fact, she was asking for Yang Ji and Yang Xu to help isolate this Space.","Unfortunately, it seemed like this boy was able to sense that a huge cage was being formed. So, he let go of all pretenses and smirked, directly challenging, “Think you can trap me?”","Before the Space could be isolated, he turned illusionary. His figure became fleeting, as though made of mist, with light being able to easily pass through. Soon, he completely disappeared, and was no longer in sight.","Even when Yang Ji and Yang Xu used their Divine Sense to scan the area, they found nothing. It was as if his very existence was erased. They were about to ask the Heavenly Demon Queen, when she just declared, “Wait.”","It was a tone that allowed no disobedience. However, how could such a tone possibly stop the Twins?","“Since you are not moving, I guess he is still here?” Yang Xu concluded, and then turned to her Brother.","Yang Ji gave a nod and the two of them started to clench their fist. As they did so, Space Principles moved and the ‘cage’ began to shrink.","Space cracked and tore, with the Void inching ever closer, tearing apart everything within. Only three figures were spared in the onslaught, and these three were looking around to spot any oddities.","“Do you intend to persist in concealing yourself? We shall render this entire Space into the Void if necessary.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stood still as she declared with eyes narrowed.","From what she knew, if this man truly wished to escape, it would be hard for them to stop him. However, such actions would also bring great risks to him.","However, even with that last warning, nothing appeared.","“Maybe he is not here?” Yang Xu asked, but Yang Ji corrected, “Maybe, but we already destroyed so much of the area here. Might as well go all the way.”","Yang Ji slammed his fist down and the whole Space tore, with everything sent into the Void.","In the next instant, all three figures were in the Void, which was filled with broken pieces of debris. However, at this point, seeing that the person was truly gone, Yang Ji held no interest in remaining and had just sent everyone back out.","Once he was out, the scene before him reminded him of the scoldings he was going to get.","The walls and floors were torn with gnashes, as if a Monster Beast had just clawed through everything. The plants around were also not spared, as every bit missing had been sent to the Void.","“Haa... looks like we are going to get scolded again.” Yang Xu commented, but the Heavenly Demon Queen added, “That conclusion does not necessarily hold merit. This Space is interwoven with a multitude of Arrays, one of which is designed to mend the destroyed. Moreover, the verdant growth shall inevitably return, nourished by the inexhaustible vitality radiating from that World Tree.”","“What we need to concern ourselves with is that man. One must marvel that he maintains his concealment even in the wake of such devastation...” The Heavenly Demon Queen said as she sighed."]},{"number":6080,"title":"Chapter 6080, Just What Have You Done?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6080, Just What Have You Done?","Author: Silavin","“Moreover, there remains a matter of utmost significance that appears to have escaped your collective notice, by what means does he exercise his power within this place?” The Heavenly Demon Queen’s words struck to the heart of the matter.","“Wait, we can’t use Qi here?” Yang Ji seemed confused. After all, he did not feel any restriction on his Qi circulation here. In fact, he also doubted his Sister felt any different. They did just collapse the Space here, after all.","Yang Xu’s eyes immediately turn sharp. She stared daggers at the Heavenly Demon Queen, “You must have done something to the Array, didn’t you?”","“A keen observation, as expected. You are right. I have made certain arrangements that we three shall encounter no impediments whatsoever. Fear not, the Array continues to function precisely as designed. Only we are granted this particular exemption.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated as though she did nothing wrong. In fact, from her tone, she was expecting the Twins to show their gratitude.","“So that’s why you were out for the whole night! How did you even mess with an Array so deep underground!!? Argh! Father is going to kill us if they find out about it!” Yang Xu felt like she wanted to cry at this moment. She and her Brother did nothing wrong, yet this chaos incarnate was here to drag them to the pits of Hell.","“Calm down. We didn’t do it. Mother and Father will surely understand.” Yang Ji, at the side added. His concern lay elsewhere, namely, that boy who had disappeared right in front of them. He had faith in the Heavenly Demon Queen, despite her personality flaws. She was not one to boast about feats she could not have accomplished. She had a certain ‘pride’ to her.","This was also a public place, where both mortals and cultivators might cross paths. It was unlike the classroom or their Dormitory, where only cultivators were allowed. So, the Grand Array below was surely going to prevent them from using Qi here.","Yang Ji stood there and scanned the scene again, trying to locate the boy. However, he still found nothing. [Seriously, how did he manage to disappear like that? A Movement Technique? Can someone so weak actually use a Movement Technique that can bypass our senses, even without using Qi?]","While they were considering various things, they had forgotten how such a ruckus failed to attract any attention?","“Wait. Someone’s coming.” Yang Xu immediately exclaimed as she looked towards the source.","Obviously, it was a teacher, who had moved due to the commotion they had caused. Since even Yang Xu could see the person, they must have spotted them as well.","“Okay, let’s get out of here first.” Since there was nothing else to do here, Yang Ji gave a nod, and he quickly tore Space again, leaving in the blink of an eye, taking both Yang Xu and the Heavenly Demon Queen with him.","When they had already disappeared, the teacher landed on the ground and then scanned the surrounding devastation–walls in tatters, floors no longer traversable, and scenery destroyed.","“How is this possible?” The teacher took out his Token and deactivated it using his Divine Sense. Soon, he felt his body turn sluggish, Qi unable to circulate. Even moving an arm took a noticeable effort compared to before. “The Array is still working. How had two students managed to not be affected by this?”","This teacher was in the Dao Seal Realm, and even this Grand Array had a great effect on him. So, how was it conceivable for two youths to circumvent its effects?","“I need to tell the Principal about this.” The teacher soon reactivated his Token and poured his Divine Sense into it, transmitting a message to the Disciplinary Board.","With the Space Principles here in a huge mess, it was obvious who the perpetrators of this incident were, not to mention how he had already spotted the Twins. The Principal had also given out special instructions that anything to do with his Children should first be reported to the Disciplinary Board.","“It’s only the first day, and they have already caused trouble. No wonder the Principal had warned all of us about them...” The teacher commented and looked back at the devastation, shaking his head.","...","The Twins naturally went back to the place which was most familiar to them, which was their room. More specifically, Yang Ji had brought them directly into his room. This was naturally crossing the line of another rule, which was no girls were allowed in the male building, but at this moment, neither Twins were really that concerned about this.","“*Phew* I think we got away.” Yang Ji said, but Yang Xu just sighed, resigned to her fate.","“Brother, it was obviously us. No one in the School, besides the teachers, could manipulate Space Principles to that degree.”","“Yeah, I know. But, being questioned by a teacher would be worse than being directly questioned by Mother or Father.” Yang Ji was still convinced they would not get punished since they had not really done anything wrong. He believes he would be able to explain things if they could just meet up with the Parents, rather than get punished by a teacher they did not know. After all, their Mother Su Yan had told them to not easily expose the Heavenly Demon Queen’s existence.","“Anyways, what’s important isn’t that. What’s important is that boy.” Yang Ji now directed his attention to the Heavenly Demon Queen, who was basically hovering around him with a nonchalant expression. “Who is he?”","“He is known by the name Ye Lun, a soul bereft of parentage. Reportedly of the same age as you two. Also, of no association.” The Heavenly Demon Queen answered like it was nothing.","“Wait, how do you even know all of this?” Yang Xu could not help but feel like her head was going to blow. [How could she possibly overhear such details? She must have looked through the teacher’s student list.]","[It has already been a day and she has already caused so much chaos. What’s worse is that no one can punish her! We would be blamed for everything she did!] If eyes could kill, Yang Xu’s eyes would be the epitome of it. She stared at the little worm as she wished to run a stake through her ten thousand times. However, this raised an even more concerning issue in her mind.","“Just what have you done last night!?” Yang Xu pointed and asked, almost clenching her jaws from anger.","However, in contrast, the Heavenly Demon Queen played coy, “To divulge such matters at this juncture would merely spoil the revelation that awaits. I can offer only this assurance: the academic life that lies before you both shall prove most... intriguing. However, I must counsel you with utmost gravity to remain ever vigilant for that particular man. He poses a threat of considerable magnitude, not solely to yourselves, but even to your esteemed Father.”","“Even to Father?” Yang Ji, who remained calm despite his Sister’s rage, fell into disbelief. “Impossible. Father is the strongest. Besides, if he is that strong, then he would not need to escape from us.”","“You may choose to heed my counsel or dismiss it as you see fit. The warning has been delivered, and my duty fulfilled. In any case, I have labored through the entirety of the night. The hour has come for me to take my rest.” The Heavenly Demon Queen simply shrugged. She did not even care about the girl staring daggers at her, as she nonchalantly dove straight into Yang Ji, disappearing from sight. In fact, even when Yang Xu screamed at her, using her Divine Sense or otherwise, the Heavenly Demon Queen did not respond.","“She dares to throw all this crap at us and run away!?” Yang Xu clenched her fist, almost ready to kill. She had never felt this spiteful towards someone, ever.","“Calm down. I know she has caused a lot of problems, but I don’t think she means any harm.” Yang Ji said as he moved to pet her head.","However, Yang Xu, who would normally enjoy such intimate acts, swiped his arm away and questioned, “Why are you even supporting her so much!? She has already caused us so many problems, and has gotten us into trouble. Ever since she came, you’ve always been taking her side.”","“But, she hasn’t really caused us any trouble. And besides, she is our pet... I guess pet is not right anymore. Our friend. We can’t really leave her alone, right?” Yang Ji sighed.","However, contrary to his words, his door was soon knocked on...","“Yang Ji, the Disciplinary Board is here. Come out right now.” A voice of great authority soon ran out, a familiar voice, which seemed able to pass through even the Isolation Arrays, if they were up and running.","“See! I told you!” Yang Xu stomped her feet and cursed, [All because of that little shit!]"]},{"number":6081,"title":"Chapter 6081, Disciplinary Hall","paragraphs":["Chapter 6081, Disciplinary Hall","Author: Silavin","The Disciplinary Board was based not on the surface but underground, in the Disciplinary Hall. Yang Ji and Yang Xu did not know why their Father had placed it here, but the appearance it gave did strike fear into others.","Chains would be hung up on the walls, with skulls decorating the place. If they were fake, they were certainly well designed. But, it would most likely be easier to obtain real ones instead. Since no sunlight touched this land, it was naturally dark, with only Luminous Pearls and blue flames lightning up the place. With the strange howling and screams from below, it certainly made the place look like this was where death would slumber.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu were being escorted down by two members of the Disciplinary Board. As though to make a show, they had been escorted all the way from their dorm to this underground world without teleporting. Just this process alone had taken a few hours, which means it was already close to evening outside.","Along the way, the Twins were naturally talking to each other, just that it was through their Divine Sense. One was enraged and cursing, while the other was trying to calm her down. As for the two teachers escorting them, they mostly kept their silence. After all, this was the first day. They did not think that their assigned role, as members of the Disciplinary Board, would be put to work so quickly after class...","Furthermore, all teachers had been briefed about the identity of these two. It had to be mentioned that not all of Yang Kai’s children had received such attention, just the Twins. After all, in general, none of the others really caused that much trouble–though to be fair, not like they could cause much trouble with their limited strength. With the Twins’ mastery over the Dao of Space and Dao of Time, it was no wonder ‘incidents’ happened.","The two teachers quickly escorted them into a room, where the Head of the Disciplinary Board sat.","The room was large, enough to fit two classes. Yet, most of the space inside had been decorated by bones of exotic Monster Beasts skulls. If there were paintings, they would all be in red, as though made by blood. Naturally, there was an eerie feel to it, more intense than the outside. Even Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not help but feel unnerved by it.","In front of the twins was a large desk made of bones.","When the figure turned around his seat from the large sphere behind him, Yang Ji and Yang Xu had their eyes opened wide.","“Uncle Shi!?” Yang Ji and Yang Xu both exclaimed.","Uncle Shi, also known as Wu Kuang, famed as the Heaven Devouring Great Emperor. He was the only survivor of the ten first Open Heaven Realm Masters, who taught the Human Race how to cultivate.","To call him an ancient fossil would be degrading how ancient he was. After all, he was already around before the rise of the Human Race, during the era where the Divine Spirits ruled.","He was naturally an illusionary figure, who many might not even know the existence of. However, he had met the Twin before, since he was the man that their Father had consulted in regards to their innate Cultivation Technique, the Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique.","From what the Twins knew, Uncle Shi was an unparalleled expert on cultivation techniques. He was the one who made the infamous Heaven Devouring Battle Law, which was known as the most powerful and evil technique, and about half of all known Secret Techniques in modern times.","They had only met him a few times, and during those times, it was mainly just him trying to deduce the origins and effects of the Heaven Earth Symmetry Cultivation Technique.","In the end, Shi did gain some insights and had imparted a simplified version of a portion of the technique before leaving. He had some guesses that there was a connection between the Profound Source Gate and this cultivation technique. However, the Twins remained unaware of this.","After he left, the Twins had not seen him since. Not until today at least.","“What are you doing here?” Yang Ji asked, curious.","It had to be mentioned that at this point, most children would cry or pee themselves. After all, the aura of an expert of Shi’s level was Soul crushing. Even more so, due to the evil nature of the Heaven Devouring Battle Law, the aura he exposed had a malicious and vile nature to it.","In fact, its effects could be seen on the two teachers, who could not help but tense up. Despite their cultivation being higher than the Twins, they were more unnerved by Shi’s aura than them. The Twins seem mostly unaffected by it.","Shi soon withdrew his aura, gave a nod to the two teachers and dismissed them, going so far as to seal off the room before he started to speak.","“Good to see that you two are well. Looks like I’m going to have to work for twenty years now thanks to you two.” There was defeat in his tone as Shi gave a sigh. “To think that you two would get into trouble on your first day. Yang Xue and Yang Kai were right, you two really are trouble markers.”","“It was not our fault.” Yang Xu immediately shot back.","“Yes, yes, like how you two did not just destroy an alleyway within the school.” Shi rolled his eyes. He reached out his hand and the large sphere at the back of the room lit up. On it showed the current scene of destruction, the alleyway.","“Do you take my eyes for those of a fool? Though the school will repair these damages on its own over time, we still have rules here. Yet, you two wantonly unleashed Space Principles to crush a common area.” Shi reprimanded, unleashing pressure which would force even Dao Source Realm Masters onto their knees.","However, as predicted, the Twins still managed to stand upright, seemingly almost unaffected by the pressure.","“Seems like you two are still able to use your cultivation. How?” Shi asked with his eyes sharp, and at each word, the pressure increased.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu could feel their bones creaking at this point. They were still able to stand, but the pressure was indeed noticeable now.","Yang Xu readily admitted, “The Grand Array doesn’t work on us.”","Instantly, the pressure on them subsided. Since it was so weak, it was obvious Shi only did it to show off his authority, not wishing to cause them any harm.","“Like I thought.” Shi gave a nod and then walked towards the Twins. He placed his hand out and told them, “Tell her to come out.”","“Her?” Yang Ji pretended not to know what he was talking about. However, Shi immediately explained. “Who else? That being that calls herself the Heavenly Demon Queen. Call her out.","Your Aunt Yang Xue had already informed me about what happened in the Profound Source Gate, and your Mother Su Yan has told me in greater detail. There is no need to hide her existence from me.”","Yang Ji looked at Yang Xu, who was also looking back at him. Soon...","“Cease your endless chattering. You merely require me to grace this man with my presence, no? Fine.” Suddenly, the Heavenly Demon Queen came out, her voice only to the Twins.","The Twins were truly children, if they could not force her out, they would annoy her till she got out...","When Shi caught sight of her, he gave a profound nod and circled around her, like an appraiser viewing a priceless gem. “I did catch sight of you using the Viewing Orb, but you are a truly peculiar being. You are clearly not of this world, but your aura is perfectly intertwined with the Twins. How interesting...”","“At least your eyes are no mere decorations. Speak, what compels you to seek me?” The Heavenly Demon Queen asked, side-eyeing him as he went round her, completely relaxed, certain he could not do anything to her.","“You are not afraid of me. Seems like anything I do to you would also bring harm to the children. Yet, you are conscious of their Father, and not their Mother. If I could, I would dissect your Soul to see your memories.” Shi said, his words cold and unnerving, as though he was looking at an experimental test subject rather than a person. After all, from his perspective, the Heavenly Demon Queen was a foreign entity, that might be hostile, who could be said to have taken the Twins as hostages.","“I am quite certain you did not summon my presence merely to issue hollow threats through trivial rhetoric.” The Heavenly Demon Queen shot back, not backing down in the slightest.","“Then, if we are to begin, tell me what made you so afraid of their Father?” Shi grinned awaiting a response. Though, as expected, she did not answer.","“Seems like any question that inconveniences you will just be met with silence. Oh well, how typical. Go back. I’ve already figured out the most important points just from your presence.” Shi stopped looking at her and turned his attention to the large sphere.","In the meantime, the Heavenly Demon Queen just gave *hmph* and retreated back into Yang Ji.","It could be seen from the side that Yang Xu was celebrating with a wide grin.","Then, there was silence in the room. Shi seemed to be in deep thought, while the Twins did not dare to interrupt him.","It took a while before Shi shook his head and waved his hand against the sphere. There, a new image appeared, which took Yang Ji and Yang Xu by surprise.","There, on it was the image of the very boy who had disappeared from their sight earlier today. He was walking normally through the school as though nothing had just happened to him.","“It’s him.” Yang Ji exclaimed, and Yang Xu asked, “He’s okay?”","“Why do you think your only punishment is going to be about using your powers and destroying school property? If he had died, I can swear to you that even your Parents won’t be able to save you.” Shi coldly stated, offering no excuses.","Though cultivators would die seeking opportunities, this was a school. It was not a Sect. As the now Head of the Disciplinary Board, he would naturally be the one to enforce the rules.","Naturally, this was but one of the deals he had made before he accepted this position: to be left alone in how he handled cases. After all, he did not wish for those annoying Parents to get in his way of disciplining children. That was for the Principal to deal with.","Besides, losing him was equivalent to losing an entire library of Secret Techniques and Cultivation Techniques. Would the school really be willing to refuse such requests?","“No, Uncle Shi, we didn’t think we would be able to kill him. Just that... he vanished. We don’t even know how he did it. He really just vanished right in front of us.” Yang Ji stated, confused as he recalled the events that played out earlier. [He really did vanish, even after we sealed off Space.]","“Vanished? Tell me more about it.” Shi’s eyes narrowed. After all, after the Twins sealed off that Space, before they collapsed it, he had not been able to see anything that happened inside."]},{"number":6082,"title":"Chapter 6082, Can’t Do Anything To Her","paragraphs":["Chapter 6082, Can’t Do Anything To Her","Author: Silavin","The Twins went into great detail about the whole event, not missing a single detail. There was nothing to hide for them.","Once he heard everything, Shi showed minimal expression despite his true feelings on the matter. He wished to pursue the matter further, but would the Heavenly Demon Queen tell them anything?","There were many questions in his mind, questions he wanted answers to. However, he knew where to draw the line.","Still, he had confirmed the major matter. So, now, it was time for the Twins to receive their punishment.","Since it was the first day, typically, Shi decided to be extra harsh. After all, he had to show the authority of the Discipline Council.","However, he soon received a message. No, multiple messages. Divine Senses keep bombarding him, advising him what to do.","Naturally, who else could that be from? They were from the Twins’ Parents plus Yang Xue.","He could not help getting annoyed. Could they not let him do his job?","Why did they not step in when he was checking the Heavenly Demon Queen? Why did they only step in when it came to the punishment?","In the end, Shi scolded them back before turning to the Twins and deciding on his own punishment for the.","“You two are going to take care of Lei Ao and help shuttle your classmates from the dorm to the class for a month. Also, you two will be helping me in the Disciple Council.” Shi stated with his the blood vessels on his head bludging.","[Seriously, some complain about not using physical violence. Some want me to hit them harder. Some wonder if it would really hurt them. But all of them want me to help them make friends!? Are all of you mad? This is not a childcare centre! I’m running the Disciple Council!]","Still, it was not like Shi could ignore the rallying cry from ten women. In fact, he could feel Yang Kai’s pain as the Father himself just kept silent throughout this ordeal.","When the Twin heard this, they immediately agreed to it. After all, it did not sound like much of a punishment to them.","Fetching someone to and fro? They were proficient in the Dao of Space, do not underestimate them!","Taking care of others? They have so many Siblings. How could they not be good at taking care of others?","Disciple Council? Who besides them has the most righteousness and disciple? They were certain their Mothers would vouch for them (lies).","As if afraid he would change his mind, the Twins were quick to find a means of escaping any further conversation.","Naturally, when the Mothers looked at this scene, they could not help but think of a particular individual.","...","“I know you have done a ton of evil, but don’t you think this design is overkill?” Yang Kai appeared right next to Shi. Furthermore, he was not alone. Yang Xue was also present. As for the other Wives, they were just listening in.","They had been hiding themselves in another room, one which was far off from this one. They had been able to hear the conversation and watch the scene from that room.","“From my experience, if you want kids to obey, you need to make them fear.” Shi said with nonchalance. Though, it was doubtful if the whole design of the Disciplinary Hall was actually to his liking or not.","“Well, I’ve lost. Really did not think your kids would cause so much trouble on the very first day.” Shi admitted as though surrendering.","“So, what have you uncovered so far?” Yang Xue could not care less about the frivolous bet these two men had agreed upon. Ten years, twenty years, when their lifespans reached over a million years, do those small digits really matter?","“Though I said that she has taken them hostage, it’s more like they are coexisting together. Any harm to them would also be detrimental to her. I have honestly never seen something like this before. Those two kids of yours are truly eye-opening.” Shi said. They might have Soul Clones or Avatars, which might damage the main body when destroyed, as they are intrinsically linked, but this being was a foreign body that happened to ‘connect’ with them.","“Her very existence is tied to them. I can only attribute this to the strange cultivation technique that they use. Regardless, from the way things are, I doubt she will bring any harm to them.” Shi shrugged, truly certain of this one point.","“She was also very wary. I do not know but I get the sense that she was aware of everyone watching.”","“Anyways, have you figured out what she did to your Arrays? How did it not prevent those kids from using their Qi?” Shi snapped his finger and the Viewing Orb now showed an underground space, deep within the earth. This was where the Grand Array had been laid out. Furthermore, to prevent anyone from accidentally damaging it, there were Protective Arrays surrounding this pace as well.","The Grand Array they were now viewing was the structure keeping everyone from using Qi at common areas of the school, unless one had a Token like the teachers.","At the moment, those mysterious marks on the Grand Array were glowing, showing that it was operating. However, the layout of the Array had changed slightly from Yang Kai’s memory.","“After looking through it, there are Principles implemented that I do not understand.” Yang Kai shook his head while sighing.","This shocked Yang Xue. After all, her Older Brother had already mastered the 3,000 Daos. What kind of Principles did he not understand? If he did not know it, who did?","Yet, Shi remained completely calm, as though he had anticipated this.","Despite his long years, there were still mysteries of the world he did not know about. Since that being was a mystery itself, was this really that shocking?","“Big Brother, we can’t just leave her like this!” Yang Xue pleaded. If the Heavenly Demon Queen fears him, surely he must have some way to remove her, right?","However, it was no use. Yang Kai refused to do anything. If there was a risk to the Twins, he would definitely do something about her.","It might be risky for his children, with Shi’s and Little Eleven’s assurance, he was more at ease. Furthermore, this was an opportunity to uncover certain mysteries of the world. He simply could not let this opportunity slide.","Even if Yang Kai remained oblivious to most things, he could keenly tell that there was something in the world preventing others from finding out the truth about the world.","“It is not like we can Soul Search her. Since she is not willing to speak, then we can only keep a close eye on her for now. Just leave the Grand Array as is. If she is adamant, I doubt we can really stop her from changing the Arrays. But, you’d best check all the Arrays to see if anything else has been tempered with.”","Yang Kai naturally gave a firm nod as he took control over the Viewing Orb and switched the focus to the male student who had caught the Heavenly Demon Queen’s eye. Then, he took out a scroll.","The bright scroll rolled open, seemingly capable of containing an entire world of its own. There were no words written in it. It was just empty. However, the moment Yang Kai injected his Divine Sense, he was able to see the name list of all the students, including a portrait of them.","In an instant, Yang Kai was able to uncover all the details of the boy.","Still, his origins were mysterious.","Wu Lun, 14 years old, male, River Ocean World, Orphan, No Master, No Sect, Separation And Reunion.","The River Ocean World was one of those relatively newly restored Worlds within the 3,000 Worlds. It was nothing special or noteworthy. Furthermore, the child had no backing: no parents, no nothing. At only fourteen, to reach the Separation and Reunion Realm showed that he was mediocre.","Yet, how did someone like this attract the attention of the Heavenly Demon Queen and escape from Yang Ji and Yang Xu?","He was an anomaly, one they needed to watch out for."]},{"number":6083,"title":"Chapter 6083, Travelling Coach Service!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6083, Travelling Coach Service!","Author: Silavin","“Eh? What is that?”","“Travelling Coach?”","“Oh, its those two. They are really early today!”","There was clamour from the people around them.","“I wonder when did they have enough time to create this.” However, as though unbothered by them, Yang Ji merely stared in wonder at the scene before him.","There was a group of students directly in front of him, all lined up in an orderly fashion. They were all his classmates, on the platform in the middle of the dorm. Naturally, to his side was Yang Xu, his Sister who looked at the huge sign above their heads.","This huge sign was a manifestation of Qi. It was created when they injected their Qi into a pair of Tokens that Li Wu Yi had given them, which had the characters ‘纪堂’ written on them, signifying their position as part of the Disciplinary Board. Still, they believe only their Tokens had the ability to manifest this sign high up in the sky, ‘Travelling Coach’.","Sad to say, the Twins had no ability to modify the words being manifested. So, from then on, it was certain that they would be known as the travelling coachmen.","“Dad created this.” Yang Xu noted how these Tokens were obviously freshly made, as there was the lingering aura of their Father on it. Obviously, the decision to have them fulfil this role had been a hasty one, with their Father needing to create this Artifact overnight.","Thankfully, they were just simple Tokens. They did not have any other functions. Still, they were bonded to them, and could not be used by anyone else. In a way, it was a perfect disguise for them. With these Tokens, they could act as though they were given close to the same authority as the Teachers. They could use Qi freely without facing as much scrutiny. Their status as part of the Disciplinary Board further highlighted this.","Though Shi had made a fuss over how they had broken the rules, in reality, they did not get caught by any other student. Furthermore, the site of destruction had already been fixed. So, the question of whether this could be counted as punishment might as well be forfeited.","Besides, the only other student who knew the truth was Wu Lun. Would he make a move to denounce them? Would he act out?","Any reaction from him was welcomed.","Still, it could be said that one of their punishments was needing to gather before all other classmates. Ironically, teachers too, since Li Wu Yi would need to ensure they were at the platform on time.","“Alright. Everyone is gathered.” Li Wu Yi looked around and gave a nod. “For a whole month, Yang Ji and Yang Xu will be shuttling everyone here to and from class. All of you need to be here before sunrise or you will need to travel on your own.”","Li Wu Yi did not explain why the Twins were forced to do this. He just left it up to the Twins to clarify. Furthermore, with the Disciplinary Board Token shining brightly, certainly the few students should have guessed a few things.","Li Wu Yi just gave the Twins a nod, and with a *snap* from Yang Ji, everyone was transported into the classroom. In fact, each student was standing behind their table.","Though it looked like Yang Ji had transported everyone at once, he actually did it one by one. He tore space and threw them into their respective locations. It just happened so fast that to most students, they thought it was a mass teleportation.","Furthermore, it highlighted how skilled Yang Ji was with no one experiencing any ill-effects from the sudden transportation through the Void.","Li Wu Yi, checking once more that all students were present, gave a nod. He had already expected this much from the Twins. This further highlighted how they should not be wasting time in his class, where he could only teach the basics for the other new fledglings. Thankfully, Shi had truly given him the perfect excuse.","“You two sure are skilled. I do not think the basic class would be of much benefit to you two. I recall that you two are tasked to take care of Lei Ao. Please hand this over to him. In the meantime, try to teach him if he asks any questions.” Li Wu Yi stated and directly threw a scroll to Yang Xu.","When Yang Xu caught it, Li Wu Yi directly sent a message through his Divine Sense. “You’ve shown off your strength and mastery over the Dao of Space. I doubt any of your classmates would feel despondent about you two skipping class. I believe Shi has anticipated this and had arranged it so your two could move freely. Just... just try to reign in your Brother, okay?”","Yang Xu looked at Yang Ji, who was already wearing a disgruntled face.","“Reign me in? What is he trying to say?” Yang Ji immediately commented, which could only be heard by Yang Xu.","Yang Xu quickly just cupped her fist and bowed before disappearing from the scene, taking Yang Ji with her.","Naturally, Li Wu Yi had noticed Yang Ji’s facial expression. He could not help but wonder, [Must you really tell your Brother I said that?]","Little did he know, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could basically listen in to any Divine Sense messages sent to either party. If Yang Xu wanted to keep her privacy, she could naturally do it. It was just that for most cases, she saw no need to. This was just one of the examples.","...","“Uncle Li Wu Yi! That is slander! Sister, why did you take me away? I have to correct him on this!” Yang Ji said using his Divine Sense.","However, the one responding to him was not Yang Xu but the Heavenly Demon Queen instead.","“Hahaha. His message was confined to your sister’s ears alone, not shouted across the assembly. He has already shown you more consideration than perhaps you deserve. Now, setting your pride aside, is his evaluation wrong?” The Heavenly Demon Queen snorts and directs her attention to Yang Xu. “It may well be that her tendency to defer to your judgment, following willingly where you guide, has made it abundantly clear to all present whose will truly governs your actions.”","“Moreover, do not mistake those utterances for insults. Consider them instead as counsel offered in good faith. You would be wise to embrace them as such.” The Heavenly Demon Queen advised before returning to silence once more, not wanting to hear any rebuttal from Yang Ji or Yang Xu.","“Seriously. You come and go as you like.” Yang Ji quipped. However, seeing how Yang Xu did not even try to refute her, he believes there must be some truth to those words.","“Okay, okay. Let’s not talk about this anymore. We still have to find out where this Lei Ao person is. Since he is injured, he should be in the Recovery Hall.” Yang Ji took a step and the scene around the Twins changed, from the original open sky, back to the ground below. The Dao of Space was truly convenient.","Now, behind them were fields and fields of medicine plants. Furthermore, in front of them stood a huge building multiple floors tall. However, this building was only the entrance. It was just the reception building, but with multiple Space Arrays inside.","In fact, this was quite distant from the school and the Recovery Hall was just one part of this compound. In this compound, there was the Alchemy Hall and Plantation Hall as well.","In this front building, there were multiple Space Arrays connected to different parts of the school. This was to reduce the time it took for students, regardless if they were cultivators or Mortals, and staff to travel. Naturally, due to how large this place was, a reception area was necessary.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu walked through and arrived at a large reception desk. It was circular, and had multiple people inside. However, there was one energetic beautiful woman who greeted them, seemingly stealing the show from her colleagues.","“Oh, what can I do for you two cuties today?”","“We are here to look for Lei Ao.” Yang Ji was annoyed at being called ‘cutie’ and quickly stated his business. He even took out his Disciplinary Board Token and Identity Plate.","The receptionist took the Identity Plate and injected her Divine Sense into it. “Ah. The first student to get hospitalised. You are from the same class. Guess your teacher must have given you some kind of instruction. Okay. No problem. Let your Big Sis here show you the way.”","She soon passed back the items and led the Twins through the door at the back, leading them to the Recovery Hall.","Along the way, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not help but marvel at how the plants and buildings here seem to merge. It was as though they entered another world, where nature had taken root into all things.","Yang Ji wanted to think this was something his Father had designed. However, he had an inkling that his Father was not this talented. As for Yang Xu, she was certain this was not designed by Yang Kai.","The receptionist continued to move in a way that showed off her bountiful assets. Though Yang Ji hardly noticed, how could this escape Yang Xu’s eyes? Still, it was questionable if this was just how she normally walked or if she was trying to show something. Nevertheless, since her Brother had not noticed, Yang Xu might as well not mention it.","Eventually, the scenery merged and all focus came onto a single door.","The receptionist made quite an overt gesture and said, “Here we are. Patient Lei Ao is inside. Currently, he is awake and is scheduled to be discharged in a few days.”","She then moved her hand to rub over Yang Xu’s hair before walking back, “If you need anything, your beautiful Big Sis will be at the reception desk.”","Even when walking back, her hips continued to sway, making Yang Xu conclude that it must be how she moved.","As for Yang Ji, he could not care less about her and directly opened the door, entering without hesitation. He did not even greet. He just entered as though it was the most natural thing in the world.","Of course, at this point, he caught sight of the student that got injured because he had pushed himself too hard. However, what he caught sight of was more than that...","“Lei Ao...?” Yang Ji greeted but his words were trapped in the back of his throat.","Why?","Because he saw this young man, who was so steadfast and proud, around the same age as them, lying down and drinking from a milk bottle!","“Wow~”"]},{"number":6084,"title":"Chapter 6084, Yang Ji’s Gift","paragraphs":["Chapter 6084, Yang Ji’s Gift","Author: Silavin","That ‘wow’ rumbled like thunder in Lei Ao’s ears. His heart started to fall and his face turned pallid.","*Bang!*","However, such a scene was quickly hidden by Yang Ji, who quickly closed the door as he turned towards Yang Xu, who had her hands in front of her mouth, shocked by what she had just done.","“Sister, that was too much...” Yang Ji said, seemingly finding it hard to explain.","“Sorry...” Yang Xu could not say much else. She understood that her small exclamation had ruined the pride of a ‘man’. This was something Mother Yu Ru Meng had taught her before, which was that men were prideful creatures. Her Father was no different, and her Brothers were no different.","Yang Ji paced around outside, trying to think. Then, he settled on it. “Sister, how about you go out for a moment. Leave Lei Ao to me. I can handle this task. I think meeting a girl at this time would be quite difficult for him.”","Yang Xu thought for a moment. [It will be hard for me to see him right now. Anyways, Brother will be alone with a guy, so that’s fine...]","“Okay, then, I’ll leave it to you.” With that thought, Yang Xu agreed and she passed the scroll over to him. She even went as far as to disappear from his sight, though Yang Ji could still easily sense her presence nearby.","*Haa...* Since this hot potato had been accepted by him, Yang Ji let out a sigh and reopened the door. The moment he did, Lei Ao was sitting up on his bed, all proper, as though nothing had happened.","Yang Ji had controlled his facial expression, but his lips could not help but twitch. Still, he celebrated inside. [Are you seriously going to act like nothing happened? Good, that makes things less awkward for me.]","“Teacher Li Wu Yi has asked me to assist you in catching up in class. He even prepared a scroll containing the lessons we would cover during the few days you are not in class.” Since this was how Lei Ao wanted to play it, Yang Ji would just get straight to the point.","However, Lei Ao just scoffed, “You? Teach me? *Ha!*”","Yang Ji’s eyes narrowed. “Oh? For someone who cannot even manage to bear with our bath water, you sure talk big.”","“Th-that’s because your cultivation realm is much higher than mine! That has nothing to do with my mastery over the Dao of Space!” Lei Ao rebutted.","“You are only in the Transcendent Realm. How much of the Dao of Space could you possibly master? What’s more, you are even going through two Daos at the same time.” Yang Ji said as matter-of-factly. However, this revelation struck Lei Ao like thunder. He could not help but tremble.","“W-wait! How do you know!? Your Father might by the Principal, but that doesn’t give you the right to see our private information!” Lei Ao said but was quickly countered.","“What? Why would my Father need to show me anything? I can feel the fluctuations of Space Principles and Time Principles on you. It’s not really a secret or anything. You don’t even seem intent on hiding it. What’s more, your cultivation realm is even lower than my Little Brother’s. Of course I can easily see through you.” Yang Ji said in a calm manner. However, if one were to listen from a third-party, one might think he was showing off–though he had no intention to.","“Wait! Then... then just what cultivation realm have you reached?” Lei Ao’s eyes were wide, and his heart was palpitating.","“I’m in the–” Yang Ji was about to readily say everything. However, a voice immediately came to his mind, warning him.","“Cease this! Should you unveil the truth in his current state, you shall irreparably damage this child’s cultivation. His Dao Heart wavers even now. Say more and it would shatter completely.” The Heavenly Demon Queen explained.","“Wait, are you serious?” Yang Ji used his Divine Sense to ask. However, no reply came back.","[Are Dao Hearts really so fragile?] Yang Ji wondered. However, he truly did not know the answer to this question.","Seeing how he should avoid answering, Yang Ji just said, “I’m obviously in a higher realm than you. But, if you want to find out, uncover it once you get stronger than me.”","Lei Ao’s eyes narrowed. This was a challenge he could not possibly refuse. “Fine! I will get stronger than you! Much stronger! Just you wait and see! I, Lei Ao, the Young Master of Red Clouds Cave Heaven, swear that I will defeat you!”","Those words about defeat passed through Yang Ji’s ears like white noise. Yang Hao had said the same thing numerous times in the past. However, after more than seven years, nothing much has changed. However, something did stand out that caught Yang Ji’s attention.","[Oh? He’s from a Cave Heaven?] Yang Ji’s eyes widened a little. Though he had met a few children from the 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises, he had not met everyone. When he tried to recall if he had met anyone from the Red Clouds Cave Heaven, nothing came to mind.","Still from what he knew, Red Clouds Cave Heaven was a Sect that focuses on gathering rare materials and was well known for their Auctions. He was not certain about the inner workings of the Sect, but he was well aware that those from a Cave Heaven or Paradise could not be underestimated.","So far, though those children he had met could never beat he nor Yang Xu, they could give his Little Brothers and Sisters a run for their money.","[Oh, no wonder why he’s here. High Heaven Palace is well known for its experts that study the Dao of Space and Dao of Time. Other Sects would at most be proficient in one of these so-called ‘abstruse’ Daos, but High Heaven Palace is good at both. At the same time, if its Red Clouds Cave Heaven, having their Young Master come here to gain more connections would also be beneficial to the Sect...] Yang Ji realised this and gave a nod. [Wait... rare materials, Auctions! Oh!!!]","Soon, Yang Ji’s eyes turn sharp. It was as though he was a tiger looking upon a fawn. [My good ‘friend’. I’m sure you know a lot of interesting places.]","Under such an intense glare, Lei Ao could not help but shudder, [Wait. Is he getting angry because I said I would defeat him?]","However, with such thoughts, a more competitive spirit was aroused from him. Instead of shrinking back, he forcibly met it.","Seeing how Lei Ao was also ‘interested’, Yang Ji gave a nod. [Mothers did say that I have to be nice to make friends. Let me give him a gift then.]","Yang Ji then thought for a moment, and then came up with something. [Yeah! Father gave that to me and Yang Xu as a gift. He will definitely be grateful if I give him this!]","“Since this is our first official proper meeting, then let me give this to you as a gift.” Yang Ji gave a smile that looked so innocent that it would certainly make his Sister’s heart skip a beat.","However, this smile would soon be eternally remembered by Lei Ao... A smile that seemed to be that of the Devil itself.","Yang Ji closed his eyes for a moment and took a deep breath. Then, his eyes flashed opened. Before Lei Ao could even react, Yang Ji stabbed his index finger to Lei Ao’s forehead.","At that moment, Lei Ao thought that he was about to die. The aura concentrated into Yang Ji’s finger was just that potent. It was to an unfathomable degree and it was coming at him so quickly that he did not even have time to blink.","Once his forehead made contact, Lei Ao could feel his entire body freeze. Then, he could feel his Soul unable to move. It felt like his whole being was being sucked into quicksand, unable to break free. He tried to struggle but it was all futile. The darkness below him was slowly creeping up, devouring his Soul.","At the final moment, before the whole world faded to black, he could see that smile. The smile he would never forget.","...","Yang Ji exhaled as a bead of sweat rolled down his forehead. He had just used a lot of Spiritual Energy and Qi to impart his ‘gift’ onto Lei Ao. He had even tapped into Yang Xu’s reserves. So, it could be said that he was utterly spent imparting this ‘gift’ onto Lei Ao.","As for what this ‘gift’ was, it was his experience exploring Space Principles and Time Principles. He had imparted a ‘small’ bit of his memorable experience and was making Lei Ao go through it.","However, it could be said that Yang Ji was being ‘very considerate’. He had not tossed Lei Ao’s body into such a Space and had only made his Soul go through the experience.","To Yang Ji, this was akin to the gift his Father had given him, the Array Plate he and Yang Xu could enter to train. The same one that had managed to trap Fang Tian Ci for a short amount of time.","This would kill two birds with one stone. He could impart his knowledge of the Dao of Space to Lei Ao, and also give him a great gift at the same time! Yang Ji was certain that this was the start of a wondrous friendship!","However, Yang Ji had truly overestimated this ‘good friend’ of his. If he had only imparted just knowledge of the Dao of Space, that would still be fine. After all, Lei Ao would most likely be able to free himself after a few years in that mentalscape. Once he broke free, if their current class was about beginner knowledge, then he would already master intermediate and advanced knowledge of the Dao of Space.","However, Yang Ji had added the Dao of Time into the mix. This... complicated matters to a severe degree. After all, the Dao of Time was even more abstruse than the Dao of Space. Mixing them together made it even harder to tell these two apart.","Though such a matter was easy for Yang Ji and Yang Xu, this was not the case of others.","To break free, one had to master the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time to a certain degree. Could Lei Ao truly do it? If not, would he be eternally trapped here?","Yang Ji had never asked those questions. To him, was it not easy to escape from this space? So, he naturally had not even borne a hint of worry about these matters. In fact, he was currently regretting how small of a gift he could only give.","[If only I comprehended more... If I did, my gift would have been much better...] Yang Ji sighed a little. He felt that this paled greatly in comparison to what his Father had given him before. Those training grounds or tools his Father had given him were so much better, much more challenging. Compared to them, Yang Ji felt that this ‘small gift’ was truly lacklustre...","After all, if Yang Ji had given this to Yang Xu, she would immediately be able to resolve it.","Yang Ji thought to wait for Lei Ao to wake up. However, Yang Xu suddenly contacted him so he could only leave as well.","Naturally, before he left, he wished Lei Ao the best, “Best of luck. Let’s go on an adventure some day.”","However, even though only a few seconds had just passed, Lei Ao had already experienced several years... Yet, the only thing that he could remember before being sent to this accursed space, of boundless darkness and unending time, was that innocent smile...","...","At that moment, Yang Kai sneezed. He, an expert in the World Creation Realm, had sneezed. This was a horrendous premonition."]},{"number":6085,"title":"Chapter 6085, He Will Come To Us","paragraphs":["Chapter 6085, He Will Come To Us","Author: Silavin","“Hey, what happened?” Yang Ji immediately appeared next to Yang Xu, who was in the sky, looking straight at a figure.","This figure was in class, seemingly attentive. Though, he sat close to the window and would look at the sky and smile back. In fact, when the teacher was not looking, he would even daringly wave his hand.","It truly gave one the shivers when they realised how odd of a thing this was.","“I found him.” Yang Xu said with narrowed eyes. “He really is completely fine. He’s even smiling and waving at us. How can someone in the Qi Condensation possibly do that?”","Yang Xu then turned her eyes towards her Brother and questioned with curiosity, not showing any sign of blame. “Also, why did you use so much of my Qi just now? I even felt a little drained.”","“Oh, that. I was actually passing on some of my experience in the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time to Lei Ao. Get this, he is the Young Master of the Red Clouds Cave Heaven. I’ve given him something good to establish ties to Red Clouds Cave Heaven.” Yang Ji opened his arms wide as though he had come up with an ingenious plan. “Once he awakens, he will be so grateful to us that we might go there to play some time. I heard that Red Clouds Cave Heaven is one of the top Sects when it comes to auctions. Surely, we would be able to get some treasure map or Secret Realm key from it.”","Yang Xu, hearing this, had her eyes widened. “Ah. Then we could go on more adventures.”","“Right.” Yang Ji grinned like he had just won the lottery. “Not only that, since he is already busy learning the Daos from my experience, I’m already done for the day. Seeing that we have no class, I guess we can do whatever we want now.”","Yang Xu gave a nod, then pointed over to the figure by the window. “Then, shouldn’t we do something about him?”","Yang Ji looked towards the figure and then said, “If we want to get him, then we should do it after his class ends. It would be bad if we get others involved in this.”","Yang Xu agreed. However, at this time, the Heavenly Demon Queen spoke up, “You need take no action whatsoever. That duplicitous shameless wretch will shortly be compelled by circumstance to appear before the two of you.”","“Oh? Did you do something?” Yang Ji curiously asked. It seemed like the Heavenly Demon Queen bore quite the grudge against him for framing her previously.","“A trifling matter, truly. I have introduced subtle changes to the Grand Array mantling this domain. Changes calculated to prove so insufferable for him to rectify that confrontation becomes his only viable course. So, you need not consider facing him now. He will come to you two instead.” The Heavenly Demon Queen said as matter-of-factly.","However, this further raised the question when had she made these changes? After all, she was only away from them during that single night. That would mean she had planned all this out from the very beginning, and had executed everything in that single night.","When Yang Ji realised how amazing that was, he could not help but praise. “Wow. To think you’ve seen through him so early on.”","*Hmph* The Heavenly Demon Queen gave a snort that seemed to answer back ‘of course’. However, that seemingly small smile on her small face seems to betray the aloof front she tried to showcase.","“In that case, I guess we don’t need to do anything to him right now.” Yang Ji said as he turned to Yang Xu.","Yang Xu shrugged, “I guess that’s true. We already know that he is in Sword Class 7. We can look for him whenever. As for his name, it seems like he is called Wu Lun.”","“Wu Lun? Oh?” Yang Ji used his Divine Sense and he immediately saw the characters on Wu Lun’s Identity Plate, ‘无轮’, which was hung by his waist.","“What a strange name.” Yang Ji commented.","“Indeed. But we shouldn’t do anything to him right now. Brother, then what should we do?” Yang Xu asked, as though it was natural to seek his opinion first.","“We should head back to our rooms first and try to connect Space without the Void.” Yang Ji answered almost immediately.","Yang Xu naturally immediately agreed to it. After all, she would love nothing more than to connect her room to her Brother’s. She was so eager to get started once more that she immediately teleported them back to the dormitory.","Seeing his Sister so excited, Yang Ji could only shrug and shake his head.","Following her lead, he too headed back to this room to begin cultivating once more. However, before he started, the Heavenly Demon Queen left his body.","“Where are you going?” Yang Ji could not help but ask. However, she just gave him a curt response. “Out.”","Since Yang Ji could not think of a reason to stop her, nor did he believe she would stop because he had asked her to, he just gave a nod. Then, he asked, “In that case, can you help transport my classmates back to class after it ends?”","“For what reason should your duty devolve upon my shoulders? This is manifestly a matter of your own charge and concern. I would counsel you against the unseemly practice of shirking your responsibilities by foisting them upon others.”","“Well, for one, we got into trouble because of you, because I tried to help you. I haven’t said much of it but I’m sure my Sister is resentful of the fact. Second, do you not want us to focus on our cultivation of the True Dao of Space that you’ve mentioned? Such minor tasks just take up our time and focus. Since you are going out, why not help us out a little?” Yang Ji openly said.","Seeing that all these were true, the Heavenly Demon Queen reluctantly agreed. However, instead of openly saying anything, she just left.","Still, Yang Ji could feel her answer. Maybe it was due to the special connection they bore or maybe he had just gotten used to how she communicated. Either way, he had already gotten the answer he needed as he just put in full focus in feeling out the Dao of Space.","Unfortunately, unbeknownst to him, the Heavenly Demon Queen did more than help. After she left his room, outside, she modified the Array, isolating his room from the outside world. She did not weaken it but instead strengthened it, to the point only she or the Twins could open it.","After all, since she was going out of the way to ‘help’ him, she might as well also go all the way to make sure he focuses without any distractions.","One might get the impression that she was being vindictive, but it was more so the fact that Yang Ji would truly need time to comprehend this aspect of the Dao of Space. Though not at the level of True Dao of Space, comprehending this detail would not be a simple task. Stopping everyday to send children to and from class would just be disruptive to his progress.","So, the Heavenly Demon Queen agreed to help. More than agree, she readily sought to prepare everything so that Yang Ji would not leave his room until he fully comprehended this aspect of the Dao of Space.","Naturally, that would mean her next destination would Yang Xu’s room.","Of course, after settling matters here, she still planned on accomplishing her goal, which was to visit that little girl, Yang Ling.","...","“Okay, class has ended.” Li Wu Yi said as the students all stood up to thank him for the lesson. However, before they did, all of them got transported out of the classroom in a ruthless manner. In fact, the only thing Li Wu Yi could hear was the immediate deafening silence of the room.","“...” Seeing this sudden change and the heavy yet familiar Space Principles warping space, he could not help but sigh.","Soon, a message was directly transmitted to him from his Token... once he read it, he could not help but sigh once more...","He truly felt like he was getting too old for this, despite him still being in his prime and not having any children of his own...","He wondered if he ever got a child, would they be as unruly as those two?"]},{"number":6086,"title":"Chapter 6086, Space vs Void","paragraphs":["Chapter 6086, Space vs Void","Author: Silavin","What was Space? What was the Void?","Yang Ji sat there, cross-legged, asking these questions as he continuously tore Space apart, and waited for Space Principles to mend his destruction.","He did not focus on time, in fact, time felt illusory at this point. Even his Sister’s voice no longer rang in his ear. It might be due to his intense focus or it might be her also too focused to contact him. Regardless, it seemed like all sound was drowned out as only the tearing and mending of Space were in his eyes.","Yang Ji also tried to enter and exit those Void Cracks, using his Divine Sense to focus in on every detail, in case his eyes missed a single detail.","The first thing he noticed was that his whole entire room was completely isolated. It was not just Space itself that was isolated, but the Void as well.","If he were to travel within the Void for a distance and come out, he would always appear back in his room. Though the position might be slightly different, it does not change the fact that he could now no longer leave the room through the Void.","Naturally, he was aware that only the Heavenly Demon Queen would do this. In fact, to make it such that time could no longer be seen through the window, when he tried to gaze outside, it was pitch black.","[There must have been a reason she did this.] Yang Ji concluded, trusting the little worm that he had picked up.","Following this, he would spread out his Divine Sense into the Void while he himself would remain in the room. There, he would use his Divine Sense to pierce through the Void, while he tried to locate where the openings would appear in his room.","The process was long and tedious. Every few metres, he would pierce through the Void. He also did so in every direction. He could not understand how the distance of a metre in the Void would translate to mere nanometres in his room while sometimes translating to a metre itself . So, he continued to spread his Divine Sense through the Void at a breakneck pace, continuously piercing.","This was the mystery and abstruseness of Space. How does distance in the Void compare to the distance outside? What made this difference? Why were there weak points between the two dimensions and strong points?","Once Yang Ji started to wonder about these things, the more he felt his knowledge over the Dao of Space had been truly superficial. Certainly, he had high mastery when compared to others of this world, that no student in the academy could compare to, where teachers were on par with him and his Sister. Yet, were they not all just stepping onto the mysteries of the Dao of Space?","Right now, he felt that the difference between him and the other students was ten steps. While he and Li Wu Yi were but one step.","A single step, yet one might take more than a hundred years to cross it. That was just how profound the Dao of Space was. Yet, Yang Ji and his Sister had already crossed over more than one of such steps to reach where they were. They managed to do so in their twelve years of living no less.","Right now, Yang Ji was able to ‘see’ the further steps ahead. He was also able to ‘see’ another path. He was still unable to see its end, like the one he was on right now, but this path was certainly further than what Li Wu Yi was on. In fact, it was further than the path they, everyone of the 3,000 Worlds, was on. He could also keenly feel that this path was something his Father was about to step onto but had not yet crossed over.","Furthermore, even though he could ‘see’ that path, could not step onto it right now. After all, that path was not connected to the one he was on.","His Father might have been further ahead along their current path, but since even he had not crossed it, as the pinnacle of this world, that must mean this path was something that was not of this world.","[So, that’s the True Dao of Space...] Yang Ji could not help but comment in his heart. He was both in awe and aggrieved. Why? Because it felt like he had been on the wrong path all along. All the effort into this current path, was it not a dead end?","However, he was also in awe because this new path was something he had never seen before. Something truly incomprehensible and deep. It felt like this was the new adventure that he sought for.","He even felt that if he could move onto that path, he might even be able to surpass his Father. After all, if his Father stood at the peak of the current path, that was it, the end. If he continued onto this current path, at most he would stand by his Father’s side as an equal. He would never be able to surpass him.","When Yang Ji ‘looked’ back at the steps he could already take, he was even tempted to start over. Tempted to abandon everything he knew about the Dao of Space and start from scratch.","However, at that moment, seemingly sensing that his Dao Heart was wavering, a voice sounded in his mind.","“You will find yourself perpetually unable to traverse that divide, even were you to commence anew from the very foundation.”","Naturally, it was the Heavenly Demon Queen. Her voice sounded cold but certain.","“Then what must I do to cross this divide?” Yang Ji asked back but there was no response. It was uncertain whether it was because she could not answer or chose not to for his own benefit.","Either way, this was the first time Yang Ji had felt his Dao Heart wavering. He mocked himself, [And I thought others were easily affected. It seemed like I am no different...]","Seeing how starting from scratch would most likely do more harm than good, Yang Ji turned back to ‘look forward’. He would not just concentrate on this one task, which was to separate Space itself from the Void and link up his room to Yang Xu’s.","...","Time continued to pass.","Yang Ji did not know if a month or years had passed. But finally, he has struck onto a different point within the Void, which opened up within the same place within his room.","...","More points were uncovered in the Void that lead to the same point in his room...","Yang Ji could not help but draw a map in his mind. But that only caused him more confusion. Then, he soon realised something... [Wait... is the Void... moving?]","[How? The Void can move? When did it even start moving? How did I not realise this before?] Yang Ji fell into deep contemplation. He could clearly feel that there were points that had moved a little compared to when he had first pierced through the Void. The result was also slightly different.","It had to be noted that the difference was not much. In fact, it was barely noticeable. However, for Yang Ji, who was trying to have two points in the Void match up in his room, where even the slightest change would yield a different result, this made it obvious.","[Why had Father never told me about this before? Wait, could it be that even Father had not realised this?] Yang Ji could not help but think back on all the basics, everything his Father had taught him. There was never any mention of this. Not even his Mother, a Phoenix of the Ninth Order, who instinctively mastered the Dao of Space, had mentioned this phenomenon before.","This basically overturned everything he knew about the Void. If it could move, did it mean that the Void was a living being? If not, then how could it move? Or, was Space always moving? Drifting through the Void?","More and more questions pop up in his head, yet Yang Ji had not even found a single answer to them. Now, more than ever, he felt like he needed to study the True Dao of Space to truly understand all of this.","Still, he had proven one thing. It was that Space itself was not directly tied to the Void. The two planes exist separate from each other. In short, the Heavenly Demon Queen was not wrong. It should be possible for him to manipulate Space itself without the Void.","Once he realised this, Yang Ji got even more engrossed.","Mapping out the Void? Creating Void Cracks? He might as well live in the Void as Void Cracks appeared all around him.","Furniture? Artifacts? None of those mattered to him right now. Void Cracks would appear anywhere and everywhere. Once one closed up, he would open another one up. If furniture disappeared? Well, he would be able to find them later in the Void if they did not get torn to smithereens.","In fact, Yang Ji had never realised how slowly Void Cracks closed up. So, while he opened up Void Cracks, he even tried to close them so that he could open more up.","He did so repeatedly and tried to comprehend the difference between the Void, Space, their Principles and the Dao."]},{"number":6087,"title":"Chapter 6087, It’s Only Been A Month!","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Meanwhile, inside her room, Yang Xu was screaming at the Heavenly Demon Queen. “How long is my Brother going to be in seclusion!? It’s been a month already!!!”","“This is a matter of his own enlightenment. Comprehending such profundities within the span of a single year is worthy of considerable commendation. And yet, you presume to admonish me?” The Heavenly Demon Queen scoffed back.","During the month, someone had to settle those punishments. No need to speak much of Lei Ao, since he was still in a coma after a month. Still, his condition had naturally caused no small amount of upheaval in Yang Kai’s office. However, since Yang Ji had immediately entered secluded cultivation, no punishment had been dealt–despite mounting pressure from Red Clouds Cave Heaven.","Nevertheless, there was still the preexisting punishment. So, someone had to send their classmates to and from school. Naturally, that task fell onto Yang Xu... eventually.","After all, this was a punishment for the Twins. Even if the Heavenly Demon Queen covered up for them, would Li Wu Yi not realise it? So, eventually, Yang Xu would have cover for the both of them.","...","During that month, Yang Xu had a scare when she suddenly felt that her Brother’s Dao Heart was wavering. It could be said that her Daos were his Daos, and his Daos were her Daos. Though not fully mutual, with their inexplicit connection, she could feel that her Brother was about to abandon his mastery over the Dao of Space.","Naturally, she would panic. She wanted to hurriedly rush over and scream at him. In fact, she was about to scream into his head through their connection. However, the Heavenly Demon Queen stopped her. “Desist. Do you intend to nullify the entirety of his endeavors? Your disturbance serves only to divert him ever furthering his goals. You pledged, with your word, using your Dao Heart as a wager, that he would remain unperturbed throughout this time.”","“You said that he would be fine, that this was going to take awhile. But it has already been a few days and his Dao Heart has already started to shake! What if it collapses!?” Yang Xu was more than ready to push this worm into the Void and forever seal her at this point.","“You declared your faith in him. Where, I ask, has that conviction gone?” The Heavenly Demon Queen mocked.","However, Yang Xu was having none of this. She raised her hand, ready to grab at the Heavenly Demon Queen. Though she knew she would fail, she really just needed a punching bag to unleash all her anger.","Then suddenly, “Eh?”","“His Dao Heart has stabilized?” Yang Xu’s eyes turned wide as she could feel that not only was his Dao Heart stable, but their mastery over the Dao of Space had been slightly strengthened.","“What happened?” Yang Xu wondered and the Heavenly Demon Queen explained, a rare occurrence. However, maybe because she felt it would be troublesome if Yang Xu continued to pressure her to explain. “Your brother has passed beyond the first threshold. Though it stands as merely one of many such trials, he has nonetheless crossed the first one.”","“Wait. Then, this is going to happen again!?”","“Such an occurrence may yet transpire again, but it ought not befall him during his period of seclusion.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated and reenphased, “As for you, you would do well to honor your word, lest you inflict harm upon him rather than render him aid.”","...","Then, more weeks had passed and a month had gone by, whereby their punishment for being ‘travelling coaches’ ceased.","That was when Yang Xu pressured the Heavenly Demon Queen once more. She truly regretted ever promising to not contact her Brother. This past month has been hard on her–truly hard. It had to be noted that since birth, the Twins had never been apart. Certainly, in terms of physical space, they have been separated. However, their Souls had never been separated like this, where one could not contact the other.","To Yang Xu, this whole month has been uncomfortable. She could never fathom how others manage to deal with the loneliness of the world, where there was no one behind their backs at all times. Where was the tree they leaned on?","This feeling was not like losing a powerful Father or unparalleled Master. It was as though a part of her had been lost. If Yang Xu were to put it into words, it would be more severe than losing one’s other half.","That was just how deep their connection was, and how difficult it was to separate themselves.","She even felt blessed that she had this connection with her Brother. She felt blessed that throughout all her life, he had always been there for her.","She wanted to immediately speak to him, to immediately hear his voice and feel his warmth. It need not be physical, just establishing the same connection she once had with him was enough, where she could speak and share with him anything, at any time.","However, the Heavenly Demon Queen was conniving. After all, with her years of experience, how could she not know that maintaining such a distance between two parties, who had been instinctively linked since birth, would not cause some kind of backlash?","So, she had found a way to convince Yang Xu to make an oath upon her Dao Heart, swearing to Heaven that she would refrain from contacting Yang Ji during this time.","Still, it should be said that their connection was not all lost. Though they were barred from communicating during this period, their cultivation was still linked, since Yang Xu could still help him cultivate when she had the time. So, whenever Yang Ji makes a minor breakthrough in gaining some form of enlightenment, Yang Xu would immediately be able to sense it.","Unfortunately, whether this was beneficial for her or not could be argued. After all, each time she felt a change in her cultivation, she would flare up and ask the Heavenly Demon Queen when her Brother would come out.","It did not help that her other Family members would also ask her if Yang Ji was doing okay, since he had never entered seclusion for this long before. This was odd since Yang Hao would enter seclusion for a month or two on occasion and they were not that concerned.","Su Yan was especially concerned, to the point she would come to Yang Xu each day to ask about Yang Ji’s progress.","As for why they could not just break the Isolation Array and check themselves? It was because the Heavenly Demon Queen had warned them against it, that it would ruin all his efforts and even affect his insights into the Dao of Space. Also, she had specifically made it such that spying on Yang Ji would cause a backlash against him.","Why she had done so, no one but her knows. This only serves to make her relationship with the Yang Family more hostile, but the Heavenly Demon Queen did not care. It seemed like she had a greater plan in mind, and did not wish for any disruptors.","Nevertheless, it was odd how she could view the inside of the room, but she did not allow others to view it, not even Yang Xu. She was also the only one who could communicate with Yang Ji during this time, and even she kept minimal contact unless necessary.","Naturally, due to this, the Heavenly Demon Queen would be bombarded with questions regarding his status. She might be able to hide from his other Family members inside of Yang Xu, but how could she possibly hide from Yang Xu herself?","If the Heavenly Demon Queen had to say who was the bane of her life, this little girl would certainly be the first. Even her greatest enemy was not as annoying as her. She lost count of how many times this girl had asked her when Yang Ji would come out.","She forgot how many times she would have to say that he was still busy comprehending the Dao of Space, that he still needed more time!","She could not even fathom why everyone else was starting to be concerned when Yang Ji had been inside his room for only a week! It was only a week! People would spend decades, centuries, some even millennia to comprehend the Dao. Yet, these people were fussing over a boy doing it for just a week!? This was so absurd she wanted to scream!","Even worse, these people were all cultivators! They have experienced how it was like to comprehend a single Dao. Yet, here they were, concerned about a young boy who had only been in seclusion for a week?","Still, thankfully, all these questions and answers would cease today.","Yang Xu keenly felt something stirring inside her. Soon, her eyes flashed and she immediately waved her hand, tearing through Space. However, this tear was not a Void Crack. It did not have the usual murky dark and mysterious space inside. Rather, It was clear as though a window had been placed in front of her. It clearly showed her the exit.","It was a perfect passway to the outside, to the platform. If the other students were to see this, they would certainly be astonished at the sigh of it, and the sight of Yang Xu’s gaping mouth.","However, she was not the only one shocked. There was another party that was too shocked for words, and this person now had a true look of frustration on her face, as though she had eaten a turd many times over.","Naturally, this person was none other than the Heavenly Demon Queen."]},{"number":6088,"title":"Chapter 6088, Reporting to Yang Kai","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","When Yang Xu saw this portal, her eyes opened wide in disbelief. This was the first time she was seeing a tear in Space portraying its exit so vividly.","She took her first step through it and appeared directly outside, on the platform in the centre of their dorm. She even looked back to see that the portal was still there, and was not closing. It was as though this was just part of Space now. It was no longer a tear but an actual entrance, like a built door. Thus, there was no damage to Space and there was no need for any repairs.","In fact, when she moved through it, she could clearly feel that she did not even move through the Void. This portal was completely dissociated to the Void.","[Brother... you really did it...] Yang Xu praised in her heart and turned towards the room on the opposite side. Then, unexpectedly, an answer came. It was not from her Brother’s room but from the portal itself.","“Long time no see.” It was a familiar voice, one which she had missed for an entire month. One which she could never forget even if this was another life. Yang Xu turned to look through the portal and saw Yang Ji, in another portal connected to her room, having an exhausted smile...","For some reason, tears started to well up in her eyes as she dashed through the two portals like a bolt of lightning.","Seeing this, Yang Ji immediately opened his arms up and sighed. He even used his new mastery over the Dao of Space to harden the Space behind him as the collision came.","*Bang!* Though a hug, it might as well be classified as an attack. Yang Xu certainly did not hold back as she used all her strength to rush up to her Brother. Yang Ji believes that if he did not prepare for impact, she might actually send him through the wall.","Still, with her Brother now in her arms, Yang Xu wrapped around him like no tomorrow as she unrestrainedly cried on his shoulder, mucus even coming out.","“Sheesh. You are making my clothes dirty.” Yang Ji complained but Yang Xu just shook her head, not letting go.","“She has besieged me ceaselessly during your absence from one another. Ensure that you compensate her for the entirety of that time apart.” The Heavenly Demon Queen spoke in her head and quickly ignored the both of them, as though this was no longer her problem, and that seeing these two were a pain in the eyes.","Since even the ever quiet Heavenly Demon Queen had spoken up, Yang Ji could only relent.","...","After a few hours. In fact, when the sun was about to set, Yang Xu had finally let go. Her Brother had basically turned into a wooden statue, not moving and letting her do as she pleased. He just focused on cultivating while passing the time.","Once she let go, Yang Ji finally opened his eyes and exclaimed, “Got that out of your system?”","Yang Xu however, defiantly shook her head. Giving a *hmph!*.","Still, being Siblings, Yang Ji just shrugged and grabbed her hand. Then, they teleported out of the room and up into the sky.","When Yang Xu looked down, she saw that the portal into her room was closed. This was most likely done by her Brother, who must have realised that her room would be unprotected if it had been left open. Not to mention, their classmates were heading back from school around this time...","“First, we would need to report to Mother, then tell Father.” Yang Ji said.","“Tell Father about what?” Though it was not strange for them to report to their Mother, Su Yan, after they were done with their secluded cultivation, it felt odd needing to report to their Father. After all, Yang Kai was typically away or busy most of the time.","“You forgot to reconnect to me...” Yang Ji sighed and reminded her. [Honestly, for those few hours, you’ve been hugging me non-stop but you actually forgot to reconnect our thoughts and memories.]","“Oh...” Yang Xu, a little embarrassed that her emotional outburst had caused her to forget something so important, quickly did as she was told.","She had temporarily forgotten that the connection between the two of them could be closed by either side at will. However, it had to also be opened by the side that closed it. This was how Yang Xu and Yang Ji could keep some semblance of privacy. Though, truth be told, Yang Ji hardly bothered closing his connection to Yang Xu while Yang Xu did it often, especially during the ‘female council gathering’...","Soon, Yang Ji’s memories flooded Yang Xu’s mind and even she furrowed her brows, “Brother... isn’t this...”","Yang Ji gave a nod with a sad sigh. “To think that everything we’ve done so far has been limited and wrong...”","“But, from your experience, Father must have known about this, no?” Yang Xu said.","“I believe so. Father once mentioned about the Taboo Realm... I think that place might have something to do with this.” Yang Ji said as he looked into the distance. Now, he truly felt that the world was so vast and he was so small. He was no different to a frog in a well.","“In that case, we should first report to Father. Actually... there is another problem that I failed to mention...” Yang Xu scratched her face in awkwardness. She tend send her memories over to Yang Ji, which causes him to frown.","“Wait. Lei Ao still isn’t awake? How is that possible? And then, because of me, Red Clouds Cave Heaven has been complaining to Father, souring our relationship?” Yang Ji mourned. His two birds in one stone plan had fallen through. Worse, he might really receive punishment for this...","“Brother, him not being able to free himself is something Mother Ji Yao would describe as his lack of ability. You’ve bestowed upon him such a great opportunity but he had been too inept to accept it. That is not your fault, and I don’t think Father and Red Clouds Cave Heaven can really fault you for that.” Yang Xu said, trying to say that he had not done anything wrong.","“Regardless, it is my fault that I failed to assess how long it would take him to break free. Okay, let’s talk to Father first.” Yang Ji said as they teleported once more, this time into the Principal’s office.","...","At this time, Yang Kai had his hand on his forehead and he paced around to think of a solution. Beside him was Su Yan, who was advising him.","Then, the two suddenly felt Space Principles fluctuate and turn their attention to the corner of the room. Soon, two familiar figures appeared.","Su Yan, who was not bothered by the problem in the slightest, bloomed into a smile as it seemed like all worries in her heart had been lifted. As for Yang Kai, he sighed in relief. However, soon, his eyes narrowed as he was about to open his mouth, but soon shut close because Su Yan gave him a sharp look.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu soon entered this seemingly tense atmosphere with wide eyes.","Yang Xu, the ever cunning girl, quickly ran to their Mother, “Mom!”","She opened her arms wide, as though she was the most precious little thing in the world, seeking for her Mother’s ever loving embrace. As for Yang Ji, he was a little late in acting in a similar fashion, and was mostly prompted to do so by his Sister.","Through their Divine Sense, “Brother, please let Mom handle this. It is a blessing that she is inside the room.”","“Yeah, but we are already twelve, you know? Aren’t you a little embarrassed to do this same tactic?” Yang Ji asked back. At this point, it was strange for him to say this while burying his face in Su Yan’s arm, hugging both his Sister and Su Yan in a big embrace.","“If Yang Ai can do it, why can’t we?” Yang Xu shot back.","“She’s only six...” Yang Ji lamented.","Seeming those two cunning devils tactically go to his Wife first, the corner of Yang Kai’s lip twitched. [Cunning! Too cunning! Where did these two learn this from!?]","Still, Yang Kai had to play his role as the Father here and hold his foot down. ”Yang Ji, do you know what you did wrong?”","However, before Yang Ji answered, it was Su Yan who said, “Husband, like I said before, our Son did nothing wrong. He gave the boy an opportunity and that’s it. There is no need to agree with what Red Clouds Cave Heaven is requesting of him.”","“*Haa...* This won’t do. He passed on not just his insights in the Dao of Space but the Dao of Time as well. Even if he is still just a child, he needs to properly see this through to the end. Red Clouds Cave Heaven would fully recognise him, all 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises would as well.” Yang Kai said, expressing his frustration.","When Yang Ji heard this, he felt something was off. [Wait. Is this so serious that the 36 Cave Heavens and 72 Paradises are going to punish me for this?]","Even Yang Xu, who heard what Yang Kai had said, started to get nervous.","“Then, let’s wait for Lei Ao to wake up first before making such a massive decision.” Su Yan added.","[Wait, massive decision for what!?] Yang Ji could already feel his back turn cold with sweat.","“If we could, I would prefer that as well. But, his Father and Mother have already declared that Yang Ji will be Lei Ao Master going forth, and that Yang Ji will have the same status as them...” Yang Kai said with a sigh.","[Huh?] At this point, Yang Ji and Yang Xu had their mouths open, They were confused.","[How did things turn out like this?]"]},{"number":6089,"title":"Chapter 6089, Might As Well Put Everyone Into A Coma","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","“Father, you can’t be serious. I’m about the same age as Lei Ao. All I did was pass him some of my insights into the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time. I didn’t really do much else. Why am I now considered to be his Master? That just doesn’t make sense.” Yang Ji expressed his doubts.","“Yeah, that doesn’t make any sense. Aunt Hu Mei’er and Aunt Hu Jiao’er also shared some of their insights as Twins with us. You, Aunt Yang Xue and Uncle Yang Xiao also taught us about the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time. Yet, we do not have a Master-Disciple relationship with anyone.” Yang Xu added.","Yang Kai gave a heavy sigh. Their past actions had come back to bite them. In a way, they had distorted their children’s view of what was normal.","Even within a Sect, sharing one’s insight with someone else would make the former a Half-Master. Typically, if one did not already have a Master, the person sharing their insight would directly take the latter as their Personal Disciple.","This should not be confused with insights widely shared around. If an insight was shared to the public, that would just be the share of knowledge from a Senior to Junior. Furthermore, such insights would not contain the truly deep understanding of the Master.","Naturally, as Yang Xu had said, typically, Hu Mei’er and Hu Jiao’er would have been considered the Twins’ Masters. After all, they shared insights to their peculiar bond and shared cultivation. Furthermore, they were within the same Sect, High Heaven Palace, and held the same position as Qiu Yi Meng, all being Elders. Thus, no one would deny their position as the Twins’ Masters.","However, the two Sisters were the ones who turned down Yang Kai’s offer to have them become the Twins’ Masters. According to them, they felt that they would not be able to teach the Twins much, and were unconfident about being their Masters. Gaining that position would just be taking advantage of the Twins’ talent and status, as Young Master and Young Mistress of High Heaven Palace.","In fact, Yang Xiao and Yang Xue had all tried to teach the Twins. However, they too felt inadequate to be their Master. If even those two felt inadequate, then who else in the world could take them in? Yang Kai might be able to but he was already their Father. He need not be recognised to be their Master, which was technically a lower position (in Chinese culture).","Due to this incident, and since the Twins were the Eldest amongst the Children, no one in High Heaven Palace sought to take them in as Disciples. With them basically being contained within High Heaven Palace’s Starry Sky Palace, Yang Hao and the rest still did not have their own Masters. Instead, they took in insights shared to them by their Father, who basically mastered all 3,000 Daos.","Naturally, for Yang Kai’s children, it was inevitable that such blatant ‘pampering’ had caused them to have some misunderstandings.","It should be said that if Yang Ji had merely shared some surface insight, this whole conundrum would not have occurred.","The issue was, Yang Ji had shared insight of both the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time simultaneously. Both Daos were obscure and it was hard to even catch a glimpse of understanding from either. Understanding of such Daos was so rare that Red Clouds Cave Heaven had even sent their Young Master to High Heaven Academy just to receive teachings from other experts in this field.","Even so, experts who had explored both fields were insanely rare. Even Yang Kai’s three Disciples only took on one Dao. How many in the world had actually stepped their toes into two of such obscure Daos?","Worse yet, Yang Ji had imparted his insight into balancing the two Daos, utilising them simultaneously.","Even if Yang Kai were to claim that what they shared was nothing significant, would Red Clouds Cave Heaven accept it?","Besides, the Cave Heaven Master of Red Clouds Cave Heaven had other goals when he personally came down with his Wife to meet Yang Kai.","Red Clouds Cave Heaven was well known to run Auction Houses across the 3,000 Worlds. In short, their very nature was that of mercantilism. To them, any trade must be a fair one, especially when dealing with the apex High Heaven Palace. So, having his Son being granted such an opportunity, the Cave Heaven Master felt the need to repay Yang Ji in some way.","Though, that might just be all smoke and mirrors. After all, old-foxes like these were sure to scheme. It had been easy to tell that the Red Clouds Cave Heaven Master took this opportunity to push for the Master-Disciple status, to tie Red Clouds Cave Heaven to the ascendant High Heaven Palace.","That man did not even say anything about his Son being in a coma. He also had no qualms in putting his Son under Yang Ji, no qualms about being of the same status as Yang Ji, since one would be the Father and the other would be the Master of Lei Ao.","When Yang Kai first heard of how Yang Ji was now Lei Ao’s Master, the corner of his lip could not help but twitch. He even internally cursed at how this old-fox was so shameless.","Worse yet, Yang Kai could not do much to refute. After all, due to the usual convention of the world, others would indeed see Yang Ji and Lei Ao’s Master after this. Other Cave Heaven and Paradises would also not stand by his side in this.","Why? Because this presented an opportunity to tie themselves to one of Yang Kai’s children!","Be it if they shared their insight to them, or the children shared their insight to someone within their Sect, was this not another avenue they could exploit?","When Yang Kai explained all of this to the Twins, he could not help but press his temple once Yang Ji answered.","“But Father, all I gave is really just superficial insights. It is nothing major. At his level, Sister and I would just need a day to break free. I’ve even taken into consideration he was on Yang Hao’s level when sharing my insights.” Yang Ji stated in indignation, as though the world had been the one in the wrong for accusing him.","However, Yang Kai explained, “*Haa...* How many times must I say this, you cannot use you and your Sibilins as benchmarks. You two might take a day but Lei Ao still hasn’t woken up even after a month has passed. I estimate he won’t be able to wake up for another year... and the more time he takes to break free, the more inclined the others will view you as his Master.”","“Then, I can just wake him up.” Yang Ji said coldly, like it did not matter if his plan was ruined. After all, better to avoid the awkwardness of having a Disciple the same age as him then be provided with some fun adventure.","“My boy, this is an opportunity for him. Are you really going to take it away? I can speak for the rest of your Mothers, that we will stand by you if you do not wish to take him in as your Disciple. But, as Mothers, we do not wish to see you destroy another child’s opportunity just because of a whim. That would be far too cruel.” Su Yan suddenly gently spoke.","What she did not say was that sudden disruptions one while in the state of enlightenment might cause a tragic backlash, and Lei Ao might even get crippled. If that happened, her Son would bear the burden of crippling an innocent young child. This was not something any Mother would want.","“Husband, matters of Master and Disciple relations cannot be taken lightly. We cannot allow our Son to be used in such a manner.” Su Yan stated. However, it just made Yang Kai sigh.","“I naturally agree with you. But, what else can we do?” Yang Kai said,","It was then that Yang Ji came up with a brilliant idea. “Father, why don’t I just share the same insights to everyone? You said that insights shared to the public would be recognised as nothing special, right?”","Yang Kai immediately shook his head. Even Su Yan paled a little at the thought. After all, what Yang Ji was proposing he was willing to do was to force more children into a coma!","Then, Yang Xu added, supporting her Brother. “Yeah. Mom said that this is an opportunity to Lei Ao. Why don’t we give this opportunity to everyone? If everyone receives this insight, then it would no longer be anything special. Then, no one can pressure my Brother to take in a Disciple.”","Yang Kai looked at Su Yan, and Su Yan looked back at him. What the children said did indeed make sense. This would certainly solve the problem. However, the price would be as the Principal, Yang Kai would be allowing who knows how many children to suddenly be bedridden for who knows how long...","At this point, the silence in the room was suffocating. Su Yan seemed to have made a decision and suddenly gave a nod, “Why not? Husband, you’ve already shared some of your insights into the different Daos with the Arrays setup inside each student’s room. Yes, our boy has shared far more than what you have in the two Daos, but why not think of it as an advanced class or a special class? It can even be an elective. If we make this the norm, then no one would say anything.”","Su Yan looked at her two precious babies, “We did tell our children to teach Lei Ao. We can say Lei Ao wanted to learn from them as well, so he has received this ‘elective class’. When he wakes up, I’m sure he too would not want his Master to be of the same age as him. So, I’m sure he would play along.”","Yang Ji quickly gave a nod and excitedly added, “Father, you can also tell Red Clouds Cave Heaven that Lei Ao is our good friend. That’s why we let him take this advanced class first. Tell them that I wish to go to their Auction Houses one day. That way, we would still have a connection between High Heaven Palace and Red Clouds Cave Heaven.”","Yang Xu also added, “En. I will also help!”","Yang Kai looked at the three and sighed. He did expect that being a Principle would be hard work, but to think his own children would be the cause of most of the stress.","Unfortunately, though this was a great plan, he still had to consult with the teachers. After all, this was stepping into their domain. There were also teachers like Li Wu Yi, who became a teacher because he was looking for a Disciple. Passing on deep insights like this would be detrimental to his plan. So, Yang Kai had to tread carefully here.","“Okay. I will think about it. For now, you two should just return back to your room.” Yang Kai said.","However, that was when Yang Ji spoke up. “Wait. Father, I need to ask you something.”"]},{"number":6090,"title":"Chapter 6090, Questions Left Unanswered","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Yang Kai looked at Yang Ji and saw something deep in his eyes. He immediately understood that this had to do with what he had uncovered during his secluded cultivation. “What is it?”","“Father, have you been aware this whole time that we were all cultivating an incomplete path? That our Daos would cease from here?” Yang Ji said with a voice that contained both frustration and disappointment.","However, to his surprise, Yang Kai readily admitted. He did not even need to pause. In fact, such a straightforward admission made Yang Ji even more vexed. “Yes.”","“Why?”","“Why have I said nothing so far? What difference would it make?” Yang Kai said with a sigh. He truly did not expect one of his children to reach this stage. After all, even his Wives had not uncovered this truth. They only found out because Yang Kai had told them.","Despite those seemingly cold hard facing words, Yang Ji took in a deep breath and gave a nod. “Is there really no other way? Will we continue to be misled?”","At this point, Yang Kai resolutely stated, “No. We are trying to find ways to overcome this as well. That’s why–”","Su Yan raised her hand and interjected, “Ji’er, Xu’er, this matter cannot be carelessly spread. Before we continue to speak, please swear that you will never speak of this matter to others.”","“But Mom. Shouldn’t we let everyone know? That what we are pursuing is a dead end?” Yang Ji quickly said.","“Absolutely not. There is no point in causing such mayhem in this world. Why shake the Dao Hearts of others when they might never even reach the stage to receive your realisation. My babies, please promise your Mother that you will never speak of this to anyone else who is unaware of the truth. If you can’t, then your Father and I will stop speaking of this matter with you” Su Yan declared.","It was extremely rare for their Mother to be so stern. The Twins looked at each other and swore.","““I swear.””","Su Yan gave Yang Kai a glance and he immediately continued. “Then, let me explain...”","Yang Kai started off describing how he had come to this realization. However, it was due to him hitting a seemingly insurmountable wall in the Dao of Space. This wall seemed to be ever-present in every single Dao he had mastered. All 3,000 Daos, yet, all of them have the same wall?","One might think that he had simply reached the peak, that his cultivation simply had no room left to grow. However, Yang Kai did not believe that to be the case. He did not doubt it for even a single second. After all, he had met beings of other worlds besides the 3,000 Worlds. They wielded different Principles. It could be assumed that the Daos they strived towards was different as well.","However, the differences were like variants. They were not wholly different. The rudimentary Daos like the Sword Dao and Spear Dao seem to exist in both worlds, but were different at the same time. This only became more obvious after he clashed with such beings in the Taboo Realm.","This was the secondary reason why he sought to explore other worlds, far away from the 3,000 Worlds. If there was something the Taboo Realm taught him, it was that there was so much he did not know. He, like those trapped there, were like frogs in a well.","Certainly, saving his friend Chong Jiu was important. But, the different worlds, with their different cultivation systems and different Daos definitely need to be studied. After all, it was clear that everything they had cultivated towards was a dead-end, and even the Open Heaven Realm method was flawed. The only option was to seek out the unknown for answers.","However, this matter had become quite sensitive.","Such matters could only be felt or realised by experts who had reached the pinnacle in their respective Daos. If they found out that to further their pursuit they needed to leave the 3,000 Worlds, what would happen?","Obviously, for beings who dedicated their life to their respective Daos, they would run despite their exhaustion. They would stop at nothing and continuously shrive towards their goal. After all, to get to where they were, every single one of them must have been driven and adamant.","Unfortunately, Yang Kai could not possibly allow them to leave the 3,000 Worlds unguarded. If all such experts rushed out, who could protect their 3,000 Worlds if trouble were to come?","These people did not have any clue of the destination nor the route, yet they would be more than willing to be like flies towards the flame, as long as there was said ‘opportunity’ beyond some unknown horizon.","The 3,000 Worlds could not take such risks at this time. They still had to recover from the war, and they still needed people here to guide the future generation.","Of course, some would describe Yang Kai’s actions as being too heavy handed and wary. However, Yang Kai could clearly feel that there was some unknown Force at play behind the scenes. A Force that Yang Kai was wary of, who was already in the World Creation Realm. After all, could he really create a situation whereby Little Eleven could not speak of certain matters? Could he truly gather those experts from the various worlds, without them being able to resist, and create the Taboo Realm? Were these truly made from nature? Even with his current strength, Yang Kai was not omnipotent to that degree.","So, for the sake of the 3,000 Worlds, they decided to keep this matter a secret. It would only be known amongst a few. His Wives were naturally one of those few, including Shi, Yang Xiao and Yang Xue. As for others outside of High Heaven Palace, there were few but they were people Yang Kai trusted greatly.","Since Yang Ji and Yang Xu had stumbled upon this secret themselves, and expressed their doubts, Yang Kai felt like there was no need for them to hide the truth from them. Thus, he openly stated it. In fact, he had predicted this day would eventually come. It was just, not so soon...","Yang Ji gave a nod and he asked the Heavenly Demon Queen with his Divine Sense, “Is what my Father said true? That there is an enemy that strong.”","This time, the Heavenly Demon Queen actually readily admitted, “Certainly, one that lies beyond the realm of your conception.”","“Do we have a chance against them?” Yang Ji asked with his heart starting to race.","“No.”","That one short answer made Yang Ji’s and Yang Xu’s hearts drop. If even their Father could not stand up to such a being, then who could?","However, the Heavenly Demon Queen then continued, “It is impossible while you remain confined to this realm.”","“Wait. So, if Father leaves, then we have a chance!” With hope, Yang Xu immediately exclaimed. However, the Heavenly Demon Queen did not respond, which just vexed them even more.","“Argh! Why do you stop answering whenever we need real answers!?” Yang Xu wished she could strangle this worm.","“Sister, it’s fine. I believe she is under some kind of restriction like Uncle Eleven...” Yang Ji tried to calm her down.","*Heh* Then a snicker came, which only infuriated Yang Xu even more.","“Brother, don’t you see that she is not answering on purpose!!” Yang Xu chided but Yang Ji just shook his head. “If she doesn’t want to answer, we can’t really force her to. Besides, our fates are essentially tied. She also holds no malice towards us.”","...","This conversation naturally happened within an instant, and was not perceptible by Yang Kai and Su Yan. Thus, Yang Ji had to relay what the Heavenly Demon Queen stated to his parents.","Yang Kai gave a nod and looked at Su Yan. He did not even bother demanding to see the Heavenly Demon Queen. It seemed like he knew she would refuse to see him for who knows what reason. “That was helpful. For now, I need to discuss matters with your Mother.”","Yang Xu quickly cupped her fists and bow, rushing Yang Ji along as well. She even rushed out of the place by teleporting with her Brother. Naturally, not rushed to the point it seemed suspicious though.","“What’s the rush? We rarely get to see Father. I still have a few thingsI wish to ask him.” Yang Ji said.","Yang Xu quickly answered, “Now that Father and Mother are too focused on this matter, this is the best time.”","It did not even take Yang Ji a second to realise what ‘best time’ meant. “Are you serious? We can just wait for them to allow us before doing it.”","“I trust our Mothers will support it. Also, they did say that this is an opportunity.”","Yang Ji could not believe what he was hearing. “Why are you acting like this? You normally try to avoid punishments.”","Certainly, Yang Ji was typically the one who would take the initiative, while Yang Xu would follow along. It was truly rare for her to be the one taking the initiative now, especially when they knew they would most likely get into trouble if they did this.","“Well...” Yang Xu hesitated to say.","“Hmm...” Such a response naturally drew more attention.","Unable to hide it, Yang Xu just plainly admitted. “Okay, okay. Mother Yu Ru Meng told me to do it. While you were busy cultivating, I already found out about Red Clouds Cave Heaven. The Cave Heaven Master did not even bother hiding his aura when he came here. He was basically announcing his presence. I could naturally sense it and had to ask out Mothers why someone was being so pompous. That was how I came to find out about the matter.”","“When talking to our Mothers, Mother Yu Ru Meng already told me what might happen and the plan going forward. It’s just, I could not act on it since you were busy cultivating. That time, when you shared your insight, you needed to draw Qi from me. I could not possibly do that while you were in secluded cultivation. So, I needed to wait till you got out.”","“Sorry that I kept this from you.”","Clearly, she had not sent her full memory directly to Yang Ji the first time. She even took the effort to explain how events had played out. This certainly drew Yang Ji’s attention, but he did not say anything since he would like to respect his Sister’s privacy whenever possible.","“Wait, then at the time, you were shocked about?” Yang Ji recalled what happened in that room, when their mouths were both wide open at the news.","“I was shocked that the other party acted so quickly. It’s only been around a week since they found out, you know? To have the entire Cave Heaven accept that you are going to be on par with their Elders, isn’t that ridiculous?” Yang Xu explained.","Yang Ji gave a nod, then asked, “Then, why did you feel the need to hide the plan from me?”","“Well...” Yang Xu could not say that she did not want to expose how she and the Mothers would have their ‘girls’ meetings’ from time to time. Furthermore, she did not want to say that one of their Mothers was teaching her to do ‘things’.","“A man of integrity does not intrude upon a maiden’s confidences.” That was when the Heavenly Demon Queen interjected and quickly sent a private Divine Sense message to Yang Xu, “You owe me one.”","“Fine, fine. I’ll not ask any further. If this is something that Mother Yu Ru Meng has asked us to do, then we might as well get this over with. If our Mothers are the ones holding up Heaven, then I guess even if we have every student fall into a deep coma, it would be fine.” Yang Ji rolled his eyes at this odd team up."]},{"number":6091,"title":"Chapter 6091, ‘Opportunity’ For Everyone!","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Seeing as to how her Brother has already agreed to it, Yang Xu struck while the iron was hot. She immediately took out a scroll from her Space Ring. When she unfurrowed it, there was a list of names written down, including their class, what Dao and who should pass their insights.","Yang Ji looked at it and marvelled. [Mothers, you all really work fast...]","From what Yang Xu had suggested, this meant that the Mothers had started to take action within a week or so. To come up with such a list, didn’t they have to check all the students prior, or with all their teachers?","There were even names that highlighted who they should not touch. Though Yang Ji did not know why that was, that was not the most important point.","The most important point was that they were to pass their insights onto children that were not even proficient in the Dao of Space or the Dao of Time... Naturally, these insights were not of the two Daos. Instead, they were about the more common Spear Dao, Sword Dao, Dao of Spirit Arrays and Alchemic Dao...","This only made Yang Ji confused. They were not that proficient in those other Daos. If they were to describe their mastery of Daos in levels, their mastery of the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time could be said to reach level nine, while the others were just at two or three...","From Yang Ji’s point of view, such mastery was lacklustre. It was a little embarrassing to teach someone else when he himself felt like he had not mastered much of those Daos. After all, even against a Territory Lord, they did not even use a weapon. For Pills, they had their Mother Xia Ning Chang providing so much... no, too much... concocting their own Pills would be just for fun. Something they could do with their Younger Siblings. As for Spirit Arrays, they definitely understood a thing or two, since their Uncle Eleven had been exploring this field and they hung out with him. However, what they knew was truly just shallow knowledge.","What Yang Ji failed to realise was that those the Twins were dealing with were just beginners, not just in cultivation but in life as well. All were less than sixteen of age, how much do they comprehend? For those extraordinary geniuses, which one of them did not have the backing to make it to such heights? And, how many of them would be enrolled in High Heaven Academy?","This was only the first year of the school. No, it could be said to only be the first month. There was hardly any reputation to it except for the fame of High Heaven Palace and Yang Kai. Even so, would those truly powerful and ancient Sects with profound heritages actually care to send their most stunning prodigies to the academy? They had the resources for that. It was only in cases like Lei Ao, where he pursued a Dao different from what Red Clouds Cave Heaven experienced in that they sought to send them to High Heaven Academy. If not, maybe they would send their secondary prodigies, who could serve to establish connections to High Heaven Palace.","Therefore, for most children here, they had not even reached level one. Even if the gap was only a level in terms of mastery of a Dao, that would still be a precious opportunity that could save them years if not decades of hard work.","Yang Ji looked through the list in amazement. There were more than two hundred names written inside. It was a strange sensation that the Daos he was most proficient in would be the least he needed to impart, but that could not be helped since there was a limited number of students who were talented in either of those Daos.","“Okay, so our Mothers has already planned it all out. So, which class should we go for first?” Yang Ji asked.","“Mother Shan Qing Luo said that we should do as much as possible in a single night.” Yang Xu explained.","“Ah... in that case, we can’t do our class. There are only eleven students on this list and doing one would be exhausting.” Yang Ji said while recalling how that one instance with Lei Ao required him to tap into Yang Xu’s Qi reserves. “We should also do it at night. Mother doesn’t want us to get noticed, right?”","“No, they said we need to do it while Father is busy. So, we will be doing it immediately.” Yang Xu said and she looked down.","Out in the school, there were countless students walking about minding their own business. After class, most cultivators had free time to practice.","“Wait... you are telling me we are going to look for them in board daylight? Wouldn’t it be easier once they are back at their dorms, where we can tell who they are from the sign outside their room.” Yang Ji felt exasperated. This whole thing seemed so rushed.","“We can use our Divine Sense to check their Identity Plates while everyone is moving. Our Mothers also said that the teachers will not interfere with this.” Yang Xu said and pointed to a student in the distance.","Technically, from the sky, she was pointing at a building but due to her sharing her senses to Yang Ji, he immediately ‘saw’ who she was pointing to.","“Okay, okay. I get it.” Yang Ji relented. “I’ll go back to my room first. Since you have the list on you, you can just throw them to me. Once I’m done, we’ll switch.”","“En. I’ll help you send them to the Recovery Hall as well.” Yang Xu said with a smile, that seemed normal to Yang Ji but would look truly odd if a third party saw it.","...","This day was one to be remembered in the annals of history. On this day, students disappeared in droves and without a sound. It was as though they had been spirited away.","From one moment, clamours and laughter to silence and fear. One might be enjoying a conversation in one moment to find that no response came back. Some doubted their eyes, wondering where their friend had gone. They were here just seconds ago, yet their whole presence had disappeared.","Such occurrences happened one after another, without stopping.","Those students who were sharp enough naturally noticed something was amiss. However, they might be the very same people ‘spirited away’ next.","As for the teachers?","Did none of them not notice?","Of course they did. They naturally knew what was happening. How else did that list come about? Surely, the High Heaven Palace Mistresses did not personally move to inspect all children to select these two hundred or so. The teachers had to have some hand in it.","The only person who could potentially claim ignorance was the Principal, but could he truly say he had not guessed this would happen? After all, he had been married to those women for years.","As for why no one had strongly opposed this, besides the overwhelming influence of the Wives, it was because this was an ‘opportunity’ for these children. Those selected for the less illusive Daos need not worry as much since the Twins did not have extremely high attainment in those fields. It was only those targeted for the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time that they needed to pay extra attention to.","Still, it was a little unnerving as Li Wu Yi watched student after student suddenly disappear in his Divine Sense, and suddenly appear in the Recovery Hall.","“Elder, are you sure this will be fine?” Xu Yi, at the side, asked.","Li Wu Yi gave a sigh. “We’ve already presented them with the list. I can’t take most of the other students as my Disciple. Especially not those from the Phoenix Clan. Our understanding of the Dao of Space is too different. Also, we are in the same post in High Heaven Palace. You don’t need to keep addressing me as Elder.”","“Sorry, it has become a habit...” Xu Yi said and he turned towards the Recovery Hall in the far off distance. “The Recovery Hall is already scrambling... They’re already done with twenty students... Even if the student body is huge, wouldn’t we be taking away their opportunity to compete in the other events we have planned?”","“What can we do? This whole mess started because of those two. Our months of planning for the school curriculum has basically gone down the drain. But then again, this is our first year. I guess it is a lesson learnt...” Li Wu Yi sighed once more. He wondered how many times he sighed since becoming the form teacher of those two. Even though he hardly taught them, they sure gave him tons of mess to clean up. Honestly, he wondered if he was a nanny rather than a teacher.","“You can say that again...” Suddenly, a familiar voice played out. It was melodious, causing Li Wu Yi’s heart to skip a beat.","“Jiu Feng, what brings you here?” Li Wu Yi asked while presenting a hardened face.","“What else, like you two, I need to supervise those two when they mess with my kids.” Jiu Feng said with exasperation. “Seriously, the Palace Master should not have even enrolled them. Even we teachers can’t teach them.”","Li Wu Yi could only nod to that statement. It was sadly true. Those two were too exceptional to the point they became outliers.","“Now, more than half our classes will be empty because the rest will be in a coma... I can’t even disagree because the Palace Mistress is the one with the highest authority in the Phoenix Clan...” Jiu Feng lamented. “All those talented Divine Beasts here got selected, since the Palace Mistresses have a heavy influence on that side.”","“Thankfully, that also means their parents wouldn’t cause too much of a ruckus once they find out... But, for the Human side...” Jiu Feng shook her head and patted Li Wu Yi’s and Xu Yi’s shoulders. After all, they were the ones that were going to bear the brunt of it.","“*Haaa...* Stop... don’t remind me. The other children will most likely get off light and awaken in a month or two. But, our class... *haa...*” Li Wu Yi at this point took out a jar of wine and a cup, and he started to drink.","After all, how many students had the talent to use the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time? Whose class had the most of such talents?","In other words, his class would be the one that has students in a coma for who knows how long...","At this point, no complaining would solve it. A man’s best friend was his wine.","“Ah. I feel your pain.” Jiu Feng readily took a cup out and she even passed Xu Yi a cup.","“You... so that’s why you’re here!” Li Wu Yi chided but Jiu Feng just giggled. “Oh come on, drinking alone would be boring, no? Besides, you’ve already narrowed down who you are going to take in as your Disciple with that list. Isn’t it time to celebrate?”","Li Wu Yi just rolled his eyes. He had been keeping this wine for years. Thousand Year Ice Warming Liquor, a rarity in the world that could only be bought through auction! Now, this sly woman was trying to get a taste without giving him any rewards.","“What a narrow minded man. No wonder you haven’t gotten any dates even with your position.” Jiu Feng rolled her eyes back at him.","“That’s because–” Li Wu Yi nearly said what was in his heart. However, in the end, he chose to keep it shut. After all, he already knew the answer before he said it out loud. After so many years, has anything changed between them?","“Fine, fine. How about this? I’ll do you a favour in return.”","“This...” Li Wu Yi reeled back a bit. However, that brief hesitation was enough.","Jiu Feng quickly took that jar and filled up all three cups.","“Come on! Drink up!” Jiu Feng clicked her cup with Li Wu Yi’s and Xu Yi. She smiled as she took a sip as her face glowed from the chilling sensation in her tongue and the warm sensation in her body. [Idiot.]","Meanwhile, Xu Yi could only stare at them in confusion, “Wait, don’t we still have class tomorrow?”","Silavin: Their relationship has certainly gotten closer over the years, but Li Wu Yi has just never taken that final step. This event was Jiu Feng trying to push him.","Actually, I thought about how Jiu Feng had even thought about doing this, but I don’t think I would be able to fit everything here. The release rate is only once a week, and I wish to start the next arc.","School for the Twins is a little too easy."]},{"number":6092,"title":"Chapter 6092, Each With Their Own Arrangements","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Sharing insights repeatedly was... exhausting.","This exhaustion struck not only Yang Ji but Yang Xu as well. Though she mostly just transported the children to the Recovery Hall, her Qi had eventually been sapped by Yang Ji.","Thankfully, they had an abundance of Eight Revolutions Qi Recovering Pills. So, they could do this continuously.","‘Continuously’ as in, even through the night.","Naturally, they had to take breaks in between. Even if one of them shared insight while the other took Pills to recover, the speed of recovery could not offset the speed in which they committed the target to slumbering cultivation. So, it was only natural that after the first few children, the speed bodies appearing in the Recovery Hall slowed down.","And due to these Pills, they did not even stop at night. They continued on. After all, neither knew when they might get in trouble. To support their Mothers’ plan, they would need to act fast before any opposition arrives.","It should be said that they even grew skillful at it. Those being ‘treated’ started to ‘show’ less resistance. Initially, one might still see one of the Twins’ faces. However, soon enough, they did not even realise what had happened before their world turned dark and they were confined inside their own Knowledge Sea...","But, should this not cease once it turned dark and the students all went back to their dorms? What about the Isolation Arrays in the dorms?","Initially, the Twins had expected themselves to stop as well. Who knew that the Heavenly Demon Queen would willingly volunteer to land them a hand?","With the help of this peerless expert in Arrays, what could stop them?","The dormitories were being raided left right and centre. It could be said that once these children were stationary, it was easier to capture them.","So, they continued.","Again, one by one, children got sucked into their hands and ended up in the Recovery Hall...","Naturally, that meant that the Recovery Hall was working round the clock, accommodating those children. If they had not prepared beforehand, things might have been a problem. However, with the help from the other Halls, these children were taken care of in an orderly fashion.","Yet, for this busy site, the receptionist who received Yang Ji had all but disappeared.","No one knew where she went, nor who she was at this point. It was as if her existence had completely disappeared. In fact, it was a mystery as to why no one was looking for her.","...","And while the Twins were busy at work...","“I presume, then, that we are in accordance?”","“My my. Men don’t like their girls to be so stern. Smile a little, why don’t you.”","A stony silence filled the air as this dorm room felt cold as ice...","“Sheesh. Can’t even take a joke. But, I have to say, how daring of you to come here alone. Are you not afraid of what I might do to you after what you’ve done to me?”","“Should such coercion have any effect upon my person, you would scarcely be where you are today. That much, at least, should be evident to you.”","“Oh. How pompous of you to say that.”","The boy could hear a cold scoff and he gave a sigh.","“For a noble Lady like you, to resort to such methods to coerce me. Well, should I say that I’m honoured? Fine. I’ll agree to your demands. Not like I have much choice in this matter, anyways.”","“The guarantee.”","“I’ll swear on my Dao Heart.”","“That will not suffice.”","“Damn. It is seriously tough to deal with Primordial Beings like you. In that case, I’ll let you keep that as your bargaining chip. Happy now?”","“Enter into a covenant with that child.”","The boy thought for a while and relented. “Fine. But I have some conditions.”","....","“You all didn’t need to do this behind my back. To think you actually received all the teachers’ acknowledgement without me knowing, all just in case.” Yang Kai’s voice rang out through his room as a woman placed her arms around his neck.","“Husband, is it not better for you to distance yourself from this matter?” A gentle seductive voice filled his ear, a whisper that came from behind. Naturally, it was Yu Ru Meng.","“Exactly. Leave the politics to us. There is no need for you to do everything.” Another melodious voice came out which tugged at ones’ heart. It was Shan Qing Luo.","“All of you made me the Principal. I need to be responsible for this seat.” Yang Kai said but Yu Ru Meng just shook her head.","“Husband, they are not seeing you as just a mere Principal of a school. They are seeing you as, Yang Kai, the sole man who entered the World Creation Realm and created High Heaven Palace, the strongest Sect in this world. Otherwise, they would not have wanted to so seriously make use of their children like this. Taking your hand away from this matter would be best for your position. Leave the politics to us.”","“Besides, it is not like you are unaware as to why we wanted you to become the Principal. It is not to entertain matters like this.”","“Yes, I am aware. You want me to have a seat here for our kids. At least, that would allow me to spend more time with them before they are grown up. Also, as a punishment, take care of this massive child-rearing project...” Yang Kai thought back on how they were so adamant that this was to be his punishment.","“En. But, honestly, even we are stumped that those two could cause so much chaos before the month was up. Even so, since this chaos is caused by our children, it will be dealt with by their Parents, in our capacity as their Mothers.” Shan Qing Luo added.","“So, you all plan to keep High Heaven Palace and High Heaven Academy separate. But, will this really work out? All of you are Palace Mistresses. Certainly...” Yang Kai wanted to continue to speak but at this point, Yu Ru Meng covered his mouth and just said, “Just leave it to us. We are more adept at politics than you think.”","Seeing how these two women have moved to the forefront to protect Yang Ji and Yang Xu, Yang Kai could only relent at this point. Certainly, if one were to consider soft politics, they would have him beat. Yang Kai had most relied on other factors in having an edge over others. However, these two women were especially adept at dealing with people on the same level as them. If not, people with positions higher than them.","Furthermore, it had to be said that in terms of management of High Heaven Palace, was it not done by others instead of the Palace Master?","“Fine. I’ll take my hands off this matter. But, in that case, why didn’t you just tell me the plan in the first place? You could have saved me so much headache.” Yang Kai asked but at this point, even he did not expect a straightforward answer.","“To mess with you.” Yu Ru Meng straightforwardly answered.","“Are you serious?” Yang Kai frowned but the answer Yu Ru Meng gave made him chuckle instead. “After we gave you your punishment, what did you do, huh? Us Sisters still have our bodies aching.”","“Besides, what’s wrong with a Father having headaches over his children? We are going to clean up the mess because you have the sacred position of Palace Master, and our punishments cannot come as a detriment to the Sect. The least you could do is share some of the suffering.” Shan Qing Luo rolled her eyes as she said this.","“Yes, yes, I made you all suffer a lot that night.” Yang Kai chuckled.","“That night? You mean a week.” Shan Qing Luo’s eyes narrowed. But, since it was technically not such a rare occurrence, she just relented and continued to say, “Sister Xue Yue has gone out to Red Clouds Cave Heaven. As for the other children, here is the list. For now, us Sister will go meet their Parents. In the meantime, as the Principal, you would need to prepare a speech for the students to explain why this is happening.”","“In short, leave matters outside of the academy to us. We will deal with those. You just need to take care of the academy itself.” Yu Ru Meng reiterated."]},{"number":6093,"title":"Chapter 6093, Why We Dream","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","It took more than a day and a night of non-stop work, with Yang Ji and Yang Xu taking turns. The list had gone as far as to assign who should give insight to what child. So, they naturally took turns.","Unfortunately, with the time it took to recover had caused them to eat into day two. Teachers in the know, mostly those who had their students chosen, who could sense the Space fluctuations had not ceased, chose to stop class for the day. After all, who would want their students to suddenly get spirited away while they were in their classroom seats?","Though it did seem strange to some students, not all classes followed this trend. For example, Li Wu Yi’s class and Jiu Feng’s class, which had a truly valid reason for not opening.","Thousand Year Ice Warming Liquor. It was a rarity that had to be obtained through auction. Naturally, its rarity and demand was due to one thing, which was that it was one of the few rare liquors that could make an Open Heaven Realm Master feel drunk.","Ordinary alcohol would no longer have any effect on an Open Heaven Realm Master, if they wanted to dissipate its effect. However, the Thousand Year Ice Warming Liquor was different. In using the natural effect of Yin and Yang, bolstering its effect, this alcohol would even seep into their Small Universes and affect all beings inside. One could only wait for it to take its natural course, to relieve themselves of their stupor.","So, on this day, the three teachers were basically out of commission and could not hold class. It was only fortunate that on their side, Jiu Feng and Xu Yi had told the academy prior to getting drunk.","As for their classes, they were the final ones chosen by Yang Ji and Yang Xu.","It took no small amount of effort to impart their Daos to the remaining children. The Twins did not expect they would even get mentally exhausted over this task.","This was a kind of exhaustion that could be alleviated by Pills, but the Twins found that sleep was the best remedy for it. Besides, if the Twins had something they loved to do, it would be sleep. That was why they, even if they did not crave food, still slept when they could.","This time, they could permanently connect their rooms so they could share beds once more.","And, in their dreams...","*Boom! Boom! Boom!*","Unable to get injured here, they naturally could spar as much as they wanted. Their environment could also change to whatever they wanted.","It could be said that this was their true playground, where they could do whatever they wanted without any consequences. Naturally, this was also only possible because they were connected to each other, and could share dreams. Otherwise, what a lonely world it would be if they could only dream of themself, and them alone.","Unfortunately, such dreams also had their limitations, as the Twins would eventually wake up and falling asleep was not as easy a thing for them. It was not so much that they had an illness like insomnia, but rather due to their cultivation realm, like their diet, they did not need to sleep nor eat. So, it was inevitable that they could not sleep that easily, even if they wanted to play around in their dreams.","Right now, Yang Ji had raised his fist and punched forward with just pure strength. It caused the landscape to shift as Space cracked and lands were split in half.","Yang Xu barely avoided the blow as she dived in to launch an uppercut, capable of shattering buildings.","However, how could Yang Ji not have predicted this blow? Even if Space was torn asunder, he easily blocked it with his forehead by facing down.","The fist barely struck his nose as it landed squarely on his forehead. With a *Boom!* the two children ceased and they separated.","“Brother, that’s cheating. There is no way you would have been able to survive if you took the full brunt of it.” Yang Xu complained as the world around them returned back to normal.","However, Yang Ji countered, “No no no. My forehead would hardly hurt from that.”","“*Haaa...* Though we can play around as much as we want, I guess if it doesn’t really hurt, we would not be able to tell. I don’t really want to play anymore...” Yang Xu said as she turned around and changed the scenery.","They were now back at home, in their usual room within Starry Sky Palace. Every centimetre was recreated within the dream, the touch, the smell, even the warmth. She immediately moved to the bed and said, “As I thought, this place always feels the best.”","Yang Ji just shook his head. “Yes, it’s been a while since we’ve been to our room. But, we rarely get this opportunity. Shouldn’t we do something more fun?”","“Brother, aren’t you tried? We’ve been sharing our insights non-stop for almost two full days. The first thing you did after we slept is ask me to spar with you. We’ve been doing that for two hours already. What else do you want to do? Can’t we just lie on the bed?” Yang Xu said with a pitiful look on her face.","“But we rarely get to spar. Out in the real world, you dare not use your full strength and always refuse.” Yang Ji sighed.","“Let’s just chat, okay?” Yang Xu said and laid down, completely unwilling to do anything else. Despite being able to share information instantaneously if she so chooses, Yang Xu strangely loves to do such things.","Yang Ji relented and sat on the bed with her, then he asked, “Fine. So, what do our Mothers plan to do now?”","“They said they will handle the Parents. That we do not need to do anything else. But Brother, don’t you think we’ve caused them quite a bit of trouble for them this time?” Yang Xu said with a hint of worry.","“Our Mothers are all one of the strongest in this world. Surely this bit of trouble is nothing to them. But, I do feel bad forcing them to cover for us. Maybe I shouldn’t have done that to Lei Ao?” Yang Ji thought back on his impulsive action. He did not mean for all this to happen. He really thought he was just doing good. “What if we just sped up time for them? That way, they will awaken far earlier.”","“Brother, Mother and Father warned us about using Time Principles on others. Let’s not cause anymore trouble. I’m sure if any of them had wanted to wake them up, they would have done so earlier. There must be a reason they avoid doing that. Just like how they don’t allow Yang Hao to go into a cultivation room that has a different flow of time, even when he pleaded with them.”","“Oh...”","Seeing how her Brother’s mood had been affected, Yang Xu quickly tried to change the topic.","“By the way, I’m sure you noticed by now, but that worm has been acting really strange lately, going so far as to help us out. She thinks I had not noticed but she’s gone to a room that is not designated as one of our targets, you know?” Yang Xu highlighted. Whenever she thought of the Heavenly Demon Queen, she could not help but frown.","“I’m sure she has just visited that mysterious Wu Lun. I don’t think she intends to hide it from us. After all, we can sense her position at all times. I do get that you doubt her, but it is undeniable that she will not harm us because we are connected. In fact, she might be listening in to us for all we know. Though she did not appear in our last dream and this one, that doesn’t mean she can’t overhear us. She is also connected to us, after all.” Yang Ji said while looking around the room, as though hinting at something. However, no answer came back, as everything remained silent.","“If she can listen in on us even here, then our privacy has really been ruined by her.” Yang Xu sighed as besides the bed they were on, the room around them had changed. It turned into the cultivation room at Mo Na Ye’s place, or at least what was left of it.","Yang Xu thought back to before the Heavenly Demon Queen appeared. Then, the scene changed to display what they had seen in the past. This time, they were viewing themselves in third person.","Yang Ji commented, “It seems like it is still a little hard to recreate scenes... Luckily we have the two of us, so we can see each other. We normally just go around to different places to see different environments so that we can recreate them. I guess we should have practiced more for this.”","Yang Ji imposed his own memories to help Yang Xu, and the two watched the scene that happened a few months ago. Only, even after watching the whole scene play out, they did not get any clues.","Then, the scene changed to playback on when they last saw Little Eleven, when he created that Array with those dark symbols.","“Argh... why didn’t I study more on the Dao of Spirit Arrays?” Yang Xu moaned as she could not comprehend what Little Eleven was doing.","“Well, judging from how proficient she is at Arrays, I doubt you would be able to seal her even if you were on Father’s level.” Yang Ji shook his head. Though he understood why his Sister wished to learn how to recreate this Array, he doubted it would work. After all, the Heavenly Demon Queen broke away from it once, why not a second time. Even if for the first time, she did it from the outside, where it was weak.","“I’m more interested in this...” Yang Ji focused and then the scene changed. This time, it was no longer anything neither of them saw or heard before. After all, this was not something they had experienced before.","In fact, the world was dark. Except for their bed, they could hardly see anything.","However, they did hear two muffled and faint voices.","‘I presume, then...’","*Crack!*","However, before anything could continue, the darkness seemed to crack, like glass, spiderwebs-like fissures formed and expanded. Try as they might, the Twins were no longer able to control this destruction.","Still, in the midst of this sudden change, Yang Ji grinned."]},{"number":6094,"title":"Chapter 6094, Erased","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","“You! So you’ve been listening in all along!? I knew it!” Immediately woken up from her slumber, Yang Xu immediately cursed.","Meanwhile, Yang Ji, who was just beside her on the bed, woke up as well and just silently waited for an answer.","“What are you staying silent for? Say something.” Yang Xu pressed and a sigh could be heard playing out inside their heads.","“To what end should I explain, when you refuse to grant faith to any utterance of mine? I bestowed upon you space within your own dreamscape. Yet you transgressed upon my boundaries, thereby obliging me to rouse you both from your slumber.” The Heaven Demon Queen said plainly and clearly, without any sign of guilt in her actions. It seemed as though she felt what she did was only right, since the Twins had stepped upon something they should not have.","“And we are supposed to believe that? How can we trust you!? You interfere in our conversations as you wish, you take actions without permission and questionable motives. Tell me, how can we really trust you?” Yang Xu questioned.","At this point, Yang Ji finally opened his mouth to calm Yang Xu down. It was obvious that even after a month together, the two had not gotten any closer to each other. In fact, it seems more likely that they just tolerated each other for his sake.","“Calm down. What I did doesn’t prove that she was listening in on us. But, it does show that it is not a one way street, correct?” Yang Ji then turned towards the Heavenly Demon Queen with that question and anticipated her response.","“*Haaa...* In the manner by which I may survey your lived experiences, you possess reciprocal capacity to survey mine as well. Naturally, not of the past beyond when we met but of the present times. It is for this singular reason, I deemed it neither necessary to mask my traces from you two, just the outsiders that may interfere.” The Heavenly Demon Queen said and continued, “What’s more, you should desist from probing any further. It is beneath a man of honor to interrogate a lady regarding matters she wishes to hold private.”","“In that case, since I’m not a man, I’ll do it.” Yang Xu rolled her eyes and scoffed but the Heavenly Demon Queen added, “It’s futile. That memory ceased existing.”","“What are you talking about?” Yang Ji asked while Yang Xu closed her eyes and focused.","“Then, stop playing around and let me check. Just pass me your memories of that time.” Yang Xu scolded. Typically, she and Yang Ji did not know how to access another party’s memories without their permission. In fact, she herself did not know how Yang Ji had managed to read the Heavenly Demon Queen’s memories while they were dreaming. Still, it was interesting that the Heavenly Demon Queen had admitted that she and her Brother could do the same to the Heavenly Demon Queen as she did to them–basically, spying on their every conversation and move.","“...” The Heavenly Demon Queen went silent for a while and surprisingly did as she was told. She flooded the Twins with memories of that time. In fact, she handed over memories of the entire day, till she returned to the Twins.","However, like a movie being played, everything was there but a section that went black and was without a sound.","Before the Twins produced any reaction, the Heavenly Demon Queen repeated, “As I had endeavored to convey, that memory has been removed from existence.”","“You did it on purpose!” Yang Xu was fuming at this point, and even Yang Ji did not calm her down. It was obvious that it was intentionally done. After all, that had seen part of that scene within the dream. How was it that this entire memory was completely void?","It was obvious the Heavenly Demon Queen must have erased it once she found out they could read part of her memories. There was no other explanation for this other than that.","At this point, Yang Xu could not help but try to attack the Heavenly Demon Queen. Unfortunately, since she was still within them, there was nothing physical she could do.","“Did you do it intentionally?” Yang Ji tried to calmly ask.","“What relevance does that possess?” The Heavenly Demon Queen said, but she received a stern silence in response, which pressured her to continue speaking. “I no longer know.”","“*Haaa...* Yang Ji sighed and then looked at Yang Xu and shook his head. [Be it if she is lying or not, we have no way to force her to talk. No point dwelling on this any further. Sure, we can’t have full faith in her, but since she is still answering our questions, it means she doesn’t want us to completely fall out.]","“Since there is nothing else to gain from this, let’s just leave this matter here. I guess we just have to wait until the plan you both have plays out.” Whatever the case, since their Father was present, Yang Ji did not feel the need to worry about this matter too much as he closed this chapter.","...","Over the course of the next few days, it seemed like matters had settled down. The cracks in the relationship between the Twins and the Heavenly Demon Queen did not make any progress in being resolved though.","Two parties were not interested in speaking and one party was not interested in asking. So, it seemed like a wall had been placed between them.","As for the academy, classes resumed as per normal.","To calm the nervous students down, there was naturally an announcement regarding the disappearances of certain students. The opinions were mixed on this, mostly positive. Many were disappointed they were not chosen while some felt frightened at how one could so easily get swiped in during the day within the school.","Still, even better news came as a few children actually managed to wake up within those few days. Naturally, these were not those who were granted insight into the Dao of Space or the Dao of Time. These children were those that had been granted insight into the Sword Dao or the Spear Dao.","It had to be said that it was fortunate that they woke up so quickly, since Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s mastery over those Daos were still quite rudimentary and these children were extremely talented in those Daos.","Of course, who was to say that the Wives did not have an estimate as to when a few of these children would wake up? After all, by some ‘coincidence’, the Wives handled a gathering of Parents the next day after the first child woke up.","Naturally, those children who underwent this ‘trial’ demonstrated their gains to better convince not only the other children, but the Parents as well–that this whole matter was a great opportunity for them.","It further cemented the idea that this had been a great opportunity, since these children had their strength increase by leaps and bounds. Some had even broken through their bottleneck the very moment they woke up!","In the face of this, how could the Parents truly criticise the school’s methods?","In fact, the Wives manage to turn things around in such a way that made it seem like these children had been fortunate to be selected. Though it had to be noted that technically these children had been filtered by their teachers first, before being selected by the Wives. Some might have lost the opportunity to take up these teachers as their Master, but not like the Parents would know, right?","Besides, could they not spin it in a way that opportunities were abound in High Heaven Academy, and the Parents should have faith in the school?","Of course, Yang Kai’s capable Wives knew how to play politics well against even top Forces. As Yang Ji had originally wanted, ties to Red Clouds Cave Heaven had gotten stronger. Though they had dropped the matter, in trying to tie their Young Master to be Yang Ji’s Disciple, the Wives have nevertheless established deeper ties to the Cave Heaven by purchasing partial stake in a few auction houses from them, while having the Cave Heaven’s people still run the business.","Also, due to those children that had the insight of both the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time needing to be more closely watched, the Wives gave their contact tokens to these children’s Parents.","All in all, as the Wives had promised Yang Kai, they neatly handled the matter without him needing to even show his face.","However, there was still one matter which had been left hanging, and that was the person in Yang Kai’s office that very day.","...","“I truly can’t see through you...” Yang Kai’s eyes widened as he looked at the young man in front of him, trying to peer into the latter’s Soul and uncover all his secrets. However, that seems impossible as this young man, Wu Lun, truly seems to just be in the Qi Condensation Realm.","Yet, how did a youth in the Qi Condensation Realm possibly reach his office, with Yang Kai only able to detect him when he entered the room?","Wu Lun smiled with confidence, as though nothing in the world could touch him. As though even the strongest of the 3,000 Worlds meant little to him.","“Wow. You aren’t as wary as that girl.” Wu Lun’s nonchalant smile made it seem like he was mocking Yang Kai, but he was genuinely praising him.","“So, what do you want?” Yang Kai sat up from his seat and asked, unamused by Wu Lun.","“Seriously, both of you two are so serious.” Wu Lun shrugged and got straight to the point, “I’ve come to an agreement with that girl. But, as their Father, I thought I’d best inform you about it prior, in case you case after me seeking revenge. I don’t want a misunderstanding to cause that kind of horrendous karma.”","“You speak as though I could actually do something to you.” Yang Kai mused at the thought, as even he could tell that Wu Lun was not someone he could handle while keeping the school safe.","Wu Lun’s eyes at that moment turned a little colder, “Who knows? Karma’s a bi⸸ch, and I would like to reduce as much of it as possible. But, I have an agreement that I need to abide by so I’m here to just inform you that we are going to take those three children away.”","“What!?” At this point, Yang Kai could not keep calm any longer."]},{"number":6095,"title":"Chapter 6095, Inevitable Parting","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","*Ziii* At that very instant, space around the two seemed to freeze over as the world turned dark. Dark to the point where no light was in sight, where time seemed to hold no meaning.","This was the first time since reaching the World Creation Realm that Yang Kai had been enraged to this extent. Who was this young man, who dared to make demands of a Father to relinquish his children!?","The pressure Yang Kai bore down, crushing space with his mere Will, upon the other party could easily decimate an Open Heaven Realm Master. Yet, Wu Lun just stood there, seemingly unaffected.","In fact, he still bore a smile, a more tired one, as he raised both his hands up in seeming resignation. “Look, I really mean no harm. I’m just here to talk. If you want to blame someone, blame that parasite clinging onto those Twins of yours. We merely established an agreement, and I have to keep my end of the bargain.”","Wu Lun’s eyes soon turned sharp as he exhaled, “Or, do you really want to try me?”","As soon as those words left his mouth, a seemingly unexplainable power oozed out from his very being. Yang Kai had never felt this before, as it seemed both foreign and familiar at the same time. Nevertheless, this seemingly small move was enough to fracture the space that Yang Kai had isolated them in, and they returned back to the real world.","“As I suspected, like her, you are not from here, are you?” Yang Kai took a deep breath and asked. Despite the rage he felt earlier, after so many years spent raising children and taking care of High Heaven Palace, he had gained a more collected head.","If it were the past, he might have directly lashed out with all his might, staking even his life. However, after having children, it could be said that Yang Kai had mellowed out considerably.","Even if out of anger, that earlier move was just a probe. Even so, that move was not something just anyone could undo, especially not with such ease. Yang Kai had a feeling that he would not be able to handle Wu Lun without sacrifices, and this just proved it.","As for risking the lives of those around him with this probe, Yang Kai knew that if Wu Lun wanted to harm others, he could have easily done so while hiding in the dark. No need to expose himself like this.","Wu Lun, seemingly also knowing that the probing was done, chuckled, “My my. No need to probe into me so much. I have no interest in men. On a more serious note, though I can’t tell you much, I believe you already know the answer to most of those questions in your heart.”","Yang Kai ignored his attempt at a joke and then thought a little before asking, “Then, are you from the Taboo Realm?”","“Taboo Realm?” Wu Lun seemed surprised at the sudden mention of this term. So, he gave a pause and clicked his fingers, “Oh. That. So that’s what you call it here.”","Wu Lun stopped saying anything and just shook his head. Then, he placed his index finger on his lips and smiled.","Yang Kai, seeming to piece the puzzles together, gave a nod and with a wave of his hand, used his Divine Sense to move a tea set in front of Wu Lun, preparing it for the latter. After all, he felt like there was much to talk about with this mysterious man, and he seemed amicable to provide a few answers, though they might not resolve much.","However, Wu Lun shook his head, and refused the tea, gently pushing the floating set away from him. “Though it smells of delight, like I said, I am not one who hopes to get tied to more karma. It would do neither of us any good for me to stay here any longer. Besides informing you about your children, I am here for nothing else. This is where the karma between us ends.”","Seeing that he was being quite adamant on his stance, Yang Kai also hardened his stance and shook his head, refusing, “And I did not allow you to take them away, did I? Sit and explain, else we will really have a problem.”","Wu Lun just sighed. At the very next moment, his form turned illusionary, as though he was a mere manifestation.","In front of Yang Kai, he faded into nothingness, leaving behind nothing. Not a scent, not a hair. It was as if he had never even entered this room.","Naturally, Yang Kai immediately tried to use his Divine Sense to scan for his location, but it was to no avail. It was truly as if he had just vanished into thin air.","“Are you serious?” Yang Kai’s eyes widened in shock. Many things came to mind at this very moment. [How did he do that? How am I unable to sense him? He’s no longer even in High Heaven Academy.]","As he tried to think things through, a voice suddenly echoed in his mind.","“You need not worry. They will also be attending school...”","“Wait!” Yang Kai shouted but no response came back. Wu Lun truly moved as though no one could have stopped him.","...","“And even you could no longer sense him?”","“No, and I’m the one that created this space. How does that even make sense? Unless...”","“You’re right. That’s the only possibility. I can’t think of anything else. But to think that such a being came here of all places...”","Two voices were talking about the events that took place moments ago in this very spot.","Naturally, those two voices were from Yang Kai and Shi. Not wanting to alarm his Wives, Yang Kai could only choose to confide in the possibly last remaining person who would know about such mysterious matters within the 3,000 Worlds, Shi.","These two men had conversed for days and nights about the Taboo Realm and other such matters. After all, only such an ancient being like Shi might possess clues as to the truth of the world that Yang Kai wanted to uncover.","Still, the mysteries of the world remained out of reach. They had been stuck on certain problems, and had been unable to resolve them, until now.","It seemed like the Twins, be it a blessing or a curse, seem to attract the attention of beings outside of this world. First was the Heavenly Demon Queen, then came Wu Lun. Two such instances, were they a mere coincidence, or was fate playing with the lives of the two children?","And, it seemed like there was a force drawing away those two, away from the 3,000 Worlds.","Yang Kai knew that those two loved to go on adventures. In fact, other material objects held little interest to them. If they were to be allowed to choose a life of absolute luxury, or a life of arduous adventure, the Twins would naturally incline towards the latter.","[Maybe, such is their fate, to explore the truth of the world...]","From what they gathered, there was a place far more mysterious than the Taboo Realm. It could not be mentioned nor touched upon. There seemed to be some kind of Restriction, where those who knew something would suffer a backlash upon trying to broach the subject.","Nevertheless, such a matter was basically proven when Wu Lun could easily break through the Principles Yang Kai had manipulated.","He could not possibly be from another world that was of equal status to theirs, where their World Principles were on the same level as theirs. Otherwise, it would not be possible for him to unravel the Principles controlled by Yang Kai with such ease.","This difference was akin to a Flood Dragon trying to deal with a True Dragon. The difference was so stark, it was painful.","It was clear that Wu Lun had mastered a Dao outside of the 3,000 Daos that Yang Kai had mastered, and it was a Dao that was of a higher caliber than the 3,000 Daos that Yang Kai knew of.","For Yang Kai, there was only one thing that made this possible. It was that other path he had stepped half a foot into but had yet to reach. The path which Yang Ji had seen yet failed to step foot into and was frustrated by the knowledge of their current ‘mistaken’ path.","“And he said that he was going to take my children away...” Yang Kai sighed and looked at Shi, but the man seemed to be contemplating something before answering, in earnest, “Then, why not let him?”","“What!? How could you even say that? He is going to take my children to Heaven knows where.” Yang Kai was taken aback at how Shi was so cold to them.","Shi then raised his hand, stopping Yang Kai. “You too left your home at a relatively young age. What’s more, keeping them here would only hinder their future potential. Just look around you. How has this whole place benefitted them? Have they gained any friends? Have they gotten stronger?”","Yang Kai paused for a moment and Shi took the opportunity to continue. “You and your Wives would just be deceiving yourselves if all of you believe you can raise those two within this safe nest of yours. The other children, sure. But those two? Just look at this whole school. Your Wives had to move to fix up their mess. In the end, who benefits? Did this whole ordeal teach them anything else except about Master-Disciple etiquette and their customs?”","“You and your Wives have sheltered them long enough. Even I would find it difficult to teach them anything useful about cultivation. They... Their path is something that they should walk themselves. Even if reluctant, as their Father, are you going to hinder them?” Shi stared deep into Yang Kai’s eyes. He could tell that the once adventurous young man had matured so much. Yet, as a Parent, he had yet to take the final step, which was to let go.","The two men knew that this was the truth. However, while one had aged and seen much growth and death, connecting and parting, the other was still hoping to cling on for longer. He knew they would inevitably go their separate ways, but he just hoped that it was not now.","After all, even at the world behind the Profound Source Gate, Yang Kai had not allowed the Twins to leave his sight. Although he was harsher towards them, it was only relative to his Wives and his Parents.","Even when giving them trials, when did he ever allow their lives to be up to fate?","He thought that he was already being very disciplined when he dealt with them, that he was being the harsh Parent. However, he failed to see that he too was still soft on them. At least, this was a far cry from when he tried to raise Yang Xiao.","Yang Kai closed his eyes for a moment and took a deep breath. It was... difficult for him to accept. He knew the answer but his heart was reluctant.","And like that, Shi just shook his head and talked about other matters for now.","After all, even if one runs away from the inevitable, it would still one day arrive to face them."]},{"number":6096,"title":"Chapter 6096, Bet","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","After a few days had passed to cool down...","Yang Ji and Yang Xu were both still in Yang Ji’s room, wide awake after the whole fiasco with the Heavenly Demon Queen. As for the culprit, she remained in her habitat for the whole time, where she could ignore the world once more.","Strangely enough, Yang Xu was hanging upside down, with her feet on the ceiling as she paced around in frustration.","Still, since her Brother was here, she did not do much else. It was also questionable if having the blood rushing to her brain affected her mood, since their high cultivation realm should render such things moot.","Yet, she still took care of her appearance, where her long hair seemingly defied gravity with her, same as her dress. It was as if the gravity of the room was split in two, in two different directions.","Maybe it was a hidden sign to show her discontent, that she was of the opposite opinion of her Brother, who was sitting on the bed, looking at her.","“I just don’t get it...” Yang Xu muttered as she continued to pace around in deep thought.","“What don’t you get?”","“Brother, just how did you manage to look through her memories? If we can do it now...” Yang Xu seemed to be waiting for that question.","However, Yang Ji just shrugged his shoulders, “Your guess is as good as mine. I just felt like we could have done it then, and once we woke up, it doesn’t seem to be possible. I don’t know if it was really erased like she said, or if there is something more at play. One thing I do know is that the us in our dreams are different from how we are right now.”","“Besides, are you fine with us talking about this now? You’ve been keeping quiet the past few days, Isn’t it because she might overhear us?” Yang Ji asked, curious as to why she was bringing this up now when the matter should have already been over.","Yang Xu snorted and shook her head, “If she is always listening in on us, then when will I be able to ask you these questions? It’s like having a stalker that constantly spies on us. There’s no point in waiting for the right time. I might as well just ask it now rather than let this curiosity of mine eat me from the inside out.”","“Wait. What’s a stalker?” Hearing this unknown term for the first time, Yang Ji asked but Yang Xu quickly glossed over the topic. “Just another name for a really skilled spy.”","“Brother, can we get back on topic and not get distracted? Let’s focus on the dream... What makes it so different?”","Yang Ji thought for a moment and then, with a *snap* of his fingers, the whole room changed. The connection to Yang Xu’s room was cut off. In fact, the connection to the outside world seemed to have been entirely served as the walls, ceiling and floor wrapped with mysterious images that seemed to come and go in a blur. Eventually, the scene before them settled and Yang Xu blinked a few times before everything settled.","However, what was around them was strange. If Yang Xu did not know what Yang Ji was trying to do, she would have thought they had landed in some nightmare.","The current room was inspired by their memories of their own room back in Starry Sky Palace. Naturally, this was in no way connected to their actual room. Even if Yang Ji had profound mastery over the Dao of Space, there was still a barrier between this world and the world outside. Unless he could break through that barrier, he would not be able to connect the rooms.","Instead, this was a ‘faithful’ recreation of the room. However, it was not just any faithful recreation. It was a recreation making use of Space Principles.","Meaning, the flooring, walls, furniture and so on were all created through manipulating Space Principles, to emulate the room, which the Twins had perfect memory of considering the time they spent there and their cultivation realm.","Yet, this scene was off. Even if it looked perfect to the eyes, that was all it could be. The tactile feeling of the walls, how light bounced off of the walls, the scent of the room and so forth, all of these were lacking one way or another.","If one looked closely, they could obviously see mismatches in every aspect of the room. Add them all together, and it looked eerie and disgusting, like something not of this world.","Nevertheless, Yang Xu got the point Yang Ji was trying to convey without any explanation.","For some reason, in their dreams, recreating things was so effortless. No matter the temperature, the pressure, the texture or the touch, everything felt so real it was eerie. Everything was an emulation of what happened, like their memory had become a real world. Even the sensation of touch and scent was the same, which even if one of them did not take notice at the time, the other surely would.","Then, if both took notice and recreated the scene, but nothing felt off, was this not proof of a perfect recreation?","Yet, they could not do the same in the real world, despite their high cultivation and having the same memory.","It should be added that at their Father’s level, he could create worlds. So, it stands to reason they should be able to recreate at least something more akin to what was in their memories than this...","In short, there were still things they did not understand about themselves, about their connection when in their unconscious state, which allowed them to tap into the Heavenly Demon Queen’s memories.","And for some reason, when out of their unconscious state, they lost that connection.","“I had a feeling that our connection was always stronger when we were asleep. I wondered if the same was true with the Heavenly Demon Queen, and it seems to be so.” Yang Ji said with a curious smile, “Now, I wonder if there is going to be a difference if one of us goes to sleep while the other stays awake. Hey, are you listening? What’s the matter with you?”","Yang Xu twirled her finger and the room returned back to normal. She, too, returned back to the ground without even a kick, and just rotated in mid-air.","She honestly could not stand the sight of that off-putting scene. Before she spoke, she had to erase that scene from her eyes by taking a few seconds.","“Brother, I don’t understand how you are fine with that. Please never do that again. I have goosebumps.” Yang Xu still had her eyes closed as she spoke.","“Come on, it wasn’t that bad.” Yang Ji rolled his eyes. [How exaggerated. Still, that at least got her mind off the Heavenly Demon Queen for now,]","“Brother, I don’t understand how you tolerate all these things. You were fine with that thing’s appearance, and then you are fine with this.” Yang Xu just shook her head at how nonchalant he seemed to be in the face of such disgust.","“I honestly just don’t find it that disgusting. I found those kids drooling when they got knocked out more disgusting, you know? You didn’t even want to touch them and just made a portal underneath them.” Yang Ji shot back.","However, at this point, Yang Xu rolled her eyes, “It’s not like it makes that much of a difference. They landed safely without injury.”","“Sure. Then, how about we go check?” Yang Ji said and he opened a direct portal to the Recovery Hall.","“What are we betting on?” Yang Xu grinned this time, confident that this was in the bag.","*Hmmm...* Yang Ji paused for a long while, and seriously pondered for a moment.","However, it was Yang Xu who snapped her finger and pointed at Yang Ji, “If you lose, you will have to help me do something. I won’t say what it is now, I’ll tell you later.”","Yang Ji was a little taken aback at how Yang Xu’s eyes started glittering. It was a far cry from how she looked the past few days. “F-fine. If you lose, you will have to help me do something then.”","Thus, the two made a bet, with one already having an idea of what to demand, and the other assuming the other party also had no idea what to demand and just followed along, thinking that more time was needed to decide."]},{"number":6097,"title":"Chapter 6097, Blamed Without Evidence","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","*Ziii*","A portal opened up and the Twins stepped into the Recovery Hall once more. The moment they did, they noticed that there were a few students that were shuffling about. Some were walking out towards the reception room, while some entered deeper into the plant-like buildings.","“Oh? They’re awake already.” Yang Ji commented as he saw a familiar face. It was one of the students that was in the name list. He was one of the earliest targets, which meant that he received one of the more basic Dao insights.","There were also other students here this time. Maybe they were here to visit their friends, or here because they were injured. Anyways, the Recovery Hall certainly had not been as crowded as this when the Twins first visited.","Yang Xu just continued with a confident smile as she looked around and gestured to another student, her voice only heard through Divine Sense, “Brother, see her? I was the one who moved her over here. See? No injuries, right?”","Yang Ji took a surreptitious scan using his Divine Sense, and indeed, there were no injuries.","Yang Ji then used his Divine Sense to check through the entire Recovery Hall... and only one person was injured...","Of course, when he focused on the child, that child was completely unfamiliar to him and his Sister. After all, this child was not on the list, and his injuries were due to another matter.","As others, Yang Ji’s Divine Sense naturally could not penetrate through the individual rooms, as those had a multitude of Arrays built into them, one of them being an Isolation Array.","Still, with his Divine Sense checking through the Area, Yang Ji began to frown... he truly got played by his Sister. [No wonder she wanted to make a bet so readily...]","This whole place, the Recovery Hall, was not just any ordinary space. It was akin to its own world, where plants and buildings seem to have merged, where vitality was in abundance and one would feel refreshed and invigorated inside. Not to mention any Pills, just staying here for a few days would help a person recover from any superficial injuries. In fact, it might not even take a few days with those Arrays...","[*Haa...* Why didn’t I think of this...] Yang Ji sighed in his heart and shook his head. If there had been any injuries, they would be long gone by now. This place, with its Arrays, might not help a person in gaining insight, but they certainly made students quickly return to class after an injury or illness.","It was just the school’s fortune that the Twins had managed to help occupy those ownerless beds for a prolonged period of time.","Yang Xu grinned and signalled to Yang Ji, “Brother, so how is it? Found anyone injured?”","Yang Ji paused for a moment then turned his head towards the reception desk, “I know what you’re playing at. And no, I haven’t found anyone that you’ve injured. But, I’m not willing to give up just yet.”","Yang Xu shrugged and rolled her eyes, “Come on. Just give up already. You know that I’ve won so let’s just settle the bet.”","“Mother said that a man must always honour their word, and I will do precisely that. But, this bet isn’t over until both of us agree to it. Even if their injuries have healed up by now, I’m sure some of those helping to carry them into their rooms would remember a thing or two.” Yang Ji quickened his pace and walked to the reception building outside, where the building at least looked more like a building than a plant.","Yang Ji looked around and saw that the familiar woman was nowhere to be seen. Instead, another person had taken over the reception desk. No, more actually, there were a few other women instead, but they were not as ‘bountiful’ as the previous one.","It made sense, after all. Initially, the reception building was not predicted to have that many people visiting. More intense programs were scheduled at the later part of the year, and since the school had just opened, the staff had to focus more on internal matters, like structuring their new workplace, planting, training, etc.","So, the reception building had been only left with that single woman. However, now that more time has passed with the Recovery Hall, Alchemy Hall and Plantation Hall all having been properly structured, along with sky high demand from visitors, it was no wonder the reception building had to assign more staff to man the counter.","Fortunately, when Yang Ji had come over, there was an empty counter with a woman smiling at him, forcibly. In fact, those who had recognised them seem to have apprehensive expressions on their faces for a moment before trying their best to hide it.","“G-Greetings, how may I assist you today?” For some reason, even when the woman was speaking with a smile, she seemed awfully nervous. Her luscious lips were quivering a little as she spoke.","“Hmm? Is something wrong?” Yang Ji could not help but notice how strange she was acting, the same for Yang Xu.","Small beads could be seen flowing down her skin as she quickly responded, “Nothing’s wrong. Please, how may I help you today?”","Yang Ji’s eyes narrowed for a moment, then he turned back to look at his Sister. He knew his curiosity was not the priority at the moment. So, he just let the matter slide and asked, “Back then, when we brought in students, were there any problems?”","The woman took a moment but still could not give a clear answer, “Erm... no... I don’t know...”","“Oh, were you not here? It’s impossible for you to forget otherwise, since you are in the Origin Returning Realm.” Yang Ji’s eyes narrowed as he tried to think of why she was acting like this.","The woman seemed to have gotten a little paler at that moment.","“Brother, could it be that she is nervous because she recognises us?” Yang Xu questioned through her Divine Sense, which made Yang Ji tilt his head in wonder. “But, the previous receptionist wasn’t like this, and I don’t think it is that hard to identify us.”","After all, who were Yang Ji and Yang Xu? They were experts in the Dao Source Realm, while most of these receptionists were in the Origin Returning Realm. Naturally, these receptionists would be able to easily see through all the children except for them. Furthermore, with them always appearing as a pair, how hard would it be to identify them? The moment any faculty member of the school could not detect a child’s cultivation, and that child was always accompanied by another child of the opposite gender, who else could they be but the infamous Twins?","“Well, maybe the previous receptionist simply didn’t know who we were. After all, we didn’t really cause a major incident at that time, unlike now.” Yang Xu said.","“I guess that’s possible. Let me ask first.” Yang Ji ceased using his Divine Sense to communicate with Yang Xu in secret and asked with his own voice, “Why are you acting like that? What is making you so nervous?”","“I’m so sorry Young Master Ji, and Young Mistress Xu. Please don’t make me disappear like Mei Qing.” The receptionist immediately lowered her head and pleaded. This naturally drew a lot more attention to her and the Twins, with some staff members turning pale and some students backing away.","Yang Ji frowned. He was never the kind of person that liked all this attention. So, he raised his hand and Space started to distort. Space Principles were warped and compressed, as they were forced to form a thick wall where no voice or Divine Sense would be able to pass through.","Seeing herself suddenly kidnapped into this unknown space, the woman was now begging for them to let her go.","Yang Ji turned to Yang Xu and questioned her, “Mei Qing? Mei Qing... I don’t think I’ve seen that name on the namelist. She isn’t anyone that I know of... she must be referring to the previous receptionist. But, I didn’t do anything to her, did you?”","Yang Xu rolled her eyes and questioned back, “Of course not. What would I even do with her?”","“But, if not you, then who? The fear that she is showing is real. So, something must have happened to her. And this is despite this being in the reception building, within a world Father has created.” Yang Ji pointed out.","Yang Ji then explained to the woman, trying to calm her down. “Please don’t panic, I’m just making these walls to stop people from eavesdropping on us. Mei Qing has just helped guide us to our classmate, Lei Ao. After we left, we did not meet again. How did you even get the idea that we did something to her?”","The woman’s eyes seem shifty. She just shook her head and pleaded, “Please, please just let me go. I will make any amends.”","“Wait... didn’t you hear what I said? What are you...” Yang Ji felt his heart drop. He never thought that others would be so afraid of him to such an extent.","He turned to look at his Sister, who also had the same bewildered expression.","[Argh... I just wanted to know if Yang Xu injured anyone during the process. Why did it have to turn out like this?] Yang Ji pondered over what he did wrong. He felt like if he said anything to this woman, all words would go in one ear and out the other. [Should I get someone else then?]","Yang Xu saw that he was about to open the wall and hurriedly stop him. She conveyed her thoughts secretly “Brother, can you let me try something first? Something’s fishy about this. I suspect even if we get another receptionist to answer, we’d just be going in circles.”","Seeing Yang Ji nod, Yang Xu had received his acknowledgement and started to put on a ferocious act.","“If you don’t tell me something I’d like to hear, you know how you will end up right?” Yang Xu purposely said it in a vague manner, and she even clenched her fist to cause the Space Principles around the woman to tighten.","Naturally, this caused the woman to panic even more. Her eyes danced between the two continuously as she exclaimed, “Please, I have to support my Mother. I’m begging you, please, just let me go. I’ll answer anything you wish.”","In her eyes, the young girl looked no different from a Demon ready to squeeze out all her Life Force, as she felt her body tightened and her breathing more like desperate gasps of air.","Of course, Yang Xu did not have any intention of hurting her. She merely just made use of Space Principles to make the space around the woman more dense, creating a pressure that squeezed every corner of her body. Though Yang Xu was just applying a slight pressure, with their difference in cultivation realm, it was no wonder the woman could not even offer any form of resistance and panicked.","Of course, even if Yang Xu mistakenly used too much strength, Yang Ji was there to help prevent any mishaps from occurring.","Yang Xu grinned evilly, “Tell me, what do you think I will do to you?”","The woman at this point had tears streaming down her face and she begged, “Please... please... have mercy. I-I can’t disappear like that. M-My Mother is still ill. I need to take care of her!”","[So, we are suspected of making people disappear? But, we have sent everyone on the list to the Recovery Hall. So, why are we being blamed for this?] Yang Xu wondered in her mind as her expression remained chilly.","“Sister, could it be that another student has disappeared, one that is not on the list? Then, mixed with that receptionist called Mei Qing, we are highly suspicious? After all, this may have been done while the two of us were busy with the students on the list. And, it might be the case where we were the last ones to meet with Mei Qing before she disappeared.” Yang Ji hypothesised but without any evidence, this was merely just speculation. Still, he did not see how else this sin they had not committed had fallen onto their heads.","Furthermore, if one were to consider their status within the High Heaven Academy, they would not be able to avoid","“Brother, but if it is as you say... then...” Yang Xu turned toward him and frowned.","Yang Ji gave a hard nod and then asked the being deep inside of him that had been silent until now. “What did you do to them? I know you are listening, so don’t pretend to be mute.”","This time, the Heavenly Demon Queen gave a response. She held nothing back, as though this secret was... of no importance, unlike the other mysteries. “I must confess, though unintentional, it would be most unbecoming of my station to allow such unwarranted blame to fall upon your shoulders. It would be beneath my honour to allow your name to bear the burden of my transgressions. Therefore, I graciously yield to your inquiry, for it is the very least that honour demands of me.”","“That woman was not whom you think she is. It was I who removed her from where she stood, yet she is no longer in my company. As for the other student who has so conspicuously vanished, you both know who he is.” The Heavenly Demon Queen answered only that much and returned back to silence.","Yang Ji then turned to Yang Xu, “You heard her right? Then, the one who went missing is Wu Lun. But how can that be? Since even we could not trap him, did someone stronger than us take action? If so, then why did they pin the blame on us? Didn’t they even try to investigate? ”","Yang Xu shook her head. There were a few things Yang Ji did not know about the incident regarding the listed students. During those few days where they were having those students ‘spirited away’, there had not been any investigation. After all, basically, the whole faculty knew who was doing it. So, no investigation into any of the missing children would be brought up.","Secondly, this was a case where Wu Lun was involved. In their Parents’ eyes, he was both a mysterious and dangerous entity. So, when he disappeared, who would look for him? Yang Kai preferred that the school would have nothing to do with that young man, since even he could not see through him. Better not poke the hornets’ nest by getting too involved with him.","So, even if a case was brought out, as long as Wu Lun’s name was inside, Yang Kai would try his best to stay clear of him. If there was any investigation, he could not send out others lest they fell into danger. Best for him to investigate on his own.","In the end, the matter regarding the ‘kidnapping’, be it the students on the list or Mei Qing and Wu Lun, had been quietly suppressed by the higher ups. And, who were the children of these higher-ups? No one else but Yang Kai’s children stood at the very top of the hierarchy.","Considering this happened at the same time as Yang Ji and Yang Xu’s ‘sweep’ of students on the list, and how even the Principal was preventing an investigation, it was not difficult for some people to reach the conclusion that it was the Twins who made Mei Qing and Wu Lun vanish.","Yang Xu explained how the situation had panned out and Yang Ji just sighed, “Since the Heavenly Demon Queen admitted that she was the one who kidnapped Mei Qing, then these people are partially correct. Since the Heavenly Demon Queen is tied to us, technically, we are also at fault...”","This whole event just killed Yang Ji’s mood. “Alright, alright. I give in. If we need to ask the other receptionist and they all act like this, then there is no point. *Argh* and we didn’t even do anything wrong...”","Yang Ji had his palm on his face as he rubbed his eyes in frustration. He waved his hand and the three of them all returned to the reception building.","When they returned, there was clear panic in the reception building. After all, another receptionist had just been kidnapped, and this time, in broad-daylight!","Even if it were the Twins, this matter was too serious to cover up, as even students had seen who the culprits were. They would certainly need to report this matter to their superiors, even if they believed no repercussions would be dealt to the Twins.","When those two came back, obviously their hearts jumped. After all, even if Yang Ji had forced Yang Xu to release the receptionist they caught, manipulating Space Principles to both tear down the space they were in and his Sister’s grasp on the receptionist, the woman in question was still in tears, continuously pleading even after she had been returned back.","In fact, her pleading got even stronger once she got out of that space and saw others around her...","If one were to see such a situation, what would they normally think? That the Twins were having tea with her? Chatting casually?","Yang Ji and Yang Xu both sighed at that moment. They just wanted to return her back to her original place... they did not do anything to her... Yet, everyone around them was looking at them like they were sinister beasts.","Silavin: Sorry for the belated chapter. I didn’t really want to split this into two, despite the length. I felt like it was both a mystery that was not too deep, but I wanted to cover it in one chapter since a wait of 1 week would be a little too much.","Sure, the overall mystery has not been solved, but that one is a bigger question that the Twins would have to find out later. The Heavenly Demon Queen will definitely not state it at this juncture."]},{"number":6098,"title":"Chapter 6098, Acceptance, This Plane Is Too Small For You Two","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","There was fear in their eyes. It was certainly not forged, and it came from both the students and the staff members.","“Why is everyone looking at us like this?” Yang Ji muttered under his breath. This was certainly... uncomfortable. He and his Sister had never been looked at with such eyes.","Of course, that was natural, because they just had never noticed. They rarely interacted with others outside their circle. They had been confined to Starry Sky Palace for most of their lives, and when they sought adventure, it was typically in more riskier places rather than populated ones. They had little interest in towns and cities across the world, and sought out areas of true adventure.","Even if others saw them, they had rarely used their powers on others. This could be considered the first time they had wantonly used it on someone else, who did not truly know them. As such, with the fear of their backing and the fear of these two acting as they pleased, it was no wonder that others started to fear them.","Rather than awe or shock that typically veiled their eyes, to the weak, were these two children no different than tyrants born to a massive Family, one that could not be challenged? They could do as they pleased, and no one would be able to do anything to them.","The scene of the receptionist loudly crying after being released merely pushed to cement everyone’s negative impression of them. Her desperate pleading just made it seem like they had done the worst to her.","Even if the Twins did something in the wrong, no one stood up against them. After all, who dared to go against them?","Though these people were none the wiser to the true mechanisations behind the scenes, and this impression of the Twins was a false one, it was not like the Twins could explain their way out of this situation. Who would believe them?","In fact, Yang Ji could clearly feel that any explanation was meaningless at this point. So, he just controlled his emotions and left with his Sister.","Though Yang Xu wanted to promptly explain, she too was overwhelmed when she saw her Brother leave with just dejection on his face. He did not force her to leave with him by transporting her away, but she just left after him.","As for the receptionist, her tears did not stop even after they were gone. She continued to sob until her fellow staff members came to comfort her.","...","“Brother, why did you just leave? We got to clear things up. We did none of those things.” Yang Xu quickly tried to convince him to go back but Yang Ji just shook his head.","“It’s useless. Would they believe us? We have no evidence that the matter with Wu Lun and the other receptionist, Mei Qing, was not our doing. Besides, we did actually threaten her.”","“But aren’t you angry? We’re being blamed for something we didn’t do.” Yang Xu asked with a grievous face, though she was more mad about her Brother facing this injustice than caring about how these people viewed her. In her mind, she could not care less about them and she knew it.","However, her Brother was different. He was in a way, trying to be like their Father, who was like a hero in the eyes of others. For them to suddenly look at him with such eyes, it certainly struck him.","Yang Ji just shook his head. “Though I’m not as well versed as you when it comes to dealing with people, I at least know that the more we try to explain, the more unbelievable it will seem. If we really want to prove ourselves innocent, then we would need to bring back Wu Lun and Mei Qing, no?”","Standing up in the sky, overseeing the entire school, Yang Ji then points to a particular location. “See, he’s not even hiding anymore.”","“Eh?” Yang Xu exclaimed as her eyes narrowed towards where Yang Ji was pointing towards.","After all, this was the place where the Twins had first met Wu Lun. The same small alleyway within the school. And, the mysterious youth was just standing there, waving his hand as though welcoming the Twins, despite the clear obvious distance between them.","“Is this some kind of trap?” Yang Xu questioned but Yang Ji did not believe that to be the case, “If even Father is wary of him, then it means that he could have done whatever he wished without us being able to resist. Since he is obviously welcoming us, we might as well see how things play out.”","When the two appeared before him, Wu Lun acted so familiar with them, he came in for a huge hug. However, Yang Ji immediately made a wall, made from compressing Space Principles, and protected his and his Sister’s innocence.","“That was uncalled for. I was just going in for a little hug.” Wu Lun did not seem at all bothered about his face being planted into a sudden wall. In fact, he did not even seem the slightest bit injured. He just looked at the Twins and gave a nod, “Seems like you two have gone through a lot while we last met. Missed me?”","Yang Xu rolled her eyes at his nonchalance. As for Yang Ji, his eyes narrowed and he straight forwardly asked, “Why did you do it?”","Wu Lun seemed surprised by his question. His eyes widened as a look of astonishment covered his features, “My my. What do you mean? What exactly did I do?”","“Why did you kidnap the receptionist, Mei Qing?” Yang Ji straightforwardly asked once more.","“Oh, that.” Wu Lun paused for a while and looked up into the sky. He shook his head and smiled, “I have no need for third-parties to know about this. Just know that she is safe and well. Besides, the reason I’m here to see you two is more important than her.”","Wu Lun paused for a while, gauging to see if the Twins were going to pursue this topic further. However, seeing them keep silent, he continued, “Due to some dreadful terms a cunning beast had left behind, I am forced to take you two away. But before that, I wish to explain further so that you understand your situation.”","Wu Lun’s expression changed at this moment. It was no longer that of a child fooling around, but that of an eternal being who had witnessed the vestige of time and the mortality of worlds. His eyes glowed and his voice deepened, sounding both foreign and mysterious. “You two will not grow further in this plane. So, come with me. Refusal is impossible due to the Convent. I have also seen how your Will also has no effect on fate.”","“So, that’s what you two were talking about at that time. So you and that worm are in cahoots to kidnap us?” Yang Xu suddenly blurted out.","At this point, Wu Lun smiled, “How is it kidnapping when even your Parents have agreed to it?”","This answer rang in the Twins’ ears. They could not believe their Father or Mothers would ever agree to such a thing.","“That’s not possible.” Yang Xu replied.","“Then, do you believe that they are not aware of our meeting?” Wu Lun smiled and pointed up at the sky. “You two have basically outgrown whatever they can teach you. Most of your journey in cultivation has been self-learnt rather than taught. Unlike any of your Siblings, neither of you two have a real Master. Have you two never considered why? What use is this school to the two of you? Continuing like this just hinders the growth of others, and your own growth.”","Wu Lun then snaps his fingers, and the world around them changed. This was not them switching positions, rather they were just seeing the sights of another location. They were watching the inside of the reception building, where the receptionist was still crying, where people were discussing about the Twins.","Everything was clearly illusionary. So, Yang Ji, having his doubts, opened up an opening through Space, a small portal to hear if the conversation matched up to what they were seeing and hearing from Wu Lun’s mysterious creation.","And... it was exactly the same...","“I’m so glad you’re okay...”","“Since they’ve let you go, I’m sure they won’t bother you anymore.”","“We can’t say that for certain. What if they come back to retaliate? What then? Do you think their Parents will do anything?”","“But, their Father is Senior Yang Kai, the great hero. Surely he will protect us.”","“Bah! Protect us? Have you not seen him cover up for his kids? What about those missing? We haven’t even received so much as an explanation, and we know he had the power to monitor this entire world he created.”","There were voices of worry and dissent amongst them, As the sobbing receptionist got comforted, others also turned towards those in senior positions and asked.","“Senior, if the same thing happens to us, what are we to do?”","“Senior, has there been any response from the higher-ups?”","The overall in charge shook his head and he addressed their concern. Though, his answer was not much... “*Haaa...* Such matters are difficult. As you know, those two are not ordinary children. I’ve heard even Cave Heavens and Paradises bend to them. Just listen to my advice and avoid them as much as possible.”","...","Such conversations were occurring everywhere. Though the Twins did nothing wrong, it did not matter. The truth of the matter was, regardless of how they act, these people were more afraid of offending them.","Though Yang Kai and his Wives hope to alleviate the class disparity amongst people, it could not be rooted out immediately. Even if there were some who believe that Yang Kai was just, they would hold their breath as the current evidence does point counter to their own thoughts.","Furthermore, did Yang Ji and Yang Xu not wantonly do as they pleased just because they had the strength to do so? Did this not run counter to the ideals of High Heaven Academy?","Though Yang Kai’s Wives wanted to integrate their children into this school, it was obvious that the school itself could not accommodate them. In that case, why limit them here?","The only thing restricting them from taking that final step in accepting this reality was the longing of Parents towards their Children.","However, Wu Lun had brought reality in front of all their faces. He highlighted how inadequate the school was for the Twins. That, as Parents, their own emotions were limiting their own Children’s growth.","Faced with this reality, what else could they choose?","Faced with this reality, how could they refuse?","Even if reluctant, even if pained, Yang Kai could only make a choice. Even if his Wives got angry with him, even if his Parents threw him out of the house for the next few decades, he knew as a Father, this was what was best for his kids.","They needed to see a wider world, a world that could fit them.","This world was simply too small for talent like theirs.","As a Father, he was proud. But as a Father, he was also fearful. Would they be safe? They were going to be alone in that mysterious plane.","However, when Yang Kai looked into the mirror, and saw his own reflection, part of him calmed down a little. They were, after all, his Children. If he did not believe them, who else would?","So, the decision was made.","And Wu Lun moved..."]},{"number":6099,"title":"Chapter 6099, Are You Willing To Go?","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","The showcase continued on for a few minutes before Wu Lun had enough and dispersed the illusions with a wave of his hands. He looked towards the Twins and asked once more, “Do you not see it already? This is merely fate, an inevitability. You two simply do not belong here.”","Seeing the two children still seemingly unconvinced, maybe because they refused to accept reality for what it was, or maybe because they refused to accept whatever Wu Lun says. Regardless, Wu Lun looked towards the empty sky and asked with a smile, “Well, regardless of their Will, I will be taking them away. Are you sure you do not wish to bid them farewell?”","At that moment, the space in front of Wu Lun warped and out came the very man who created this whole school.","As Yang Kai stepped out of the Void, he truly looked haggard. His eyes were sunken, with eye bags beneath more glaring than usual. It was obvious that this matter had dealt him considerable stress. After all, even if he did not sleep for a year, he would not feel physically tired. So, this exhaustion must be of the mind and Soul rather than anything physical.","Yang Kai looked towards the Twins and smiled. It was a weak smile, one they had never seen their Father display before. He had always been the strong and imposing figure, the man who towered over all others. However, at this moment, he truly looked to be like any ordinary man. No, he was just a Father at this moment.","However, this time, strangely, only he had turned up. Their Mothers did not appear.","When the Twins noticed this, they could not help but feel a deep pit in their stomachs.","“Come here.” Yang Kai gestured to them and bent down.","The two obediently came over, and Yang Kai used both arms to embrace them. There was no explanation. He just sporadically did it. The Twins then communicated to each other in a panic.","“Wait... are we really going to be sent off?”","“From how Father looks, it seems like he has made up his mind...”","“But Brother, aren’t you usually excited by being able to go somewhere new?”","“Yeah, But, we most likely won’t be able to return, you know? Trips that take a month or two are fine but this... isn’t this too much? I don’t really want to go.”","“Same here. Maybe we can plead to stay? Mother will definitely not allow Father to send us off like this.”","“Maybe that’s why she’s not here?”","The Twins both gave a tacit nod and they both pushed Yang Kai away.","They both asked in tandem, at the same time, in unison. “Father, what’s going on? Why are you the only one here?”","Yang Kai gave a sigh and then he looked towards Wu Lun.","The smiling man gave a gentle nod and then disappeared. Though, whether he was truly gone was questionable at best.","Yang Kai then put up a barrier, to seal this alleyway from the world, where no one would be able to listen in on their conversation. He then turned to the Twins and started explaining.","“Where should I start... right. I should start by explaining what kind of place you two are going to...”","Yang Kai soon sat the two down as he began elaborating on what he had found over the years.","“You two are well aware that we are building a large Artifact that functions as a ship which will cross over to other worlds, outside of the 3,000 Worlds. This will be a ship where your Mothers and I will board after all your children grow up. But, are you aware of why there is a need for us to do this?”","Yang Ji raised his hand and answered, “Father, isn’t it because you want to save your friend? The one trapped in a place you call the Taboo Realm?”","Yang Kai looked at a far off distance and reminisced. “Yes, but that is only part of the reason. The bigger reason is the existence of the Taboo Realm itself and the other mysteries plaguing this world. Mysteries that even those who stand at the peak of this world are unaware of.”","Yang Kai then closed his eyes for a moment and moved his hand. Soon, a majestic river formed between his hands, seemingly able to encapsulate the whole world. Naturally, this was the perfected Space-Time River, where all 3,000 Daos exists.","Yang Kai spread out the Space-Time River and covered not just the Twins but himself as well.","The river water completely drowned the Twins. However, they found that despite it rushing towards them like a torrent, when it struck, it was as gentle as the caress from the wind. There was no hard impact, only a soft embracing wrap.","The water was neither cold nor warm, neither wet nor dry. It felt like they were oddly standing in the air, with their surroundings now turned into the night. There were the gleams of stars all around them, but the supposed dark night was instead a golden-yellow hue, which made the world seem all brighter than possible.","Still, those seeming stars were manifestations of worlds, condensed into what seemed like glowing rocks.","Yang Kai picked one from the seemingly infinite sky and held it in his hand. It was no different from a ball at this moment, yet when he released it, as the ball fell, it began to expand at a speed visible to the naked eye.","Yang Ji and Yang Xu thought that at this rate, it was going to hit them. However, contrary to their thoughts, this ball just expanded past them, engulfing them inside of it as they now stepped into the world Yang Kai wished for them to see.","The golden-yellow water was now replaced by an ever lasting darkness that refused to retreat.","This was naturally not a new world. Rather, Yang Kai’s memory of a place which they had all been to. Yes, this was none other than the world behind the Profound Source Gate, where darkness reigned.","The Twins looked around and were shocked as they saw themselves there, off in the distance. Their projections were currently in battle against that Royal Lord, while they were in the sky.","Obviously, they were standing where Yang Kai had been when he was monitoring them at the time. He was so distant that the Twins would never be able to notice him, despite their high attainment over the Dao of Space.","Yang Kai, who did not have a projected self here, appeared as himself and was standing next to Su Yan. Technically, standing behind her with his hand holding her arms as though she was ready to charge ahead and save them.","However, to say that this was a completely accurate replaying of that moment was wrong. After all, Su Yan just froze for a moment and disappeared. Obviously, Yang Kai did not want to show his children how their Father had to handle his Wife in this situation.","Yang Kai just coughing and pointed over at a distance. “*Ahem.* Despite being so deep in enemy territory, you two were still too far away to notice that the enemy was actually closing in on your two. Furthermore, it was not just that Royal Lord and Territory Lord. Those were just scouts. There was an even greater force brewing deep inside.”","With a wave, Yang Kai shifted their position to move away from where the Twins stood, to another far off location where the Twins could never reach. In fact, it was so distant that they would have taken days even if they travelled through the Void to quicken things up. However, it was only fortunate that with Yang Kai’s ridiculous Divine Sense, able to pierce through the mysterious multilayered space of the Source World, that he had managed to map out this area and recreate it.","At this location, there was a mass horde that would overwhelm any world. In fact, this might be enough to take half of the 3,000 Worlds if Yang Kai had not been around. Their numbers were so terrifying that the land beneath was only filled with insectoid heads.","This army was not standing on any structure. They built no buildings to house themselves. They seemed mindless, only filled with the desire to slaughter. Yet, they moved as though they were a single unit, like a swarm following a single order.","Yang Kai pointed to this swarm and asked, “Do you not notice the oddity here?”","Yang Xu gave a nod and pointed out. “There are too many of them.”","“Exactly. Without any resources, how is it possible for an army to be created?” Yang Kai stressed with a grim face, “In short, they must have plundered another world. And this army, this is most likely not even half of what they actually have.”","“But Father, if you knew about this, then why did you not wipe them out? It should be easy for you, no?” Yang Ji asked the most glaring question in his mind.","“I tried once, but I can only eliminate these creations. I can’t do much about the two free sources of trouble. They hide too well within this place, and they can retreat all the way to other worlds if they have to. Also, your Uncle Eleven had told me not to interfere too much with this world, that there are wider repercussions that I cannot bear. He did not explain much at the time, but it was obvious he couldn’t explain rather than he lacked the will to explain.” Yang Kai’s eyes narrowed and he sighed. “Well, that’s the situation on this side. But, this is a matter for your Father and your Uncles to worry about. This is a matter that we will resolve before ever allowing children of your generation to have to step up to the plate.”","Yang Kai then pointed to another location, “This is what I truly want you two to focus on.”","There was a door, ancient as if born from the start of time itself. It laid well hidden within the veil of darkness. However, its existence was made noticeable by how a myriad of figures were moving through it. So, as it remained open, some light managed to pass through and it managed to show itself.","Still, when the Twins caught sight of this, their eyes naturally widened. Yang Ji exclaimed, “Isn’t this the Profound Source Gate we went through?”","Yang Kai immediately shook his head. “This is a different one, but it looks exactly like the one on our side.”","“Our side? Then, Father, you are saying that there are more of these?” Yang Ji exclaimed and then realised, “So that’s what you mean by ‘plundered another world’ this is the Profound Source Gate that leads to another world.”","“But, then, that’s strange. Father, if you knew about the existence of this other gate, why do you need to build that ship, which is prepared for a long voyage?” Yang Xu soon opened her mouth to question. “You could have just travelled here and entered the other world. I believe with how proficient you are in the Dao of Space, you would be able to move faster than any ship. At least, that would be how Brother and I would have done it”","Yang Kai gave a nod and answered, “I too would have done the same. Did Little Eleven not say that many years ago, I came here? I naturally found another of these gates but guess what, I could not open it. Even with all my strength I could not open a single door, and I had found quite a few.”","“Years later, when asked Little Eleven why that was, he could not answer. So, there must be some kind of mystery related to these gates which we are unaware of. But, from what I know, Mo or Little Eleven cannot open these gates themselves as well. At least not from the inside. Else, he would not be trapped here before Mu came and released him into our 3,000 Worlds.” Yang Kai theorised and the Twins naturally understood most of his thoughts, since they had learnt a ton of history from their Aunt Yang Xue before.","“So, the only way we can realistically travel to the other worlds is from the outside. That’s why we still need the ship, since most of the space beyond the 3,000 Worlds is just empty.” Yang Kai said and pointed back to the Profound Source Gate. “It is equally strange how we are able to open the gate on our side to enter and exit but not the other gates. So, it is a wonder how this gate is actually opened.”","“But Father, what does this have to do with needing us to be sent away?” Yang Xu questioned as so far, there was no link to the two topics.","“Of course it is related. Now, here is the question, do you think these gates are made naturally?” Yang Kai asked with a critical expression.","The Twins looked at each other and wondered for a while. It felt like a trick question, since from what they were told, the original Profound Source Gate had been made by Heaven and Earth. So, how could it be from the hands of man?","“No?” Yang Ji answered with uncertainty.","Yang Kai soon shook his head, “Initially, I too thought that it was naturally made, born from Heaven and Earth itself. But, when I look at things from a wider lens, I began to notice a flaw in this. The nature of Heaven and Earth is such that no two things are perfectly the same (天下没有两片相同的叶子). So. how is it that these gates all look perfectly identical to one another?”","“Then, Father, you are saying...”","“As what must have come to your mind as I said it. Someone must have created all these, and we do not know who nor what. A being that even I cannot fathom. Even if I spend years trying to comprehend how these gates are made, I could not make any headway. No matter how rare the material, what haven’t I seen? No matter how profound the Dao, what haven’t I mastered? Yet, how is it that even I cannot comprehend the creation of such Artifacts?” Yang Kai’s eyes narrowed and there was a trace of fear inside.","When he was younger, this fear might not have appeared so easily. However, now that he had so many loved ones, it was inevitable for him to fear–not for himself, but for his loved ones. If he had to lay his life down to protect his children, then so be it. But if he was keenly aware he was not strong enough to protect them from this unknown entity, then how could he not start to worry?","“This material, it is not from our world. I’m certain that it can’t be. It can’t be from any world that exists on the same level as our world.” Yang Kai said and continued narrating in a softer tone as he spoke of his past. “Yang Ji, Yang Xu, as you both know, our Yang Family are not originally from the 3,000 Worlds. We were from the Tong Xuan Continent, or more precisely, the Great Han Dynasty within what we now call the Tong Xuan Realm, which cannot even be considered a Universe World. It is just a Cultivation Star, and an isolated one at that. Just some backwards place, where the top experts are only in the Immortal Ascension Realm.”","“Through my journey, it was only later that we found out that the Tong Xuan Realm lies within the Heng Luo Star Field. Funnily enough, this situation repeats itself as the Heng Luo Star Field lies within Star Boundary, which lies within the 3,000 Worlds...”","“Each revelation or expansion was like we were all frogs at the bottom of the well. The world would enlarge each time I had to travel to a distant place, where my enemies would grow stronger with each turn, where treasures and Artifacts would grow more profound, and stronger Secret Techniques would replace my old ones. Each time, I grew and I would never have grown to this extent if I never left the Tong Xuan Realm. In fact, at the time, we did not even know that above the Immortal Ascension Realm, there was the Transcendent Realm. We used to call it the Above Immortal Ascension Realm, silly, right?” Yang Kai’s eyes seemed to carry a hint of joy at these nostalgic memories.","However, those eyes soon turn resolute. “It is because I know the potential you two share that I cannot allow you two to be limited here. Even if I do not wish for you two to leave, I must push you two to.”","“If I had never stepped out of the Tong Xuan Realm, I would most likely be dead by now. Not due to the world ending, but my own limited lifespan. What’s more, the world around us would have been completely annihilated by Black Ink Strength, and I would have died none the wiser.”","“In short, I need to send you two out not only for your sake, but for the sake of everyone else here. In fact, I want to be the one to make this trip if possible, but I know I can’t. This place still needs me. Unlike last time, where I was a lone man wandering the cosmos, where my responsibilities lay solely on preserving my own life, this time, I have placed far too many matters on my shoulders that I can no longer walk away from.”","“I need to remain here, to protect this place. So, I can only count on the two of you to make the trip.” Yang Kai moved closer to the Twins, and with his hands, he gently placed them on their shoulders. “Besides, out of all the children, no, out of everyone here, you two are probably the closest to that place. The Cultivation Technique that you two use, it is definitely not of this world. Being stuck here is no different from chaining down your real potential.”","Yang Kai then tried to crack up a joke to lighten the mood. “Also, did you two think we did not notice how you two have been slacking off in cultivating, only focusing on gaining insights into the Daos or testing new power? If you two were really focused, with that strange Cultivation Technique of yours, one could play around while the other would cultivate. I believe that if you two wish, both of you would have touched the threshold of the Dao Seal Realm by now.”","“No, that’s not it... we just...” Yang Ji wanted to explain but Yang Kai just shook his head.","“I know. You did not want to leave your Siblings too far behind, right? Though, I guess studying the Dao of Space and the Dao of Time have been a lot more interesting to the two of you than just plain cultivating. Otherwise, how would you two have reached attainment comparable to even Open Heaven Realm Masters and manipulate Principles when still only in the Dao Source Realm. Honestly, what are we to do with the two of you?” Yang Kai chuckled, and then took a moment before reiterating, “This is something that I’ve failed in. Even after so many years, I could not help make a proper environment for the two of you to grow in. I could not find a proper Master for the two of you and I could not truly properly guide you two as well. That’s all the more reason why I need to send you out there. Learn, and get stronger. Who knows, maybe in the far off future, we might be able to cross blades with all our might and drink under the stars. What joy that would be.”","Yang Kai gave a more hopeful spin to it as his hand moved towards the top of their heads and he gave a gentle caress. “After listening to all this, are you two willing to go? If not, then as your Father, I will do everything in my might to make you stay. But if you are willing, then, this will be our parting, and I will await the time when you two will be old enough to be able to drink.”","The Twins looked at each other, one was worried while the other was resolute. When Yang Xu saw her Brother’s eyes, she already knew the answer.","Since he had already decided, then she would simply have to follow him. It was no different from usual.","So, the Twins gave each other a nod and spoke in unison, “Father, we will go.”","Yang Kai’s expression at that moment held his mixed feelings. He had hoped for them to refuse and had hoped for them to go. Realising the feelings rushing through him at the moment, he took back his hands and focused on his expression, controlling it to give a forced smile.","He then closed his eyes for a short moment to take it all in.","“Understood.” With that one single word, the world around them shattered and the Space-Time River retreated back to its owner. It all happened in an instant, with the world returning back to normal...","Silavin: 天下没有两片相同的叶子 – Under the Heaven, there are no two leaves that are the same.","Another late chapter, but I can’t bear to break this chapter up TT^TT."]},{"number":6100,"title":"Chapter 6100, Left The 3,000 Worlds","paragraphs":["Author: Silavin","Once they returned back into the alleyway, Yang Kai closed his eyes for a moment and took a deep breath. It was as though he was trying to digest this decision once more, and the consequences that followed.","He then sent a message through Divine Sense to his Wives, to have them prepare. Since this was the last time they might be able to see their Eldest Children, they naturally had to bid them farewell.","Not to mention... he had to break the news to his Parents, especially his Mother...","In all honesty, he hoped his Wives would be able to support him in holding back his Mother. He also now realised how hard his Father must have worked while Yang Kai was still young, to keep her calm enough to accept his departures, be it for High Heaven Pavilion or any of his other solo adventures.","Still, it seemed like all plans for this would be dashed as Wu Lun suddenly appeared behind the Twins. None of them had even been able to sense him before Wu Lun hugged them around the neck and smiled to Yang Kai, “Alright. Now that you’ve bid your farewell, I’ll be taking them away.”","Yang Kai immediately instinctively locked the Space around them as he shouted, “Wait!” However, it was far too late. No, it would not have worked in the first place. If it did, Wu Lun would not be considered to be such a dangerous being.","Phasing through Space like a ghost, seeming to swim through solid matter without a care in the world, the frozen Space could not hinder him in the slightest as Wu Lun simply fell backwards with the Twin in his arms.","At the same time, Yang Ji and Yang Xu instinctively tried to resist. The former tried to manipulate Space Principles while the latter tried to manipulate Time Principles. However, it was all in vain.","Principles seemed to freeze over and were unable to respond. It felt as though their arms and feet were tied, as something they did as naturally as breathing was now being hampered.","Shock filled their faces as they were about to try to call out to their Father but... he had disappeared from sight by then.","...","With Wu Lun’s disappearance, Yang Kai immediately received another message. This time, it was from Xia Ning Chang.","“Husband! Yang Ling... she’s gone!”","Sensing the panic in her voice, Yang Kai could not help but frown. He immediately used his Divine Sense to sweep through this world, and as she said, Yang Ling was truly gone. He could not sense her presence, much like he could not sense Yang Ji, Yang Xu and Wu Lun...","“That bastard!” Yang Kai immediately clenched his teeth so tight one could hear them scream.","The flooring underneath him started to crack, and walls of buildings started to tremble.","However, before he rushed out and did something rash, Shi immediately appeared and cordoned off the area. He quickly deployed the Heaven Devouring Battle Law and used it to absorb any excess energy Yang Kai was leaking out.","Be it his aura or just his voice infused with a trace amount of his Qi, the children surrounding the school would not be able to handle such pressure. If Yang Kai were to release just a trace of it, even if there were Arrays protecting the students, they still might get hurt.","“Stop! Are you planning to destroy the school by meaninglessly rampaging here!?” Shi roared and held his fist tight to contain the excess energy.","Thankfully, Yang Kai was quick enough to collect his cool and he took deep breaths to calm himself. His eyes still blazed with fury though, as he was about to take a step, Shi stopped him. “You can’t even sense him. What is the point of trying to go after him?”","“I–” Yang Kai wanted to speak but Shi was quick to point out.","“Just stop here. We both know that he has taken them to the other Plane. Rather than spend time worrying about them, you might as well console your Wives first.” Shi added, and sighed. “Part of you still doesn’t want them to go, I understand that. But, the arrow has left the bow, there is no taking it back now.”","“If you yourself are not convinced, what are you going to say to the rest of your Family members? Su Yan is only being held back by your Sister right now. The rest of your Wives are also unconvinced, but have held back since you’ve said you will leave the decision to the Twins. Now that Yang Ling has been taken, how do you think they would react?”","“Yeah. But what if...” Yang Kai tried to rebut but Shi immediately shot him down.","“You did not even explain to them the limitations of our Open Heaven Realm Cultivation Method earlier. It is obvious that you are as reluctant as your Wives to see them go. But, you know better than to limit their potential. As for their safety, with that thing inside of them, relying on them, you think they would be in any real danger over there?” Shi added, “Just trust them. They are your children after all. As for Yang Ling, I’m sure they have some plans for her.”","“If they do not wish to permanently draw the line between them and the Twins, they would do well to protect her. Otherwise, maybe this is an opportunity for her as well?” Shi said in a calm tone.","“*Haa...*” Yang Kai took a deep breath, sighed and then turned to the sky, his thoughts messy. His aura had also deflated and Shi finally stopped operating the Heaven Devouring Battle Law.","Yang Kai turned towards Shi and wanted to thank him, but before he could, Shi put his palm up.","“We don’t have much time for small talk. Go deal with your women.” Shi said as he used his thumb to point behind him, where he could sense Space being torn.","At this point, Yang Kai’s expression changed. Now, he had a face that had written ‘Brother, can you please help me this once?’ on it.","However, Shi, the eternal bachelor, looked straight into Yang Kai’s eyes and immediately disappeared from sight.","...","““Let go!”” Yang Ji and Yang Xu screamed out.","“Sure.” Wu Lun readily answered with a smile as always.","They had been only hugged for what felt like a second, and taken away in that very instant to see another area. This time, it was oddly a more familiar area to the two of them...","After all, they were both located at the bottom of High Heaven Academy, at where the Grand Array lay.","It was a massive underground facility which was used to house the Arrays made to facilitate the different functions of the school. Naturally, this place was massive enough to basically cover the whole school, and it was below ground.","Due to the nature of Arrays, there were markings all over the place, complex markings that were made of different materials that glowed with multi-coloured light. It was strangely mesmerising for any viewer. Yet, to the Twins, this just raised more questions. After all, they were obviously in a secured location that was protected by powerful Arrays. Yet, they had been so easily transported here.","Furthermore, due to the sensitive nature of this location, were there no guards or observers? Due to the nature of Arrays, certain points were more fragile than others. They could not have some random child coming in here and picking up some glowing rock. There had to be someone overseeing this place.","Yet, within this massive space, Yang Ji and Yang Xu could not detect a single presence other than theirs.","“Wait. Why are we here?” Yang Ji’s eyes narrowed as he scanned his surroundings.","Wu Lun ignored him and directly addressed, “I’ve already brought them here. Come out and do the rest.” before disappearing once more.","And, the one he spoke to naturally appeared, out of Yang Ji, and turned to address the Twins directly.","“For it is through the Array here that our path to the long-sought Plane shall be made to manifest.” The Heavenly Demon Queen finally came out to explain.","And, the instant she did, Wu Lun had returned. This time, with two more guests: Mei Qing, the receptionist, and Yang Ling.","Mei Qing was in an unconscious state, and was being carried by Wu Lun over his shoulder. As for Yang Ling, she was just held by the hand, and led here.","When Yang Ji and Yang Xu saw Yang Ling, their eyes widened with shock.","[Why is she here!?] They both simultaneously thought but had not voiced it out before the Heavenly Demon Queen opened her mouth to ask Yang Ling, “Are you certain?”","Yang Ling, suddenly ‘kidnapped’, did not seem surprised and just gave a nod.","The Heavenly Demon Queen looked to Wu Lun and stated, “If I am not mistaken, it falls upon me to conduct our passage to the Source Realm as the first undertaking. Once we have arrived, I trust the remainder shall rest in your hands.”","“What else? This was your whole plan, wasn’t it? That’s why you modified the Arrays here.” Wu Lun rolled his eyes.","“I understand.” The Heavenly Demon Queen’s eyes opened wide for a brief moment but she gave a nod at the end.","“Then, let’s begin.” The Heavenly Demon Queen stated and she closed her eyes.","Soon, part of the Grand Array glowed brighter than the rest. This was an Array hidden within the Grand Array. Naturally, the Heavenly Demon Queen had modified the Grand Array to hold various hidden functions.","For example, one of them was to allow the Twins the ability to use their Qi even within school. The other was selective concealment, to conceal the presence of a few selected people when they were within the Grand Array. Naturally, other functions were included such as how she had retained leverage over Wu Lun and the most troublesome one, which was a Teleportation Array to the Source Realm...","Naturally, there was a worry that Yang Kai might change the Arrays here at any given moment. So, the Heavenly Demon Queen had also made it such that if one part was modified, she would be alerted.","“Wait a second! What is Yang Ling doing here!? Hey!” Yang Ji grew more panicked as he noticed they were about to be transported away.","“Yang Ling, you knew about this!?” Yang Xu rushed over and questioned.","However, before they could get any answers, Wu Lun clicked his tongue and said, “Just stay still. Even if that friend of yours is a genius in the True Dao of Spirit Arrays, it is still not easy to modify another’s work and add so many functionalities with no additional resources. I can’t risk anything happening to the four of you.”","Once more, Yang Ji and Yang Xu felt as though the Principles around them were frozen. Worse yet, their physical bodies could not move, as though they were being pressed down in all directions by mountains.","It did not hurt if they stood still, but once they tried to so much as blink, they could feel as though their bodies were being torn apart by a thousand blades.","“Don’t hurt my Older Brother and Older Sister!” Yang Ling, seeing them suddenly stop moving and were in awkward positions, pouted and complained, but it did not work on Wu Lun. For the man was genuinely willful to the extreme.","The Heavenly Demon Queen soon opened her eyes and the world turned bright.","At that very moment, all three children were no longer in the 3,000 Worlds."]}]);
